    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-55e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55E Participant must comply with notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-55e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.31",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A surcharge participant commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the surcharge participant is given a surcharge information\nnotice; and\n\n(b) the surcharge participant fails to comply with the notice\nwithin the period for so complying.\nPenalty: 30 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.\nNote:\nSections 137.1 and 137.2 of the Criminal Code create offences for\nproviding false or misleading information or documents.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A surcharge participant commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the surcharge participant is given a surcharge information\nnotice; and\n\n(b) the surcharge participant fails to comply with the notice\nwithin the period for so complying.\nPenalty: 30 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.\nNote:\nSections 137.1 and 137.2 of the Criminal Code create offences for\nproviding false or misleading information or documents.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
