      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-55m",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55M Infringement notice compliance period for infringement notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-55m"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to this section, the infringement notice compliance period\nfor an infringement notice is the period of 28 days beginning on the\nday after the day that the infringement notice is issued by the\nCommission.\n\n(2) The Commission may extend, by notice in writing, the\ninfringement notice compliance period for the infringement notice\nif the Commission is satisfied that it is appropriate to do so.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nPayment surcharges  Part IVC\nInfringement notices  Division 4\n\nSection 55N\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) Only one extension may be given and the extension must not be for\nlonger than 28 days.\n\n(4) Notice of the extension must be given to the person who was\nissued the infringement notice.\n\n(5) A failure to comply with subsection (4) does not affect the validity\nof the extension.\n\n(6) If the Commission extends the infringement notice compliance\nperiod for an infringement notice, a reference in this Division to\nthe infringement notice compliance period for an infringement\nnotice is taken to be a reference to the infringement notice\ncompliance period as so extended.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to this section, the infringement notice compliance period\nfor an infringement notice is the period of 28 days beginning on the\nday after the day that the infringement notice is issued by the\nCommission.\n\n(2) The Commission may extend, by notice in writing, the\ninfringement notice compliance period for the infringement notice\nif the Commission is satisfied that it is appropriate to do so.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nPayment surcharges  Part IVC\nInfringement notices  Division 4\n\nSection 55N\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) Only one extension may be given and the extension must not be for\nlonger than 28 days.\n\n(4) Notice of the extension must be given to the person who was\nissued the infringement notice.\n\n(5) A failure to comply with subsection (4) does not affect the validity\nof the extension.\n\n(6) If the Commission extends the infringement notice compliance\nperiod for an infringement notice, a reference in this Division to\nthe infringement notice compliance period for an infringement\nnotice is taken to be a reference to the infringement notice\ncompliance period as so extended.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-55m-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-55m-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-55m-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-55m-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-55m-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-55m-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8158b9b57da538ecd48ff73a61bdb5f1b407fd3b203118e33a922f67854d9753"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-55m",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55M Infringement notice compliance period for infringement notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to this section, the infringement notice compliance period\nfor an infringement notice is the period of 28 days beginning on the\nday after the day that the infringement notice is issued by the\nCommission.\n\n(2) The Commission may extend, by notice in writing, the\ninfringement notice compliance period for the infringement notice\nif the Commission is satisfied that it is appropriate to do so.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nPayment surcharges  Part IVC\nInfringement notices  Division 4\n\nSection 55N\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) Only one extension may be given and the extension must not be for\nlonger than 28 days.\n\n(4) Notice of the extension must be given to the person who was\nissued the infringement notice.\n\n(5) A failure to comply with subsection (4) does not affect the validity\nof the extension.\n\n(6) If the Commission extends the infringement notice compliance\nperiod for an infringement notice, a reference in this Division to\nthe infringement notice compliance period for an infringement\nnotice is taken to be a reference to the infringement notice\ncompliance period as so extended."
    },
