    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ad",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56AD Minister’s tasks before designating a sector or declaring",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ad"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "actions etc.\n\n(1) Before making an instrument under subsection 56AC(2) or\nsection 56ACA, the Minister must consider all of the following:\n\n(a) the likely effect of making the instrument on:\n\n(i) the interests of consumers; and\n\n(ii) the efficiency of relevant markets; and\n\n(iii) the privacy or confidentiality of consumers’\ninformation; and\n\n(iv) promoting competition; and\n\n(v) promoting data-driven innovation; and\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "actions etc.\n\n(1) Before making an instrument under subsection 56AC(2) or\nsection 56ACA, the Minister must consider all of the following:\n\n(a) the likely effect of making the instrument on:\n\n(i) the interests of consumers; and\n\n(ii) the efficiency of relevant markets; and\n\n(iii) the privacy or confidentiality of consumers’\ninformation; and\n\n(iv) promoting competition; and\n\n(v) promoting data-driven innovation; and\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ad-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ad-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ad-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c82ab171e8731e0ccd33a4dd3b0498cb43373a3c100a5376fac254658a8a9ae8",
      "skos:note": "Consider all relevant factors before making an instrument."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ad",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56AD Minister’s tasks before designating a sector or declaring",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 41,
      "values:originalText": "actions etc.\n\n(1) Before making an instrument under subsection 56AC(2) or\nsection 56ACA, the Minister must consider all of the following:\n\n(a) the likely effect of making the instrument on:\n\n(i) the interests of consumers; and\n\n(ii) the efficiency of relevant markets; and\n\n(iii) the privacy or confidentiality of consumers’\ninformation; and\n\n(iv) promoting competition; and\n\n(v) promoting data-driven innovation; and\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
