    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ae",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56AE Secretary must arrange for analysis, consultation and report",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ae"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.43",
      "values:originalText": "about an instrument proposing to designate a sector or\ndeclare actions\n\n(1) The Secretary of the Department complies with this section in\nrelation to the making of an instrument under subsection 56AC(2)\nor section 56ACA if the Secretary arranges for all of the following:\n\n(a) an analysis of the matters in paragraphs 56AD(1)(a) to (e) in\nrelation to the instrument;\n\n(b) public consultation about those matters in relation to the\ninstrument:\n\n(i) for at least 28 days; and\n\n(ii) in one or more ways that include making information\navailable on the Department’s website and inviting the\npublic to comment;\n\n(c) consultation with each of the following about those matters\nin relation to the instrument:\n\n(i) the Commission;\n\n(ii) the Information Commissioner;\n\n(iii) for an instrument under subsection 56AC(2)—the\nperson or body (if any) that the Secretary believes to be\nthe primary regulator of the sector that the instrument\nwould designate;\n\n(iiia) for an instrument under section 56ACA—a person or\nbody (if any) that the Secretary believes to be a\nregulator of a type of actions that the instrument would\ndeclare;\n\n(iv) any person or body prescribed by the regulations;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "about an instrument proposing to designate a sector or\ndeclare actions\n\n(1) The Secretary of the Department complies with this section in\nrelation to the making of an instrument under subsection 56AC(2)\nor section 56ACA if the Secretary arranges for all of the following:\n\n(a) an analysis of the matters in paragraphs 56AD(1)(a) to (e) in\nrelation to the instrument;\n\n(b) public consultation about those matters in relation to the\ninstrument:\n\n(i) for at least 28 days; and\n\n(ii) in one or more ways that include making information\navailable on the Department’s website and inviting the\npublic to comment;\n\n(c) consultation with each of the following about those matters\nin relation to the instrument:\n\n(i) the Commission;\n\n(ii) the Information Commissioner;\n\n(iii) for an instrument under subsection 56AC(2)—the\nperson or body (if any) that the Secretary believes to be\nthe primary regulator of the sector that the instrument\nwould designate;\n\n(iiia) for an instrument under section 56ACA—a person or\nbody (if any) that the Secretary believes to be a\nregulator of a type of actions that the instrument would\ndeclare;\n\n(iv) any person or body prescribed by the regulations;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ae-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ae-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ae-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "10b2a040aa3561e537f5f5008094bf1d6b9fcea5d699b2b7c8e54245da737dfc",
      "skos:note": "The Secretary must arrange for analysis, consultation and report on an instrument proposing to designate a sector or declare actions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ae",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56AE Secretary must arrange for analysis, consultation and report",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 43,
      "values:originalText": "about an instrument proposing to designate a sector or\ndeclare actions\n\n(1) The Secretary of the Department complies with this section in\nrelation to the making of an instrument under subsection 56AC(2)\nor section 56ACA if the Secretary arranges for all of the following:\n\n(a) an analysis of the matters in paragraphs 56AD(1)(a) to (e) in\nrelation to the instrument;\n\n(b) public consultation about those matters in relation to the\ninstrument:\n\n(i) for at least 28 days; and\n\n(ii) in one or more ways that include making information\navailable on the Department’s website and inviting the\npublic to comment;\n\n(c) consultation with each of the following about those matters\nin relation to the instrument:\n\n(i) the Commission;\n\n(ii) the Information Commissioner;\n\n(iii) for an instrument under subsection 56AC(2)—the\nperson or body (if any) that the Secretary believes to be\nthe primary regulator of the sector that the instrument\nwould designate;\n\n(iiia) for an instrument under section 56ACA—a person or\nbody (if any) that the Secretary believes to be a\nregulator of a type of actions that the instrument would\ndeclare;\n\n(iv) any person or body prescribed by the regulations;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ae-norm",
