    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ak",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56AK Meaning of accredited data recipient",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ak"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is an accredited data recipient, of CDR data, if:\n\n(a) the person is an accredited person; and\n\n(b) the CDR data is held by (or on behalf of) the person; and\n\n(c) the CDR data, or any other CDR data from which it was\ndirectly or indirectly derived, either:\n\n(i) was disclosed to the person under the consumer data\nrules; or\n\n(ii) is covered by subsection (2) for the person; and\n\n(d) the person is neither a data holder, nor a designated gateway,\nfor the first-mentioned CDR data; and\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 56AL\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(e) the first-mentioned CDR data is not being held by (or on\nbehalf of) the person as an action service provider for a type\nof CDR action.\nNote:\nFor paragraph (d), the person will be a data holder of that CDR data if\nsubsection 56AJ(4) applies.\n\n(2) This subsection covers CDR data for a person if:\n\n(a) the CDR data is information that relates to a CDR consumer\nfor a CDR action; and\n\n(b) the person is authorised by the consumer data rules to use or\ndisclose that information to prepare or give a valid\ninstruction for the performance of the CDR action on behalf\nof the CDR consumer.\nNote:\nThis CDR data is information that is CDR data because of\nparagraph 56AI(1)(aa). Paragraph 56BGA(1)(d) ensures the rules can\ngive the authorisation referred to in paragraph (b) of this subsection.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person is an accredited data recipient, of CDR data, if:\n\n(a) the person is an accredited person; and\n\n(b) the CDR data is held by (or on behalf of) the person; and\n\n(c) the CDR data, or any other CDR data from which it was\ndirectly or indirectly derived, either:\n\n(i) was disclosed to the person under the consumer data\nrules; or\n\n(ii) is covered by subsection (2) for the person; and\n\n(d) the person is neither a data holder, nor a designated gateway,\nfor the first-mentioned CDR data; and\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 56AL\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(e) the first-mentioned CDR data is not being held by (or on\nbehalf of) the person as an action service provider for a type\nof CDR action.\nNote:\nFor paragraph (d), the person will be a data holder of that CDR data if\nsubsection 56AJ(4) applies.\n\n(2) This subsection covers CDR data for a person if:\n\n(a) the CDR data is information that relates to a CDR consumer\nfor a CDR action; and\n\n(b) the person is authorised by the consumer data rules to use or\ndisclose that information to prepare or give a valid\ninstruction for the performance of the CDR action on behalf\nof the CDR consumer.\nNote:\nThis CDR data is information that is CDR data because of\nparagraph 56AI(1)(aa). Paragraph 56BGA(1)(d) ensures the rules can\ngive the authorisation referred to in paragraph (b) of this subsection.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ak-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ak-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2c7d5e7bd6bfb830942562e58ad40d6e2566ea1cc459d5aa8caa65a79279e08e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ak",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56AK Meaning of accredited data recipient",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is an accredited data recipient, of CDR data, if:\n\n(a) the person is an accredited person; and\n\n(b) the CDR data is held by (or on behalf of) the person; and\n\n(c) the CDR data, or any other CDR data from which it was\ndirectly or indirectly derived, either:\n\n(i) was disclosed to the person under the consumer data\nrules; or\n\n(ii) is covered by subsection (2) for the person; and\n\n(d) the person is neither a data holder, nor a designated gateway,\nfor the first-mentioned CDR data; and\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 56AL\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(e) the first-mentioned CDR data is not being held by (or on\nbehalf of) the person as an action service provider for a type\nof CDR action.\nNote:\nFor paragraph (d), the person will be a data holder of that CDR data if\nsubsection 56AJ(4) applies.\n\n(2) This subsection covers CDR data for a person if:\n\n(a) the CDR data is information that relates to a CDR consumer\nfor a CDR action; and\n\n(b) the person is authorised by the consumer data rules to use or\ndisclose that information to prepare or give a valid\ninstruction for the performance of the CDR action on behalf\nof the CDR consumer.\nNote:\nThis CDR data is information that is CDR data because of\nparagraph 56AI(1)(aa). Paragraph 56BGA(1)(d) ensures the rules can\ngive the authorisation referred to in paragraph (b) of this subsection."
    },
