    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56am",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56AM Meanings of chargeable CDR data, chargeable circumstances",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56am"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.52",
      "values:originalText": "and fee-free CDR data\n\n(1) CDR data is chargeable CDR data if the CDR data is information\nwithin a class specified, as described in paragraph 56AC(2)(d), in\nan instrument designating a sector under subsection 56AC(2) (the\ndesignation instrument).\n\n(2) The chargeable CDR data is disclosed in chargeable\ncircumstances if it is disclosed in circumstances specified:\n\n(a) for that class of information; and\n\n(b) as described in subparagraph 56AC(2)(d)(i);\nin the designation instrument.\n\n(3) The chargeable CDR data is used in chargeable circumstances if it\nis used in circumstances specified:\n\n(a) for that class of information; and\n\n(b) as described in subparagraph 56AC(2)(d)(ii);\nin the designation instrument.\n\n(4) CDR data is fee-free CDR data if:\n\n(a) the consumer data rules require it to be disclosed; and\n\n(b) it is not chargeable CDR data.\n56AMA  Meanings of CDR action and CDR declaration\n\n(1) A CDR action is an action of a type declared under\nsection 56ACA.\n\n(2) A CDR declaration, for a type of CDR action, is the declaration\nunder section 56ACA that declares actions of that type.\n56AMB  Meanings of action service provider and voluntary action\nservice provider\n\n(1) A person is an action service provider, for a type of CDR action, if\nthe person:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 56AMC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) is within a class of data holders (of CDR data) declared in the\nCDR declaration for that type of CDR action; or\n\n(b) is a voluntary action service provider for that type of CDR\naction.\nNote 1:\nA data holder covered by paragraph (a) has no choice about being an\naction service provider for CDR actions of that type.\nNote 2:\nA data holder covered by paragraph (a) for one or more types of CDR\nactions will not be an action service provider for any other type of\nCDR action unless the data holder chooses to apply to be a voluntary\naction service provider.\n\n(2) A person is a voluntary action service provider, for a type of CDR\naction, if:\n\n(a) paragraph (1)(a) does not apply to the person for that type of\nCDR action; and\n\n(b) the person holds an approval, of the kind described in\nsubsection 56BHA(1), under the consumer data rules for that\ntype of CDR action.\nNote:\nThe person will need to have applied to be approved as an action\nservice provider for CDR actions of that type (see\nsubsection 56BHA(1)).\n56AMC  Meaning of accredited action initiator\n\nA person is an accredited action initiator for a type of CDR action\nif:\n\n(a) the person is an accredited person; and\n\n(b) the person’s accreditation authorises the person to initiate\nthat type of CDR action.\nNote 1:\nThe consumer data rules may include rules about accreditation,\nincluding about different levels of accreditation (see\nsubsection 56BH(1)).\nNote 2:\nThe Register of Accredited Persons may include information about\nwhat a person’s level of accreditation authorises the person to do (see\nsection 56CE).\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "and fee-free CDR data\n\n(1) CDR data is chargeable CDR data if the CDR data is information\nwithin a class specified, as described in paragraph 56AC(2)(d), in\nan instrument designating a sector under subsection 56AC(2) (the\ndesignation instrument).\n\n(2) The chargeable CDR data is disclosed in chargeable\ncircumstances if it is disclosed in circumstances specified:\n\n(a) for that class of information; and\n\n(b) as described in subparagraph 56AC(2)(d)(i);\nin the designation instrument.\n\n(3) The chargeable CDR data is used in chargeable circumstances if it\nis used in circumstances specified:\n\n(a) for that class of information; and\n\n(b) as described in subparagraph 56AC(2)(d)(ii);\nin the designation instrument.\n\n(4) CDR data is fee-free CDR data if:\n\n(a) the consumer data rules require it to be disclosed; and\n\n(b) it is not chargeable CDR data.\n56AMA  Meanings of CDR action and CDR declaration\n\n(1) A CDR action is an action of a type declared under\nsection 56ACA.\n\n(2) A CDR declaration, for a type of CDR action, is the declaration\nunder section 56ACA that declares actions of that type.\n56AMB  Meanings of action service provider and voluntary action\nservice provider\n\n(1) A person is an action service provider, for a type of CDR action, if\nthe person:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 56AMC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) is within a class of data holders (of CDR data) declared in the\nCDR declaration for that type of CDR action; or\n\n(b) is a voluntary action service provider for that type of CDR\naction.\nNote 1:\nA data holder covered by paragraph (a) has no choice about being an\naction service provider for CDR actions of that type.\nNote 2:\nA data holder covered by paragraph (a) for one or more types of CDR\nactions will not be an action service provider for any other type of\nCDR action unless the data holder chooses to apply to be a",
