    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56am-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56AM(2) Meanings of chargeable CDR data, chargeable circumstances",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56am-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.52",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A person is a voluntary action service provider, for a type of CDR\naction, if:\n\n(a) paragraph (1)(a) does not apply to the person for that type of\nCDR action; and\n\n(b) the person holds an approval, of the kind described in\nsubsection 56BHA(1), under the consumer data rules for that\ntype of CDR action.\nNote:\nThe person will need to have applied to be approved as an action\nservice provider for CDR actions of that type (see\nsubsection 56BHA(1)).\n56AMC  Meaning of accredited action initiator\n\nA person is an accredited action initiator for a type of CDR action\nif:\n\n(a) the person is an accredited person; and\n\n(b) the person’s accreditation authorises the person to initiate\nthat type of CDR action.\nNote 1:\nThe consumer data rules may include rules about accreditation,\nincluding about different levels of accreditation (see\nsubsection 56BH(1)).\nNote 2:\nThe Register of Accredited Persons may include information about\nwhat a person’s level of accreditation authorises the person to do (see\nsection 56CE).\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A person is a voluntary action service provider, for a type of CDR\naction, if:\n\n(a) paragraph (1)(a) does not apply to the person for that type of\nCDR action; and\n\n(b) the person holds an approval, of the kind described in\nsubsection 56BHA(1), under the consumer data rules for that\ntype of CDR action.\nNote:\nThe person will need to have applied to be approved as an action\nservice provider for CDR actions of that type (see\nsubsection 56BHA(1)).\n56AMC  Meaning of accredited action initiator\n\nA person is an accredited action initiator for a type of CDR action\nif:\n\n(a) the person is an accredited person; and\n\n(b) the person’s accreditation authorises the person to initiate\nthat type of CDR action.\nNote 1:\nThe consumer data rules may include rules about accreditation,\nincluding about different levels of accreditation (see\nsubsection 56BH(1)).\nNote 2:\nThe Register of Accredited Persons may include information about\nwhat a person’s level of accreditation authorises the person to do (see\nsection 56CE).\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56am"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56am-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56am-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
