    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56aq",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56AQ CDR provisions bind the Crown",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56aq"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.57",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The CDR provisions bind the Crown in each of its capacities.\n\n(2) However, the CDR provisions do not make the Crown:\n\n(a) liable to a pecuniary penalty or to be prosecuted for an\noffence; or\n\n(b) subject to a remedy under section 56EY (about actions for\ndamages for contravening the privacy safeguards); or\n\n(c) subject to a remedy under Part VI (about enforcement) other\nthan section 87B (about enforceable undertakings); or\n\n(d) subject to a remedy under Part 4 (about civil penalties) or 7\n(about injunctions) of the Regulatory Powers Act; or\n\n(e) subject to Part XID of this Act (about search and seizure).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The CDR provisions bind the Crown in each of its capacities.\n\n(2) However, the CDR provisions do not make the Crown:\n\n(a) liable to a pecuniary penalty or to be prosecuted for an\noffence; or\n\n(b) subject to a remedy under section 56EY (about actions for\ndamages for contravening the privacy safeguards); or\n\n(c) subject to a remedy under Part VI (about enforcement) other\nthan section 87B (about enforceable undertakings); or\n\n(d) subject to a remedy under Part 4 (about civil penalties) or 7\n(about injunctions) of the Regulatory Powers Act; or\n\n(e) subject to Part XID of this Act (about search and seizure).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56aq-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56aq-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8837e13dea7d6c8567c001676d6cd3f3f53171aed4cfe4c97770c17aed201cb9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56aq",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56AQ CDR provisions bind the Crown",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 57,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The CDR provisions bind the Crown in each of its capacities.\n\n(2) However, the CDR provisions do not make the Crown:\n\n(a) liable to a pecuniary penalty or to be prosecuted for an\noffence; or\n\n(b) subject to a remedy under section 56EY (about actions for\ndamages for contravening the privacy safeguards); or\n\n(c) subject to a remedy under Part VI (about enforcement) other\nthan section 87B (about enforceable undertakings); or\n\n(d) subject to a remedy under Part 4 (about civil penalties) or 7\n(about injunctions) of the Regulatory Powers Act; or\n\n(e) subject to Part XID of this Act (about search and seizure)."
    },
