      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.57",
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, the CDR provisions do not make the Crown:\n\n(a) liable to a pecuniary penalty or to be prosecuted for an\noffence; or\n\n(b) subject to a remedy under section 56EY (about actions for\ndamages for contravening the privacy safeguards); or\n\n(c) subject to a remedy under Part VI (about enforcement) other\nthan section 87B (about enforceable undertakings); or\n\n(d) subject to a remedy under Part 4 (about civil penalties) or 7\n(about injunctions) of the Regulatory Powers Act; or\n\n(e) subject to Part XID of this Act (about search and seizure).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) However, the CDR provisions do not make the Crown:\n\n(a) liable to a pecuniary penalty or to be prosecuted for an\noffence; or\n\n(b) subject to a remedy under section 56EY (about actions for\ndamages for contravening the privacy safeguards); or\n\n(c) subject to a remedy under Part VI (about enforcement) other\nthan section 87B (about enforceable undertakings); or\n\n(d) subject to a remedy under Part 4 (about civil penalties) or 7\n(about injunctions) of the Regulatory Powers Act; or\n\n(e) subject to Part XID of this Act (about search and seizure).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56aq"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56aq-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56aq-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56aq-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        },
