        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56aq-ss-2-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c79f3b546eb42f9ea7e96d57b8130a4a5396280b19669eb7ca93a722adcad1e2",
      "skos:note": "The Crown is not subject to certain remedies under specified laws."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56aq-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56AQ(2) CDR provisions bind the Crown",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 57,
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, the CDR provisions do not make the Crown:\n\n(a) liable to a pecuniary penalty or to be prosecuted for an\noffence; or\n\n(b) subject to a remedy under section 56EY (about actions for\ndamages for contravening the privacy safeguards); or\n\n(c) subject to a remedy under Part VI (about enforcement) other\nthan section 87B (about enforceable undertakings); or\n\n(d) subject to a remedy under Part 4 (about civil penalties) or 7\n(about injunctions) of the Regulatory Powers Act; or\n\n(e) subject to Part XID of this Act (about search and seizure)."
    },
