        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56at",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56AT Participating government entities of a State or Territory—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56at"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.60",
      "values:originalText": "revocation\n\n(1) The Minister may, by notifiable instrument, revoke a declaration\nmade under subsection 56AS(1) that an entity is a participating\nentity for a State or Territory.\n\n(2) If a State or Territory requests in writing the Minister to revoke a\ndeclaration made under subsection 56AS(1) that an entity is a\nparticipating entity for the State or Territory, the Minister must,\nunder subsection (1) of this section, revoke the declaration as soon\nas practicable.\n\n(3) If the Minister revokes a declaration made under\nsubsection 56AS(1) in relation to an entity, then, despite the\nrevocation, subsection 56AR(2) continues to apply to the entity in\nrelation to:\n\n(a) any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued\nor incurred before the revocation; and\n\n(b) any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of\nany such right, privilege, obligation or liability;\nas if the declaration were still in force.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 56AU\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSubdivision F—Application to acts done by or in relation to\nagents etc. of CDR entities",
      "skos:definition": "revocation\n\n(1) The Minister may, by notifiable instrument, revoke a declaration\nmade under subsection 56AS(1) that an entity is a participating\nentity for a State or Territory.\n\n(2) If a State or Territory requests in writing the Minister to revoke a\ndeclaration made under subsection 56AS(1) that an entity is a\nparticipating entity for the State or Territory, the Minister must,\nunder subsection (1) of this section, revoke the declaration as soon\nas practicable.\n\n(3) If the Minister revokes a declaration made under\nsubsection 56AS(1) in relation to an entity, then, despite the\nrevocation, subsection 56AR(2) continues to apply to the entity in\nrelation to:\n\n(a) any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued\nor incurred before the revocation; and\n\n(b) any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of\nany such right, privilege, obligation or liability;\nas if the declaration were still in force.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 56AU\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSubdivision F—Application to acts done by or in relation to\nagents etc. of CDR entities",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56at-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56at-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56at-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2a3c5fe92785106889f22a9633aef8bd8ff1ca1d6a82f3808ecc732dc56b12bd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56at",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56AT Participating government entities of a State or Territory—",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 60,
      "values:originalText": "revocation\n\n(1) The Minister may, by notifiable instrument, revoke a declaration\nmade under subsection 56AS(1) that an entity is a participating\nentity for a State or Territory.\n\n(2) If a State or Territory requests in writing the Minister to revoke a\ndeclaration made under subsection 56AS(1) that an entity is a\nparticipating entity for the State or Territory, the Minister must,\nunder subsection (1) of this section, revoke the declaration as soon\nas practicable.\n\n(3) If the Minister revokes a declaration made under\nsubsection 56AS(1) in relation to an entity, then, despite the\nrevocation, subsection 56AR(2) continues to apply to the entity in\nrelation to:\n\n(a) any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued\nor incurred before the revocation; and\n\n(b) any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of\nany such right, privilege, obligation or liability;\nas if the declaration were still in force.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 56AU\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSubdivision F—Application to acts done by or in relation to\nagents etc. of CDR entities"
    },
