    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56au",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56AU Acts done by or in relation to agents etc. of CDR entities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56au"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.61",
      "values:originalText": "Conduct of agents etc. of a CDR entity attributable to the CDR\nentity\n\n(1) For the purposes of this Part and the consumer data rules, each of\nthe following provisions applies to a CDR entity who is not a body\ncorporate in a corresponding way to the way that provision applies\nto a CDR entity who is a body corporate:\n\n(a) section 84 of this Act;\n\n(b) section 97 of the Regulatory Powers Act (to the extent that it\napplies in relation to a provision of this Part).\nActs done in relation to an agent of a CDR entity taken to be done\nin relation to the CDR entity\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Part and the consumer data rules, if an act\nis done by a person in relation to another person (the agent) who:\n\n(a) is acting on behalf of a CDR entity; and\n\n(b) is so acting within the agent’s actual or apparent authority;\nthe act is taken to have also been done in relation to the CDR\nentity.\nDefinitions\n\n(3) In this section:\nCDR entity means any of the following:\n\n(a) a data holder of CDR data;\n\n(b) an accredited person;\n\n(c) a designated gateway for CDR data;\n\n(d) an action service provider for a type of CDR action.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "Conduct of agents etc. of a CDR entity attributable to the CDR\nentity\n\n(1) For the purposes of this Part and the consumer data rules, each of\nthe following provisions applies to a CDR entity who is not a body\ncorporate in a corresponding way to the way that provision applies\nto a CDR entity who is a body corporate:\n\n(a) section 84 of this Act;\n\n(b) section 97 of the Regulatory Powers Act (to the extent that it\napplies in relation to a provision of this Part).\nActs done in relation to an agent of a CDR entity taken to be done\nin relation to the CDR entity\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Part and the consumer data rules, if an act\nis done by a person in relation to another person (the agent) who:\n\n(a) is acting on behalf of a CDR entity; and\n\n(b) is so acting within the agent’s actual or apparent authority;\nthe act is taken to have also been done in relation to the CDR\nentity.\nDefinitions\n\n(3) In this section:\nCDR entity means any of the following:\n\n(a) a data holder of CDR data;\n\n(b) an accredited person;\n\n(c) a designated gateway for CDR data;\n\n(d) an action service provider for a type of CDR action.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56au-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56au-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56au-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e57d809235848be4b9e17af2997c0b285613ecbc91c81a9d8f666dcf9060636a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56au",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56AU Acts done by or in relation to agents etc. of CDR entities",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 61,
      "values:originalText": "Conduct of agents etc. of a CDR entity attributable to the CDR\nentity\n\n(1) For the purposes of this Part and the consumer data rules, each of\nthe following provisions applies to a CDR entity who is not a body\ncorporate in a corresponding way to the way that provision applies\nto a CDR entity who is a body corporate:\n\n(a) section 84 of this Act;\n\n(b) section 97 of the Regulatory Powers Act (to the extent that it\napplies in relation to a provision of this Part).\nActs done in relation to an agent of a CDR entity taken to be done\nin relation to the CDR entity\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Part and the consumer data rules, if an act\nis done by a person in relation to another person (the agent) who:\n\n(a) is acting on behalf of a CDR entity; and\n\n(b) is so acting within the agent’s actual or apparent authority;\nthe act is taken to have also been done in relation to the CDR\nentity.\nDefinitions\n\n(3) In this section:\nCDR entity means any of the following:\n\n(a) a data holder of CDR data;\n\n(b) an accredited person;\n\n(c) a designated gateway for CDR data;\n\n(d) an action service provider for a type of CDR action.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
