        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ba-ss-2-logic-ltl-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3cc63f41173a3862292005ea41f21f6cc7c5157de2db8d7eb1877494843f0409",
      "skos:note": "Consumer data rules must include requirements for deleting CDR data on request from consumer Cannot delete CDR data under certain conditions",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ba-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BA(2) Minister may make consumer data rules",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, a rule described in subsection (1) must not require\ndeletion of all or part of the CDR data if:\n\n(a) the accredited data recipient is required to retain the CDR\ndata by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order;\nor\n\n(b) the CDR data relates to any current or anticipated:\n\n(i) legal proceedings; or\n\n(ii) dispute resolution proceedings;\n\nto which the accredited data recipient is a party; or\n\n(c) the CDR data relates to any current or anticipated:\n\n(i) legal proceedings; or\n\n(ii) dispute resolution proceedings;\n\nto which the CDR consumer is a party.\nConsumer data rules may include rules in relation to the\nrequirement"
    },
