      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The accredited data recipient is required to retain the CDR data",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The rule cannot require deletion of all or part of the CDR data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ba-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BA(3) Minister may make consumer data rules",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ba-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The consumer data rules may include the following rules in\nrelation to the requirement:\n\n(a) rules about:\n\n(i) how the CDR consumer may make a valid request; and\n\n(ii) what must be included in a request for it to be valid and\nwhen a request ceases to be a valid request;\n\n(b) rules specifying circumstances (in addition to those in\nsubsection (2)) in which the accredited data recipient may\nrefuse to delete the CDR data despite the requirement;\n\n(c) rules about how an accredited data recipient is to delete the\nCDR data covered in a valid request;\n\n(d) rules about how the requirement is to be complied with\ndepending on the class of CDR data requested to be deleted;\n\n(e) rules about how an accredited data recipient is to notify the\nCDR consumer of:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The consumer data rules may include the following rules in\nrelation to the requirement:\n\n(a) rules about:\n\n(i) how the CDR consumer may make a valid request; and\n\n(ii) what must be included in a request for it to be valid and\nwhen a request ceases to be a valid request;\n\n(b) rules specifying circumstances (in addition to those in\nsubsection (2)) in which the accredited data recipient may\nrefuse to delete the CDR data despite the requirement;\n\n(c) rules about how an accredited data recipient is to delete the\nCDR data covered in a valid request;\n\n(d) rules about how the requirement is to be complied with\ndepending on the class of CDR data requested to be deleted;\n\n(e) rules about how an accredited data recipient is to notify the\nCDR consumer of:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ba"
      },
