    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BB Matters that the consumer data rules may deal with",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "The consumer data rules may deal with the following matters:\n\n(a) disclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage, security or\ndeletion of CDR data for which there are one or more CDR\nconsumers (see also sections 56BC and 56BD);\n\n(b) disclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage, security or\ndeletion of CDR data for which there are no CDR consumers\n(see also sections 56BE and 56BF);\n\n(c) designated gateways for CDR data (see also section 56BG);\n\n(ca) initiating CDR actions (see also section 56BGA);\n\n(d) accreditation for the purposes of this Part (see also\nsection 56BH);\n\n(da) approving persons to be voluntary action service providers\nfor types of CDR actions (see also section 56BHA);\n\n(e) reporting, record keeping and auditing (see also\nsection 56BI);\n\n(f) matters incidental or related to any of the above matters (see\nalso section 56BJ).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nConsumer data right  Division 2\n\nSection 56BC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "The consumer data rules may deal with the following matters:\n\n(a) disclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage, security or\ndeletion of CDR data for which there are one or more CDR\nconsumers (see also sections 56BC and 56BD);\n\n(b) disclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage, security or\ndeletion of CDR data for which there are no CDR consumers\n(see also sections 56BE and 56BF);\n\n(c) designated gateways for CDR data (see also section 56BG);\n\n(ca) initiating CDR actions (see also section 56BGA);\n\n(d) accreditation for the purposes of this Part (see also\nsection 56BH);\n\n(da) approving persons to be voluntary action service providers\nfor types of CDR actions (see also section 56BHA);\n\n(e) reporting, record keeping and auditing (see also\nsection 56BI);\n\n(f) matters incidental or related to any of the above matters (see\nalso section 56BJ).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nConsumer data right  Division 2\n\nSection 56BC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bb-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "34ed134c6c2d1a8de59575500c1465b604169fb83feb04c999b75b1b28832f8a",
      "skos:note": "Matters that the consumer data rules may deal with"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BB Matters that the consumer data rules may deal with",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "The consumer data rules may deal with the following matters:\n\n(a) disclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage, security or\ndeletion of CDR data for which there are one or more CDR\nconsumers (see also sections 56BC and 56BD);\n\n(b) disclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage, security or\ndeletion of CDR data for which there are no CDR consumers\n(see also sections 56BE and 56BF);\n\n(c) designated gateways for CDR data (see also section 56BG);\n\n(ca) initiating CDR actions (see also section 56BGA);\n\n(d) accreditation for the purposes of this Part (see also\nsection 56BH);\n\n(da) approving persons to be voluntary action service providers\nfor types of CDR actions (see also section 56BHA);\n\n(e) reporting, record keeping and auditing (see also\nsection 56BI);\n\n(f) matters incidental or related to any of the above matters (see\nalso section 56BJ).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nConsumer data right  Division 2\n\nSection 56BC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bb-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bb"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BC Rules about disclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage,",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.65",
      "values:originalText": "security or deletion of CDR data for which there are CDR\nconsumers\nRequired disclosures in response to valid requests\n\n(1) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(a), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules:\n\n(a) requirements on a CDR participant for CDR data to disclose\nall or part of the CDR data, in response to a valid request by\na CDR consumer for the CDR data, to:\n\n(i) the CDR consumer for use as the CDR consumer sees\nfit; or\n\n(ii) an accredited person for use subject to the privacy\nsafeguards; or\n\n(iii) a data holder of other CDR data;\n\n(b) rules about:\n\n(i) how a CDR consumer for the CDR data may make a\nvalid request of the kind described in paragraph (a); and\n\n(ii) what must be included in a request for it to be valid,\nwhat disclosures or other matters a valid request may\ncover, and when a request ceases to be a valid request;\n\n(c) requirements on a person (other than a CDR consumer for the\nCDR data) to satisfy in order to be disclosed the CDR data in\nthe way described in paragraph (a).\nNote 1:\nThe requirements described in paragraph (a) could, for example,\ninclude a requirement that the disclosure be in accordance with the\nrelevant data standards.\nNote 2:\nA fee may be charged for such a disclosure if the CDR data is\nchargeable CDR data, unless section 56BU provides otherwise.\nAuthorised disclosures or use in accordance with valid consents\n\n(2) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(a), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "security or deletion of CDR data for which there are CDR\nconsumers\nRequired disclosures in response to valid requests\n\n(1) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(a), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules:\n\n(a) requirements on a CDR participant for CDR data to disclose\nall or part of the CDR data, in response to a valid request by\na CDR consumer for the CDR data, to:\n\n(i) the CDR consumer for use as the CDR consumer sees\nfit; or\n\n(ii) an accredited person for use subject to the privacy\nsafeguards; or\n\n(iii) a data holder of other CDR data;\n\n(b) rules about:\n\n(i) how a CDR consumer for the CDR data may make a\nvalid request of the kind described in paragraph (a); and\n\n(ii) what must be included in a request for it to be valid,\nwhat disclosures or other matters a valid request may\ncover, and when a request ceases to be a valid request;\n\n(c) requirements on a person (other than a CDR consumer for the\nCDR data) to satisfy in order to be disclosed the CDR data in\nthe way described in paragraph (a).\nNote 1:\nThe requirements described in paragraph (a) could, for example,\ninclude a requirement that the disclosure be in accordance with the\nrelevant data standards.\nNote 2:\nA fee may be charged for such a disclosure if the CDR data is\nchargeable CDR data, unless section 56BU provides otherwise.\nAuthorised disclosures or use in accordance with valid consents\n\n(2) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(a), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bc-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bc-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2092dab859e04a8a48a03f29e55af42f9870c7bae72277e07da4e026a9434669"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BC Rules about disclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage,",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 65,
      "values:originalText": "security or deletion of CDR data for which there are CDR\nconsumers\nRequired disclosures in response to valid requests\n\n(1) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(a), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules:\n\n(a) requirements on a CDR participant for CDR data to disclose\nall or part of the CDR data, in response to a valid request by\na CDR consumer for the CDR data, to:\n\n(i) the CDR consumer for use as the CDR consumer sees\nfit; or\n\n(ii) an accredited person for use subject to the privacy\nsafeguards; or\n\n(iii) a data holder of other CDR data;\n\n(b) rules about:\n\n(i) how a CDR consumer for the CDR data may make a\nvalid request of the kind described in paragraph (a); and\n\n(ii) what must be included in a request for it to be valid,\nwhat disclosures or other matters a valid request may\ncover, and when a request ceases to be a valid request;\n\n(c) requirements on a person (other than a CDR consumer for the\nCDR data) to satisfy in order to be disclosed the CDR data in\nthe way described in paragraph (a).\nNote 1:\nThe requirements described in paragraph (a) could, for example,\ninclude a requirement that the disclosure be in accordance with the\nrelevant data standards.\nNote 2:\nA fee may be charged for such a disclosure if the CDR data is\nchargeable CDR data, unless section 56BU provides otherwise.\nAuthorised disclosures or use in accordance with valid consents\n\n(2) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(a), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bc-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BC(1) Rules about disclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage,",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bc-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.65",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(a), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules:\n\n(a) requirements on a CDR participant for CDR data to disclose\nall or part of the CDR data, in response to a valid request by\na CDR consumer for the CDR data, to:\n\n(i) the CDR consumer for use as the CDR consumer sees\nfit; or\n\n(ii) an accredited person for use subject to the privacy\nsafeguards; or\n\n(iii) a data holder of other CDR data;\n\n(b) rules about:\n\n(i) how a CDR consumer for the CDR data may make a\nvalid request of the kind described in paragraph (a); and\n\n(ii) what must be included in a request for it to be valid,\nwhat disclosures or other matters a valid request may\ncover, and when a request ceases to be a valid request;\n\n(c) requirements on a person (other than a CDR consumer for the\nCDR data) to satisfy in order to be disclosed the CDR data in\nthe way described in paragraph (a).\nNote 1:\nThe requirements described in paragraph (a) could, for example,\ninclude a requirement that the disclosure be in accordance with the\nrelevant data standards.\nNote 2:\nA fee may be charged for such a disclosure if the CDR data is\nchargeable CDR data, unless section 56BU provides otherwise.\nAuthorised disclosures or use in accordance with valid consents",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(a), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules:\n\n(a) requirements on a CDR participant for CDR data to disclose\nall or part of the CDR data, in response to a valid request by\na CDR consumer for the CDR data, to:\n\n(i) the CDR consumer for use as the CDR consumer sees\nfit; or\n\n(ii) an accredited person for use subject to the privacy\nsafeguards; or\n\n(iii) a data holder of other CDR data;\n\n(b) rules about:\n\n(i) how a CDR consumer for the CDR data may make a\nvalid request of the kind described in paragraph (a); and\n\n(ii) what must be included in a request for it to be valid,\nwhat disclosures or other matters a valid request may\ncover, and when a request ceases to be a valid request;\n\n(c) requirements on a person (other than a CDR consumer for the\nCDR data) to satisfy in order to be disclosed the CDR data in\nthe way described in paragraph (a).\nNote 1:\nThe requirements described in paragraph (a) could, for example,\ninclude a requirement that the disclosure be in accordance with the\nrelevant data standards.\nNote 2:\nA fee may be charged for such a disclosure if the CDR data is\nchargeable CDR data, unless section 56BU provides otherwise.\nAuthorised disclosures or use in accordance with valid consents",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bc"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bc-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bc-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e590a84bc829f789039fd5bdd55b2d54f81aeb4fba59140b100119d50fc5400c",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure requirements for CDR data",
      "dc:description": "CDR data upon request"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bc-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BC(1) Rules about disclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage,",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 65,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(a), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules:\n\n(a) requirements on a CDR participant for CDR data to disclose\nall or part of the CDR data, in response to a valid request by\na CDR consumer for the CDR data, to:\n\n(i) the CDR consumer for use as the CDR consumer sees\nfit; or\n\n(ii) an accredited person for use subject to the privacy\nsafeguards; or\n\n(iii) a data holder of other CDR data;\n\n(b) rules about:\n\n(i) how a CDR consumer for the CDR data may make a\nvalid request of the kind described in paragraph (a); and\n\n(ii) what must be included in a request for it to be valid,\nwhat disclosures or other matters a valid request may\ncover, and when a request ceases to be a valid request;\n\n(c) requirements on a person (other than a CDR consumer for the\nCDR data) to satisfy in order to be disclosed the CDR data in\nthe way described in paragraph (a).\nNote 1:\nThe requirements described in paragraph (a) could, for example,\ninclude a requirement that the disclosure be in accordance with the\nrelevant data standards.\nNote 2:\nA fee may be charged for such a disclosure if the CDR data is\nchargeable CDR data, unless section 56BU provides otherwise.\nAuthorised disclosures or use in accordance with valid consents"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bc-ss-1-norm",
