    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BD Limitations for rules about CDR data for which there are",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.67",
      "values:originalText": "CDR consumers\nOnly certain CDR data can be required to be disclosed\n\n(1) The consumer data rules can only require a disclosure of CDR data\nfor which there are one or more CDR consumers if:\n\n(a) the CDR data is covered by paragraph 56AI(1)(a) or (aa); and\n\n(b) the disclosure is to:\n\n(i) one or more of those CDR consumers; or\n\n(ii) an accredited person; or\n\n(iii) a designated gateway for the CDR data; or\n\n(iv) a data holder of the CDR data by a designated gateway\nfor the CDR data; or\n\n(iva) a data holder of other CDR data; or\n\n(ivb) an action service provider for a type of CDR action; or\n\n(v) a person acting on behalf of a person referred to in any\nof subparagraphs (ii) to (ivb).\nNote 1:\nThis means CDR data cannot be required to be disclosed if it is only\nCDR data because it is directly or indirectly derived from:\n(a) other CDR data within a class specified, as described in\nparagraph 56AC(2)(a), in an instrument designating a sector\nunder subsection 56AC(2); or\n(b) other CDR data, about a CDR consumer for a CDR action, that\nan accredited action initiator is authorised to use to prepare or\ngive a valid instruction for the performance of the CDR action.\nNote 2:\nThe consumer data rules can include other rules relating to this other\nderived CDR data.\nNote 3:\nVoluntary disclosures of this other derived CDR data can be\nauthorised under the consumer data rules.\nNo fee when fee-free CDR data is required to be disclosed\n\n(2) The consumer data rules cannot allow a fee to be charged for:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "CDR consumers\nOnly certain CDR data can be required to be disclosed\n\n(1) The consumer data rules can only require a disclosure of CDR data\nfor which there are one or more CDR consumers if:\n\n(a) the CDR data is covered by paragraph 56AI(1)(a) or (aa); and\n\n(b) the disclosure is to:\n\n(i) one or more of those CDR consumers; or\n\n(ii) an accredited person; or\n\n(iii) a designated gateway for the CDR data; or\n\n(iv) a data holder of the CDR data by a designated gateway\nfor the CDR data; or\n\n(iva) a data holder of other CDR data; or\n\n(ivb) an action service provider for a type of CDR action; or\n\n(v) a person acting on behalf of a person referred to in any\nof subparagraphs (ii) to (ivb).\nNote 1:\nThis means CDR data cannot be required to be disclosed if it is only\nCDR data because it is directly or indirectly derived from:\n(a) other CDR data within a class specified, as described in\nparagraph 56AC(2)(a), in an instrument designating a sector\nunder subsection 56AC(2); or\n(b) other CDR data, about a CDR consumer for a CDR action, that\nan accredited action initiator is authorised to use to prepare or\ngive a valid instruction for the performance of the CDR action.\nNote 2:\nThe consumer data rules can include other rules relating to this other\nderived CDR data.\nNote 3:\nVoluntary disclosures of this other derived CDR data can be\nauthorised under the consumer data rules.\nNo fee when fee-free CDR data is required to be disclosed\n\n(2) The consumer data rules cannot allow a fee to be charged for:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bd-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bd-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "12aadd05c25ce039c0cdd11b97bb48043343c8bb434ba1e45420005fbe078b9f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BD Limitations for rules about CDR data for which there are",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 67,
      "values:originalText": "CDR consumers\nOnly certain CDR data can be required to be disclosed\n\n(1) The consumer data rules can only require a disclosure of CDR data\nfor which there are one or more CDR consumers if:\n\n(a) the CDR data is covered by paragraph 56AI(1)(a) or (aa); and\n\n(b) the disclosure is to:\n\n(i) one or more of those CDR consumers; or\n\n(ii) an accredited person; or\n\n(iii) a designated gateway for the CDR data; or\n\n(iv) a data holder of the CDR data by a designated gateway\nfor the CDR data; or\n\n(iva) a data holder of other CDR data; or\n\n(ivb) an action service provider for a type of CDR action; or\n\n(v) a person acting on behalf of a person referred to in any\nof subparagraphs (ii) to (ivb).\nNote 1:\nThis means CDR data cannot be required to be disclosed if it is only\nCDR data because it is directly or indirectly derived from:\n(a) other CDR data within a class specified, as described in\nparagraph 56AC(2)(a), in an instrument designating a sector\nunder subsection 56AC(2); or\n(b) other CDR data, about a CDR consumer for a CDR action, that\nan accredited action initiator is authorised to use to prepare or\ngive a valid instruction for the performance of the CDR action.\nNote 2:\nThe consumer data rules can include other rules relating to this other\nderived CDR data.\nNote 3:\nVoluntary disclosures of this other derived CDR data can be\nauthorised under the consumer data rules.\nNo fee when fee-free CDR data is required to be disclosed\n\n(2) The consumer data rules cannot allow a fee to be charged for:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
