    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bf",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BF Limitations for rules about product data",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bf"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.69",
      "values:originalText": "Only certain kinds of product data can be required to be disclosed\n\n(1) The consumer data rules can only require a disclosure of CDR data\nfor which there are no CDR consumers if:\n\n(a) the CDR data is about the eligibility criteria, terms and\nconditions, price, availability or performance of:\n\n(i) a product or other kind of good; or\n\n(ii) a service; and\n\n(b) in the case where the CDR data is about availability or\nperformance—the CDR data is publicly available.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "Only certain kinds of product data can be required to be disclosed\n\n(1) The consumer data rules can only require a disclosure of CDR data\nfor which there are no CDR consumers if:\n\n(a) the CDR data is about the eligibility criteria, terms and\nconditions, price, availability or performance of:\n\n(i) a product or other kind of good; or\n\n(ii) a service; and\n\n(b) in the case where the CDR data is about availability or\nperformance—the CDR data is publicly available.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bf-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "04fceebaf6f475a48cc943bc6970a33ccca55a82d67e02235db44df3c5c9ddd8",
      "skos:note": "Only certain kinds of product data can be required to be disclosed."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bf",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BF Limitations for rules about product data",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 69,
      "values:originalText": "Only certain kinds of product data can be required to be disclosed\n\n(1) The consumer data rules can only require a disclosure of CDR data\nfor which there are no CDR consumers if:\n\n(a) the CDR data is about the eligibility criteria, terms and\nconditions, price, availability or performance of:\n\n(i) a product or other kind of good; or\n\n(ii) a service; and\n\n(b) in the case where the CDR data is about availability or\nperformance—the CDR data is publicly available.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bf-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
