    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BH Rules about accreditation for the purposes of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.75",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(d), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules:\n\n(a) rules conferring functions or powers on the CDR Accreditor;\n\n(b) the criteria for a person to be accredited under\nsubsection 56CA(1);\n\n(c) rules providing that accreditations may be granted subject to\nconditions, and that conditions may be imposed on an\naccreditation after it has been granted;\n\n(d) rules providing that accreditations may be granted at different\nlevels corresponding to different risks, including the risks\nassociated with:\n\n(i) specified classes of CDR data; or\n\n(ii) specified classes of activities; or\n\n(iia) specified types of CDR actions; or\n\n(iii) specified classes of applicants for accreditation;\n\n(da) rules specifying what a person accredited at a particular level\nis authorised to do (or not authorised to do);\n\n(e) rules for the period, renewal, transfer, variation, suspension,\nrevocation or surrender of accreditations;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(d), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules:\n\n(a) rules conferring functions or powers on the CDR Accreditor;\n\n(b) the criteria for a person to be accredited under\nsubsection 56CA(1);\n\n(c) rules providing that accreditations may be granted subject to\nconditions, and that conditions may be imposed on an\naccreditation after it has been granted;\n\n(d) rules providing that accreditations may be granted at different\nlevels corresponding to different risks, including the risks\nassociated with:\n\n(i) specified classes of CDR data; or\n\n(ii) specified classes of activities; or\n\n(iia) specified types of CDR actions; or\n\n(iii) specified classes of applicants for accreditation;\n\n(da) rules specifying what a person accredited at a particular level\nis authorised to do (or not authorised to do);\n\n(e) rules for the period, renewal, transfer, variation, suspension,\nrevocation or surrender of accreditations;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bh-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0173953960ea9561d14de9edfc8660e7554ab894024d09e47d01808f0232018a",
      "skos:note": "Rules about accreditation for the purposes of this Part"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bh",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BH Rules about accreditation for the purposes of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 75,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(d), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules:\n\n(a) rules conferring functions or powers on the CDR Accreditor;\n\n(b) the criteria for a person to be accredited under\nsubsection 56CA(1);\n\n(c) rules providing that accreditations may be granted subject to\nconditions, and that conditions may be imposed on an\naccreditation after it has been granted;\n\n(d) rules providing that accreditations may be granted at different\nlevels corresponding to different risks, including the risks\nassociated with:\n\n(i) specified classes of CDR data; or\n\n(ii) specified classes of activities; or\n\n(iia) specified types of CDR actions; or\n\n(iii) specified classes of applicants for accreditation;\n\n(da) rules specifying what a person accredited at a particular level\nis authorised to do (or not authorised to do);\n\n(e) rules for the period, renewal, transfer, variation, suspension,\nrevocation or surrender of accreditations;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bh-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
