      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bj",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BJ Rules about incidental or related matters",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bj"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.81",
      "values:originalText": "Without limiting paragraph 56BAA(3)(f) or 56BB(f), the consumer\ndata rules may include the following rules:\n\n(a) rules that refer to the data standards;\n\n(b) the circumstances in which persons are, or may be, relieved\nfrom complying with requirements in the consumer data rules\nthat would otherwise apply to them;\n\n(c) a rule that depends on a person being satisfied of one or more\nspecified matters;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "Without limiting paragraph 56BAA(3)(f) or 56BB(f), the consumer\ndata rules may include the following rules:\n\n(a) rules that refer to the data standards;\n\n(b) the circumstances in which persons are, or may be, relieved\nfrom complying with requirements in the consumer data rules\nthat would otherwise apply to them;\n\n(c) a rule that depends on a person being satisfied of one or more\nspecified matters;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bj-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bj-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "700ebde8ebda7bb5b3c64c0681cac88451e4bba22906f12342e787befd5a9e33",
      "skos:note": "Rules about incidental or related matters"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bj",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BJ Rules about incidental or related matters",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 81,
      "values:originalText": "Without limiting paragraph 56BAA(3)(f) or 56BB(f), the consumer\ndata rules may include the following rules:\n\n(a) rules that refer to the data standards;\n\n(b) the circumstances in which persons are, or may be, relieved\nfrom complying with requirements in the consumer data rules\nthat would otherwise apply to them;\n\n(c) a rule that depends on a person being satisfied of one or more\nspecified matters;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bj-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bj"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bj-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Applicable",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Applies to the obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The text states that persons are relieved from complying with requirements",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The obligation is lifted under certain circumstances"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bk",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BK Further limitations on the consumer data rules",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bk"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.83",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The consumer data rules cannot impose on a person a requirement\nthat has a retrospective commencement or application.\nExample: The rules cannot require a data holder to disclose CDR data on a day\nbefore the rules are registered, or on a day before the registration of a\nvariation to the rules that includes the requirement.\nNote:\nOther limitations on the consumer data rules are in sections 56BD,\n56BF and 56BG.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, the consumer data rules may require a person to do\nsomething on a particular day, in relation to CDR data generated or\ncollected on an earlier day, if the person:\n\n(a) is a data holder of the CDR data; or\n\n(b) is an accredited person; or\n\n(c) is a person who has given a valid request under the consumer\ndata rules relating to the CDR data; or\n\n(d) is a designated gateway for the CDR data; or\n\n(e) is an action service provider for a type of CDR action.\nExample: A data holder is given a valid request to disclose CDR data that was\ngenerated before the rules are registered. The rules can require that\ndisclosure.\n\n(4) Subsection (1) applies despite any other provision of this Division.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The consumer data rules cannot impose on a person a requirement\nthat has a retrospective commencement or application.\nExample: The rules cannot require a data holder to disclose CDR data on a day\nbefore the rules are registered, or on a day before the registration of a\nvariation to the rules that includes the requirement.\nNote:\nOther limitations on the consumer data rules are in sections 56BD,\n56BF and 56BG.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, the consumer data rules may require a person to do\nsomething on a particular day, in relation to CDR data generated or\ncollected on an earlier day, if the person:\n\n(a) is a data holder of the CDR data; or\n\n(b) is an accredited person; or\n\n(c) is a person who has given a valid request under the consumer\ndata rules relating to the CDR data; or\n\n(d) is a designated gateway for the CDR data; or\n\n(e) is an action service provider for a type of CDR action.\nExample: A data holder is given a valid request to disclose CDR data that was\ngenerated before the rules are registered. The rules can require that\ndisclosure.\n\n(4) Subsection (1) applies despite any other provision of this Division.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bk-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bk-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bk-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dd4f1ca56738a0cbc239958552f75db24025b1b3ff4700a7172afd9ad87fd6f2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bk",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BK Further limitations on the consumer data rules",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 83,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The consumer data rules cannot impose on a person a requirement\nthat has a retrospective commencement or application.\nExample: The rules cannot require a data holder to disclose CDR data on a day\nbefore the rules are registered, or on a day before the registration of a\nvariation to the rules that includes the requirement.\nNote:\nOther limitations on the consumer data rules are in sections 56BD,\n56BF and 56BG.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, the consumer data rules may require a person to do\nsomething on a particular day, in relation to CDR data generated or\ncollected on an earlier day, if the person:\n\n(a) is a data holder of the CDR data; or\n\n(b) is an accredited person; or\n\n(c) is a person who has given a valid request under the consumer\ndata rules relating to the CDR data; or\n\n(d) is a designated gateway for the CDR data; or\n\n(e) is an action service provider for a type of CDR action.\nExample: A data holder is given a valid request to disclose CDR data that was\ngenerated before the rules are registered. The rules can require that\ndisclosure.\n\n(4) Subsection (1) applies despite any other provision of this Division.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
