    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bn",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BN Misleading or deceptive conduct—offence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bn"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.85",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the person does so knowing that the conduct:\n\n(i) is misleading or deceptive; or\n\n(ii) is likely to be misleading or deceptive; and\n\n(c) the conduct misleads or deceives, or is likely to mislead or\ndeceive, another person (the second person) into believing\nthat:\n\n(i) a person is a CDR consumer for CDR data; or\n\n(ii) a person is making a valid request or consent, or has\nsatisfied other criteria, for the disclosure of CDR data\nunder the consumer data rules; or\n\n(iii) a person is a CDR consumer for a CDR action; or\n\n(iv) a person has satisfied any criteria under the consumer\ndata rules for the making of a request, the giving of a\nvalid instruction, or the processing of a valid instruction,\nfor the performance of a CDR action.\nNote:\nThe person mentioned in subparagraph (c)(i), (ii), (iii) or (iv) could be\nthe first-mentioned person, the second person or a third person.\nDefence\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the conduct is not misleading or\ndeceptive in a material particular.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the person does so knowing that the conduct:\n\n(i) is misleading or deceptive; or\n\n(ii) is likely to be misleading or deceptive; and\n\n(c) the conduct misleads or deceives, or is likely to mislead or\ndeceive, another person (the second person) into believing\nthat:\n\n(i) a person is a CDR consumer for CDR data; or\n\n(ii) a person is making a valid request or consent, or has\nsatisfied other criteria, for the disclosure of CDR data\nunder the consumer data rules; or\n\n(iii) a person is a CDR consumer for a CDR action; or\n\n(iv) a person has satisfied any criteria under the consumer\ndata rules for the making of a request, the giving of a\nvalid instruction, or the processing of a valid instruction,\nfor the performance of a CDR action.\nNote:\nThe person mentioned in subparagraph (c)(i), (ii), (iii) or (iv) could be\nthe first-mentioned person, the second person or a third person.\nDefence\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the conduct is not misleading or\ndeceptive in a material particular.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bn-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bn-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "63ef16a9f30c5c60ddba0bae2c670ce73916818150f296a4794b5a712f69e52d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bn",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BN Misleading or deceptive conduct—offence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 85,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the person does so knowing that the conduct:\n\n(i) is misleading or deceptive; or\n\n(ii) is likely to be misleading or deceptive; and\n\n(c) the conduct misleads or deceives, or is likely to mislead or\ndeceive, another person (the second person) into believing\nthat:\n\n(i) a person is a CDR consumer for CDR data; or\n\n(ii) a person is making a valid request or consent, or has\nsatisfied other criteria, for the disclosure of CDR data\nunder the consumer data rules; or\n\n(iii) a person is a CDR consumer for a CDR action; or\n\n(iv) a person has satisfied any criteria under the consumer\ndata rules for the making of a request, the giving of a\nvalid instruction, or the processing of a valid instruction,\nfor the performance of a CDR action.\nNote:\nThe person mentioned in subparagraph (c)(i), (ii), (iii) or (iv) could be\nthe first-mentioned person, the second person or a third person.\nDefence\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the conduct is not misleading or\ndeceptive in a material particular.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
