    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bo",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BO Misleading or deceptive conduct—civil penalty",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bo"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.86",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person must not engage in conduct that misleads or deceives, or\nis likely to mislead or deceive, another person (the second person)\ninto believing that:\n\n(a) a person is a CDR consumer for CDR data; or\n\n(b) a person is making a valid request or consent, or has satisfied\nother criteria, for the disclosure of CDR data under the\nconsumer data rules; or\n\n(c) a person is a CDR consumer for a CDR action; or\n\n(d) a person has satisfied any criteria under the consumer data\nrules for:\n\n(i) the making of a request; or\n\n(ii) the giving of a valid instruction; or\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nConsumer data right  Division 2\n\nSection 56BP\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(iii) the processing of a valid instruction;\n\nfor the performance of a CDR action.\nNote 1:\nThe person mentioned in paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) could be the\nfirst-mentioned person, the second person or a third person.\nNote 2:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI (including section 76 for an order for\npayment of a pecuniary penalty).\nDefence\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the conduct is not misleading or\ndeceptive in a material particular.\n\n(3) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (2) bears the burden of\nadducing or pointing to evidence that suggests a reasonable\npossibility that the conduct is not misleading or deceptive in a\nmaterial particular.\nSubdivision C—Process for making consumer data rules etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person must not engage in conduct that misleads or deceives, or\nis likely to mislead or deceive, another person (the second person)\ninto believing that:\n\n(a) a person is a CDR consumer for CDR data; or\n\n(b) a person is making a valid request or consent, or has satisfied\nother criteria, for the disclosure of CDR data under the\nconsumer data rules; or\n\n(c) a person is a CDR consumer for a CDR action; or\n\n(d) a person has satisfied any criteria under the consumer data\nrules for:\n\n(i) the making of a request; or\n\n(ii) the giving of a valid instruction; or\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nConsumer data right  Division 2\n\nSection 56BP\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(iii) the processing of a valid instruction;\n\nfor the performance of a CDR action.\nNote 1:\nThe person mentioned in paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) could be the\nfirst-mentioned person, the second person or a third person.\nNote 2:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI (including section 76 for an order for\npayment of a pecuniary penalty).\nDefence\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the conduct is not misleading or\ndeceptive in a material particular.\n\n(3) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (2) bears the burden of\nadducing or pointing to evidence that suggests a reasonable\npossibility that the conduct is not misleading or deceptive in a\nmaterial particular.\nSubdivision C—Process for making consumer data rules etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bo-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bo-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bo-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5a81f96c5bebaf54daef7615192aed150f8733f45ac63deac995b1cb67ef67f2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bo",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BO Misleading or deceptive conduct—civil penalty",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 86,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person must not engage in conduct that misleads or deceives, or\nis likely to mislead or deceive, another person (the second person)\ninto believing that:\n\n(a) a person is a CDR consumer for CDR data; or\n\n(b) a person is making a valid request or consent, or has satisfied\nother criteria, for the disclosure of CDR data under the\nconsumer data rules; or\n\n(c) a person is a CDR consumer for a CDR action; or\n\n(d) a person has satisfied any criteria under the consumer data\nrules for:\n\n(i) the making of a request; or\n\n(ii) the giving of a valid instruction; or\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nConsumer data right  Division 2\n\nSection 56BP\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(iii) the processing of a valid instruction;\n\nfor the performance of a CDR action.\nNote 1:\nThe person mentioned in paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) could be the\nfirst-mentioned person, the second person or a third person.\nNote 2:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI (including section 76 for an order for\npayment of a pecuniary penalty).\nDefence\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the conduct is not misleading or\ndeceptive in a material particular.\n\n(3) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (2) bears the burden of\nadducing or pointing to evidence that suggests a reasonable\npossibility that the conduct is not misleading or deceptive in a\nmaterial particular.\nSubdivision C—Process for making consumer data rules etc."
    },
