      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 86,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person must not engage in conduct that misleads or deceives, or\nis likely to mislead or deceive, another person (the second person)\ninto believing that:\n\n(a) a person is a CDR consumer for CDR data; or\n\n(b) a person is making a valid request or consent, or has satisfied\nother criteria, for the disclosure of CDR data under the\nconsumer data rules; or\n\n(c) a person is a CDR consumer for a CDR action; or\n\n(d) a person has satisfied any criteria under the consumer data\nrules for:\n\n(i) the making of a request; or\n\n(ii) the giving of a valid instruction; or\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nConsumer data right  Division 2\n\nSection 56BP\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(iii) the processing of a valid instruction;\n\nfor the performance of a CDR action.\nNote 1:\nThe person mentioned in paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) could be the\nfirst-mentioned person, the second person or a third person.\nNote 2:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI (including section 76 for an order for\npayment of a pecuniary penalty).\nDefence"
    },
