    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56br",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BR Commission and Information Commissioner must analyse the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56br"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.88",
      "values:originalText": "proposed rules\n\nWhen consulted under paragraph 56BQ(c), the Commission and\nthe Information Commissioner must each analyse the kinds of\nmatters referred to in paragraphs 56BP(a) and (aa) in relation to the\nmaking of the rules.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nConsumer data right  Division 2\n\nSection 56BS\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n56BS  Emergency rules: public consultation not required etc.\n\n(1) The Minister may make consumer data rules under\nsubsection 56BA(1):\n\n(a) without complying with paragraph 56BP(b) or (c); but\n\n(b) after consulting the Commission and Information\nCommissioner;\nif the Minister believes (whether or not that belief is reasonable)\nthat it is necessary to do so in order to avoid a risk of serious harm\nto:\n\n(c) the efficiency, integrity or stability of any aspect of the\nAustralian economy; or\n\n(d) the interests of consumers.\nNote:\nThe Minister still needs to comply with paragraph 56BP(a).\n\n(2) However, a failure to comply with paragraph (1)(b) of this section\ndoes not invalidate consumer data rules made as described in\nsubsection (1).\nNote:\nSuch rules may have a limited life (see section 56BT).",
      "skos:definition": "proposed rules\n\nWhen consulted under paragraph 56BQ(c), the Commission and\nthe Information Commissioner must each analyse the kinds of\nmatters referred to in paragraphs 56BP(a) and (aa) in relation to the\nmaking of the rules.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nConsumer data right  Division 2\n\nSection 56BS\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n56BS  Emergency rules: public consultation not required etc.\n\n(1) The Minister may make consumer data rules under\nsubsection 56BA(1):\n\n(a) without complying with paragraph 56BP(b) or (c); but\n\n(b) after consulting the Commission and Information\nCommissioner;\nif the Minister believes (whether or not that belief is reasonable)\nthat it is necessary to do so in order to avoid a risk of serious harm\nto:\n\n(c) the efficiency, integrity or stability of any aspect of the\nAustralian economy; or\n\n(d) the interests of consumers.\nNote:\nThe Minister still needs to comply with paragraph 56BP(a).\n\n(2) However, a failure to comply with paragraph (1)(b) of this section\ndoes not invalidate consumer data rules made as described in\nsubsection (1).\nNote:\nSuch rules may have a limited life (see section 56BT).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56br-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56br-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c9bd0984316f6766ee7d63d90daf6b6171e9b67b5791a8df27d34e82f9d041ec"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56br",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BR Commission and Information Commissioner must analyse the",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 88,
      "values:originalText": "proposed rules\n\nWhen consulted under paragraph 56BQ(c), the Commission and\nthe Information Commissioner must each analyse the kinds of\nmatters referred to in paragraphs 56BP(a) and (aa) in relation to the\nmaking of the rules.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nConsumer data right  Division 2\n\nSection 56BS\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n56BS  Emergency rules: public consultation not required etc.\n\n(1) The Minister may make consumer data rules under\nsubsection 56BA(1):\n\n(a) without complying with paragraph 56BP(b) or (c); but\n\n(b) after consulting the Commission and Information\nCommissioner;\nif the Minister believes (whether or not that belief is reasonable)\nthat it is necessary to do so in order to avoid a risk of serious harm\nto:\n\n(c) the efficiency, integrity or stability of any aspect of the\nAustralian economy; or\n\n(d) the interests of consumers.\nNote:\nThe Minister still needs to comply with paragraph 56BP(a).\n\n(2) However, a failure to comply with paragraph (1)(b) of this section\ndoes not invalidate consumer data rules made as described in\nsubsection (1).\nNote:\nSuch rules may have a limited life (see section 56BT)."
    },
