    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bt",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BT Emergency rules: consequences if made",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bt"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.89",
      "values:originalText": "If:\n\n(a) the Minister makes consumer data rules as described in\nsubsection 56BS(1) (the emergency rules); and\n\n(b) the emergency rules are made without consulting either the\nCommission or the Information Commissioner, or both;\nthe emergency rules cease to be in force 6 months after the day\nthey are made.\nNote:\nIf the emergency rules vary other consumer data rules, this section\ncauses only the emergency rules to cease to be in force.\n56BTA  Other matters\n\nA failure to comply with section 56BP, 56BQ or 56BR does not\ninvalidate consumer data rules made under subsection 56BA(1).\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "If:\n\n(a) the Minister makes consumer data rules as described in\nsubsection 56BS(1) (the emergency rules); and\n\n(b) the emergency rules are made without consulting either the\nCommission or the Information Commissioner, or both;\nthe emergency rules cease to be in force 6 months after the day\nthey are made.\nNote:\nIf the emergency rules vary other consumer data rules, this section\ncauses only the emergency rules to cease to be in force.\n56BTA  Other matters\n\nA failure to comply with section 56BP, 56BQ or 56BR does not\ninvalidate consumer data rules made under subsection 56BA(1).\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bt-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bt-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e81a41d2199a539e116bca135e3025b06bce29bcb1ddcd351bc89db8f70141fd",
      "skos:note": "Emergency rules cease after 6 months if made without consulting Commission or Information Commissioner."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bt",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BT Emergency rules: consequences if made",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 89,
      "values:originalText": "If:\n\n(a) the Minister makes consumer data rules as described in\nsubsection 56BS(1) (the emergency rules); and\n\n(b) the emergency rules are made without consulting either the\nCommission or the Information Commissioner, or both;\nthe emergency rules cease to be in force 6 months after the day\nthey are made.\nNote:\nIf the emergency rules vary other consumer data rules, this section\ncauses only the emergency rules to cease to be in force.\n56BTA  Other matters\n\nA failure to comply with section 56BP, 56BQ or 56BR does not\ninvalidate consumer data rules made under subsection 56BA(1).\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bt-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bt"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bt-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits emergency rules made without consulting Commission or Information Commissioner.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bu",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BU Charging a fee in inappropriate circumstances when required",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bu"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.90",
      "values:originalText": "to disclose CDR data\n\n(1) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n\n(a) the person is a CDR participant for CDR data; and\n\n(b) the person is required under the consumer data rules to\ndisclose all or part of the CDR data; and\n\n(c) the person charges (or causes to be charged) a fee for either\nor both of the following matters:\n\n(i) the disclosure (or a related disclosure by a designated\ngateway or other CDR participant for the CDR data);\n\n(ii) the use of the CDR data as the result of the disclosure\n(or of that related disclosure); and\n\n(d) subsection (2) or any of the following subparagraphs applies:\n\n(i) the CDR data is fee-free CDR data;\n\n(ii) to the extent that the fee is charged for the disclosure of\nchargeable CDR data—the fee purports to cover a\ndisclosure in circumstances that are not chargeable\ncircumstances;\n\n(iii) to the extent that the fee is charged for the use of\nchargeable CDR data—the fee purports to cover use in\ncircumstances that are not chargeable circumstances.\nNote:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI (including section 76 for an order for\npayment of a pecuniary penalty).\n\n(2) This subsection applies if:\n\n(a) any fee (the reasonable fee):\n\n(i) that has been determined under subsection 56BV(1) or\n(2) for the person; or\n\n(ii) that can be worked out from a method determined under\nsubsection 56BV(1) or (2) for the person;\n\ncovers either or both of the matters in paragraph (1)(c) of this\nsection; and\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nConsumer data right  Division 2\n\nSection 56BV\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) the portion of the fee charged as described in that paragraph\nfor those matters exceeds the corresponding portion of the\nreasonable fee.",
      "skos:definition": "to disclose CDR data\n\n(1) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n\n(a) the person is a CDR participant for CDR data; and\n\n(b) the person is required under the consumer data rules to\ndisclose all or part of the CDR data; and\n\n(c) the person charges (or causes to be charged) a fee for either\nor both of the following matters:\n\n(i) the disclosure (or a related disclosure by a designated\ngateway or other CDR participant for the CDR data);\n\n(ii) the use of the CDR data as the result of the disclosure\n(or of that related disclosure); and\n\n(d) subsection (2) or any of the following subparagraphs applies:\n\n(i) the CDR data is fee-free CDR data;\n\n(ii) to the extent that the fee is charged for the disclosure of\nchargeable CDR data—the fee purports to cover a\ndisclosure in circumstances that are not chargeable\ncircumstances;\n\n(iii) to the extent that the fee is charged for the use of\nchargeable CDR data—the fee purports to cover use in\ncircumstances that are not chargeable circumstances.\nNote:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI (including section 76 for an order for\npayment of a pecuniary penalty).\n\n(2) This subsection applies if:\n\n(a) any fee (the reasonable fee):\n\n(i) that has been determined under subsection 56BV(1) or\n(2) for the person; or\n\n(ii) that can be worked out from a method determined under\nsubsection 56BV(1) or (2) for the person;\n\ncovers either or both of the matters in paragraph (1)(c) of this\nsection; and\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nConsumer data right  Division 2\n\nSection 56BV\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) the portion of the fee charged as described in that paragraph\nfor those matters exceeds the corresponding portion of the\nreasonable fee.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bu-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bu-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56bu-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ab419250bfbcebe57f519d1f2d2a07e41d75b1b3017cbc199baf29ef589c2007"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56bu",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BU Charging a fee in inappropriate circumstances when required",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 90,
      "values:originalText": "to disclose CDR data\n\n(1) A person contravenes this subsection if:\n\n(a) the person is a CDR participant for CDR data; and\n\n(b) the person is required under the consumer data rules to\ndisclose all or part of the CDR data; and\n\n(c) the person charges (or causes to be charged) a fee for either\nor both of the following matters:\n\n(i) the disclosure (or a related disclosure by a designated\ngateway or other CDR participant for the CDR data);\n\n(ii) the use of the CDR data as the result of the disclosure\n(or of that related disclosure); and\n\n(d) subsection (2) or any of the following subparagraphs applies:\n\n(i) the CDR data is fee-free CDR data;\n\n(ii) to the extent that the fee is charged for the disclosure of\nchargeable CDR data—the fee purports to cover a\ndisclosure in circumstances that are not chargeable\ncircumstances;\n\n(iii) to the extent that the fee is charged for the use of\nchargeable CDR data—the fee purports to cover use in\ncircumstances that are not chargeable circumstances.\nNote:\nFor enforcement, see Part VI (including section 76 for an order for\npayment of a pecuniary penalty).\n\n(2) This subsection applies if:\n\n(a) any fee (the reasonable fee):\n\n(i) that has been determined under subsection 56BV(1) or\n(2) for the person; or\n\n(ii) that can be worked out from a method determined under\nsubsection 56BV(1) or (2) for the person;\n\ncovers either or both of the matters in paragraph (1)(c) of this\nsection; and\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nConsumer data right  Division 2\n\nSection 56BV\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) the portion of the fee charged as described in that paragraph\nfor those matters exceeds the corresponding portion of the\nreasonable fee."
    },
    {
