    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ca",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56CA Granting accreditations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ca"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.102",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The CDR Accreditor may, in writing, accredit a person if the CDR\nAccreditor is satisfied that the person meets the criteria for\naccreditation specified in the consumer data rules.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, a person may be accredited even if the person:\n\n(a) is not a body corporate established by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth, of a State or of a Territory; and\n\n(b) is neither an Australian citizen, nor a permanent resident\n(within the meaning of the Australian Citizenship Act 2007).\n\n(3) An accreditation is granted on the basis that no compensation is\npayable if the accreditation is varied, transferred, suspended,\nrevoked or surrendered in any way.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The CDR Accreditor may, in writing, accredit a person if the CDR\nAccreditor is satisfied that the person meets the criteria for\naccreditation specified in the consumer data rules.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, a person may be accredited even if the person:\n\n(a) is not a body corporate established by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth, of a State or of a Territory; and\n\n(b) is neither an Australian citizen, nor a permanent resident\n(within the meaning of the Australian Citizenship Act 2007).\n\n(3) An accreditation is granted on the basis that no compensation is\npayable if the accreditation is varied, transferred, suspended,\nrevoked or surrendered in any way.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ca-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ca-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ca-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "facba625de548d32e53a6b5755eb08e659bc0556513f1aa87d063564d18e8769"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ca",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56CA Granting accreditations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 102,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The CDR Accreditor may, in writing, accredit a person if the CDR\nAccreditor is satisfied that the person meets the criteria for\naccreditation specified in the consumer data rules.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, a person may be accredited even if the person:\n\n(a) is not a body corporate established by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth, of a State or of a Territory; and\n\n(b) is neither an Australian citizen, nor a permanent resident\n(within the meaning of the Australian Citizenship Act 2007).\n\n(3) An accreditation is granted on the basis that no compensation is\npayable if the accreditation is varied, transferred, suspended,\nrevoked or surrendered in any way."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ca-ss-1",
