    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ca-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56CA(2) Granting accreditations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ca-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.102",
      "values:originalText": "(2) To avoid doubt, a person may be accredited even if the person:\n\n(a) is not a body corporate established by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth, of a State or of a Territory; and\n\n(b) is neither an Australian citizen, nor a permanent resident\n(within the meaning of the Australian Citizenship Act 2007).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) To avoid doubt, a person may be accredited even if the person:\n\n(a) is not a body corporate established by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth, of a State or of a Territory; and\n\n(b) is neither an Australian citizen, nor a permanent resident\n(within the meaning of the Australian Citizenship Act 2007).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ca"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ca-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "128e13fbdce0a77542b44a46af067874d3a6505beb42113d150c7ac5e7879677",
      "skos:note": "Granting accreditations to individuals not meeting certain citizenship requirements."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ca-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56CA(2) Granting accreditations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 102,
      "values:originalText": "(2) To avoid doubt, a person may be accredited even if the person:\n\n(a) is not a body corporate established by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth, of a State or of a Territory; and\n\n(b) is neither an Australian citizen, nor a permanent resident\n(within the meaning of the Australian Citizenship Act 2007)."
    },
    {
