    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56cg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56CG Appointment of the CDR Accreditor",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56cg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.103",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint as the CDR\nAccreditor a person who:\n\n(a) is the accountable authority of a Commonwealth entity\n(within the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013); or\n\n(b) is a Commonwealth entity (within the meaning of that Act).\nNote 1:\nFor variation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint as the CDR\nAccreditor a person who:\n\n(a) is the accountable authority of a Commonwealth entity\n(within the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013); or\n\n(b) is a Commonwealth entity (within the meaning of that Act).\nNote 1:\nFor variation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56cg-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56cg-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a54766b270ce3382087b90a26bb29c75463924d3b1a9a2c3d59b2d5b4f72d15f",
      "skos:note": "The Minister must appoint a CDR Accreditor."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56cg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56CG Appointment of the CDR Accreditor",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 103,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint as the CDR\nAccreditor a person who:\n\n(a) is the accountable authority of a Commonwealth entity\n(within the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013); or\n\n(b) is a Commonwealth entity (within the meaning of that Act).\nNote 1:\nFor variation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
