    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ch",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56CH Functions, powers and annual report",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ch"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.104",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The functions of the CDR Accreditor are:\n\n(a) to accredit persons under subsection 56CA(1); and\n\n(b) such other functions as are conferred by the consumer data\nrules.\n\n(2) The CDR Accreditor has the power to do all other things necessary\nor convenient to be done for or in connection with the performance\nof the CDR Accreditor’s functions.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, for a person who is the CDR Accreditor, both:\n\n(a) the person’s functions and powers in their capacity other than\nas the CDR Accreditor (their primary capacity); and\n\n(b) if the person is not a body corporate—the functions that may\nbe performed, and the powers that may be exercised, by\nanyone appointed under a Commonwealth law to act as the\nperson in that primary capacity;\nare taken to include the functions and powers of the CDR\nAccreditor while the person is the CDR Accreditor.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) a person is the CDR Accreditor at any time during a period;\nand\n\n(b) an annual report for the period is prepared under section 46\nof the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability\nAct 2013:\n\n(i) by the person in the person’s primary capacity; or\n\n(ii) about the person in the person’s primary capacity;\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nAccreditation etc.  Division 3\n\nSection 56CI\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe annual report must include information about the performance\nof the CDR Accreditor’s functions, and the exercise of the CDR\nAccreditor’s powers, at that time.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The functions of the CDR Accreditor are:\n\n(a) to accredit persons under subsection 56CA(1); and\n\n(b) such other functions as are conferred by the consumer data\nrules.\n\n(2) The CDR Accreditor has the power to do all other things necessary\nor convenient to be done for or in connection with the performance\nof the CDR Accreditor’s functions.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, for a person who is the CDR Accreditor, both:\n\n(a) the person’s functions and powers in their capacity other than\nas the CDR Accreditor (their primary capacity); and\n\n(b) if the person is not a body corporate—the functions that may\nbe performed, and the powers that may be exercised, by\nanyone appointed under a Commonwealth law to act as the\nperson in that primary capacity;\nare taken to include the functions and powers of the CDR\nAccreditor while the person is the CDR Accreditor.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) a person is the CDR Accreditor at any time during a period;\nand\n\n(b) an annual report for the period is prepared under section 46\nof the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability\nAct 2013:\n\n(i) by the person in the person’s primary capacity; or\n\n(ii) about the person in the person’s primary capacity;\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nAccreditation etc.  Division 3\n\nSection 56CI\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe annual report must include information about the performance\nof the CDR Accreditor’s functions, and the exercise of the CDR\nAccreditor’s powers, at that time.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ch-ss-1"
        },
