    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56cj",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56CJ Delegation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56cj"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.105",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The CDR Accreditor may delegate any or all of the CDR\nAccreditor’s functions or powers to:\n\n(a) an SES employee, or an acting SES employee, in the\nDepartment, in the Commission or in the Commonwealth\nentity appointed under paragraph 56CG(1)(b) (if any); or\n\n(b) an APS employee who is holding or performing the duties of\na specified office or position that:\n\n(i) is in the Department, in the Commission or in the\nCommonwealth entity appointed under\nparagraph 56CG(1)(b) (if any); and\n\n(ii) is an office or position that the CDR Accreditor is\nsatisfied is sufficiently senior for the APS employee to\nperform the function or exercise the power.\n\n(2) In doing anything under a delegation under this section, the\ndelegate must comply with any directions of the CDR Accreditor.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The CDR Accreditor may delegate any or all of the CDR\nAccreditor’s functions or powers to:\n\n(a) an SES employee, or an acting SES employee, in the\nDepartment, in the Commission or in the Commonwealth\nentity appointed under paragraph 56CG(1)(b) (if any); or\n\n(b) an APS employee who is holding or performing the duties of\na specified office or position that:\n\n(i) is in the Department, in the Commission or in the\nCommonwealth entity appointed under\nparagraph 56CG(1)(b) (if any); and\n\n(ii) is an office or position that the CDR Accreditor is\nsatisfied is sufficiently senior for the APS employee to\nperform the function or exercise the power.\n\n(2) In doing anything under a delegation under this section, the\ndelegate must comply with any directions of the CDR Accreditor.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56cj-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56cj-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fbef106b6c4b9381bb43822a5c9cfafb722ad7a0dfa97efb0c503d51a4308bba"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56cj",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56CJ Delegation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 105,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The CDR Accreditor may delegate any or all of the CDR\nAccreditor’s functions or powers to:\n\n(a) an SES employee, or an acting SES employee, in the\nDepartment, in the Commission or in the Commonwealth\nentity appointed under paragraph 56CG(1)(b) (if any); or\n\n(b) an APS employee who is holding or performing the duties of\na specified office or position that:\n\n(i) is in the Department, in the Commission or in the\nCommonwealth entity appointed under\nparagraph 56CG(1)(b) (if any); and\n\n(ii) is an office or position that the CDR Accreditor is\nsatisfied is sufficiently senior for the APS employee to\nperform the function or exercise the power.\n\n(2) In doing anything under a delegation under this section, the\ndelegate must comply with any directions of the CDR Accreditor.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
