    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ck",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56CK Appointment of the Accreditation Registrar",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ck"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.106",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint as the\nAccreditation Registrar a person who:\n\n(a) is the accountable authority of a Commonwealth entity\n(within the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013); or\n\n(b) is a Commonwealth entity (within the meaning of that Act).\nNote 1:\nFor variation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nNote 2:\nThe Commission will be the Accreditation Registrar in the absence of\nan appointment under this subsection (see the definition of\nAccreditation Registrar in subsection 4(1)).\n\n(2) The Minister may, at any time by written instrument, terminate an\nappointment made under subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint as the\nAccreditation Registrar a person who:\n\n(a) is the accountable authority of a Commonwealth entity\n(within the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013); or\n\n(b) is a Commonwealth entity (within the meaning of that Act).\nNote 1:\nFor variation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nNote 2:\nThe Commission will be the Accreditation Registrar in the absence of\nan appointment under this subsection (see the definition of\nAccreditation Registrar in subsection 4(1)).\n\n(2) The Minister may, at any time by written instrument, terminate an\nappointment made under subsection (1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ck-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ck-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5540305e6038234f009f8355edc6b5a3c941da28237dd42c72ace0d7500d0a0e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ck",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56CK Appointment of the Accreditation Registrar",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 106,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint as the\nAccreditation Registrar a person who:\n\n(a) is the accountable authority of a Commonwealth entity\n(within the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013); or\n\n(b) is a Commonwealth entity (within the meaning of that Act).\nNote 1:\nFor variation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nNote 2:\nThe Commission will be the Accreditation Registrar in the absence of\nan appointment under this subsection (see the definition of\nAccreditation Registrar in subsection 4(1)).\n\n(2) The Minister may, at any time by written instrument, terminate an\nappointment made under subsection (1)."
    },
