    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56cm",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56CM Directions by Minister",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56cm"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.107",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, give written directions\nto the Accreditation Registrar about the performance of its\nfunctions and the exercise of its powers.\nNote:\nSection 42 (disallowance) and Part 4 of Chapter 3 (sunsetting) of the\nLegislation Act 2003 do not apply to the directions (see regulations\nmade for the purposes of paragraphs 44(2)(b) and 54(2)(b) of that\nAct).\n\n(2) A direction under subsection (1) must be of a general nature only.\n\n(3) The Accreditation Registrar must comply with a direction under\nsubsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, give written directions\nto the Accreditation Registrar about the performance of its\nfunctions and the exercise of its powers.\nNote:\nSection 42 (disallowance) and Part 4 of Chapter 3 (sunsetting) of the\nLegislation Act 2003 do not apply to the directions (see regulations\nmade for the purposes of paragraphs 44(2)(b) and 54(2)(b) of that\nAct).\n\n(2) A direction under subsection (1) must be of a general nature only.\n\n(3) The Accreditation Registrar must comply with a direction under\nsubsection (1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56cm-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56cm-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56cm-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8e49b942f683a358e3129b02f85caa2b9d782d96315717a7569bef66e3682002"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56cm",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56CM Directions by Minister",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 107,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, give written directions\nto the Accreditation Registrar about the performance of its\nfunctions and the exercise of its powers.\nNote:\nSection 42 (disallowance) and Part 4 of Chapter 3 (sunsetting) of the\nLegislation Act 2003 do not apply to the directions (see regulations\nmade for the purposes of paragraphs 44(2)(b) and 54(2)(b) of that\nAct).\n\n(2) A direction under subsection (1) must be of a general nature only.\n\n(3) The Accreditation Registrar must comply with a direction under\nsubsection (1)."
    },
