      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ed-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Must",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Entity must provide information",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ed-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56ED(5) Privacy safeguard 1—open and transparent management of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ed-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.114",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the CDR entity is an accredited person who is or who may\nbecome an accredited data recipient of any CDR data, the CDR\nentity’s policy must contain the following information:\n\n(a) the classes of CDR data that is or may become held by (or on\nbehalf of) the CDR entity as an accredited data recipient, and\nhow such CDR data is held or is to be held;\n\n(b) the purposes for which the CDR entity may collect, hold, use\nor disclose such CDR data with the consent of a CDR\nconsumer for the CDR data;\n\n(c) how a CDR consumer for such CDR data may access the\nCDR data and seek the correction of the CDR data;\n\n(d) how a CDR consumer for such CDR data may complain\nabout a failure of the CDR entity to comply with this Part or\nthe consumer data rules, and how the CDR entity will deal\nwith such a complaint;\n\n(e) whether the CDR entity is likely to disclose such CDR data\nto accredited persons who are based overseas;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If the CDR entity is an accredited person who is or who may\nbecome an accredited data recipient of any CDR data, the CDR\nentity’s policy must contain the following information:\n\n(a) the classes of CDR data that is or may become held by (or on\nbehalf of) the CDR entity as an accredited data recipient, and\nhow such CDR data is held or is to be held;\n\n(b) the purposes for which the CDR entity may collect, hold, use\nor disclose such CDR data with the consent of a CDR\nconsumer for the CDR data;\n\n(c) how a CDR consumer for such CDR data may access the\nCDR data and seek the correction of the CDR data;\n\n(d) how a CDR consumer for such CDR data may complain\nabout a failure of the CDR entity to comply with this Part or\nthe consumer data rules, and how the CDR entity will deal\nwith such a complaint;\n\n(e) whether the CDR entity is likely to disclose such CDR data\nto accredited persons who are based overseas;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ed"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ed-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ed-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ff40407d64149ae3ae862986ca7601387c36322cba7a5dc3e4e6686e9e1ad7da",
      "skos:note": "CDR entity must provide certain information to accredited data recipients",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ed-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56ED(5) Privacy safeguard 1—open and transparent management of",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 114,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the CDR entity is an accredited person who is or who may\nbecome an accredited data recipient of any CDR data, the CDR\nentity’s policy must contain the following information:\n\n(a) the classes of CDR data that is or may become held by (or on\nbehalf of) the CDR entity as an accredited data recipient, and\nhow such CDR data is held or is to be held;\n\n(b) the purposes for which the CDR entity may collect, hold, use\nor disclose such CDR data with the consent of a CDR\nconsumer for the CDR data;\n\n(c) how a CDR consumer for such CDR data may access the\nCDR data and seek the correction of the CDR data;\n\n(d) how a CDR consumer for such CDR data may complain\nabout a failure of the CDR entity to comply with this Part or\nthe consumer data rules, and how the CDR entity will deal\nwith such a complaint;\n\n(e) whether the CDR entity is likely to disclose such CDR data\nto accredited persons who are based overseas;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
