    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ef",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EF Privacy safeguard 3—soliciting CDR data from participants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ef"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.118",
      "values:originalText": "under the consumer data rules\n\n(1) A person covered by column 1 of an item of the following table\nmust not seek to collect CDR data under the consumer data rules\nfrom another person covered by column 2 of that item unless:\n\n(a) a CDR consumer for the CDR data has validly requested this\nunder the consumer data rules for the purposes described in\ncolumn 3 of that item; and\n\n(b) the person complies with all other requirements in the\nconsumer data rules for the collection of the CDR data from\nthat other person.\n\nSoliciting CDR data from participants under the consumer data rules\nItem\nColumn 1\nA person\nwho:\nColumn 2\nmust not seek to\ncollect CDR data\nfrom:\nColumn 3\nunless a CDR consumer for the\nCDR data has requested this for\nthe purposes of:\nis an\naccredited\nperson\na CDR participant\nfor the CDR data\na use or disclosure under the\nconsumer data rules\nis acting as\none of the\nkinds of CDR\naction\nparticipant\nthe other kind of\nCDR action\nparticipant\na valid instruction to be given:\n(a) by one of the CDR action\nparticipants (as an accredited\naction initiator for a type of\nCDR action) to the other; and\n(b) under the consumer data rules;\nand\n(c) for the performance of a CDR\naction of that type\nNote 1:\nFor item 2, the kinds of CDR action participants are accredited action\ninitiators and action service providers (see section 56AMD).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPrivacy safeguards  Division 5\n\nSection 56EG\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote 2:\nFor column 3 of item 2, the CDR consumer for the CDR data would\nneed to have requested the collection of the CDR data as a CDR\nconsumer for the CDR action.\nNote 3:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether the collection is directly or\nindirectly from the person covered by column 2 of the table.\nNote:\nThe collection (whether direct or indirect) would need to be under the\nconsumer data rules for subsection (1) to apply.\nExample: The valid request referred to in column 3 of item 1 of the table could\nbe given under the consumer data rules through a designated gateway\n(see section 56BG).",
      "skos:definition": "under the consumer data rules\n\n(1) A person covered by column 1 of an item of the following table\nmust not seek to collect CDR data under the consumer data rules\nfrom another person covered by column 2 of that item unless:\n\n(a) a CDR consumer for the CDR data has validly requested this\nunder the consumer data rules for the purposes described in\ncolumn 3 of that item; and\n\n(b) the person complies with all other requirements in the\nconsumer data rules for the collection of the CDR data from\nthat other person.\n\nSoliciting CDR data from participants under the consumer data rules\nItem\nColumn 1\nA person\nwho:\nColumn 2\nmust not seek to\ncollect CDR data\nfrom:\nColumn 3\nunless a CDR consumer for the\nCDR data has requested this for\nthe purposes of:\nis an\naccredited\nperson\na CDR participant\nfor the CDR data\na use or disclosure under the\nconsumer data rules\nis acting as\none of the\nkinds of CDR\naction\nparticipant\nthe other kind of\nCDR action\nparticipant\na valid instruction to be given:\n(a) by one of the CDR action\nparticipants (as an accredited\naction initiator for a type of\nCDR action) to the other; and\n(b) under the consumer data rules;\nand\n(c) for the performance of a CDR\naction of that type\nNote 1:\nFor item 2, the kinds of CDR action participants are accredited action\ninitiators and action service providers (see section 56AMD).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPrivacy safeguards  Division 5\n\nSection 56EG\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote 2:\nFor column 3 of item 2, the CDR consumer for the CDR data would\nneed to have requested the collection of the CDR data as a CDR\nconsumer for the CDR action.\nNote 3:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether the collection is directly or\nindirectly from the person covered by column 2 of the table.\nNote:\nThe collection (whether direct or indirect) would need to be under t",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ef-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ef-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0863069ed8f79dba7e3b38b9cd4abd04a9445214ecbd9e3be15ac2810d0e2ed6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ef",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EF Privacy safeguard 3—soliciting CDR data from participants",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 118,
      "values:originalText": "under the consumer data rules\n\n(1) A person covered by column 1 of an item of the following table\nmust not seek to collect CDR data under the consumer data rules\nfrom another person covered by column 2 of that item unless:\n\n(a) a CDR consumer for the CDR data has validly requested this\nunder the consumer data rules for the purposes described in\ncolumn 3 of that item; and\n\n(b) the person complies with all other requirements in the\nconsumer data rules for the collection of the CDR data from\nthat other person.\n\nSoliciting CDR data from participants under the consumer data rules\nItem\nColumn 1\nA person\nwho:\nColumn 2\nmust not seek to\ncollect CDR data\nfrom:\nColumn 3\nunless a CDR consumer for the\nCDR data has requested this for\nthe purposes of:\nis an\naccredited\nperson\na CDR participant\nfor the CDR data\na use or disclosure under the\nconsumer data rules\nis acting as\none of the\nkinds of CDR\naction\nparticipant\nthe other kind of\nCDR action\nparticipant\na valid instruction to be given:\n(a) by one of the CDR action\nparticipants (as an accredited\naction initiator for a type of\nCDR action) to the other; and\n(b) under the consumer data rules;\nand\n(c) for the performance of a CDR\naction of that type\nNote 1:\nFor item 2, the kinds of CDR action participants are accredited action\ninitiators and action service providers (see section 56AMD).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPrivacy safeguards  Division 5\n\nSection 56EG\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote 2:\nFor column 3 of item 2, the CDR consumer for the CDR data would\nneed to have requested the collection of the CDR data as a CDR\nconsumer for the CDR action.\nNote 3:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether the collection is directly or\nindirectly from the person covered by column 2 of the table.\nNote:\nThe collection (whether direct or indirect) would need to be under the\nconsumer data rules for subsection (1) to apply.\nExample: The valid request referred to in column 3 of item 1 of the table could\nbe given under the consumer data rules through a designated gateway\n(see section 56BG)."
    },
