    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56eg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EG Privacy safeguard 4—dealing with unsolicited CDR data from",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56eg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.119",
      "values:originalText": "participants in CDR\n\n(1) A person must destroy CDR data as soon as practicable after\ncollecting it if:\n\n(a) the person (the collector) collected the CDR data while\ncovered by column 1 of an item of the following table, and\nfrom a person covered by column 2 of that item; and\n\n(b) the collector collected the CDR data:\n\n(i) purportedly under the consumer data rules; but\n\n(ii) not as the result of seeking to collect the CDR data\nunder the consumer data rules; and\n\n(c) the collector is not required to retain the CDR data by or\nunder an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; and\n\n(d) in the case where item 3 of the table applies, the\ncircumstances specified in the consumer data rules do not\napply.\n\nDealing with unsolicited CDR data from participants in CDR\nItem\nColumn 1\nA collector who:\nColumn 2\ncollects the CDR data from:\nis an accredited person\na CDR participant for the CDR data\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "participants in CDR\n\n(1) A person must destroy CDR data as soon as practicable after\ncollecting it if:\n\n(a) the person (the collector) collected the CDR data while\ncovered by column 1 of an item of the following table, and\nfrom a person covered by column 2 of that item; and\n\n(b) the collector collected the CDR data:\n\n(i) purportedly under the consumer data rules; but\n\n(ii) not as the result of seeking to collect the CDR data\nunder the consumer data rules; and\n\n(c) the collector is not required to retain the CDR data by or\nunder an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; and\n\n(d) in the case where item 3 of the table applies, the\ncircumstances specified in the consumer data rules do not\napply.\n\nDealing with unsolicited CDR data from participants in CDR\nItem\nColumn 1\nA collector who:\nColumn 2\ncollects the CDR data from:\nis an accredited person\na CDR participant for the CDR data\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56eg-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56eg-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56eg-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56eg-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56eg-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "31d5d55c1c468b9f745a5c559df24baaaa64d8aed06287fb160bf3a897f569ca",
      "skos:note": "Destroy CDR data as soon as practicable after collecting it if certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56eg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EG Privacy safeguard 4—dealing with unsolicited CDR data from",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 119,
      "values:originalText": "participants in CDR\n\n(1) A person must destroy CDR data as soon as practicable after\ncollecting it if:\n\n(a) the person (the collector) collected the CDR data while\ncovered by column 1 of an item of the following table, and\nfrom a person covered by column 2 of that item; and\n\n(b) the collector collected the CDR data:\n\n(i) purportedly under the consumer data rules; but\n\n(ii) not as the result of seeking to collect the CDR data\nunder the consumer data rules; and\n\n(c) the collector is not required to retain the CDR data by or\nunder an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; and\n\n(d) in the case where item 3 of the table applies, the\ncircumstances specified in the consumer data rules do not\napply.\n\nDealing with unsolicited CDR data from participants in CDR\nItem\nColumn 1\nA collector who:\nColumn 2\ncollects the CDR data from:\nis an accredited person\na CDR participant for the CDR data\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
