        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The collector collected the CDR data not as the result of seeking to collect the CDR data under the consumer data rules.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Destroy CDR data as soon as practicable after collecting it if certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56eh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EH Privacy safeguard 5—notifying of the collection of CDR data",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56eh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.120",
      "values:originalText": "If an accredited data recipient of CDR data collected the CDR data\nin accordance with section 56EF, the accredited data recipient\nmust:\n\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the collection; and\n\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote 1:\nThe accredited data recipient could have collected the CDR data in\naccordance with section 56EF as an accredited action initiator, and\nfrom an action service provider, for the purposes of giving a valid\ninstruction of the kind described in item 2 of the table in that section.\nNote 2:\nThis section is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPrivacy safeguards  Division 5\n\nSection 56EI\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSubdivision D—Dealing with CDR data",
      "skos:definition": "If an accredited data recipient of CDR data collected the CDR data\nin accordance with section 56EF, the accredited data recipient\nmust:\n\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the collection; and\n\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote 1:\nThe accredited data recipient could have collected the CDR data in\naccordance with section 56EF as an accredited action initiator, and\nfrom an action service provider, for the purposes of giving a valid\ninstruction of the kind described in item 2 of the table in that section.\nNote 2:\nThis section is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPrivacy safeguards  Division 5\n\nSection 56EI\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSubdivision D—Dealing with CDR data",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56eh-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56eh-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1103a9eb429f8e50cb76be047751675b3d55f887b929fb45a93c2c6dae092ad1",
      "skos:note": "Accredited data recipient must notify CDR consumers of collection",
      "dc:description": "Notification to CDR consumers"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56eh",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EH Privacy safeguard 5—notifying of the collection of CDR data",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 120,
      "values:originalText": "If an accredited data recipient of CDR data collected the CDR data\nin accordance with section 56EF, the accredited data recipient\nmust:\n\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the collection; and\n\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote 1:\nThe accredited data recipient could have collected the CDR data in\naccordance with section 56EF as an accredited action initiator, and\nfrom an action service provider, for the purposes of giving a valid\ninstruction of the kind described in item 2 of the table in that section.\nNote 2:\nThis section is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPrivacy safeguards  Division 5\n\nSection 56EI\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSubdivision D—Dealing with CDR data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56eh-norm",
