    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56el",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EL Privacy safeguard 9—adoption or disclosure of government",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56el"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.124",
      "values:originalText": "related identifiers by accredited data recipients\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person is an accredited data recipient of CDR data; and\n\n(b) the CDR data includes a government related identifier\n(within the meaning of the Privacy Act 1988) of a CDR\nconsumer for the CDR data who is an individual;\nthe person must not adopt the government related identifier as the\nperson’s own identifier of the CDR consumer, or otherwise use the\ngovernment related identifier, unless:\n\n(c) the adoption or use is required or authorised by or under:\n\n(i) an Australian law other than the consumer data rules; or\n\n(ii) a court/tribunal order; or\n\n(d) subclause 9.3 of Australian Privacy Principle 9 applies in\nrelation to the adoption or use.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a person who is an accredited data recipient of CDR data\nproposes to disclose the CDR data; and\n\n(b) the CDR data includes a government related identifier\n(within the meaning of the Privacy Act 1988) of a CDR\nconsumer for the CDR data who is an individual;\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPrivacy safeguards  Division 5\n\nSection 56EM\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe person must not include the government related identifier in the\ndisclosure unless:\n\n(c) this is required or authorised by or under:\n\n(i) an Australian law other than the consumer data rules; or\n\n(ii) a court/tribunal order; or\n\n(d) subclause 9.3 of Australian Privacy Principle 9 applies in\nrelation to the disclosure.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nThis subsection applies in addition to the disclosure restrictions in\nsections 56EI, 56EJ and 56EK.\n\n(3) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(d) or (2)(d), disregard\nparagraph 56EC(4)(a) (about the APPs not applying).",
      "skos:definition": "related identifiers by accredited data recipients\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person is an accredited data recipient of CDR data; and\n\n(b) the CDR data includes a government related identifier\n(within the meaning of the Privacy Act 1988) of a CDR\nconsumer for the CDR data who is an individual;\nthe person must not adopt the government related identifier as the\nperson’s own identifier of the CDR consumer, or otherwise use the\ngovernment related identifier, unless:\n\n(c) the adoption or use is required or authorised by or under:\n\n(i) an Australian law other than the consumer data rules; or\n\n(ii) a court/tribunal order; or\n\n(d) subclause 9.3 of Australian Privacy Principle 9 applies in\nrelation to the adoption or use.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a person who is an accredited data recipient of CDR data\nproposes to disclose the CDR data; and\n\n(b) the CDR data includes a government related identifier\n(within the meaning of the Privacy Act 1988) of a CDR\nconsumer for the CDR data who is an individual;\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPrivacy safeguards  Division 5\n\nSection 56EM\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe person must not include the government related identifier in the\ndisclosure unless:\n\n(c) this is required or authorised by or under:\n\n(i) an Australian law other than the consumer data rules; or\n\n(ii) a court/tribunal order; or\n\n(d) subclause 9.3 of Australian Privacy Principle 9 applies in\nrelation to the disclosure.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nThis subsection applies in addition to the disclosure restrictions in\nsections 56EI, 56EJ and 56EK.\n\n(3) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(d) or (2)(d), disregard\nparagraph 56EC(4)(a) (about the APPs not applying).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56el-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56el-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56el-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6a9882f7afa7888e0c7dfeeeec20e3de58198081c2793b1bc8d4840a9ca4c34c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56el",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EL Privacy safeguard 9—adoption or disclosure of government",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 124,
      "values:originalText": "related identifiers by accredited data recipients\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person is an accredited data recipient of CDR data; and\n\n(b) the CDR data includes a government related identifier\n(within the meaning of the Privacy Act 1988) of a CDR\nconsumer for the CDR data who is an individual;\nthe person must not adopt the government related identifier as the\nperson’s own identifier of the CDR consumer, or otherwise use the\ngovernment related identifier, unless:\n\n(c) the adoption or use is required or authorised by or under:\n\n(i) an Australian law other than the consumer data rules; or\n\n(ii) a court/tribunal order; or\n\n(d) subclause 9.3 of Australian Privacy Principle 9 applies in\nrelation to the adoption or use.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a person who is an accredited data recipient of CDR data\nproposes to disclose the CDR data; and\n\n(b) the CDR data includes a government related identifier\n(within the meaning of the Privacy Act 1988) of a CDR\nconsumer for the CDR data who is an individual;\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPrivacy safeguards  Division 5\n\nSection 56EM\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe person must not include the government related identifier in the\ndisclosure unless:\n\n(c) this is required or authorised by or under:\n\n(i) an Australian law other than the consumer data rules; or\n\n(ii) a court/tribunal order; or\n\n(d) subclause 9.3 of Australian Privacy Principle 9 applies in\nrelation to the disclosure.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nThis subsection applies in addition to the disclosure restrictions in\nsections 56EI, 56EJ and 56EK.\n\n(3) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(d) or (2)(d), disregard\nparagraph 56EC(4)(a) (about the APPs not applying)."
    },
