    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56em",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EM Privacy safeguard 10—notifying of the disclosure of CDR",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56em"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.125",
      "values:originalText": "data\nDisclosures by data holders\n\n(1) If a data holder of CDR data is required or authorised under the\nconsumer data rules to disclose the CDR data to a person, the data\nholder must:\n\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the disclosure; and\n\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nDisclosures by accredited data recipients\n\n(2) If an accredited data recipient of CDR data discloses the CDR data,\nthe accredited data recipient must:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "data\nDisclosures by data holders\n\n(1) If a data holder of CDR data is required or authorised under the\nconsumer data rules to disclose the CDR data to a person, the data\nholder must:\n\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the disclosure; and\n\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nDisclosures by accredited data recipients\n\n(2) If an accredited data recipient of CDR data discloses the CDR data,\nthe accredited data recipient must:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56em-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56em-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "88d958c4148fc706d5b926c5ad8c034c28a0c8d20f27fb9e36444628abe82bb9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56em",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EM Privacy safeguard 10—notifying of the disclosure of CDR",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 125,
      "values:originalText": "data\nDisclosures by data holders\n\n(1) If a data holder of CDR data is required or authorised under the\nconsumer data rules to disclose the CDR data to a person, the data\nholder must:\n\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the disclosure; and\n\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nDisclosures by accredited data recipients\n\n(2) If an accredited data recipient of CDR data discloses the CDR data,\nthe accredited data recipient must:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
