    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ep",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EP Privacy safeguard 13—correction of CDR data",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ep"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.130",
      "values:originalText": "Obligation on data holders and action service providers\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a CDR consumer for CDR data gives a request to the\nfollowing person (the CDR entity):\n\n(i) a data holder of the CDR data (including a request given\nthrough a designated gateway for the CDR data);\n\n(ii) a person as an action service provider for a type of CDR\naction; and\n\n(b) the request is for the CDR entity to correct the CDR data, and\nis not given in response to advice from the CDR entity under\nsubsection 56EN(3); and\n\n(c) the CDR entity was earlier required or authorised under the\nconsumer data rules to disclose the CDR data;\nthe CDR entity must respond to the request to correct the CDR data\nby taking such steps as are specified in the consumer data rules to\ndeal with each of the matters in subsection (3) of this section.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nSubsection 56EN(4) applies instead of this subsection if the request is\ngiven in response to advice from the CDR entity under\nsubsection 56EN(3).\nObligation on accredited data recipients\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a CDR consumer for CDR data gives a request to an\naccredited data recipient of the CDR data (including a request\ngiven through a designated gateway for the CDR data); and\n\n(b) the request is for the accredited data recipient to correct the\nCDR data, and is not given in response to advice from the\naccredited data recipient under subsection 56EN(3);\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPrivacy safeguards  Division 5\n\nSection 56EQ\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe accredited data recipient must respond to the request by taking\nsuch steps as are specified in the consumer data rules to deal with\neach of the matters in subsection (3) of this section.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nSubsection 56EN(4) applies instead of this subsection if the request is\ngiven in response to advice from the accredited data recipient under\nsubsection 56EN(3).\nRelevant matters when responding to correction requests\n\n(3) The matters are as follows:\n\n(a) either:\n\n(i) to correct the CDR data; or\n\n(ii) to include a statement with the CDR data, to ensure that,\nhaving regard to the purpose for which the CDR data is\nheld, the CDR data is accurate, up to date, complete and\nnot misleading;\n\n(b) to give notice of any correction or statement, or notice of\nwhy a correction or statement is unnecessary or\ninappropriate.\n\n(4) When working out the purpose for which the CDR data is held (see\nsubparagraph (3)(a)(ii)), disregard the purpose of holding the CDR\ndata so that it can be disclosed as required under the consumer data\nrules.\nSubdivision G—Compliance with the privacy safeguards\n56EQ  Information Commissioner to promote compliance etc.\n\n(1) The Information Commissioner has the following functions:\n\n(a) making guidelines for the avoidance of acts or practices that\nmay breach the privacy safeguards;\n\n(b) promoting an understanding and acceptance of the privacy\nsafeguards;\n\n(c) undertaking educational programs for the purposes of\npromoting the protection of CDR data.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "Obligation on data holders and action service providers\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a CDR consumer for CDR data gives a request to the\nfollowing person (the CDR entity):\n\n(i) a data holder of the CDR data (including a request given\nthrough a designated gateway for the CDR data);\n\n(ii) a person as an action service provider for a type of CDR\naction; and\n\n(b) the request is for the CDR entity to correct the CDR data, and\nis not given in response to advice from the CDR entity under\nsubsection 56EN(3); and\n\n(c) the CDR entity was earlier required or authorised under the\nconsumer data rules to disclose the CDR data;\nthe CDR entity must respond to the request to correct the CDR data\nby taking such steps as are specified in the consumer data rules to\ndeal with each of the matters in subsection (3) of this section.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nSubsection 56EN(4) applies instead of this subsection if the request is\ngiven in response to advice from the CDR entity under\nsubsection 56EN(3).\nObligation on accredited data recipients\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a CDR consumer for CDR data gives a request to an\naccredited data recipient of the CDR data (including a request\ngiven through a designated gateway for the CDR data); and\n\n(b) the request is for the accredited data recipient to correct the\nCDR data, and is not given in response to advice from the\naccredited data recipient under subsection 56EN(3);\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPrivacy safeguards  Division 5\n\nSection 56EQ\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe accredited data recipient must respond to the request by taking\nsuch steps as are specified in the consumer data rules to deal with\neach of the matters in subsection (3) of this section.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nSubsection 56EN(4) applies instead of this subsection if the request",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ep-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ep-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ep-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ep-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ep-ss-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "160e394e41cfa029a680070a66b42d96d215f16ede997e4f73aeef7dd16bbbc6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ep",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EP Privacy safeguard 13—correction of CDR data",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 130,
      "values:originalText": "Obligation on data holders and action service providers\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a CDR consumer for CDR data gives a request to the\nfollowing person (the CDR entity):\n\n(i) a data holder of the CDR data (including a request given\nthrough a designated gateway for the CDR data);\n\n(ii) a person as an action service provider for a type of CDR\naction; and\n\n(b) the request is for the CDR entity to correct the CDR data, and\nis not given in response to advice from the CDR entity under\nsubsection 56EN(3); and\n\n(c) the CDR entity was earlier required or authorised under the\nconsumer data rules to disclose the CDR data;\nthe CDR entity must respond to the request to correct the CDR data\nby taking such steps as are specified in the consumer data rules to\ndeal with each of the matters in subsection (3) of this section.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nSubsection 56EN(4) applies instead of this subsection if the request is\ngiven in response to advice from the CDR entity under\nsubsection 56EN(3).\nObligation on accredited data recipients\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a CDR consumer for CDR data gives a request to an\naccredited data recipient of the CDR data (including a request\ngiven through a designated gateway for the CDR data); and\n\n(b) the request is for the accredited data recipient to correct the\nCDR data, and is not given in response to advice from the\naccredited data recipient under subsection 56EN(3);\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPrivacy safeguards  Division 5\n\nSection 56EQ\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe accredited data recipient must respond to the request by taking\nsuch steps as are specified in the consumer data rules to deal with\neach of the matters in subsection (3) of this section.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nSubsection 56EN(4) applies instead of this subsection if the request is\ngiven in response to advice from the accredited data recipient under\nsubsection 56EN(3).\nRelevant matters when responding to correction requests\n\n(3) The matters are as follows:\n\n(a) either:\n\n(i) to correct the CDR data; or\n\n(ii) to include a statement with the CDR data, to ensure that,\nhaving regard to the purpose for which the CDR data is\nheld, the CDR data is accurate, up to date, complete and\nnot misleading;\n\n(b) to give notice of any correction or statement, or notice of\nwhy a correction or statement is unnecessary or\ninappropriate.\n\n(4) When working out the purpose for which the CDR data is held (see\nsubparagraph (3)(a)(ii)), disregard the purpose of holding the CDR\ndata so that it can be disclosed as required under the consumer data\nrules.\nSubdivision G—Compliance with the privacy safeguards\n56EQ  Information Commissioner to promote compliance etc.\n\n(1) The Information Commissioner has the following functions:\n\n(a) making guidelines for the avoidance of acts or practices that\nmay breach the privacy safeguards;\n\n(b) promoting an understanding and acceptance of the privacy\nsafeguards;\n\n(c) undertaking educational programs for the purposes of\npromoting the protection of CDR data.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
