      "cml:conclusionText": "Correcting CDR data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56er",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56ER Information Commissioner may conduct an assessment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56er"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.132",
      "values:originalText": "relating to the management and handling of CDR data\n\n(1) The Information Commissioner may assess whether a CDR\nparticipant, or designated gateway, for CDR data is maintaining\nand handling the CDR data in accordance with:\n\n(a) the privacy safeguards; or\n\n(b) the consumer data rules to the extent that those rules relate\nto:\n\n(i) the privacy safeguards; or\n\n(ii) the privacy or confidentiality of the CDR data.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPrivacy safeguards  Division 5\n\nSection 56ES\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(1A) The Information Commissioner may assess whether an accredited\nperson who may become an accredited data recipient of CDR data\nis complying with:\n\n(a) section 56ED (about privacy safeguard 1); or\n\n(b) the consumer data rules to the extent that those rules relate to\nthat section.\n\n(1B) The Information Commissioner may assess whether an action\nservice provider for a type of CDR action, who has been or may be\ndisclosed CDR data under the consumer data rules, is maintaining\nand handling the CDR data in accordance with:\n\n(a) the privacy safeguards; or\n\n(b) the consumer data rules to the extent that those rules relate\nto:\n\n(i) the privacy safeguards; or\n\n(ii) the privacy or confidentiality of the CDR data.\n\n(2) The Information Commissioner may conduct an assessment under\nsubsection (1), (1A) or (1B) in such manner as the Information\nCommissioner considers fit.\n\n(3) The Information Commissioner may report to the Minister, the\nCommission or the Data Standards Chair about an assessment\nunder subsection (1), (1A) or (1B).",
      "skos:definition": "relating to the management and handling of CDR data\n\n(1) The Information Commissioner may assess whether a CDR\nparticipant, or designated gateway, for CDR data is maintaining\nand handling the CDR data in accordance with:\n\n(a) the privacy safeguards; or\n\n(b) the consumer data rules to the extent that those rules relate\nto:\n\n(i) the privacy safeguards; or\n\n(ii) the privacy or confidentiality of the CDR data.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPrivacy safeguards  Division 5\n\nSection 56ES\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(1A) The Information Commissioner may assess whether an accredited\nperson who may become an accredited data recipient of CDR data\nis complying with:\n\n(a) section 56ED (about privacy safeguard 1); or\n\n(b) the consumer data rules to the extent that those rules relate to\nthat section.\n\n(1B) The Information Commissioner may assess whether an action\nservice provider for a type of CDR action, who has been or may be\ndisclosed CDR data under the consumer data rules, is maintaining\nand handling the CDR data in accordance with:\n\n(a) the privacy safeguards; or\n\n(b) the consumer data rules to the extent that those rules relate\nto:\n\n(i) the privacy safeguards; or\n\n(ii) the privacy or confidentiality of the CDR data.\n\n(2) The Information Commissioner may conduct an assessment under\nsubsection (1), (1A) or (1B) in such manner as the Information\nCommissioner considers fit.\n\n(3) The Information Commissioner may report to the Minister, the\nCommission or the Data Standards Chair about an assessment\nunder subsection (1), (1A) or (1B).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56er-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56er-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56er-ss-1b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56er-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56er-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "82bc980ed74eb4915d7d13a4e6365f720a08404516cc5f1715e9dd76a47da80a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56er",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56ER Information Commissioner may conduct an assessment",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 132,
      "values:originalText": "relating to the management and handling of CDR data\n\n(1) The Information Commissioner may assess whether a CDR\nparticipant, or designated gateway, for CDR data is maintaining\nand handling the CDR data in accordance with:\n\n(a) the privacy safeguards; or\n\n(b) the consumer data rules to the extent that those rules relate\nto:\n\n(i) the privacy safeguards; or\n\n(ii) the privacy or confidentiality of the CDR data.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nPrivacy safeguards  Division 5\n\nSection 56ES\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(1A) The Information Commissioner may assess whether an accredited\nperson who may become an accredited data recipient of CDR data\nis complying with:\n\n(a) section 56ED (about privacy safeguard 1); or\n\n(b) the consumer data rules to the extent that those rules relate to\nthat section.\n\n(1B) The Information Commissioner may assess whether an action\nservice provider for a type of CDR action, who has been or may be\ndisclosed CDR data under the consumer data rules, is maintaining\nand handling the CDR data in accordance with:\n\n(a) the privacy safeguards; or\n\n(b) the consumer data rules to the extent that those rules relate\nto:\n\n(i) the privacy safeguards; or\n\n(ii) the privacy or confidentiality of the CDR data.\n\n(2) The Information Commissioner may conduct an assessment under\nsubsection (1), (1A) or (1B) in such manner as the Information\nCommissioner considers fit.\n\n(3) The Information Commissioner may report to the Minister, the\nCommission or the Data Standards Chair about an assessment\nunder subsection (1), (1A) or (1B)."
    },
