    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56es",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56ES Notification of CDR data security breaches",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56es"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.133",
      "values:originalText": "Object\n\n(1) The object of this section is for Part IIIC of the Privacy Act 1988 to\napply to an accredited data recipient, or designated gateway, that\nholds a CDR consumer’s CDR data in a corresponding way to the\nway that Part applies to an entity that holds an individual’s\npersonal information.\nNote:\nThat Part is about notification of eligible data breaches.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "Object\n\n(1) The object of this section is for Part IIIC of the Privacy Act 1988 to\napply to an accredited data recipient, or designated gateway, that\nholds a CDR consumer’s CDR data in a corresponding way to the\nway that Part applies to an entity that holds an individual’s\npersonal information.\nNote:\nThat Part is about notification of eligible data breaches.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56es-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56es-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "53472e96c480fc9bce701aebca540a27a800418273e759bf7266ee816321c998",
      "skos:note": "Notification of CDR data security breaches"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56es",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56ES Notification of CDR data security breaches",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 133,
      "values:originalText": "Object\n\n(1) The object of this section is for Part IIIC of the Privacy Act 1988 to\napply to an accredited data recipient, or designated gateway, that\nholds a CDR consumer’s CDR data in a corresponding way to the\nway that Part applies to an entity that holds an individual’s\npersonal information.\nNote:\nThat Part is about notification of eligible data breaches.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56es-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56es"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56es-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must notify",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56eu",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EU Civil penalty provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56eu"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.139",
      "values:originalText": "The provisions of this Division that are civil penalty provisions\n\n(1) For the purposes of subparagraph 79(2)(a)(ii) of the Regulatory\nPowers Act, each of the following provisions of this Division (the\nprivacy safeguard penalty provisions) is a civil penalty provision:\n\n(a) subsection 56ED(3);\n\n(b) subsection 56EF(1);\n\n(c) subsection 56EG(1);\n\n(d) section 56EH;\n\n(e) subsection 56EI(1) or (2);\n\n(f) subsection 56EJ(1) or (2);\n\n(g) subsection 56EK(1);\n\n(h) subsection 56EL(1) or (2);\n\n(i) subsection 56EM(1), (2) or (4);\n\n(j) subsection 56EN(1), (2), (2A), (3) or (4);\n\n(k) subsection 56EO(1) or (2);\n\n(l) subsection 56EP(1) or (2).\nEnforceable civil penalty provisions\n\n(2) Each privacy safeguard penalty provision is enforceable under\nPart 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act.\nNote:\nPart 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act allows a civil penalty provision to\nbe enforced by obtaining an order for a person to pay a pecuniary\npenalty for the contravention of the provision.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "The provisions of this Division that are civil penalty provisions\n\n(1) For the purposes of subparagraph 79(2)(a)(ii) of the Regulatory\nPowers Act, each of the following provisions of this Division (the\nprivacy safeguard penalty provisions) is a civil penalty provision:\n\n(a) subsection 56ED(3);\n\n(b) subsection 56EF(1);\n\n(c) subsection 56EG(1);\n\n(d) section 56EH;\n\n(e) subsection 56EI(1) or (2);\n\n(f) subsection 56EJ(1) or (2);\n\n(g) subsection 56EK(1);\n\n(h) subsection 56EL(1) or (2);\n\n(i) subsection 56EM(1), (2) or (4);\n\n(j) subsection 56EN(1), (2), (2A), (3) or (4);\n\n(k) subsection 56EO(1) or (2);\n\n(l) subsection 56EP(1) or (2).\nEnforceable civil penalty provisions\n\n(2) Each privacy safeguard penalty provision is enforceable under\nPart 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act.\nNote:\nPart 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act allows a civil penalty provision to\nbe enforced by obtaining an order for a person to pay a pecuniary\npenalty for the contravention of the provision.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56eu-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56eu-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "387300cb5b375686c7312e3c2f0c222a5780b5d9b1f9ee95b42fdea5c0b7d620"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56eu",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EU Civil penalty provisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 139,
      "values:originalText": "The provisions of this Division that are civil penalty provisions\n\n(1) For the purposes of subparagraph 79(2)(a)(ii) of the Regulatory\nPowers Act, each of the following provisions of this Division (the\nprivacy safeguard penalty provisions) is a civil penalty provision:\n\n(a) subsection 56ED(3);\n\n(b) subsection 56EF(1);\n\n(c) subsection 56EG(1);\n\n(d) section 56EH;\n\n(e) subsection 56EI(1) or (2);\n\n(f) subsection 56EJ(1) or (2);\n\n(g) subsection 56EK(1);\n\n(h) subsection 56EL(1) or (2);\n\n(i) subsection 56EM(1), (2) or (4);\n\n(j) subsection 56EN(1), (2), (2A), (3) or (4);\n\n(k) subsection 56EO(1) or (2);\n\n(l) subsection 56EP(1) or (2).\nEnforceable civil penalty provisions\n\n(2) Each privacy safeguard penalty provision is enforceable under\nPart 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act.\nNote:\nPart 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act allows a civil penalty provision to\nbe enforced by obtaining an order for a person to pay a pecuniary\npenalty for the contravention of the provision.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
