    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ev",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EV Civil penalty provisions—maximum amount of penalty",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ev"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.141",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Despite subsection 82(5) of the Regulatory Powers Act, the\npecuniary penalty payable:\n\n(a) by a person; and\n\n(b) under a civil penalty order under Part 4 of that Act (as that\nPart applies because of section 56EU of this Act);\nmust not be more than the maximum penalty amount worked out\nunder this section for a contravention by the person.\nMaximum amount of civil penalty for a body corporate\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the maximum penalty amount\nfor a contravention by a body corporate of a privacy safeguard\npenalty provision is the greater of the following:\n\n(a) $10,000,000;\n\n(b) if the relevant court (see subsection 56EU(4)) can determine\nthe value of the benefit that the body corporate, and any body\ncorporate related to the body corporate, have obtained\ndirectly or indirectly and that is reasonably attributable to the\ncontravention—3 times the value of that benefit;\n\n(c) if that court cannot determine the value of that benefit—10%\nof the adjusted turnover of the body corporate during the\n12-month period ending at the end of the month in which the\ncontravention happened or began.\nMaximum amount of civil penalty for other persons\n\n(4) For the purposes of subsection (1), the maximum penalty amount\nfor a contravention by a person other than a body corporate of a\nprivacy safeguard penalty provision is $500,000.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Despite subsection 82(5) of the Regulatory Powers Act, the\npecuniary penalty payable:\n\n(a) by a person; and\n\n(b) under a civil penalty order under Part 4 of that Act (as that\nPart applies because of section 56EU of this Act);\nmust not be more than the maximum penalty amount worked out\nunder this section for a contravention by the person.\nMaximum amount of civil penalty for a body corporate\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the maximum penalty amount\nfor a contravention by a body corporate of a privacy safeguard\npenalty provision is the greater of the following:\n\n(a) $10,000,000;\n\n(b) if the relevant court (see subsection 56EU(4)) can determine\nthe value of the benefit that the body corporate, and any body\ncorporate related to the body corporate, have obtained\ndirectly or indirectly and that is reasonably attributable to the\ncontravention—3 times the value of that benefit;\n\n(c) if that court cannot determine the value of that benefit—10%\nof the adjusted turnover of the body corporate during the\n12-month period ending at the end of the month in which the\ncontravention happened or began.\nMaximum amount of civil penalty for other persons\n\n(4) For the purposes of subsection (1), the maximum penalty amount\nfor a contravention by a person other than a body corporate of a\nprivacy safeguard penalty provision is $500,000.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ev-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ev-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ev-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2c1b660e47e5ed31120294bae22517b0523ab6598c67da18461ee8367721b895"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56ev",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EV Civil penalty provisions—maximum amount of penalty",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 141,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Despite subsection 82(5) of the Regulatory Powers Act, the\npecuniary penalty payable:\n\n(a) by a person; and\n\n(b) under a civil penalty order under Part 4 of that Act (as that\nPart applies because of section 56EU of this Act);\nmust not be more than the maximum penalty amount worked out\nunder this section for a contravention by the person.\nMaximum amount of civil penalty for a body corporate\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the maximum penalty amount\nfor a contravention by a body corporate of a privacy safeguard\npenalty provision is the greater of the following:\n\n(a) $10,000,000;\n\n(b) if the relevant court (see subsection 56EU(4)) can determine\nthe value of the benefit that the body corporate, and any body\ncorporate related to the body corporate, have obtained\ndirectly or indirectly and that is reasonably attributable to the\ncontravention—3 times the value of that benefit;\n\n(c) if that court cannot determine the value of that benefit—10%\nof the adjusted turnover of the body corporate during the\n12-month period ending at the end of the month in which the\ncontravention happened or began.\nMaximum amount of civil penalty for other persons\n\n(4) For the purposes of subsection (1), the maximum penalty amount\nfor a contravention by a person other than a body corporate of a\nprivacy safeguard penalty provision is $500,000.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
