    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56FA Making data standards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56fa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.147",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Data Standards Chair may, by writing, make one or more data\nstandards about each of the following matters:\n\n(a) the format and description of CDR data;\n\n(b) the disclosure of CDR data;\n\n(c) the collection, use, accuracy, storage, security and deletion of\nCDR data;\n\n(d) de-identifying CDR data, including so that it no longer\nrelates to:\n\n(i) an identifiable person; or\n\n(ii) a person who is reasonably identifiable;\n\n(da) the format and description of a valid instruction for the\nperformance of a type of CDR action;\n\n(db) the giving of a valid instruction for the performance of a type\nof CDR action;\n\n(e) other matters prescribed by the regulations.\nNote:\nFor variation and repeal, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nComplying with consumer data rules when making standards etc.\n\n(2) The Data Standards Chair must comply with the consumer data\nrules when:\n\n(a) making a data standard; or\n\n(b) varying or revoking a data standard;\nincluding complying with any related requirements specified in\nthose rules about approval, consultation and the formation of\ncommittees, advisory panels and consultative groups.\nNote:\nThe rules could, for example, require a proposed data standard to be\napproved by the Commission before it is made.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Data Standards Chair may, by writing, make one or more data\nstandards about each of the following matters:\n\n(a) the format and description of CDR data;\n\n(b) the disclosure of CDR data;\n\n(c) the collection, use, accuracy, storage, security and deletion of\nCDR data;\n\n(d) de-identifying CDR data, including so that it no longer\nrelates to:\n\n(i) an identifiable person; or\n\n(ii) a person who is reasonably identifiable;\n\n(da) the format and description of a valid instruction for the\nperformance of a type of CDR action;\n\n(db) the giving of a valid instruction for the performance of a type\nof CDR action;\n\n(e) other matters prescribed by the regulations.\nNote:\nFor variation and repeal, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nComplying with consumer data rules when making standards etc.\n\n(2) The Data Standards Chair must comply with the consumer data\nrules when:\n\n(a) making a data standard; or\n\n(b) varying or revoking a data standard;\nincluding complying with any related requirements specified in\nthose rules about approval, consultation and the formation of\ncommittees, advisory panels and consultative groups.\nNote:\nThe rules could, for example, require a proposed data standard to be\napproved by the Commission before it is made.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fa-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "77c7c820fc5a594e765f6b15dcd56adb873a58485193cf8c4c6f0b9f97b5c424"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56fa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56FA Making data standards",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 147,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Data Standards Chair may, by writing, make one or more data\nstandards about each of the following matters:\n\n(a) the format and description of CDR data;\n\n(b) the disclosure of CDR data;\n\n(c) the collection, use, accuracy, storage, security and deletion of\nCDR data;\n\n(d) de-identifying CDR data, including so that it no longer\nrelates to:\n\n(i) an identifiable person; or\n\n(ii) a person who is reasonably identifiable;\n\n(da) the format and description of a valid instruction for the\nperformance of a type of CDR action;\n\n(db) the giving of a valid instruction for the performance of a type\nof CDR action;\n\n(e) other matters prescribed by the regulations.\nNote:\nFor variation and repeal, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nComplying with consumer data rules when making standards etc.\n\n(2) The Data Standards Chair must comply with the consumer data\nrules when:\n\n(a) making a data standard; or\n\n(b) varying or revoking a data standard;\nincluding complying with any related requirements specified in\nthose rules about approval, consultation and the formation of\ncommittees, advisory panels and consultative groups.\nNote:\nThe rules could, for example, require a proposed data standard to be\napproved by the Commission before it is made.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
