    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fe",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56FE Enforcement of binding data standards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56fe"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.150",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a person who is under an obligation to comply with a binding\ndata standard fails to meet that obligation, an application to the\nCourt may be made by:\n\n(a) the Commission; or\n\n(b) a person aggrieved by the failure.\n\n(2) After giving an opportunity to be heard to the applicant and the\nperson against whom the order is sought, the Court may make an\norder giving directions to:\n\n(a) the person against whom the order is sought; or\n\n(b) if that person is a body corporate—the directors of the body\ncorporate;\nabout compliance with, or enforcement of, the binding data\nstandard.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (1), an obligation to comply with a\nbinding data standard includes an obligation arising under a\ncontract referred to in section 56FD.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nData standards etc.  Division 6\n\nSection 56FF\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSubdivision B—Data Standards Chair",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a person who is under an obligation to comply with a binding\ndata standard fails to meet that obligation, an application to the\nCourt may be made by:\n\n(a) the Commission; or\n\n(b) a person aggrieved by the failure.\n\n(2) After giving an opportunity to be heard to the applicant and the\nperson against whom the order is sought, the Court may make an\norder giving directions to:\n\n(a) the person against whom the order is sought; or\n\n(b) if that person is a body corporate—the directors of the body\ncorporate;\nabout compliance with, or enforcement of, the binding data\nstandard.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (1), an obligation to comply with a\nbinding data standard includes an obligation arising under a\ncontract referred to in section 56FD.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nData standards etc.  Division 6\n\nSection 56FF\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSubdivision B—Data Standards Chair",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fe-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fe-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fe-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "768fe4230cf3a42db1bea2066cbe730478db4c38a2d36754fe3addf9923f0ba2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56fe",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56FE Enforcement of binding data standards",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 150,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a person who is under an obligation to comply with a binding\ndata standard fails to meet that obligation, an application to the\nCourt may be made by:\n\n(a) the Commission; or\n\n(b) a person aggrieved by the failure.\n\n(2) After giving an opportunity to be heard to the applicant and the\nperson against whom the order is sought, the Court may make an\norder giving directions to:\n\n(a) the person against whom the order is sought; or\n\n(b) if that person is a body corporate—the directors of the body\ncorporate;\nabout compliance with, or enforcement of, the binding data\nstandard.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (1), an obligation to comply with a\nbinding data standard includes an obligation arising under a\ncontract referred to in section 56FD.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nData standards etc.  Division 6\n\nSection 56FF\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSubdivision B—Data Standards Chair"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fe-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56FE(1) Enforcement of binding data standards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
