    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fe-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56FE(2) Enforcement of binding data standards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56fe-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.150",
      "values:originalText": "(2) After giving an opportunity to be heard to the applicant and the\nperson against whom the order is sought, the Court may make an\norder giving directions to:\n\n(a) the person against whom the order is sought; or\n\n(b) if that person is a body corporate—the directors of the body\ncorporate;\nabout compliance with, or enforcement of, the binding data\nstandard.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) After giving an opportunity to be heard to the applicant and the\nperson against whom the order is sought, the Court may make an\norder giving directions to:\n\n(a) the person against whom the order is sought; or\n\n(b) if that person is a body corporate—the directors of the body\ncorporate;\nabout compliance with, or enforcement of, the binding data\nstandard.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fe"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fe-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fe-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "571c4a103a24c2b753836b9947e91b296fcfac62051d08e50925fc00d313fc8b",
      "skos:note": "Court may give directions to comply with binding data standard"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56fe-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56FE(2) Enforcement of binding data standards",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 150,
      "values:originalText": "(2) After giving an opportunity to be heard to the applicant and the\nperson against whom the order is sought, the Court may make an\norder giving directions to:\n\n(a) the person against whom the order is sought; or\n\n(b) if that person is a body corporate—the directors of the body\ncorporate;\nabout compliance with, or enforcement of, the binding data\nstandard."
    },
