    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fj",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56FJ Appointment of the Data Standards Body",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56fj"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.152",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint as the Data\nStandards Body:\n\n(a) the Department; or\n\n(b) another Commonwealth entity (within the meaning of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act\n2013).\nNote:\nFor variation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\n(2) The Minister may, at any time by written instrument, terminate an\nappointment made under subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint as the Data\nStandards Body:\n\n(a) the Department; or\n\n(b) another Commonwealth entity (within the meaning of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act\n2013).\nNote:\nFor variation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\n(2) The Minister may, at any time by written instrument, terminate an\nappointment made under subsection (1).",
