    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fk",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56FK Function and powers of the Data Standards Body",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56fk"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.152",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The function of the Data Standards Body is to assist the Data\nStandards Chair.\n\n(2) The Data Standards Body has the power to do all other things\nnecessary or convenient to be done for or in connection with the\nperformance of the Data Standards Body’s function.\n\n(3) The Data Standards Body must comply with the consumer data\nrules when assisting the Data Standards Chair, including\ncomplying with any requirements specified in those rules about:\n\n(a) the Body’s composition; or\n\n(b) the Body’s governance or processes.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nData standards etc.  Division 6\n\nSection 56FL\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(4) To avoid doubt, for a body that is the Data Standards Body, the\nbody’s functions and powers in its capacity other than as the Data\nStandards Body are taken to include the function and powers of the\nData Standards Body while it is the Data Standards Body.\nSubdivision D—Administrative provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The function of the Data Standards Body is to assist the Data\nStandards Chair.\n\n(2) The Data Standards Body has the power to do all other things\nnecessary or convenient to be done for or in connection with the\nperformance of the Data Standards Body’s function.\n\n(3) The Data Standards Body must comply with the consumer data\nrules when assisting the Data Standards Chair, including\ncomplying with any requirements specified in those rules about:\n\n(a) the Body’s composition; or\n\n(b) the Body’s governance or processes.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nData standards etc.  Division 6\n\nSection 56FL\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(4) To avoid doubt, for a body that is the Data Standards Body, the\nbody’s functions and powers in its capacity other than as the Data\nStandards Body are taken to include the function and powers of the\nData Standards Body while it is the Data Standards Body.\nSubdivision D—Administrative provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fk-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fk-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fk-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fk-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d7e143e1c6caf762139b323d3edcb37a3da7ad3c63d96d22aed7cc47c1c1005e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56fk",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56FK Function and powers of the Data Standards Body",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 152,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The function of the Data Standards Body is to assist the Data\nStandards Chair.\n\n(2) The Data Standards Body has the power to do all other things\nnecessary or convenient to be done for or in connection with the\nperformance of the Data Standards Body’s function.\n\n(3) The Data Standards Body must comply with the consumer data\nrules when assisting the Data Standards Chair, including\ncomplying with any requirements specified in those rules about:\n\n(a) the Body’s composition; or\n\n(b) the Body’s governance or processes.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nData standards etc.  Division 6\n\nSection 56FL\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(4) To avoid doubt, for a body that is the Data Standards Body, the\nbody’s functions and powers in its capacity other than as the Data\nStandards Body are taken to include the function and powers of the\nData Standards Body while it is the Data Standards Body.\nSubdivision D—Administrative provisions"
    },
