      "values:originalText": "The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint a person to act as\nthe Data Standards Chair:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of Data Standards Chair\n(whether or not an appointment has previously been made to\nthe office); or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Data\nStandards Chair:\n\n(i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or\n\n(ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the\noffice.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and\n33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint a person to act as\nthe Data Standards Chair:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of Data Standards Chair\n(whether or not an appointment has previously been made to\nthe office); or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Data\nStandards Chair:\n\n(i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or\n\n(ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the\noffice.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and\n33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fl-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fl-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "080ebc13785ecc1d8734b435e2005731cc8134630f917976228a440a415e2c54",
      "skos:note": "The Minister may appoint a person to act as Data Standards Chair."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56fl",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56FL Acting appointments",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 153,
      "values:originalText": "The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint a person to act as\nthe Data Standards Chair:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of Data Standards Chair\n(whether or not an appointment has previously been made to\nthe office); or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Data\nStandards Chair:\n\n(i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or\n\n(ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the\noffice.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and\n33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."
    },
