    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fn",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56FN Remuneration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56fn"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.153",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Data Standards Chair is to be paid the remuneration that is\ndetermined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If no determination of\nthat remuneration by the Tribunal is in operation, the Data\nStandards Chair is to be paid the remuneration that is prescribed by\nthe regulations.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Data Standards Chair is to be paid the remuneration that is\ndetermined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If no determination of\nthat remuneration by the Tribunal is in operation, the Data\nStandards Chair is to be paid the remuneration that is prescribed by\nthe regulations.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fn-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fn-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c81827d77f1520450adc2d8d9e058f5b955b1b27060cda44f0520293fcf42362",
      "skos:note": "Data Standards Chair must be paid remuneration determined by the Remuneration Tribunal or prescribed by regulations."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56fn",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56FN Remuneration",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 153,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Data Standards Chair is to be paid the remuneration that is\ndetermined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If no determination of\nthat remuneration by the Tribunal is in operation, the Data\nStandards Chair is to be paid the remuneration that is prescribed by\nthe regulations.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
