    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fs",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56FS Delegation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56fs"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.156",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Data Standards Chair may delegate, in writing, any or all of\nthe Chair’s functions or powers to:\n\n(a) an SES employee, or an acting SES employee, in the Data\nStandards Body, in the Department or in the Commission; or\n\n(b) an APS employee who is holding or performing the duties of\na specified office or position that:\n\n(i) is in the Data Standards Body, in the Department or in\nthe Commission; and\n\n(ii) is an office or position that the Chair is satisfied is\nsufficiently senior for the APS employee to perform the\nfunction or exercise the power; or\n\n(c) if there are no APS employees (including SES employees) in\nthe Data Standards Body—a person:\n\n(i) who holds an office or position in the Data Standards\nBody that the Chair considers is sufficiently senior for\nthe person to perform the function; and\n\n(ii) who the Chair considers has appropriate qualifications\nor expertise to perform the function.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the function referred to in\nparagraph 56FH(1)(a) (about making standards).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nData standards etc.  Division 6\n\nSection 56FS\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote:\nThis subsection does not prevent a person who is acting as the Data\nStandards Chair from making a standard.\n\n(3) In performing a delegated function or exercising a delegated\npower, the delegate under subsection (1) must comply with any\ndirections of the Data Standards Chair.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Data Standards Chair may delegate, in writing, any or all of\nthe Chair’s functions or powers to:\n\n(a) an SES employee, or an acting SES employee, in the Data\nStandards Body, in the Department or in the Commission; or\n\n(b) an APS employee who is holding or performing the duties of\na specified office or position that:\n\n(i) is in the Data Standards Body, in the Department or in\nthe Commission; and\n\n(ii) is an office or position that the Chair is satisfied is\nsufficiently senior for the APS employee to perform the\nfunction or exercise the power; or\n\n(c) if there are no APS employees (including SES employees) in\nthe Data Standards Body—a person:\n\n(i) who holds an office or position in the Data Standards\nBody that the Chair considers is sufficiently senior for\nthe person to perform the function; and\n\n(ii) who the Chair considers has appropriate qualifications\nor expertise to perform the function.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the function referred to in\nparagraph 56FH(1)(a) (about making standards).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nData standards etc.  Division 6\n\nSection 56FS\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote:\nThis subsection does not prevent a person who is acting as the Data\nStandards Chair from making a standard.\n\n(3) In performing a delegated function or exercising a delegated\npower, the delegate under subsection (1) must comply with any\ndirections of the Data Standards Chair.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fs-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fs-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56fs-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0b3041f2b326b181a57d51b925d78e5720ac719390e0d94f3447e64a06af1b94"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56fs",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56FS Delegation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 156,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Data Standards Chair may delegate, in writing, any or all of\nthe Chair’s functions or powers to:\n\n(a) an SES employee, or an acting SES employee, in the Data\nStandards Body, in the Department or in the Commission; or\n\n(b) an APS employee who is holding or performing the duties of\na specified office or position that:\n\n(i) is in the Data Standards Body, in the Department or in\nthe Commission; and\n\n(ii) is an office or position that the Chair is satisfied is\nsufficiently senior for the APS employee to perform the\nfunction or exercise the power; or\n\n(c) if there are no APS employees (including SES employees) in\nthe Data Standards Body—a person:\n\n(i) who holds an office or position in the Data Standards\nBody that the Chair considers is sufficiently senior for\nthe person to perform the function; and\n\n(ii) who the Chair considers has appropriate qualifications\nor expertise to perform the function.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the function referred to in\nparagraph 56FH(1)(a) (about making standards).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nConsumer data right  Part IVD\nData standards etc.  Division 6\n\nSection 56FS\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote:\nThis subsection does not prevent a person who is acting as the Data\nStandards Chair from making a standard.\n\n(3) In performing a delegated function or exercising a delegated\npower, the delegate under subsection (1) must comply with any\ndirections of the Data Standards Chair.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
