      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.158",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary of the Department may, in writing, delegate all or\nany of the Secretary’s functions or powers under this Part to an\nSES employee, or an acting SES employee, in the Department.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary of the Department may, in writing, delegate all or\nany of the Secretary’s functions or powers under this Part to an\nSES employee, or an acting SES employee, in the Department.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56ga"
