    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56gd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56GD Exemptions by the Commission",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56gd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.161",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The provisions covered by this section are:\n\n(a) the following provisions:\n\n(i) the provisions of this Part;\n\n(ii) the provisions of regulations made for the purposes of\nthe provisions of this Part;\n\n(iii) the provisions of the consumer data rules; and\n\n(b) definitions in this Act, or in the regulations or consumer data\nrules, as they apply to references in provisions referred to in\nparagraph (a).\n\n(2) The Commission may, by written notice given to a person, exempt\nthe person in relation to:\n\n(a) particular CDR data or one or more classes of CDR data; or\n\n(b) a particular CDR action or one or more types of CDR\nactions;\nfrom all or specified provisions covered by this section.\n\n(3) An exemption under subsection (2):\n\n(a) may or may not be limited to a specified period; and\n\n(b) may apply unconditionally or subject to specified conditions.\n\n(4) The Commission must publish on its website the details of each\nexemption under subsection (2).\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The provisions covered by this section are:\n\n(a) the following provisions:\n\n(i) the provisions of this Part;\n\n(ii) the provisions of regulations made for the purposes of\nthe provisions of this Part;\n\n(iii) the provisions of the consumer data rules; and\n\n(b) definitions in this Act, or in the regulations or consumer data\nrules, as they apply to references in provisions referred to in\nparagraph (a).\n\n(2) The Commission may, by written notice given to a person, exempt\nthe person in relation to:\n\n(a) particular CDR data or one or more classes of CDR data; or\n\n(b) a particular CDR action or one or more types of CDR\nactions;\nfrom all or specified provisions covered by this section.\n\n(3) An exemption under subsection (2):\n\n(a) may or may not be limited to a specified period; and\n\n(b) may apply unconditionally or subject to specified conditions.\n\n(4) The Commission must publish on its website the details of each\nexemption under subsection (2).\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56gd-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56gd-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56gd-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56gd-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "376ab41e7255efab8170e6c152ef6e5ba88b289db2d69a9869d025b49f68e43e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56gd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56GD Exemptions by the Commission",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 161,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The provisions covered by this section are:\n\n(a) the following provisions:\n\n(i) the provisions of this Part;\n\n(ii) the provisions of regulations made for the purposes of\nthe provisions of this Part;\n\n(iii) the provisions of the consumer data rules; and\n\n(b) definitions in this Act, or in the regulations or consumer data\nrules, as they apply to references in provisions referred to in\nparagraph (a).\n\n(2) The Commission may, by written notice given to a person, exempt\nthe person in relation to:\n\n(a) particular CDR data or one or more classes of CDR data; or\n\n(b) a particular CDR action or one or more types of CDR\nactions;\nfrom all or specified provisions covered by this section.\n\n(3) An exemption under subsection (2):\n\n(a) may or may not be limited to a specified period; and\n\n(b) may apply unconditionally or subject to specified conditions.\n\n(4) The Commission must publish on its website the details of each\nexemption under subsection (2).\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
