    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56gf-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to act or omit to act in a way that affects a corporation's activities.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) The CDR provisions apply to a person if:\n\n(a) the person is a corporation; or\n\n(b) the person is not a corporation, but the person:\n\n(i) acts; or\n\n(ii) omits to act;\n\nin a way that affects, is capable of affecting or is taken with intent to affect the activities, functions, relationships or business of a corporation.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(1) The CDR provisions apply to a person if:\n\n(a) the person is a corporation; or\n\n(b) the person is not a corporation, but the person:\n\n(i) acts; or\n\n(ii) omits to act;\n\nin a way that affects, is capable of affecting or is taken with intent to affect the activities, functions, relationships or business of a corporation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56gf-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56GF(2) Application of the CDR provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56gf-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.163",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The CDR provisions also apply to:\n\n(a) a person (whether or not a corporation) acting or omitting to\nact in the course of, or in relation to, the carrying on of:\n\n(i) a postal, telegraphic, telephonic or other like service\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(v) of the\nConstitution); or\n\n(ii) the business of banking, other than State banking\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(xiii) of the\nConstitution) not extending beyond the limits of the\nState concerned; or\n\n(iii) the business of insurance, other than State insurance\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(xiv) of the\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The CDR provisions also apply to:\n\n(a) a person (whether or not a corporation) acting or omitting to\nact in the course of, or in relation to, the carrying on of:\n\n(i) a postal, telegraphic, telephonic or other like service\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(v) of the\nConstitution); or\n\n(ii) the business of banking, other than State banking\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(xiii) of the\nConstitution) not extending beyond the limits of the\nState concerned; or\n\n(iii) the business of insurance, other than State insurance\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(xiv) of the\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56gf"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56gf-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56gf-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56gf-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "80ebe20a6192320673f0981d6f5fa832b455a4e12d5f0710fceb641de6b94e8b",
      "skos:note": "The CDR provisions apply to certain businesses and services."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56gf-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56GF(2) Application of the CDR provisions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 163,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The CDR provisions also apply to:\n\n(a) a person (whether or not a corporation) acting or omitting to\nact in the course of, or in relation to, the carrying on of:\n\n(i) a postal, telegraphic, telephonic or other like service\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(v) of the\nConstitution); or\n\n(ii) the business of banking, other than State banking\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(xiii) of the\nConstitution) not extending beyond the limits of the\nState concerned; or\n\n(iii) the business of insurance, other than State insurance\n(within the meaning of paragraph 51(xiv) of the\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
