    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56gg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56GG Compensation for acquisition of property",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56gg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.165",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the operation of the CDR provisions would\nresult in an acquisition of property (within the meaning of\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution) from a person otherwise\nthan on just terms (within the meaning of that paragraph).\n\n(2) The person who acquires the property is liable to pay a reasonable\namount of compensation to the first-mentioned person.\n\n(3) If the 2 persons do not agree on the amount of the compensation,\nthe person to whom compensation is payable may institute\nproceedings in:\n\n(a) the Federal Court; or\n\n(b) the Supreme Court of a State or Territory;\nfor the recovery from the other person of such reasonable amount\nof compensation as the Court determines.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if the operation of the CDR provisions would\nresult in an acquisition of property (within the meaning of\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution) from a person otherwise\nthan on just terms (within the meaning of that paragraph).\n\n(2) The person who acquires the property is liable to pay a reasonable\namount of compensation to the first-mentioned person.\n\n(3) If the 2 persons do not agree on the amount of the compensation,\nthe person to whom compensation is payable may institute\nproceedings in:\n\n(a) the Federal Court; or\n\n(b) the Supreme Court of a State or Territory;\nfor the recovery from the other person of such reasonable amount\nof compensation as the Court determines.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56gg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56gg-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-56gg-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d7e5ed326634b595e075b96da17e0c99f87d97cb84f4b6512b53561b514e4e45"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-56gg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56GG Compensation for acquisition of property",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 165,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the operation of the CDR provisions would\nresult in an acquisition of property (within the meaning of\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution) from a person otherwise\nthan on just terms (within the meaning of that paragraph).\n\n(2) The person who acquires the property is liable to pay a reasonable\namount of compensation to the first-mentioned person.\n\n(3) If the 2 persons do not agree on the amount of the compensation,\nthe person to whom compensation is payable may institute\nproceedings in:\n\n(a) the Federal Court; or\n\n(b) the Supreme Court of a State or Territory;\nfor the recovery from the other person of such reasonable amount\nof compensation as the Court determines."
    },
