      },
      "cml:premiseText": "A person carries on or actively seeks to carry on a business...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person has multiple characteristics of an Australian repairer"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57bb-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "has",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Business activities imply cognitive abilities",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "A person carries on or actively seeks to carry on a business...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person has the cognitive abilities required for an Australian repairer"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57bc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57BC Meaning of scheme RTO and RTO course",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57bc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.168",
      "values:originalText": "A scheme RTO is a registered training organisation that provides,\nor seeks to provide, a course (an RTO course) in Australia\nproviding training in diagnosing faults with, servicing, repairing,\nmodifying or dismantling scheme vehicles.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nKey concepts  Division 2\n\nSection 57BD\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote:\nRTO is short for registered training organisation.",
      "skos:definition": "A scheme RTO is a registered training organisation that provides,\nor seeks to provide, a course (an RTO course) in Australia\nproviding training in diagnosing faults with, servicing, repairing,\nmodifying or dismantling scheme vehicles.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nKey concepts  Division 2\n\nSection 57BD\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote:\nRTO is short for registered training organisation.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57bc-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "561c088f1e0160314ea8a6f2591d7afac53e57607596899f5eea0c678dabbdd7",
      "skos:note": "Defines what an RTO course is."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57bc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57BC Meaning of scheme RTO and RTO course",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 168,
      "values:originalText": "A scheme RTO is a registered training organisation that provides,\nor seeks to provide, a course (an RTO course) in Australia\nproviding training in diagnosing faults with, servicing, repairing,\nmodifying or dismantling scheme vehicles.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nKey concepts  Division 2\n\nSection 57BD\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote:\nRTO is short for registered training organisation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57bc-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57bc"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57bd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57BD Meaning of scheme information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57bd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.169",
      "values:originalText": "Main definition\n\n(1) Scheme information is information in relation to scheme vehicles\nprepared by or for manufacturers of scheme vehicles (or their\nrelated bodies corporate) for use in diagnosing faults with,\nservicing or repairing those vehicles, as supplied to the market.\nExceptions\n\n(2) However, scheme information does not include any of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) a trade secret;\n\n(b) the intellectual property of a person, other than intellectual\nproperty protected under the Copyright Act 1968;\n\n(c) a source code version of a program;\n\n(d) data automatically generated and transmitted by a scheme\nvehicle, while it is being driven, regarding driver or vehicle\nperformance;\n\n(e) global positioning system data;\n\n(f) information supplied, or to be supplied, only to a restricted\nnumber of Australian repairers for the purposes of\ndeveloping solutions to emerging or unexpected faults with a\nscheme vehicle;\n\n(g) information that is commercially sensitive about an\nagreement between a data provider and another person;\n\n(h) information relating to an automated driving system of a\nscheme vehicle;\n\n(i) any other information prescribed by the scheme rules.\nNote:\nScheme information may include safety and security information (see\nthe definition of safety and security information in section 57BF).\nHowever, for restrictions on the supply of safety and security\ninformation to Australian repairers and scheme RTOs: see\nsection 57DB.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "Main definition\n\n(1) Scheme information is information in relation to scheme vehicles\nprepared by or for manufacturers of scheme vehicles (or their\nrelated bodies corporate) for use in diagnosing faults with,\nservicing or repairing those vehicles, as supplied to the market.\nExceptions\n\n(2) However, scheme information does not include any of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) a trade secret;\n\n(b) the intellectual property of a person, other than intellectual\nproperty protected under the Copyright Act 1968;\n\n(c) a source code version of a program;\n\n(d) data automatically generated and transmitted by a scheme\nvehicle, while it is being driven, regarding driver or vehicle\nperformance;\n\n(e) global positioning system data;\n\n(f) information supplied, or to be supplied, only to a restricted\nnumber of Australian repairers for the purposes of\ndeveloping solutions to emerging or unexpected faults with a\nscheme vehicle;\n\n(g) information that is commercially sensitive about an\nagreement between a data provider and another person;\n\n(h) information relating to an automated driving system of a\nscheme vehicle;\n\n(i) any other information prescribed by the scheme rules.\nNote:\nScheme information may include safety and security information (see\nthe definition of safety and security information in section 57BF).\nHowever, for restrictions on the supply of safety and security\ninformation to Australian repairers and scheme RTOs: see\nsection 57DB.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57bd-ss-1"
        },
