      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5da4883049f8e271ec8ba4a0e1c32be4bd271c3051094d1f627ae98e0cfd2523",
      "skos:note": "Defines safety information for a scheme vehicle"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57bf-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57BF(2) Meaning of safety and security information",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 170,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Safety information, for a scheme vehicle, is information relating to\nany of the following systems installed in the vehicle, of a kind\nprescribed by the scheme rules:\n\n(a) the hydrogen system;\n\n(b) the high voltage system;\n\n(c) the hybrid system;\n\n(d) the electric propulsion system;\n\n(e) another system prescribed by the scheme rules for the\npurposes of this paragraph.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nKey concepts  Division 2\n\nSection 57BG\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
