    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57ca-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57CA(3) Scheme information—offer to supply to Australian repairers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57ca-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.172",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the form in which scheme information is supplied allows for\nvariability in the period for which the information is supplied, the\ndata provider must make the scheme offer on terms and conditions\nthat include provision for the supply of the scheme information:\n\n(a) for any period nominated by an Australian repairer or scheme\nRTO; or\n\n(b) by day, by month and by year.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nSupply of scheme information  Division 3\n\nSection 57CA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nCivil penalty:\n\n(a) for a body corporate—600 penalty units; and\n\n(b) for a person other than a body corporate—120 penalty units.\nScheme offer not to exceed fair market price",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If the form in which scheme information is supplied allows for\nvariability in the period for which the information is supplied, the\ndata provider must make the scheme offer on terms and conditions\nthat include provision for the supply of the scheme information:\n\n(a) for any period nominated by an Australian repairer or scheme\nRTO; or\n\n(b) by day, by month and by year.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nSupply of scheme information  Division 3\n\nSection 57CA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nCivil penalty:\n\n(a) for a body corporate—600 penalty units; and\n\n(b) for a person other than a body corporate—120 penalty units.\nScheme offer not to exceed fair market price",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57ca"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57ca-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57ca-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b6109ffbb6e39b3773c6510cbad048036a4da84f47a91ea7ce6cf6cb282a9747",
      "skos:note": "Scheme information must be supplied on terms and conditions that include provision for the supply of scheme information.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57ca-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57CA(3) Scheme information—offer to supply to Australian repairers",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 172,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the form in which scheme information is supplied allows for\nvariability in the period for which the information is supplied, the\ndata provider must make the scheme offer on terms and conditions\nthat include provision for the supply of the scheme information:\n\n(a) for any period nominated by an Australian repairer or scheme\nRTO; or\n\n(b) by day, by month and by year.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nSupply of scheme information  Division 3\n\nSection 57CA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nCivil penalty:\n\n(a) for a body corporate—600 penalty units; and\n\n(b) for a person other than a body corporate—120 penalty units.\nScheme offer not to exceed fair market price"
    },
