    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57CB Scheme information—supply on request by Australian",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57cb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.174",
      "values:originalText": "repairers or scheme RTOs\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nSupply of scheme information  Division 3\n\nSection 57CB\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) a data provider makes, or is required to make, a scheme offer\nto supply scheme information in relation to a particular make,\nmodel and year of scheme vehicle; and\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) an Australian repairer has a need to access the scheme\ninformation for that particular make, model and year of\nscheme vehicle in carrying on the Australian repairer’s\nbusiness; or\n\n(ii) a scheme RTO has a need to access the scheme\ninformation to provide an RTO course; and\n\n(c) the Australian repairer or scheme RTO requests, in writing,\nthe data provider to supply the scheme information about that\nparticular make, model and year of scheme vehicle; and\n\n(d) the Australian repairer or scheme RTO pays, or offers to pay,\nthe scheme price, or another agreed price, for the scheme\ninformation.\nNote:\nRestrictions apply in relation to the supply of scheme information that\nis safety and security information: see section 57DB.\nSupply of scheme information\n\n(2) The data provider must supply the scheme information to the\nAustralian repairer or scheme RTO:\n\n(a) in accordance with terms and conditions that comply with\nsection 57CC; and\n\n(b)  within the period covered by subsection (3).\nNote:\nA pecuniary penalty of up to $10,000,000 may be imposed for a\ncontravention of this subsection: see section 76.\n\n(3) For the purposes of subsection (2), the period covered by this\nsubsection:\n\n(a) starts when (at the payment or offer time) the Australian\nrepairer or scheme RTO pays, or offers to pay, the scheme\nprice, or another agreed price, for the scheme information;\nand\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "repairers or scheme RTOs\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nSupply of scheme information  Division 3\n\nSection 57CB\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) a data provider makes, or is required to make, a scheme offer\nto supply scheme information in relation to a particular make,\nmodel and year of scheme vehicle; and\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) an Australian repairer has a need to access the scheme\ninformation for that particular make, model and year of\nscheme vehicle in carrying on the Australian repairer’s\nbusiness; or\n\n(ii) a scheme RTO has a need to access the scheme\ninformation to provide an RTO course; and\n\n(c) the Australian repairer or scheme RTO requests, in writing,\nthe data provider to supply the scheme information about that\nparticular make, model and year of scheme vehicle; and\n\n(d) the Australian repairer or scheme RTO pays, or offers to pay,\nthe scheme price, or another agreed price, for the scheme\ninformation.\nNote:\nRestrictions apply in relation to the supply of scheme information that\nis safety and security information: see section 57DB.\nSupply of scheme information\n\n(2) The data provider must supply the scheme information to the\nAustralian repairer or scheme RTO:\n\n(a) in accordance with terms and conditions that comply with\nsection 57CC; and\n\n(b)  within the period covered by subsection (3).\nNote:\nA pecuniary penalty of up to $10,000,000 may be imposed for a\ncontravention of this subsection: see section 76.\n\n(3) For the purposes of subsection (2), the period covered by this\nsubsection:\n\n(a) starts when (at the payment or offer time) the Australian\nrepairer or scheme RTO pays, or offers to pay, the scheme\nprice, or another agreed price, for the scheme information;\nand\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cb-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cb-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ab7836a64cd786e0132dbb2166e58e9320e10181af86204a7cd35bf3d573ff65"
    },
