      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cb-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "during",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The period covered by this subsection starts when the Australian repairer or scheme RTO pays or offers to pay the scheme price.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(payment or offer time)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cb-ss-3-logic-argumentation-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "implies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "If the Australian repairer or scheme RTO pays or offers to pay the scheme price, then scheme information must be provided.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(payment or offer time)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cb-ss-3-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "diffuses",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The provision of scheme information upon payment or offer diffuses to the relevant parties.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(payment or offer time)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57CC Scheme information—terms and conditions of supply and use",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57cc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.177",
      "values:originalText": "Terms and conditions of supply generally\n\n(1) Subject to this section, nothing in this Part prevents a data provider\nfrom supplying scheme information under this Part subject to\nreasonable terms and conditions that do not prevent, restrict or\nlimit the access to, or use of, the information for the purposes of\ndiagnosing faults with, servicing, repairing, modifying or\ndismantling scheme vehicles.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "Terms and conditions of supply generally\n\n(1) Subject to this section, nothing in this Part prevents a data provider\nfrom supplying scheme information under this Part subject to\nreasonable terms and conditions that do not prevent, restrict or\nlimit the access to, or use of, the information for the purposes of\ndiagnosing faults with, servicing, repairing, modifying or\ndismantling scheme vehicles.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cc-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cc-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ff9dbc9a1b30f73e5659b3c49723ef0ce6e2910cc8ae4d789be2861c68e75ca4",
      "skos:note": "Terms and conditions of supply generally allow data providers to supply scheme information for diagnostic purposes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57cc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57CC Scheme information—terms and conditions of supply and use",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 177,
      "values:originalText": "Terms and conditions of supply generally\n\n(1) Subject to this section, nothing in this Part prevents a data provider\nfrom supplying scheme information under this Part subject to\nreasonable terms and conditions that do not prevent, restrict or\nlimit the access to, or use of, the information for the purposes of\ndiagnosing faults with, servicing, repairing, modifying or\ndismantling scheme vehicles.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cc-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cc"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cc-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Allow",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permits access to scheme information for diagnostic purposes.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57CD Scheme information—interaction of supply obligations and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57cd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.178",
      "values:originalText": "other rights and obligations\nData provider must comply with supply obligations despite\nexistence of other rights and obligations\n\n(1) A data provider must comply with an obligation under this Part in\nrelation to scheme information even if such compliance would\nconstitute or result in one or more of the following:\n\n(a) an infringement of copyright by the data provider or any\nother person;\n\n(b) a breach of contract in relation to the supply of the scheme\ninformation;\n\n(c) a breach of an equitable obligation of confidence to which\nthe data provider is subject in relation to the supply of the\nscheme information.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nSupply of scheme information  Division 3\n\nSection 57CD\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote 1:\nDivision 4 of Part IVA of the Copyright Act 1968 (which provides that\ncertain uses of material by educational institutions do not infringe\ncopyright) does not apply in relation to scheme information supplied\nunder this Part (see paragraph 113P(1)(b) of that Act).\nNote 2:\nA data provider is not criminally responsible for conduct that is\njustified or excused by or under this Part: see section 10.5 of the\nCriminal Code (lawful authority).\nCompensation for third party copyright holders\n\n(2) Subsection (3) applies if:\n\n(a) a data provider supplies scheme information to an Australian\nrepairer or scheme RTO under this Part; and\n\n(b) a person (the third party claimant) holds copyright in\nrelation to some or all of the scheme information that is the\nsubject of the supply; and\n\n(c) the supply constitutes or results in an infringement of the\ncopyright of the third party claimant; and\n\n(d) apart from this section, the infringement would constitute an\nacquisition of property otherwise than on just terms (within\nthe meaning of paragraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution).\n\n(3) The data provider must pay to the third party claimant an amount\nthat represents compensation on just terms (within the meaning of\nparagraph (xxxi) of the Constitution) for the supply of the scheme\ninformation to the Australian repairer or scheme RTO.\n\n(4) An amount payable by the data provider under subsection (3):\n\n(a) is a debt due by the data provider to the third party claimant;\nand\n\n(b) may be recovered by action in a court of competent\njurisdiction.\n\n(5) In a civil action by a third party claimant against a data provider\nfor infringement of copyright in relation to scheme information\nsupplied, or offered for supply, under this Part, it is a defence if the\ndata provider proves that:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "other rights and obligations\nData provider must comply with supply obligations despite\nexistence of other rights and obligations\n\n(1) A data provider must comply with an obligation under this Part in\nrelation to scheme information even if such compliance would\nconstitute or result in one or more of the following:\n\n(a) an infringement of copyright by the data provider or any\nother person;\n\n(b) a breach of contract in relation to the supply of the scheme\ninformation;\n\n(c) a breach of an equitable obligation of confidence to which\nthe data provider is subject in relation to the supply of the\nscheme information.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nSupply of scheme information  Division 3\n\nSection 57CD\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote 1:\nDivision 4 of Part IVA of the Copyright Act 1968 (which provides that\ncertain uses of material by educational institutions do not infringe\ncopyright) does not apply in relation to scheme information supplied\nunder this Part (see paragraph 113P(1)(b) of that Act).\nNote 2:\nA data provider is not criminally responsible for conduct that is\njustified or excused by or under this Part: see section 10.5 of the\nCriminal Code (lawful authority).\nCompensation for third party copyright holders\n\n(2) Subsection (3) applies if:\n\n(a) a data provider supplies scheme information to an Australian\nrepairer or scheme RTO under this Part; and\n\n(b) a person (the third party claimant) holds copyright in\nrelation to some or all of the scheme information that is the\nsubject of the supply; and\n\n(c) the supply constitutes or results in an infringement of the\ncopyright of the third party claimant; and\n\n(d) apart from this section, the infringement would constitute an\nacquisition of property otherwise than on just terms (within\nthe meaning of paragraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution).\n\n(3) The data provider must pay t",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cd-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cd-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cd-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cd-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57cd-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0347c18eb0c867b242430cb02fd2b19a3eb2515e096e4948decad1a948b166fd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57cd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57CD Scheme information—interaction of supply obligations and",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 178,
      "values:originalText": "other rights and obligations\nData provider must comply with supply obligations despite\nexistence of other rights and obligations\n\n(1) A data provider must comply with an obligation under this Part in\nrelation to scheme information even if such compliance would\nconstitute or result in one or more of the following:\n\n(a) an infringement of copyright by the data provider or any\nother person;\n\n(b) a breach of contract in relation to the supply of the scheme\ninformation;\n\n(c) a breach of an equitable obligation of confidence to which\nthe data provider is subject in relation to the supply of the\nscheme information.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nSupply of scheme information  Division 3\n\nSection 57CD\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote 1:\nDivision 4 of Part IVA of the Copyright Act 1968 (which provides that\ncertain uses of material by educational institutions do not infringe\ncopyright) does not apply in relation to scheme information supplied\nunder this Part (see paragraph 113P(1)(b) of that Act).\nNote 2:\nA data provider is not criminally responsible for conduct that is\njustified or excused by or under this Part: see section 10.5 of the\nCriminal Code (lawful authority).\nCompensation for third party copyright holders\n\n(2) Subsection (3) applies if:\n\n(a) a data provider supplies scheme information to an Australian\nrepairer or scheme RTO under this Part; and\n\n(b) a person (the third party claimant) holds copyright in\nrelation to some or all of the scheme information that is the\nsubject of the supply; and\n\n(c) the supply constitutes or results in an infringement of the\ncopyright of the third party claimant; and\n\n(d) apart from this section, the infringement would constitute an\nacquisition of property otherwise than on just terms (within\nthe meaning of paragraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution).\n\n(3) The data provider must pay to the third party claimant an amount\nthat represents compensation on just terms (within the meaning of\nparagraph (xxxi) of the Constitution) for the supply of the scheme\ninformation to the Australian repairer or scheme RTO.\n\n(4) An amount payable by the data provider under subsection (3):\n\n(a) is a debt due by the data provider to the third party claimant;\nand\n\n(b) may be recovered by action in a court of competent\njurisdiction.\n\n(5) In a civil action by a third party claimant against a data provider\nfor infringement of copyright in relation to scheme information\nsupplied, or offered for supply, under this Part, it is a defence if the\ndata provider proves that:\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
