    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57da",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57DA Safety and security information—packaging",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57da"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.181",
      "values:originalText": "A data provider must, in a scheme offer, separate safety and\nsecurity information from other scheme information to the extent it\nis reasonably practicable to do so.\nCivil penalty:\n\n(a) for a body corporate—600 penalty units; and\n\n(b) for a person other than a body corporate—120 penalty units.",
      "skos:definition": "A data provider must, in a scheme offer, separate safety and\nsecurity information from other scheme information to the extent it\nis reasonably practicable to do so.\nCivil penalty:\n\n(a) for a body corporate—600 penalty units; and\n\n(b) for a person other than a body corporate—120 penalty units.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57da-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57da-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aa8dd1a6f34cb3f344b8ed9b1644479d58512001f7bc4a6a686312826556b8d8",
      "skos:note": "Separate safety and security information from other scheme information.",
      "dc:description": "yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57da",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57DA Safety and security information—packaging",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 181,
      "values:originalText": "A data provider must, in a scheme offer, separate safety and\nsecurity information from other scheme information to the extent it\nis reasonably practicable to do so.\nCivil penalty:\n\n(a) for a body corporate—600 penalty units; and\n\n(b) for a person other than a body corporate—120 penalty units."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57da-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57da"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57da-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide separate safety and security information.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57db",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57DB Safety and security information—supply to Australian",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57db"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.181",
      "values:originalText": "repairers and scheme RTOs\nSupply of safety and security information—restrictions on supply\n\n(1) A data provider must not supply scheme information under this\nPart that is, or includes, safety and security information for a\nscheme vehicle of a particular make, model and year unless:\n\n(a) there are reasonable grounds, based on information provided\nby the Australian repairer or scheme RTO, to believe that the\nrequirements covered by subsection (2) are satisfied in\nrelation to the scheme information for that vehicle; and\n\n(b) the Australian repairer or scheme RTO has provided the\nrequired declaration, or declarations, covered by\nsubsection (3) in relation to that vehicle.\nCivil penalty:\n\n(a) for a body corporate—600 penalty units; and\n\n(b) for a person other than a body corporate—120 penalty units.\n\n(2) The requirements covered by this subsection are that:\n\n(a) the safety and security information is solely for use by an\nindividual or individuals:\n\n(i) in the case of an Australian repairer—for the purposes\nof the Australian repairer’s business; or\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "repairers and scheme RTOs\nSupply of safety and security information—restrictions on supply\n\n(1) A data provider must not supply scheme information under this\nPart that is, or includes, safety and security information for a\nscheme vehicle of a particular make, model and year unless:\n\n(a) there are reasonable grounds, based on information provided\nby the Australian repairer or scheme RTO, to believe that the\nrequirements covered by subsection (2) are satisfied in\nrelation to the scheme information for that vehicle; and\n\n(b) the Australian repairer or scheme RTO has provided the\nrequired declaration, or declarations, covered by\nsubsection (3) in relation to that vehicle.\nCivil penalty:\n\n(a) for a body corporate—600 penalty units; and\n\n(b) for a person other than a body corporate—120 penalty units.\n\n(2) The requirements covered by this subsection are that:\n\n(a) the safety and security information is solely for use by an\nindividual or individuals:\n\n(i) in the case of an Australian repairer—for the purposes\nof the Australian repairer’s business; or\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57db-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57db-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "138fa04f22740812fcc807fc626aabb9b161ef7812a4fcaf5d402a9576de89ca"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57db",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57DB Safety and security information—supply to Australian",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 181,
      "values:originalText": "repairers and scheme RTOs\nSupply of safety and security information—restrictions on supply\n\n(1) A data provider must not supply scheme information under this\nPart that is, or includes, safety and security information for a\nscheme vehicle of a particular make, model and year unless:\n\n(a) there are reasonable grounds, based on information provided\nby the Australian repairer or scheme RTO, to believe that the\nrequirements covered by subsection (2) are satisfied in\nrelation to the scheme information for that vehicle; and\n\n(b) the Australian repairer or scheme RTO has provided the\nrequired declaration, or declarations, covered by\nsubsection (3) in relation to that vehicle.\nCivil penalty:\n\n(a) for a body corporate—600 penalty units; and\n\n(b) for a person other than a body corporate—120 penalty units.\n\n(2) The requirements covered by this subsection are that:\n\n(a) the safety and security information is solely for use by an\nindividual or individuals:\n\n(i) in the case of an Australian repairer—for the purposes\nof the Australian repairer’s business; or\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
