      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "held by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57ed",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57ED Attempt to resolve dispute before mediation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57ed"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.186",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the initiating party wishes to initiate action to resolve the dispute\nin accordance with this Division, the initiating party must give\nwritten notice to the responding party of the following:\n\n(a) the nature of the dispute;\n\n(b) the matter that is the subject of the dispute;\n\n(c) the way in which that matter relates to the application of this\nPart;\n\n(d) what outcome the initiating party wants;\n\n(e) what action the initiating party thinks will resolve the\ndispute.\n\n(2) The parties must then try to resolve the dispute.\nNote:\nFor when a party is taken to have tried to resolve a dispute, see\nsection 57EE.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nDispute resolution  Division 5\n\nSection 57EE\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) If the parties cannot agree how to resolve the dispute within 2\nbusiness days, either party may refer the matter to a mediator for\nmediation under this Division.\n\n(4) If the parties cannot agree on who should be the mediator, either\nparty may request the scheme adviser to nominate a mediator.\n\n(5) Within 2 business days after a request is made under\nsubsection (4), the scheme adviser must nominate a mediator for\nthe dispute.\n57EE  When is a party taken to have tried to resolve a dispute?\n\nFor the purposes of this Division, a party is taken to have tried to\nresolve a dispute if the party approaches the resolution of the\ndispute in a reconciliatory manner, including by doing any of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) attending and participating in meetings at reasonable times;\n\n(b) responding to communications to the party within a\nreasonable time;\n\n(c) if the party has agreed to use a technical expert in resolving\nthe dispute—considering the opinions of the technical expert;\n\n(d) if a mediation process is being used to try to resolve the\ndispute—both:\n\n(i) making the party’s intention clear, at the beginning of\nthe process, as to what the party is trying to achieve\nthrough the process; and\n\n(ii) observing any obligations relating to confidentiality that\napply during or after the process.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the initiating party wishes to initiate action to resolve the dispute\nin accordance with this Division, the initiating party must give\nwritten notice to the responding party of the following:\n\n(a) the nature of the dispute;\n\n(b) the matter that is the subject of the dispute;\n\n(c) the way in which that matter relates to the application of this\nPart;\n\n(d) what outcome the initiating party wants;\n\n(e) what action the initiating party thinks will resolve the\ndispute.\n\n(2) The parties must then try to resolve the dispute.\nNote:\nFor when a party is taken to have tried to resolve a dispute, see\nsection 57EE.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nDispute resolution  Division 5\n\nSection 57EE\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) If the parties cannot agree how to resolve the dispute within 2\nbusiness days, either party may refer the matter to a mediator for\nmediation under this Division.\n\n(4) If the parties cannot agree on who should be the mediator, either\nparty may request the scheme adviser to nominate a mediator.\n\n(5) Within 2 business days after a request is made under\nsubsection (4), the scheme adviser must nominate a mediator for\nthe dispute.\n57EE  When is a party taken to have tried to resolve a dispute?\n\nFor the purposes of this Division, a party is taken to have tried to\nresolve a dispute if the party approaches the resolution of the\ndispute in a reconciliatory manner, including by doing any of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) attending and participating in meetings at reasonable times;\n\n(b) responding to communications to the party within a\nreasonable time;\n\n(c) if the party has agreed to use a technical expert in resolving\nthe dispute—considering the opinions of the technical expert;\n\n(d) if a mediation process is being used to try to resolve the\ndispute—both:\n\n(i) making the party’s intention clear, at the beginning of\nthe p",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57ed-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57ed-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57ed-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57ed-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57ed-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2f84582679e0ee7db22c2b2657d7a433c19023e26208e0e36cecab0b38971943"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57ed",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57ED Attempt to resolve dispute before mediation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 186,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the initiating party wishes to initiate action to resolve the dispute\nin accordance with this Division, the initiating party must give\nwritten notice to the responding party of the following:\n\n(a) the nature of the dispute;\n\n(b) the matter that is the subject of the dispute;\n\n(c) the way in which that matter relates to the application of this\nPart;\n\n(d) what outcome the initiating party wants;\n\n(e) what action the initiating party thinks will resolve the\ndispute.\n\n(2) The parties must then try to resolve the dispute.\nNote:\nFor when a party is taken to have tried to resolve a dispute, see\nsection 57EE.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nDispute resolution  Division 5\n\nSection 57EE\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) If the parties cannot agree how to resolve the dispute within 2\nbusiness days, either party may refer the matter to a mediator for\nmediation under this Division.\n\n(4) If the parties cannot agree on who should be the mediator, either\nparty may request the scheme adviser to nominate a mediator.\n\n(5) Within 2 business days after a request is made under\nsubsection (4), the scheme adviser must nominate a mediator for\nthe dispute.\n57EE  When is a party taken to have tried to resolve a dispute?\n\nFor the purposes of this Division, a party is taken to have tried to\nresolve a dispute if the party approaches the resolution of the\ndispute in a reconciliatory manner, including by doing any of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) attending and participating in meetings at reasonable times;\n\n(b) responding to communications to the party within a\nreasonable time;\n\n(c) if the party has agreed to use a technical expert in resolving\nthe dispute—considering the opinions of the technical expert;\n\n(d) if a mediation process is being used to try to resolve the\ndispute—both:\n\n(i) making the party’s intention clear, at the beginning of\nthe process, as to what the party is trying to achieve\nthrough the process; and\n\n(ii) observing any obligations relating to confidentiality that\napply during or after the process."
    },
    {
