    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57ed-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57ED(5) Attempt to resolve dispute before mediation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57ed-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.186",
      "values:originalText": "(5) Within 2 business days after a request is made under\nsubsection (4), the scheme adviser must nominate a mediator for\nthe dispute.\n57EE  When is a party taken to have tried to resolve a dispute?\n\nFor the purposes of this Division, a party is taken to have tried to\nresolve a dispute if the party approaches the resolution of the\ndispute in a reconciliatory manner, including by doing any of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) attending and participating in meetings at reasonable times;\n\n(b) responding to communications to the party within a\nreasonable time;\n\n(c) if the party has agreed to use a technical expert in resolving\nthe dispute—considering the opinions of the technical expert;\n\n(d) if a mediation process is being used to try to resolve the\ndispute—both:\n\n(i) making the party’s intention clear, at the beginning of\nthe process, as to what the party is trying to achieve\nthrough the process; and\n\n(ii) observing any obligations relating to confidentiality that\napply during or after the process.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) Within 2 business days after a request is made under\nsubsection (4), the scheme adviser must nominate a mediator for\nthe dispute.\n57EE  When is a party taken to have tried to resolve a dispute?\n\nFor the purposes of this Division, a party is taken to have tried to\nresolve a dispute if the party approaches the resolution of the\ndispute in a reconciliatory manner, including by doing any of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) attending and participating in meetings at reasonable times;\n\n(b) responding to communications to the party within a\nreasonable time;\n\n(c) if the party has agreed to use a technical expert in resolving\nthe dispute—considering the opinions of the technical expert;\n\n(d) if a mediation process is being used to try to resolve the\ndispute—both:\n\n(i) making the party’s intention clear, at the beginning of\nthe process, as to what the party is trying to achieve\nthrough the process; and\n\n(ii) observing any obligations relating to confidentiality that\napply during or after the process.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57ed"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57ed-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57ed-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f61c6c3a504521664c3d93d45ccae6aa9f1ba453c26b13dadac9f38cc75f45be",
      "skos:note": "Party must nominate a mediator for the dispute within 2 business days after a request is made under subsection (4).",
      "dc:description": "Mediator nomination"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57ed-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57ED(5) Attempt to resolve dispute before mediation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 186,
      "values:originalText": "(5) Within 2 business days after a request is made under\nsubsection (4), the scheme adviser must nominate a mediator for\nthe dispute.\n57EE  When is a party taken to have tried to resolve a dispute?\n\nFor the purposes of this Division, a party is taken to have tried to\nresolve a dispute if the party approaches the resolution of the\ndispute in a reconciliatory manner, including by doing any of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) attending and participating in meetings at reasonable times;\n\n(b) responding to communications to the party within a\nreasonable time;\n\n(c) if the party has agreed to use a technical expert in resolving\nthe dispute—considering the opinions of the technical expert;\n\n(d) if a mediation process is being used to try to resolve the\ndispute—both:\n\n(i) making the party’s intention clear, at the beginning of\nthe process, as to what the party is trying to achieve\nthrough the process; and\n\n(ii) observing any obligations relating to confidentiality that\napply during or after the process."
    },
    {
