    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57eg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57EG Termination of mediation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57eg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.188",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to the mediation of a dispute if the dispute has\nnot been resolved within 30 days after the day the mediation starts.\n\n(2) The mediator may terminate the mediation at any time unless\nsatisfied that a resolution of the dispute is imminent.\n\n(3) However, if either party asks the mediator to terminate the\nmediation, the mediator must do so.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nDispute resolution  Division 5\n\nSection 57EH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(4) If the mediator terminates the mediation of a dispute under this\nsection, the mediator must issue a certificate stating the following:\n\n(a) the names of the parties;\n\n(b) the nature of the dispute;\n\n(c) whether the parties attended the mediation;\n\n(d) that the mediation has finished;\n\n(e) that the dispute has not been resolved.\n\n(5) The mediator must give a copy of the certificate to:\n\n(a) the scheme adviser; and\n\n(b) each of the parties to the dispute.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to the mediation of a dispute if the dispute has\nnot been resolved within 30 days after the day the mediation starts.\n\n(2) The mediator may terminate the mediation at any time unless\nsatisfied that a resolution of the dispute is imminent.\n\n(3) However, if either party asks the mediator to terminate the\nmediation, the mediator must do so.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nDispute resolution  Division 5\n\nSection 57EH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(4) If the mediator terminates the mediation of a dispute under this\nsection, the mediator must issue a certificate stating the following:\n\n(a) the names of the parties;\n\n(b) the nature of the dispute;\n\n(c) whether the parties attended the mediation;\n\n(d) that the mediation has finished;\n\n(e) that the dispute has not been resolved.\n\n(5) The mediator must give a copy of the certificate to:\n\n(a) the scheme adviser; and\n\n(b) each of the parties to the dispute.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57eg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57eg-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57eg-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57eg-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57eg-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f72a3d497a0605582d995171794352fa7a3d7e1625efb119c583b3c099c80bdf"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57eg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57EG Termination of mediation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 188,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to the mediation of a dispute if the dispute has\nnot been resolved within 30 days after the day the mediation starts.\n\n(2) The mediator may terminate the mediation at any time unless\nsatisfied that a resolution of the dispute is imminent.\n\n(3) However, if either party asks the mediator to terminate the\nmediation, the mediator must do so.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nMotor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Part IVE\nDispute resolution  Division 5\n\nSection 57EH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(4) If the mediator terminates the mediation of a dispute under this\nsection, the mediator must issue a certificate stating the following:\n\n(a) the names of the parties;\n\n(b) the nature of the dispute;\n\n(c) whether the parties attended the mediation;\n\n(d) that the mediation has finished;\n\n(e) that the dispute has not been resolved.\n\n(5) The mediator must give a copy of the certificate to:\n\n(a) the scheme adviser; and\n\n(b) each of the parties to the dispute."
    },
