    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57ge",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57GE Scheme rules",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57ge"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.195",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules\nprescribing matters:\n\n(a) required or permitted by this Part to be prescribed by the\nrules; or\n\n(b) necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or\ngiving effect to this Part.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, the rules may not do the following:\n\n(a) create an offence or civil penalty;\n\n(b) provide powers of:\n\n(i) arrest or detention; or\n\n(ii) entry, search or seizure;\n\n(c) impose a tax;\n\n(d) set an amount to be appropriated from the Consolidated\nRevenue Fund under an appropriation in this Act;\n\n(e) directly amend the text of this Act;\n\n(f) subject to section 57DB, authorise or require the disclosure\nof sensitive information.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules\nprescribing matters:\n\n(a) required or permitted by this Part to be prescribed by the\nrules; or\n\n(b) necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or\ngiving effect to this Part.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, the rules may not do the following:\n\n(a) create an offence or civil penalty;\n\n(b) provide powers of:\n\n(i) arrest or detention; or\n\n(ii) entry, search or seizure;\n\n(c) impose a tax;\n\n(d) set an amount to be appropriated from the Consolidated\nRevenue Fund under an appropriation in this Act;\n\n(e) directly amend the text of this Act;\n\n(f) subject to section 57DB, authorise or require the disclosure\nof sensitive information.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57ge-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-57ge-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c5b70e1d13ed3fe689c2c1112a963f9b9ef34a388872048e03937b42165e973d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-57ge",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57GE Scheme rules",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 195,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules\nprescribing matters:\n\n(a) required or permitted by this Part to be prescribed by the\nrules; or\n\n(b) necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or\ngiving effect to this Part.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, the rules may not do the following:\n\n(a) create an offence or civil penalty;\n\n(b) provide powers of:\n\n(i) arrest or detention; or\n\n(ii) entry, search or seizure;\n\n(c) impose a tax;\n\n(d) set an amount to be appropriated from the Consolidated\nRevenue Fund under an appropriation in this Act;\n\n(e) directly amend the text of this Act;\n\n(f) subject to section 57DB, authorise or require the disclosure\nof sensitive information.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
