      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ac",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58AC Regulated sectors subject to the Scams Prevention Framework",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ac"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.197",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, designate one or more\nbusinesses or services to be a regulated sector of the Australian\neconomy.\nNote 1:\nAn individual business or service could be designated, or businesses\nor services could be designated by class (see subsection 13(3) of the\nLegislation Act 2003).\nNote 2:\nFor variation and repeal, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, designate one or more\nbusinesses or services to be a regulated sector of the Australian\neconomy.\nNote 1:\nAn individual business or service could be designated, or businesses\nor services could be designated by class (see subsection 13(3) of the\nLegislation Act 2003).\nNote 2:\nFor variation and repeal, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ac-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fa0b1b0b11e5508f832ab9ebd5de395b2e41692dd47507807cb02e4b8c49c740",
      "skos:note": "Designation of regulated sectors by the Minister."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ac",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58AC Regulated sectors subject to the Scams Prevention Framework",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 197,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, designate one or more\nbusinesses or services to be a regulated sector of the Australian\neconomy.\nNote 1:\nAn individual business or service could be designated, or businesses\nor services could be designated by class (see subsection 13(3) of the\nLegislation Act 2003).\nNote 2:\nFor variation and repeal, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ac-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
