    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ad",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58AD Regulated entities for regulated sectors and their regulated",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ad"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.198",
      "values:originalText": "services\nEntities with businesses or services within the banking, insurance\nor communications constitutional powers\n\n(1) To the extent that a regulated sector includes a business or service\ncovered by paragraph 58AC(2)(a), (b) or (c):\n\n(a) the person who carries on or provides that business or service\nis a regulated entity for the sector; and\n\n(b) that business or service is a regulated service of the regulated\nentity for the sector.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection extends to a regulated sector consisting of businesses\nor services that are a subset of paragraph 58AC(2)(a), (b) or (c).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 58AD\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote 2:\nSections 58GA to 58GC extend the meaning of person for\npartnerships, unincorporated associations and trusts.\nOther entities who may be regulated entities\n\n(2) Otherwise:\n\n(a) the regulated entities for a regulated sector; and\n\n(b) the regulated services of each of those regulated entities;\nare as set out in the following table:\n\nOther regulated entities, and their regulated services, for the regulated sector\nItem\nThis person is a regulated entity:\nfor this regulated service:\na corporation that carries on or\nprovides a business or service that is\npart of the regulated sector\nthat business or service.\na person to the extent that the person\nis both:\n(a) carrying on or providing a\nbusiness or service that is part of\nthe regulated sector; and\n(b) acting using a postal, telegraphic,\ntelephonic or other like service\n(within the meaning of\nparagraph 51(v) of the\nConstitution)\nso much of that business or service\nas relates to the person acting in that\nway.\na person to the extent that the person\nis both:\n(a) carrying on or providing a\nbusiness or service that is part of\nthe regulated sector; and\n(b) acting in the course of, or in\nrelation to, a kind of trade or\ncommerce mentioned in\nsubsection (3)\nso much of that business or service\nas relates to the person acting in that\nway.\nNote 1:\nFor the meaning of corporation, see section 4.\nNote 2:\nSections 58GA to 58GC extend the meaning of person for\npartnerships, unincorporated associations and trusts.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "services\nEntities with businesses or services within the banking, insurance\nor communications constitutional powers\n\n(1) To the extent that a regulated sector includes a business or service\ncovered by paragraph 58AC(2)(a), (b) or (c):\n\n(a) the person who carries on or provides that business or service\nis a regulated entity for the sector; and\n\n(b) that business or service is a regulated service of the regulated\nentity for the sector.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection extends to a regulated sector consisting of businesses\nor services that are a subset of paragraph 58AC(2)(a), (b) or (c).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 58AD\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote 2:\nSections 58GA to 58GC extend the meaning of person for\npartnerships, unincorporated associations and trusts.\nOther entities who may be regulated entities\n\n(2) Otherwise:\n\n(a) the regulated entities for a regulated sector; and\n\n(b) the regulated services of each of those regulated entities;\nare as set out in the following table:\n\nOther regulated entities, and their regulated services, for the regulated sector\nItem\nThis person is a regulated entity:\nfor this regulated service:\na corporation that carries on or\nprovides a business or service that is\npart of the regulated sector\nthat business or service.\na person to the extent that the person\nis both:\n(a) carrying on or providing a\nbusiness or service that is part of\nthe regulated sector; and\n(b) acting using a postal, telegraphic,\ntelephonic or other like service\n(within the meaning of\nparagraph 51(v) of the\nConstitution)\nso much of that business or service\nas relates to the person acting in that\nway.\na person to the extent that the person\nis both:\n(a) carrying on or providing a\nbusiness or service that is part of\nthe regulated sector; and\n(b) acting in the course of, or in\nrelation to, a kind of trade or\ncommerce mentio",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ad-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ad-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8208c96d5ab2edc904e350e11d6a6ab0e3c565c0b638f4305e8c6d1c0d098211"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ad",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58AD Regulated entities for regulated sectors and their regulated",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 198,
      "values:originalText": "services\nEntities with businesses or services within the banking, insurance\nor communications constitutional powers\n\n(1) To the extent that a regulated sector includes a business or service\ncovered by paragraph 58AC(2)(a), (b) or (c):\n\n(a) the person who carries on or provides that business or service\nis a regulated entity for the sector; and\n\n(b) that business or service is a regulated service of the regulated\nentity for the sector.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection extends to a regulated sector consisting of businesses\nor services that are a subset of paragraph 58AC(2)(a), (b) or (c).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 58AD\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote 2:\nSections 58GA to 58GC extend the meaning of person for\npartnerships, unincorporated associations and trusts.\nOther entities who may be regulated entities\n\n(2) Otherwise:\n\n(a) the regulated entities for a regulated sector; and\n\n(b) the regulated services of each of those regulated entities;\nare as set out in the following table:\n\nOther regulated entities, and their regulated services, for the regulated sector\nItem\nThis person is a regulated entity:\nfor this regulated service:\na corporation that carries on or\nprovides a business or service that is\npart of the regulated sector\nthat business or service.\na person to the extent that the person\nis both:\n(a) carrying on or providing a\nbusiness or service that is part of\nthe regulated sector; and\n(b) acting using a postal, telegraphic,\ntelephonic or other like service\n(within the meaning of\nparagraph 51(v) of the\nConstitution)\nso much of that business or service\nas relates to the person acting in that\nway.\na person to the extent that the person\nis both:\n(a) carrying on or providing a\nbusiness or service that is part of\nthe regulated sector; and\n(b) acting in the course of, or in\nrelation to, a kind of trade or\ncommerce mentioned in\nsubsection (3)\nso much of that business or service\nas relates to the person acting in that\nway.\nNote 1:\nFor the meaning of corporation, see section 4.\nNote 2:\nSections 58GA to 58GC extend the meaning of person for\npartnerships, unincorporated associations and trusts.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
