    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ae",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58AE Minister must consider matters, and consult, before",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ae"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.201",
      "values:originalText": "designating a sector\n\n(1) Before making an instrument under subsection 58AC(1) about a\nsector of the economy, the Minister must:\n\n(a) consider all of the following:\n\n(i) scam activity in the sector;\n\n(ii) the effectiveness of existing industry initiatives to\naddress scams in the sector;\n\n(iii) the interests of persons who would be SPF consumers of\nregulated services for the sector if the instrument were\nmade;\n\n(iv) the likely consequences (including benefits and risks) to\nthe public if the instrument were made;\n\n(v) the likely consequences (including benefits and risks) to\nthe businesses or services making up the sector;\n\n(vi) any other matters the Minister considers relevant; and\n\n(b) consult the businesses or services making up the sector, or\nsuch associations or other bodies representing them as the\nMinister thinks appropriate; and\n\n(c) consult such associations or other bodies representing the\npersons referred to in subparagraph (a)(iii) as the Minister\nthinks appropriate.\nNote:\nFor the meaning of SPF consumer, see section 58AH.\n\n(2) A failure to comply with subsection (1) does not invalidate an\ninstrument made under subsection 58AC(1).",
      "skos:definition": "designating a sector\n\n(1) Before making an instrument under subsection 58AC(1) about a\nsector of the economy, the Minister must:\n\n(a) consider all of the following:\n\n(i) scam activity in the sector;\n\n(ii) the effectiveness of existing industry initiatives to\naddress scams in the sector;\n\n(iii) the interests of persons who would be SPF consumers of\nregulated services for the sector if the instrument were\nmade;\n\n(iv) the likely consequences (including benefits and risks) to\nthe public if the instrument were made;\n\n(v) the likely consequences (including benefits and risks) to\nthe businesses or services making up the sector;\n\n(vi) any other matters the Minister considers relevant; and\n\n(b) consult the businesses or services making up the sector, or\nsuch associations or other bodies representing them as the\nMinister thinks appropriate; and\n\n(c) consult such associations or other bodies representing the\npersons referred to in subparagraph (a)(iii) as the Minister\nthinks appropriate.\nNote:\nFor the meaning of SPF consumer, see section 58AH.\n\n(2) A failure to comply with subsection (1) does not invalidate an\ninstrument made under subsection 58AC(1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ae-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ae-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "555fcf3106b4558d365d760b9b621a178ed0c4b61afae14072dd43da3ac9ade2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ae",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58AE Minister must consider matters, and consult, before",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 201,
      "values:originalText": "designating a sector\n\n(1) Before making an instrument under subsection 58AC(1) about a\nsector of the economy, the Minister must:\n\n(a) consider all of the following:\n\n(i) scam activity in the sector;\n\n(ii) the effectiveness of existing industry initiatives to\naddress scams in the sector;\n\n(iii) the interests of persons who would be SPF consumers of\nregulated services for the sector if the instrument were\nmade;\n\n(iv) the likely consequences (including benefits and risks) to\nthe public if the instrument were made;\n\n(v) the likely consequences (including benefits and risks) to\nthe businesses or services making up the sector;\n\n(vi) any other matters the Minister considers relevant; and\n\n(b) consult the businesses or services making up the sector, or\nsuch associations or other bodies representing them as the\nMinister thinks appropriate; and\n\n(c) consult such associations or other bodies representing the\npersons referred to in subparagraph (a)(iii) as the Minister\nthinks appropriate.\nNote:\nFor the meaning of SPF consumer, see section 58AH.\n\n(2) A failure to comply with subsection (1) does not invalidate an\ninstrument made under subsection 58AC(1)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ae-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58AE(1) Minister must consider matters, and consult, before",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ae-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
