      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ag",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58AG Meaning of scam",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ag"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.202",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A scam is a direct or indirect attempt (whether or not successful) to\nengage an SPF consumer of a regulated service where it would be\nreasonable to conclude that the attempt:\n\n(a) involves deception (see subsection (2)); and\n\n(b) would, if successful, cause loss or harm including obtaining\nSPF personal information of, or a financial or other benefit\nfrom, the SPF consumer or the SPF consumer’s associates.\n\n(2) The attempt involves deception if the attempt:\n\n(a) deceptively represents something to be (or to be related to)\nthe regulated service; or\n\n(b) impersonates a regulated entity in connection with the\nregulated service; or\n\n(c) is an attempt to deceive the SPF consumer into:\n\n(i) performing an action using the regulated service; or\n\n(ii) facilitating another person to perform an action using\nthe regulated service; or\n\n(d) is an attempt to deceive the SPF consumer that is made using\nthe regulated service.\n\n(3) The attempt may be a single act or a course of conduct.\n\n(4) However, the attempt is not a scam if the attempt is of a kind\nprescribed by the SPF rules.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A scam is a direct or indirect attempt (whether or not successful) to\nengage an SPF consumer of a regulated service where it would be\nreasonable to conclude that the attempt:\n\n(a) involves deception (see subsection (2)); and\n\n(b) would, if successful, cause loss or harm including obtaining\nSPF personal information of, or a financial or other benefit\nfrom, the SPF consumer or the SPF consumer’s associates.\n\n(2) The attempt involves deception if the attempt:\n\n(a) deceptively represents something to be (or to be related to)\nthe regulated service; or\n\n(b) impersonates a regulated entity in connection with the\nregulated service; or\n\n(c) is an attempt to deceive the SPF consumer into:\n\n(i) performing an action using the regulated service; or\n\n(ii) facilitating another person to perform an action using\nthe regulated service; or\n\n(d) is an attempt to deceive the SPF consumer that is made using\nthe regulated service.\n\n(3) The attempt may be a single act or a course of conduct.\n\n(4) However, the attempt is not a scam if the attempt is of a kind\nprescribed by the SPF rules.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ag-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ag-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ag-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ag-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9a5e1f9396fef72e2d79ea54450e3835525ffd35d63ea7cc0423c0dd3c7f2048"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ag",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58AG Meaning of scam",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 202,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A scam is a direct or indirect attempt (whether or not successful) to\nengage an SPF consumer of a regulated service where it would be\nreasonable to conclude that the attempt:\n\n(a) involves deception (see subsection (2)); and\n\n(b) would, if successful, cause loss or harm including obtaining\nSPF personal information of, or a financial or other benefit\nfrom, the SPF consumer or the SPF consumer’s associates.\n\n(2) The attempt involves deception if the attempt:\n\n(a) deceptively represents something to be (or to be related to)\nthe regulated service; or\n\n(b) impersonates a regulated entity in connection with the\nregulated service; or\n\n(c) is an attempt to deceive the SPF consumer into:\n\n(i) performing an action using the regulated service; or\n\n(ii) facilitating another person to perform an action using\nthe regulated service; or\n\n(d) is an attempt to deceive the SPF consumer that is made using\nthe regulated service.\n\n(3) The attempt may be a single act or a course of conduct.\n\n(4) However, the attempt is not a scam if the attempt is of a kind\nprescribed by the SPF rules."
    },
