    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ai",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58AI Meaning of actionable scam intelligence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ai"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.204",
      "values:originalText": "A regulated entity identifies or has actionable scam intelligence if\n(and when) there are reasonable grounds for the entity to suspect\nthat a communication, transaction or other activity relating to,\nconnected with, or using a regulated service of the entity is a scam.\nNote 1:\nWhether there are reasonable grounds for such a suspicion is an\nobjective test. Relevant information for this test may include:\n(a) information about the mechanism or identifier being used to\nscam SPF consumers, such as URLs, email addresses, phone\nnumbers, social media profiles, digital wallets and bank account\ninformation of the scam promotors; and\n(b) information about the suspected scammer; and\n(c) information (including complaints) provided by SPF consumers.\nNote 2:\nGathering and reporting this information will minimise the harm from\nscams (see SPF principles 4 and 5 in Subdivisions E and F of",
      "skos:definition": "A regulated entity identifies or has actionable scam intelligence if\n(and when) there are reasonable grounds for the entity to suspect\nthat a communication, transaction or other activity relating to,\nconnected with, or using a regulated service of the entity is a scam.\nNote 1:\nWhether there are reasonable grounds for such a suspicion is an\nobjective test. Relevant information for this test may include:\n(a) information about the mechanism or identifier being used to\nscam SPF consumers, such as URLs, email addresses, phone\nnumbers, social media profiles, digital wallets and bank account\ninformation of the scam promotors; and\n(b) information about the suspected scammer; and\n(c) information (including complaints) provided by SPF consumers.\nNote 2:\nGathering and reporting this information will minimise the harm from\nscams (see SPF principles 4 and 5 in Subdivisions E and F of",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ai-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ai-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a0ace9f51beaa71b1ff1ae36b73a1c332c8376d7face2b545307581404a0c6e2",
      "skos:note": "Identify or have actionable scam intelligence if there are reasonable grounds to suspect a communication, transaction, or activity is a scam."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ai",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58AI Meaning of actionable scam intelligence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 204,
      "values:originalText": "A regulated entity identifies or has actionable scam intelligence if\n(and when) there are reasonable grounds for the entity to suspect\nthat a communication, transaction or other activity relating to,\nconnected with, or using a regulated service of the entity is a scam.\nNote 1:\nWhether there are reasonable grounds for such a suspicion is an\nobjective test. Relevant information for this test may include:\n(a) information about the mechanism or identifier being used to\nscam SPF consumers, such as URLs, email addresses, phone\nnumbers, social media profiles, digital wallets and bank account\ninformation of the scam promotors; and\n(b) information about the suspected scammer; and\n(c) information (including complaints) provided by SPF consumers.\nNote 2:\nGathering and reporting this information will minimise the harm from\nscams (see SPF principles 4 and 5 in Subdivisions E and F of"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ai-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ai"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ai-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "has",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Entity must identify or have actionable scam intelligence.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58aj",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58AJ Extension to external Territories and outside of Australia",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58aj"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.205",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Each of the following provisions (the SPF provisions) extends to\nevery external Territory:\n\n(a) a provision of this Part;\n\n(b) a provision of a legislative instrument made under this Part;\n\n(c) another provision of this Act to the extent that it relates to a\nprovision covered by paragraph (a) or (b);\n\n(d) a provision of the Regulatory Powers Act to the extent that it\napplies in relation to a provision covered by paragraph (a) or\n(b).\n\n(2) The SPF provisions extend to acts, omissions, matters and things\noutside Australia.\nSubdivision E—Application to acts done by or in relation to\nagents etc. of regulated entities",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Each of the following provisions (the SPF provisions) extends to\nevery external Territory:\n\n(a) a provision of this Part;\n\n(b) a provision of a legislative instrument made under this Part;\n\n(c) another provision of this Act to the extent that it relates to a\nprovision covered by paragraph (a) or (b);\n\n(d) a provision of the Regulatory Powers Act to the extent that it\napplies in relation to a provision covered by paragraph (a) or\n(b).\n\n(2) The SPF provisions extend to acts, omissions, matters and things\noutside Australia.\nSubdivision E—Application to acts done by or in relation to\nagents etc. of regulated entities",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58aj-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58aj-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c001689cedd10ee410925bfc74aa27343bd83d83d6c0e794e203387426099dc7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58aj",
