    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ba",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58BA Simplified outline of this Division",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ba"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.207",
      "values:originalText": "Each regulated entity must comply with the overarching principles\nof the Scams Prevention Framework.\nThese principles require each regulated entity to:\n\n(a)\ndocument and implement governance arrangements to\ncombat scams; and\n\n(b)\ntake reasonable steps to prevent, detect, report, disrupt\nand respond to scams.\nThese requirements are civil penalty provisions. The Commission\n(in its capacity as the SPF general regulator) will monitor,\ninvestigate and enforce compliance with these provisions.\nDivision 6 sets out remedies for non-compliance with these\nprovisions.",
      "skos:definition": "Each regulated entity must comply with the overarching principles\nof the Scams Prevention Framework.\nThese principles require each regulated entity to:\n\n(a)\ndocument and implement governance arrangements to\ncombat scams; and\n\n(b)\ntake reasonable steps to prevent, detect, report, disrupt\nand respond to scams.\nThese requirements are civil penalty provisions. The Commission\n(in its capacity as the SPF general regulator) will monitor,\ninvestigate and enforce compliance with these provisions.\nDivision 6 sets out remedies for non-compliance with these\nprovisions.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ba-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ba-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c22c0ca26fd0872b085386f2a78dc8181608603a4de59d79738ed7049dd04e74",
      "skos:note": "Each regulated entity must comply with the Scams Prevention Framework principles."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ba",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58BA Simplified outline of this Division",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 207,
      "values:originalText": "Each regulated entity must comply with the overarching principles\nof the Scams Prevention Framework.\nThese principles require each regulated entity to:\n\n(a)\ndocument and implement governance arrangements to\ncombat scams; and\n\n(b)\ntake reasonable steps to prevent, detect, report, disrupt\nand respond to scams.\nThese requirements are civil penalty provisions. The Commission\n(in its capacity as the SPF general regulator) will monitor,\ninvestigate and enforce compliance with these provisions.\nDivision 6 sets out remedies for non-compliance with these\nprovisions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ba-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ba"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:LegalPerson"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: LegalPerson"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ba-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Regulated entities must comply with the framework.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58BB Meaning of reasonable steps",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.207",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Matters relevant to whether a regulated entity has taken reasonable\nsteps for the purposes of a provision of this Division include:\n\n(a) the size of the regulated entity; and\n\n(b) the kind of regulated services concerned; and\n\n(c) the consumer base of those services; and\n\n(d) the kinds of scam risks those services face; and\n\n(e) whether the regulated entity has complied with any relevant\nSPF code obligations relating to that provision.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Matters relevant to whether a regulated entity has taken reasonable\nsteps for the purposes of a provision of this Division include:\n\n(a) the size of the regulated entity; and\n\n(b) the kind of regulated services concerned; and\n\n(c) the consumer base of those services; and\n\n(d) the kinds of scam risks those services face; and\n\n(e) whether the regulated entity has complied with any relevant\nSPF code obligations relating to that provision.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bb-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b07818a027a71fea7a56c7860c8e7dc1cc479dcc433e76db3fd42053499229b4",
      "skos:note": "Matters relevant to determining reasonable steps for regulated entities"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58BB Meaning of reasonable steps",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 207,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Matters relevant to whether a regulated entity has taken reasonable\nsteps for the purposes of a provision of this Division include:\n\n(a) the size of the regulated entity; and\n\n(b) the kind of regulated services concerned; and\n\n(c) the consumer base of those services; and\n\n(d) the kinds of scam risks those services face; and\n\n(e) whether the regulated entity has complied with any relevant\nSPF code obligations relating to that provision.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bb-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bb"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58BC Simplified outline of this Subdivision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.208",
      "values:originalText": "Each regulated entity must document and implement governance\npolicies, procedures, metrics and targets for combatting scams.\nThese must be reviewed, and certified by a senior officer of the\nentity, at least annually.\nThe entity must keep records and give reports about its compliance\nwith this principle.\nThe SPF code for the sector may include sector-specific provisions\nfor this principle.",
      "skos:definition": "Each regulated entity must document and implement governance\npolicies, procedures, metrics and targets for combatting scams.\nThese must be reviewed, and certified by a senior officer of the\nentity, at least annually.\nThe entity must keep records and give reports about its compliance\nwith this principle.\nThe SPF code for the sector may include sector-specific provisions\nfor this principle.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bc-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bc-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "224cec9e6d3e29ac237aaa97d9b7b94d81a094728eeb193c9e003f84554aa3ca",
      "skos:note": "Governance policies and procedures must be implemented and reviewed annually.",
      "dc:description": "Records of compliance, annual certification by senior officer"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58BC Simplified outline of this Subdivision",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 208,
      "values:originalText": "Each regulated entity must document and implement governance\npolicies, procedures, metrics and targets for combatting scams.\nThese must be reviewed, and certified by a senior officer of the\nentity, at least annually.\nThe entity must keep records and give reports about its compliance\nwith this principle.\nThe SPF code for the sector may include sector-specific provisions\nfor this principle."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bc-norm",
