    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58be",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58BE Annual certification about SPF governance policies,",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58be"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.209",
      "values:originalText": "procedures, metrics and targets—civil penalty provision\n\n(1) A regulated entity for a regulated sector contravenes this\nsubsection if:\n\n(a) no senior officer of the entity certifies in writing, within 12\nmonths of the day the entity becomes a regulated entity for\nthe sector, whether the entity’s SPF governance policies,\nprocedures, metrics and targets for the sector comply with\nthis Subdivision; or\n\n(b) no senior officer of the entity certifies in writing, within 7\ndays after each 12-month anniversary of the day the entity\nbecomes a regulated entity for the sector, whether the entity’s\nSPF governance policies, procedures, metrics and targets for\nthe sector comply with this Subdivision.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nThis means subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision of an SPF\nprinciple for the purposes of section 58FJ (about civil penalties).",
      "skos:definition": "procedures, metrics and targets—civil penalty provision\n\n(1) A regulated entity for a regulated sector contravenes this\nsubsection if:\n\n(a) no senior officer of the entity certifies in writing, within 12\nmonths of the day the entity becomes a regulated entity for\nthe sector, whether the entity’s SPF governance policies,\nprocedures, metrics and targets for the sector comply with\nthis Subdivision; or\n\n(b) no senior officer of the entity certifies in writing, within 7\ndays after each 12-month anniversary of the day the entity\nbecomes a regulated entity for the sector, whether the entity’s\nSPF governance policies, procedures, metrics and targets for\nthe sector comply with this Subdivision.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nThis means subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision of an SPF\nprinciple for the purposes of section 58FJ (about civil penalties).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58be-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58be-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "168ec8e13fac766dbfa215465fac1a86da7748e586e29dbfd2fc399ce6993d12"
    },
    {
