    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bf",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58BF Record keeping of compliance with SPF provisions—civil",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bf"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.209",
      "values:originalText": "penalty provision\n\n(1) A regulated entity for a regulated sector contravenes this\nsubsection if the entity fails to keep records of information of a\nmaterial nature relating to each of the following activities for at\nleast 6 years after that activity happens:\n\n(a) the initial documenting, and each revision of the\ndocumenting, of the entity’s SPF governance policies,\nprocedures, metrics and targets for the sector;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "penalty provision\n\n(1) A regulated entity for a regulated sector contravenes this\nsubsection if the entity fails to keep records of information of a\nmaterial nature relating to each of the following activities for at\nleast 6 years after that activity happens:\n\n(a) the initial documenting, and each revision of the\ndocumenting, of the entity’s SPF governance policies,\nprocedures, metrics and targets for the sector;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bf-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bf-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "289c553605aa9ffc6bab71c4b9b1bc876ffe1b930fdd0e3faacb9af9eea27fc1",
      "skos:note": "Failure to keep records of material information for at least 6 years after activity",
      "dc:description": "Records of SPF governance policies, procedures, metrics and targets"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bf",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58BF Record keeping of compliance with SPF provisions—civil",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 209,
      "values:originalText": "penalty provision\n\n(1) A regulated entity for a regulated sector contravenes this\nsubsection if the entity fails to keep records of information of a\nmaterial nature relating to each of the following activities for at\nleast 6 years after that activity happens:\n\n(a) the initial documenting, and each revision of the\ndocumenting, of the entity’s SPF governance policies,\nprocedures, metrics and targets for the sector;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bf-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bf"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bf-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Regulated entity has an obligation to keep records",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58BG Reporting about compliance with this Subdivision—civil",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.210",
      "values:originalText": "penalty provision\n\n(1) A regulated entity for a regulated sector contravenes this\nsubsection if:\n\n(a) the SPF general regulator, or the SPF sector regulator for the\nsector, gives the entity a written request for a copy of:\n\n(i) the entity’s SPF governance policies, procedures,\nmetrics and targets for the sector; or\n\n(ii) specified kinds of other records required by this\nSubdivision to be kept for the sector by the entity; and\n\n(b) the entity fails to comply with the request within:\n\n(i) 10 business days after the day the entity is given the\nrequest; or\n\n(ii) such longer period as is allowed by the SPF regulator.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nThis means subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision of an SPF\nprinciple for the purposes of section 58FJ (about civil penalties).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nOverarching principles of the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 2\n\nSection 58BH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "penalty provision\n\n(1) A regulated entity for a regulated sector contravenes this\nsubsection if:\n\n(a) the SPF general regulator, or the SPF sector regulator for the\nsector, gives the entity a written request for a copy of:\n\n(i) the entity’s SPF governance policies, procedures,\nmetrics and targets for the sector; or\n\n(ii) specified kinds of other records required by this\nSubdivision to be kept for the sector by the entity; and\n\n(b) the entity fails to comply with the request within:\n\n(i) 10 business days after the day the entity is given the\nrequest; or\n\n(ii) such longer period as is allowed by the SPF regulator.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nThis means subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision of an SPF\nprinciple for the purposes of section 58FJ (about civil penalties).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nOverarching principles of the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 2\n\nSection 58BH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bg-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "89eb91ea39814ce59b4735e2638c3be4f08f28a41e9080fe59fc840590b7c145"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58BG Reporting about compliance with this Subdivision—civil",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 210,
      "values:originalText": "penalty provision\n\n(1) A regulated entity for a regulated sector contravenes this\nsubsection if:\n\n(a) the SPF general regulator, or the SPF sector regulator for the\nsector, gives the entity a written request for a copy of:\n\n(i) the entity’s SPF governance policies, procedures,\nmetrics and targets for the sector; or\n\n(ii) specified kinds of other records required by this\nSubdivision to be kept for the sector by the entity; and\n\n(b) the entity fails to comply with the request within:\n\n(i) 10 business days after the day the entity is given the\nrequest; or\n\n(ii) such longer period as is allowed by the SPF regulator.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nThis means subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision of an SPF\nprinciple for the purposes of section 58FJ (about civil penalties).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nOverarching principles of the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 2\n\nSection 58BH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
