    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58BH Sector-specific details can be set out in SPF codes",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.211",
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of (but without limiting) subsection 58CC(1), the\nSPF code for a regulated sector may include sector-specific\nprovisions describing:\n\n(a) the matters that a regulated entity for the sector must include\nin the entity’s governance policies and procedures for the\npurposes of this Subdivision; or\n\n(b) the factors that a regulated entity for the sector must have\nregard to when developing the entity’s governance policies\nand procedures for the purposes of this Subdivision.\nSubdivision C—SPF principle 2: Prevent",
      "skos:definition": "For the purposes of (but without limiting) subsection 58CC(1), the\nSPF code for a regulated sector may include sector-specific\nprovisions describing:\n\n(a) the matters that a regulated entity for the sector must include\nin the entity’s governance policies and procedures for the\npurposes of this Subdivision; or\n\n(b) the factors that a regulated entity for the sector must have\nregard to when developing the entity’s governance policies\nand procedures for the purposes of this Subdivision.\nSubdivision C—SPF principle 2: Prevent",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bh-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bh-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ffc9975d961db2519bcfe88e932d35bec193addbc31799f4fda9e18e3c73208a",
      "skos:note": "Regulated entity must include sector-specific provisions in governance policies and procedures.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bh",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58BH Sector-specific details can be set out in SPF codes",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 211,
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of (but without limiting) subsection 58CC(1), the\nSPF code for a regulated sector may include sector-specific\nprovisions describing:\n\n(a) the matters that a regulated entity for the sector must include\nin the entity’s governance policies and procedures for the\npurposes of this Subdivision; or\n\n(b) the factors that a regulated entity for the sector must have\nregard to when developing the entity’s governance policies\nand procedures for the purposes of this Subdivision.\nSubdivision C—SPF principle 2: Prevent"
    },
    {
