    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bk",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58BK Further detail about certain concepts",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bk"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.212",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Taking reasonable steps for the purposes of subsection 58BJ(1)\nrequires more than merely acting on actionable scam intelligence\nin the form of information provided to the regulated entity by\nanother person.\nFurther sector-specific details can be set out in SPF codes\n\n(2) For the purposes of (but without limiting) subsection 58CC(1), the\nSPF code for a regulated sector may include sector-specific\nprovisions:\n\n(a) describing what are reasonable steps for the purposes of this\nSubdivision (see also section 58BB); or\n\n(b) requiring each regulated entity for the sector to:\n\n(i) identify its SPF consumers who are at risk of being\ntargeted by a scam; or\n\n(ii) identify its SPF consumers who have a higher risk of\nbeing targeted by a scam; or\n\n(c) requiring each regulated entity for the sector to provide\ninformation about such scams to an SPF consumer described\nin subparagraph (b)(i) or (ii).\nSubdivision D—SPF principle 3: Detect",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Taking reasonable steps for the purposes of subsection 58BJ(1)\nrequires more than merely acting on actionable scam intelligence\nin the form of information provided to the regulated entity by\nanother person.\nFurther sector-specific details can be set out in SPF codes\n\n(2) For the purposes of (but without limiting) subsection 58CC(1), the\nSPF code for a regulated sector may include sector-specific\nprovisions:\n\n(a) describing what are reasonable steps for the purposes of this\nSubdivision (see also section 58BB); or\n\n(b) requiring each regulated entity for the sector to:\n\n(i) identify its SPF consumers who are at risk of being\ntargeted by a scam; or\n\n(ii) identify its SPF consumers who have a higher risk of\nbeing targeted by a scam; or\n\n(c) requiring each regulated entity for the sector to provide\ninformation about such scams to an SPF consumer described\nin subparagraph (b)(i) or (ii).\nSubdivision D—SPF principle 3: Detect",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bk-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bk-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ee29b42a6da7dd26093d5ef84895c0815fa212c135bed738ed473fef654e4f02"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bk",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58BK Further detail about certain concepts",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 212,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Taking reasonable steps for the purposes of subsection 58BJ(1)\nrequires more than merely acting on actionable scam intelligence\nin the form of information provided to the regulated entity by\nanother person.\nFurther sector-specific details can be set out in SPF codes\n\n(2) For the purposes of (but without limiting) subsection 58CC(1), the\nSPF code for a regulated sector may include sector-specific\nprovisions:\n\n(a) describing what are reasonable steps for the purposes of this\nSubdivision (see also section 58BB); or\n\n(b) requiring each regulated entity for the sector to:\n\n(i) identify its SPF consumers who are at risk of being\ntargeted by a scam; or\n\n(ii) identify its SPF consumers who have a higher risk of\nbeing targeted by a scam; or\n\n(c) requiring each regulated entity for the sector to provide\ninformation about such scams to an SPF consumer described\nin subparagraph (b)(i) or (ii).\nSubdivision D—SPF principle 3: Detect"
    },
