    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bm",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58BM Taking reasonable steps to detect scams—civil penalty",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bm"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.213",
      "values:originalText": "provision\n\n(1) A regulated entity contravenes this subsection if the entity fails to\ntake reasonable steps to detect a scam relating to, connected with,\nor using a regulated service of the entity.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nThis means subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision of an SPF\nprinciple for the purposes of section 58FJ (about civil penalties).\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (1), the regulated entity fails to take\nreasonable steps to detect a scam relating to, connected with, or\nusing a regulated service of the entity if the entity fails to take\nreasonable steps to:\n\n(a) detect such a scam as it happens; or\n\n(b) detect such a scam after it happens.\nNote:\nFor further details about the meaning of reasonable steps, see\nsections 58BB and 58BP.",
      "skos:definition": "provision\n\n(1) A regulated entity contravenes this subsection if the entity fails to\ntake reasonable steps to detect a scam relating to, connected with,\nor using a regulated service of the entity.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nThis means subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision of an SPF\nprinciple for the purposes of section 58FJ (about civil penalties).\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (1), the regulated entity fails to take\nreasonable steps to detect a scam relating to, connected with, or\nusing a regulated service of the entity if the entity fails to take\nreasonable steps to:\n\n(a) detect such a scam as it happens; or\n\n(b) detect such a scam after it happens.\nNote:\nFor further details about the meaning of reasonable steps, see\nsections 58BB and 58BP.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bm-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bm-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bm-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "267d294ad2fe2618846a5755ed3bb39d60fc70850dcdefa7f210d9c2f760fd35"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bm",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58BM Taking reasonable steps to detect scams—civil penalty",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 213,
      "values:originalText": "provision\n\n(1) A regulated entity contravenes this subsection if the entity fails to\ntake reasonable steps to detect a scam relating to, connected with,\nor using a regulated service of the entity.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nThis means subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision of an SPF\nprinciple for the purposes of section 58FJ (about civil penalties).\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (1), the regulated entity fails to take\nreasonable steps to detect a scam relating to, connected with, or\nusing a regulated service of the entity if the entity fails to take\nreasonable steps to:\n\n(a) detect such a scam as it happens; or\n\n(b) detect such a scam after it happens.\nNote:\nFor further details about the meaning of reasonable steps, see\nsections 58BB and 58BP."
    },
