    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58br-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58BR(4) Reporting actionable scam intelligence to SPF regulators—",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 215,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Subsection (2) does not apply to the entity if circumstances of a\nkind prescribed by the SPF rules apply to the entity.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection (see section 96 of the Regulatory Powers Act).\nMatters relevant to reports"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58br-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58br-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58br-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58BR(5) Reporting actionable scam intelligence to SPF regulators—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58br-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.215",
      "values:originalText": "(5) For the purposes of (but without limiting) subsection (2), the SPF\nrules may prescribe:\n\n(a) that the report may be given via access to a specified data\ngateway, portal or website; and\n\n(b) that the report include the sources or evidence that the entity\nhas for that intelligence (see section 58AI); and\n\n(c) different matters for different kinds of regulated entities.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) For the purposes of (but without limiting) subsection (2), the SPF\nrules may prescribe:\n\n(a) that the report may be given via access to a specified data\ngateway, portal or website; and\n\n(b) that the report include the sources or evidence that the entity\nhas for that intelligence (see section 58AI); and\n\n(c) different matters for different kinds of regulated entities.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58br"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58br-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58br-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eb72b035bf6590ef4ff21fdb7f94aa46ec55ce741ce528080dcd477f55b28c4e",
      "skos:note": "Reporting requirements for actionable scam intelligence",
      "dc:description": "report, sources/evidence"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58br-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58BR(5) Reporting actionable scam intelligence to SPF regulators—",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 215,
      "values:originalText": "(5) For the purposes of (but without limiting) subsection (2), the SPF\nrules may prescribe:\n\n(a) that the report may be given via access to a specified data\ngateway, portal or website; and\n\n(b) that the report include the sources or evidence that the entity\nhas for that intelligence (see section 58AI); and\n\n(c) different matters for different kinds of regulated entities.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58br-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
