        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "is",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Identifies a civil penalty provision",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Subsection (2) is a civil penalty provision.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "It is an obligation to report scams to SPF regulators."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-3-logic-descriptionlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "is-a",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Classifies subsection (2) as a principle for section 58FJ",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "This means subsection (2) is a civil penalty provision of an SPF principle.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Subsection (2) is a principle for section 58FJ."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "during",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Describes the temporal relationship between subsection (2) and section 58FJ",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "It applies to section 58FJ about civil penalties.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Subsection (2) occurs during the application of section 58FJ."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-3-logic-argumentation-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "implies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Establishes a logical connection between subsection (2) and reporting scams to SPF regulators",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Reporting scams to SPF regulators is required by law.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Subsection (2) implies that reporting scams to SPF regulators is necessary."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-3-logic-diffusion-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "is",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Identifies the scope of subsection (2)",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "This applies to all cases where a scam is reported to SPF regulators.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Subsection (2) applies to all cases where a scam is reported to SPF regulators."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-3-logic-cogai-6",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "is",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Recognizes the artificial intelligence aspect of subsection (2)",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "This provision is part of an SPF principle.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Subsection (2) is a rule for artificial intelligence systems."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58BS(4) Reporting scams to SPF regulators—civil penalty provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bs-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.216",
      "values:originalText": "(4) For the purposes of (but without limiting) subsection (2), the SPF\nregulator’s request may:\n\n(a) provide that the report may be given via access to a specified\ndata gateway, portal or website; and\n\n(b) ask that the report set out:\n\n(i) what loss or harm may have resulted from the scam,\nwhat disruptive actions the entity has taken and whether\nany of those actions have been reversed; and\n\n(ii) what steps the entity is taking to disrupt similar scams,\nand to prevent loss or harm resulting from similar\nscams.\nNote:\nFor more about the data gateways, portals or websites referred to in\nparagraph (a), see section 58BT.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nOverarching principles of the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 2\n\nSection 58BT\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(4) For the purposes of (but without limiting) subsection (2), the SPF\nregulator’s request may:\n\n(a) provide that the report may be given via access to a specified\ndata gateway, portal or website; and\n\n(b) ask that the report set out:\n\n(i) what loss or harm may have resulted from the scam,\nwhat disruptive actions the entity has taken and whether\nany of those actions have been reversed; and\n\n(ii) what steps the entity is taking to disrupt similar scams,\nand to prevent loss or harm resulting from similar\nscams.\nNote:\nFor more about the data gateways, portals or websites referred to in\nparagraph (a), see section 58BT.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nOverarching principles of the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 2\n\nSection 58BT\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "520c23be6dfe99453bb1bd35ef8c50d4f83473b651afb54f583f08d863d91f5a",
      "skos:note": "Request for report format and content",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bs-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58BS(4) Reporting scams to SPF regulators—civil penalty provisions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 216,
      "values:originalText": "(4) For the purposes of (but without limiting) subsection (2), the SPF\nregulator’s request may:\n\n(a) provide that the report may be given via access to a specified\ndata gateway, portal or website; and\n\n(b) ask that the report set out:\n\n(i) what loss or harm may have resulted from the scam,\nwhat disruptive actions the entity has taken and whether\nany of those actions have been reversed; and\n\n(ii) what steps the entity is taking to disrupt similar scams,\nand to prevent loss or harm resulting from similar\nscams.\nNote:\nFor more about the data gateways, portals or websites referred to in\nparagraph (a), see section 58BT.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nOverarching principles of the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 2\n\nSection 58BT\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
