      "cml:conclusionText": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58BS(5) Reporting scams to SPF regulators—civil penalty provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bs-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.216",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The request may ask for the report to include SPF personal\ninformation. If so, the request must require the entity to de-identify\nthe information unless the SPF regulator reasonably believes that\ndoing so would not achieve the object of this Part.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The request may ask for the report to include SPF personal\ninformation. If so, the request must require the entity to de-identify\nthe information unless the SPF regulator reasonably believes that\ndoing so would not achieve the object of this Part.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b79171bd6db14ff56780c7e0db2b7e628740f0dc18010228e69273b80675bd70",
      "skos:note": "Entity must de-identify personal information unless SPF regulator believes it's necessary.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bs-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58BS(5) Reporting scams to SPF regulators—civil penalty provisions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 216,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The request may ask for the report to include SPF personal\ninformation. If so, the request must require the entity to de-identify\nthe information unless the SPF regulator reasonably believes that\ndoing so would not achieve the object of this Part."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Must",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Entity must de-identify personal information.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58BS(6) Reporting scams to SPF regulators—civil penalty provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bs-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.216",
      "values:originalText": "(6) If:\n\n(a) a regulated entity gives a scam report to an SPF regulator\nunder this section; and\n\n(b) another SPF regulator later requests a scam report under this\nsection from the regulated entity about the same matters;\nthen, despite subsection (2), the later scam report need only state\nthat an earlier scam report about those matters was given to the\nfirst-mentioned SPF regulator on a specified date and time.\nNote:\nThe SPF regulators can share the earlier scam report under\nSubdivision C of Division 5.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) If:\n\n(a) a regulated entity gives a scam report to an SPF regulator\nunder this section; and\n\n(b) another SPF regulator later requests a scam report under this\nsection from the regulated entity about the same matters;\nthen, despite subsection (2), the later scam report need only state\nthat an earlier scam report about those matters was given to the\nfirst-mentioned SPF regulator on a specified date and time.\nNote:\nThe SPF regulators can share the earlier scam report under\nSubdivision C of Division 5.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-6-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-6-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-6-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-6-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8f710b32f8910264a2154818afed9b79e5cc74c419df77feca3feed51a301032",
      "skos:note": "A regulated entity must provide a later scam report that references an earlier report to another SPF regulator.",
      "dc:description": "True"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bs-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58BS(6) Reporting scams to SPF regulators—civil penalty provisions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 216,
      "values:originalText": "(6) If:\n\n(a) a regulated entity gives a scam report to an SPF regulator\nunder this section; and\n\n(b) another SPF regulator later requests a scam report under this\nsection from the regulated entity about the same matters;\nthen, despite subsection (2), the later scam report need only state\nthat an earlier scam report about those matters was given to the\nfirst-mentioned SPF regulator on a specified date and time.\nNote:\nThe SPF regulators can share the earlier scam report under\nSubdivision C of Division 5."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-6"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-6-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Must",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The regulated entity must provide the later scam report.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-6-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The later scam report is related in time to the earlier scam report.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) another SPF regulator later requests a scam report under this section from the regulated entity about the same matters;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-6-logic-argumentation-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Implication",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The regulated entity's obligation to provide the later scam report implies that it must state the earlier scam report.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) a regulated entity gives a scam report to an SPF regulator under this section;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-6-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Propagation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The obligation to provide the later scam report is propagated from the first-mentioned SPF regulator.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) another SPF regulator later requests a scam report under this section from the regulated entity about the same matters;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bs-ss-6-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Inference",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The regulated entity's obligation to provide the later scam report is inferred from its earlier action.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) a regulated entity gives a scam report to an SPF regulator under this section;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bt",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58BT Authorised third party data gateways, portals or websites for",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bt"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.217",
      "values:originalText": "accessing reports\n\n(1) The SPF rules may prescribe a scheme for authorising third parties\nto operate data gateways, portals or websites that give access to\nreports under this Division.\n\n(2) For the purposes of (but without limiting) subsection (1), the SPF\nrules may include the following:\n\n(a) provisions conferring functions or powers on the SPF general\nregulator under the scheme;\n\n(b) the criteria for a person to be authorised under the scheme;\n\n(c) provisions providing that authorisations may be granted\nsubject to conditions, and that conditions may be imposed on\nan authorisation after it has been granted;\n\n(d) provisions providing that authorisations may be granted at\ndifferent levels corresponding to different risks;\n\n(e) provisions specifying what a person authorised at a particular\nlevel is authorised to do (or not authorised to do);\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "accessing reports\n\n(1) The SPF rules may prescribe a scheme for authorising third parties\nto operate data gateways, portals or websites that give access to\nreports under this Division.\n\n(2) For the purposes of (but without limiting) subsection (1), the SPF\nrules may include the following:\n\n(a) provisions conferring functions or powers on the SPF general\nregulator under the scheme;\n\n(b) the criteria for a person to be authorised under the scheme;\n\n(c) provisions providing that authorisations may be granted\nsubject to conditions, and that conditions may be imposed on\nan authorisation after it has been granted;\n\n(d) provisions providing that authorisations may be granted at\ndifferent levels corresponding to different risks;\n\n(e) provisions specifying what a person authorised at a particular\nlevel is authorised to do (or not authorised to do);\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bt-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58bt-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "60284427f04e3d548941e2c9f59d9a8d8e162438471a2cbbddc10e01737917f0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58bt",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58BT Authorised third party data gateways, portals or websites for",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 217,
      "values:originalText": "accessing reports\n\n(1) The SPF rules may prescribe a scheme for authorising third parties\nto operate data gateways, portals or websites that give access to\nreports under this Division.\n\n(2) For the purposes of (but without limiting) subsection (1), the SPF\nrules may include the following:\n\n(a) provisions conferring functions or powers on the SPF general\nregulator under the scheme;\n\n(b) the criteria for a person to be authorised under the scheme;\n\n(c) provisions providing that authorisations may be granted\nsubject to conditions, and that conditions may be imposed on\nan authorisation after it has been granted;\n\n(d) provisions providing that authorisations may be granted at\ndifferent levels corresponding to different risks;\n\n(e) provisions specifying what a person authorised at a particular\nlevel is authorised to do (or not authorised to do);\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
