    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ca",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58CA Simplified outline of this Division",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ca"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.230",
      "values:originalText": "The Minister may make a code for each regulated sector.\nEach code is to include sector-specific provisions for the following\noverarching principles of the Scams Prevention Framework (see\nSubdivisions B, C, D, F and G of Division 2):\n\n(a)\nSPF principle 1—governance;\n\n(b)\nSPF principle 2—prevent;\n\n(c)\nSPF principle 3—detect;\n\n(d)\nSPF principle 5—disrupt;\n\n(e)\nSPF principle 6—respond.\nRequirements in a code can be civil penalty provisions. The\nrelevant SPF sector regulator will monitor, investigate and enforce\ncompliance with these provisions. Division 6 sets out remedies for\nnon-compliance with these provisions.",
      "skos:definition": "The Minister may make a code for each regulated sector.\nEach code is to include sector-specific provisions for the following\noverarching principles of the Scams Prevention Framework (see\nSubdivisions B, C, D, F and G of Division 2):\n\n(a)\nSPF principle 1—governance;\n\n(b)\nSPF principle 2—prevent;\n\n(c)\nSPF principle 3—detect;\n\n(d)\nSPF principle 5—disrupt;\n\n(e)\nSPF principle 6—respond.\nRequirements in a code can be civil penalty provisions. The\nrelevant SPF sector regulator will monitor, investigate and enforce\ncompliance with these provisions. Division 6 sets out remedies for\nnon-compliance with these provisions.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ca-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ca-logic-alleninterval-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3b837276c267e41042ed58e4a790d65c2ce64d85d4d2cb8db8cdac9c1a24f8b6",
      "skos:note": "Minister may make code for regulated sector with sector-specific provisions based on Scams Prevention Framework principles."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ca",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58CA Simplified outline of this Division",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 230,
      "values:originalText": "The Minister may make a code for each regulated sector.\nEach code is to include sector-specific provisions for the following\noverarching principles of the Scams Prevention Framework (see\nSubdivisions B, C, D, F and G of Division 2):\n\n(a)\nSPF principle 1—governance;\n\n(b)\nSPF principle 2—prevent;\n\n(c)\nSPF principle 3—detect;\n\n(d)\nSPF principle 5—disrupt;\n\n(e)\nSPF principle 6—respond.\nRequirements in a code can be civil penalty provisions. The\nrelevant SPF sector regulator will monitor, investigate and enforce\ncompliance with these provisions. Division 6 sets out remedies for\nnon-compliance with these provisions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ca-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
