      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) Without limiting subparagraph (1)(b)(ii), an SPF code for a regulated sector may include the following:",
      "cml:conclusionText": "All regulated entities must comply with provisions regarding services and consumers"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58cc-ss-2-logic-cogai-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "has power",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Grants powers to the regulator or another person",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(d) a provision that: (i) confers powers on the SPF sector regulator for the sector or on another person; or",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The regulator has power to enforce provisions regarding services and consumers"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58cc-ss-2-logic-shacl-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:SHACL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "validates",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Validates specific requirements",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::shacl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(f) provisions about the manner or form in which persons or bodies: (i) may exercise powers under the SPF code; or",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Specific requirements must be met for exercising powers under the SPF code"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58cd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58CD Delegation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58cd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.232",
      "values:originalText": "The Minister may, in writing, delegate the Minister’s power under\nsection 58CB to make a code for a regulated sector to:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nSector-specific codes for the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 3\n\nSection 58CD\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) another Minister; or\n\n(b) the Commission; or\n\n(c) the entity that is, or is to be, the SPF sector regulator for the\nsector.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "The Minister may, in writing, delegate the Minister’s power under\nsection 58CB to make a code for a regulated sector to:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nSector-specific codes for the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 3\n\nSection 58CD\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) another Minister; or\n\n(b) the Commission; or\n\n(c) the entity that is, or is to be, the SPF sector regulator for the\nsector.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58cd-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0d507639cba6df3da6c63f77e3dcce102a637ca06544ceee689217d605963078",
      "skos:note": "Delegation of power under section 58CB"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58cd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58CD Delegation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 232,
      "values:originalText": "The Minister may, in writing, delegate the Minister’s power under\nsection 58CB to make a code for a regulated sector to:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nSector-specific codes for the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 3\n\nSection 58CD\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) another Minister; or\n\n(b) the Commission; or\n\n(c) the entity that is, or is to be, the SPF sector regulator for the\nsector.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58cd-norm",
