      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d09eb2add43704cb63bfa75a63204109edd5c54cd0db04a3ed021b570b404618",
      "skos:note": "Minister must consider certain factors before authorizing an external dispute resolution scheme."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58db-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58DB(2) Minister may authorise external dispute resolution schemes",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 234,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Before authorising a scheme, the Minister must consider:\n\n(a) the accessibility of the scheme; and\n\n(b) the independence of the scheme; and\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nExternal dispute resolution for the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 4\n\nSection 58DC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) the fairness of the scheme; and\n\n(d) the accountability of the scheme; and\n\n(e) the efficiency of the scheme; and\n\n(f) the effectiveness of the scheme; and\n\n(g) any other matters the Minister considers relevant.\nA failure to comply with this subsection does not invalidate an\ninstrument made under subsection (1) authorising the scheme."
    },
