      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58dd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58DD Scheme operator to report to SPF regulators",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58dd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.236",
      "values:originalText": "Referring contraventions, failures and systemic issues\n\n(1) If the operator of an SPF EDR scheme for a regulated sector\nbecomes aware that:\n\n(a) a serious contravention of any law may have occurred in\nconnection with a complaint under the scheme; or\n\n(b) a party to a complaint under the scheme may have failed to\ngive effect to a determination by the operator relating to the\ncomplaint; or\n\n(c) there is a systemic issue arising from the consideration of\ncomplaints under the scheme;\nthe operator must give particulars of the contravention, failure or\nissue to the SPF general regulator and to the SPF sector regulator\nfor the sector.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nExternal dispute resolution for the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 4\n\nSection 58DE\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nReferring settled complaints\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the parties to a complaint made under an SPF EDR scheme\nfor a regulated sector agree to a settlement of the complaint;\nand\n\n(b) the operator of the scheme thinks the settlement may require\ninvestigation;\nthe operator may give particulars of the settlement to the SPF\ngeneral regulator and to the SPF sector regulator for the sector.\nDe-identifying any SPF personal information\n\n(3) If any SPF personal information is to be given under subsection (1)\nor (2) by the operator of the scheme, the operator must de-identify\nthe information unless the operator reasonably believes that doing\nso would not achieve the object of this Part.",
      "skos:definition": "Referring contraventions, failures and systemic issues\n\n(1) If the operator of an SPF EDR scheme for a regulated sector\nbecomes aware that:\n\n(a) a serious contravention of any law may have occurred in\nconnection with a complaint under the scheme; or\n\n(b) a party to a complaint under the scheme may have failed to\ngive effect to a determination by the operator relating to the\ncomplaint; or\n\n(c) there is a systemic issue arising from the consideration of\ncomplaints under the scheme;\nthe operator must give particulars of the contravention, failure or\nissue to the SPF general regulator and to the SPF sector regulator\nfor the sector.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nExternal dispute resolution for the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 4\n\nSection 58DE\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nReferring settled complaints\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the parties to a complaint made under an SPF EDR scheme\nfor a regulated sector agree to a settlement of the complaint;\nand\n\n(b) the operator of the scheme thinks the settlement may require\ninvestigation;\nthe operator may give particulars of the settlement to the SPF\ngeneral regulator and to the SPF sector regulator for the sector.\nDe-identifying any SPF personal information\n\n(3) If any SPF personal information is to be given under subsection (1)\nor (2) by the operator of the scheme, the operator must de-identify\nthe information unless the operator reasonably believes that doing\nso would not achieve the object of this Part.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58dd-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58dd-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58dd-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ba67a73de43d3318fef8c5bdc803b75423fcece2d82ce761b7602edbf0ac1a3c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58dd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58DD Scheme operator to report to SPF regulators",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 236,
      "values:originalText": "Referring contraventions, failures and systemic issues\n\n(1) If the operator of an SPF EDR scheme for a regulated sector\nbecomes aware that:\n\n(a) a serious contravention of any law may have occurred in\nconnection with a complaint under the scheme; or\n\n(b) a party to a complaint under the scheme may have failed to\ngive effect to a determination by the operator relating to the\ncomplaint; or\n\n(c) there is a systemic issue arising from the consideration of\ncomplaints under the scheme;\nthe operator must give particulars of the contravention, failure or\nissue to the SPF general regulator and to the SPF sector regulator\nfor the sector.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nExternal dispute resolution for the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 4\n\nSection 58DE\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nReferring settled complaints\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the parties to a complaint made under an SPF EDR scheme\nfor a regulated sector agree to a settlement of the complaint;\nand\n\n(b) the operator of the scheme thinks the settlement may require\ninvestigation;\nthe operator may give particulars of the settlement to the SPF\ngeneral regulator and to the SPF sector regulator for the sector.\nDe-identifying any SPF personal information\n\n(3) If any SPF personal information is to be given under subsection (1)\nor (2) by the operator of the scheme, the operator must de-identify\nthe information unless the operator reasonably believes that doing\nso would not achieve the object of this Part."
    },
