      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ea",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58EA Simplified outline of this Division",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ea"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.238",
      "values:originalText": "The Commission is the regulator (the SPF general regulator) of\nmost aspects of the Scams Prevention Framework, in particular of\nthe overarching principles of the Framework.\nOther Commonwealth entities may be selected to be regulators\n(SPF sector regulators) of each of the SPF codes.\nThe SPF general regulator must enter into arrangements with the\nSPF sector regulators about the regulation and enforcement of the\nFramework. These regulators may disclose relevant information\nand documents to each other for this purpose.\nSubdivision B—Regulators of the Scams Prevention\nFramework",
      "skos:definition": "The Commission is the regulator (the SPF general regulator) of\nmost aspects of the Scams Prevention Framework, in particular of\nthe overarching principles of the Framework.\nOther Commonwealth entities may be selected to be regulators\n(SPF sector regulators) of each of the SPF codes.\nThe SPF general regulator must enter into arrangements with the\nSPF sector regulators about the regulation and enforcement of the\nFramework. These regulators may disclose relevant information\nand documents to each other for this purpose.\nSubdivision B—Regulators of the Scams Prevention\nFramework",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ea-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6338f511ef40083ecec2d9c847d77df829df77371af84e411823d2c47eadc8bb",
      "skos:note": "The Commission is the regulator of most aspects of the Scams Prevention Framework."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ea",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58EA Simplified outline of this Division",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 238,
      "values:originalText": "The Commission is the regulator (the SPF general regulator) of\nmost aspects of the Scams Prevention Framework, in particular of\nthe overarching principles of the Framework.\nOther Commonwealth entities may be selected to be regulators\n(SPF sector regulators) of each of the SPF codes.\nThe SPF general regulator must enter into arrangements with the\nSPF sector regulators about the regulation and enforcement of the\nFramework. These regulators may disclose relevant information\nand documents to each other for this purpose.\nSubdivision B—Regulators of the Scams Prevention\nFramework"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ea-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ea"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58eb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58EB General regulator of the Scams Prevention Framework",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58eb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.238",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission is the SPF general regulator for all SPF\nprovisions apart from the provisions of SPF codes.\n\n(2) The functions and powers of the SPF general regulator include:\n\n(a) reviewing, and advising the Minister about, the operation of\nthe SPF provisions; and\n\n(ab) monitoring, investigating and enforcing compliance with the\nSPF provisions, other than the provisions of SPF codes; and\n\n(b) the Commission’s powers under section 155 to the extent that\nsection 155 relates to:\n\n(i) the SPF provisions, other than the provisions of SPF\ncodes; or\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nRegulating the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 5\n\nSection 58EC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(ii) a designated scams prevention framework matter\n(within the meaning of that section) of a kind not\nmentioned in subparagraph 58ED(3)(c)(ii); and\n\n(c) developing and publishing non-binding guidance material\nrelating to the SPF provisions, other than the provisions of\nSPF codes; and\n\n(d) the functions and powers of the SPF general regulator\nconferred by any other SPF provisions.\nNote:\nParagraph (d) includes the SPF general regulator’s powers under the\nRegulatory Powers Act that are referred to in Division 6.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commission is the SPF general regulator for all SPF\nprovisions apart from the provisions of SPF codes.\n\n(2) The functions and powers of the SPF general regulator include:\n\n(a) reviewing, and advising the Minister about, the operation of\nthe SPF provisions; and\n\n(ab) monitoring, investigating and enforcing compliance with the\nSPF provisions, other than the provisions of SPF codes; and\n\n(b) the Commission’s powers under section 155 to the extent that\nsection 155 relates to:\n\n(i) the SPF provisions, other than the provisions of SPF\ncodes; or\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nRegulating the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 5\n\nSection 58EC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(ii) a designated scams prevention framework matter\n(within the meaning of that section) of a kind not\nmentioned in subparagraph 58ED(3)(c)(ii); and\n\n(c) developing and publishing non-binding guidance material\nrelating to the SPF provisions, other than the provisions of\nSPF codes; and\n\n(d) the functions and powers of the SPF general regulator\nconferred by any other SPF provisions.\nNote:\nParagraph (d) includes the SPF general regulator’s powers under the\nRegulatory Powers Act that are referred to in Division 6.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58eb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58eb-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a05755ed8fc5ce7e058cfb6f9a7be30cde505e8128b77556bfd41e51c4b24726"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58eb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58EB General regulator of the Scams Prevention Framework",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 238,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission is the SPF general regulator for all SPF\nprovisions apart from the provisions of SPF codes.\n\n(2) The functions and powers of the SPF general regulator include:\n\n(a) reviewing, and advising the Minister about, the operation of\nthe SPF provisions; and\n\n(ab) monitoring, investigating and enforcing compliance with the\nSPF provisions, other than the provisions of SPF codes; and\n\n(b) the Commission’s powers under section 155 to the extent that\nsection 155 relates to:\n\n(i) the SPF provisions, other than the provisions of SPF\ncodes; or\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nRegulating the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 5\n\nSection 58EC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(ii) a designated scams prevention framework matter\n(within the meaning of that section) of a kind not\nmentioned in subparagraph 58ED(3)(c)(ii); and\n\n(c) developing and publishing non-binding guidance material\nrelating to the SPF provisions, other than the provisions of\nSPF codes; and\n\n(d) the functions and powers of the SPF general regulator\nconferred by any other SPF provisions.\nNote:\nParagraph (d) includes the SPF general regulator’s powers under the\nRegulatory Powers Act that are referred to in Division 6."
    },
