      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.238",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The functions and powers of the SPF general regulator include:\n\n(a) reviewing, and advising the Minister about, the operation of\nthe SPF provisions; and\n\n(ab) monitoring, investigating and enforcing compliance with the\nSPF provisions, other than the provisions of SPF codes; and\n\n(b) the Commission’s powers under section 155 to the extent that\nsection 155 relates to:\n\n(i) the SPF provisions, other than the provisions of SPF\ncodes; or\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nRegulating the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 5\n\nSection 58EC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(ii) a designated scams prevention framework matter\n(within the meaning of that section) of a kind not\nmentioned in subparagraph 58ED(3)(c)(ii); and\n\n(c) developing and publishing non-binding guidance material\nrelating to the SPF provisions, other than the provisions of\nSPF codes; and\n\n(d) the functions and powers of the SPF general regulator\nconferred by any other SPF provisions.\nNote:\nParagraph (d) includes the SPF general regulator’s powers under the\nRegulatory Powers Act that are referred to in Division 6.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The functions and powers of the SPF general regulator include:\n\n(a) reviewing, and advising the Minister about, the operation of\nthe SPF provisions; and\n\n(ab) monitoring, investigating and enforcing compliance with the\nSPF provisions, other than the provisions of SPF codes; and\n\n(b) the Commission’s powers under section 155 to the extent that\nsection 155 relates to:\n\n(i) the SPF provisions, other than the provisions of SPF\ncodes; or\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nRegulating the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 5\n\nSection 58EC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(ii) a designated scams prevention framework matter\n(within the meaning of that section) of a kind not\nmentioned in subparagraph 58ED(3)(c)(ii); and\n\n(c) developing and publishing non-binding guidance material\nrelating to the SPF provisions, other than the provisions of\nSPF codes; and\n\n(d) the functions and powers of the SPF general regulator\nconferred by any other SPF provisions.\nNote:\nParagraph (d) includes the SPF general regulator’s powers under the\nRegulatory Powers Act that are referred to in Division 6.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58eb"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58eb-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58eb-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58eb-ss-2-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7ecc1d34597ca4c84223d85e64689066183a846c86e6e4e884697917e9573a4c",
      "skos:note": "The SPF general regulator has obligations to review, advise, monitor, investigate and enforce compliance with the SPF provisions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58eb-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58EB(2) General regulator of the Scams Prevention Framework",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 238,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The functions and powers of the SPF general regulator include:\n\n(a) reviewing, and advising the Minister about, the operation of\nthe SPF provisions; and\n\n(ab) monitoring, investigating and enforcing compliance with the\nSPF provisions, other than the provisions of SPF codes; and\n\n(b) the Commission’s powers under section 155 to the extent that\nsection 155 relates to:\n\n(i) the SPF provisions, other than the provisions of SPF\ncodes; or\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nRegulating the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 5\n\nSection 58EC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(ii) a designated scams prevention framework matter\n(within the meaning of that section) of a kind not\nmentioned in subparagraph 58ED(3)(c)(ii); and\n\n(c) developing and publishing non-binding guidance material\nrelating to the SPF provisions, other than the provisions of\nSPF codes; and\n\n(d) the functions and powers of the SPF general regulator\nconferred by any other SPF provisions.\nNote:\nParagraph (d) includes the SPF general regulator’s powers under the\nRegulatory Powers Act that are referred to in Division 6."
    },
    {
