      "values:originalText": "(4) The Minister may, in writing, delegate the Minister’s power under\nsubsection (1) to another Minister.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The Minister may, in writing, delegate the Minister’s power under\nsubsection (1) to another Minister.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ed"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ed-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ed-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4ee1e6cdfa8ceea2bf22049c0e5e3992cb7f41f9a19faf193645562b64a03f45",
      "skos:note": "The Minister may delegate power to another Minister in writing.",
      "dc:references": [
        "Acts Interpretation Act 1901"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ed-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58ED(4) Regulator of a regulated sector",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 240,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Minister may, in writing, delegate the Minister’s power under\nsubsection (1) to another Minister.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations."
    },
