    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ee",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58EE Delegation of an SPF sector regulator’s functions and powers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ee"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.241",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An SPF sector regulator may, by writing, delegate any of the SPF\nsector regulator’s functions and powers under:\n\n(a) an SPF provision, other than a provision of the Regulatory\nPowers Act; or\n\n(b) if the SPF sector regulator is the Commission—the\nCommission’s powers under section 155 as described in\nparagraph 58ED(3)(c);\nto a person to whom subsection (3) applies.\nNote:\nA function or power of the SPF sector regulator under a provision of\nthe Regulatory Powers Act may be able to be delegated under the\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An SPF sector regulator may, by writing, delegate any of the SPF\nsector regulator’s functions and powers under:\n\n(a) an SPF provision, other than a provision of the Regulatory\nPowers Act; or\n\n(b) if the SPF sector regulator is the Commission—the\nCommission’s powers under section 155 as described in\nparagraph 58ED(3)(c);\nto a person to whom subsection (3) applies.\nNote:\nA function or power of the SPF sector regulator under a provision of\nthe Regulatory Powers Act may be able to be delegated under the\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ee-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b76b31c4a143ca13a83c446b7e821389cf46a93aa706dce23fb75a412bc940cb",
      "skos:note": "Delegation of SPF sector regulator's functions and powers"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ee",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58EE Delegation of an SPF sector regulator’s functions and powers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 241,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An SPF sector regulator may, by writing, delegate any of the SPF\nsector regulator’s functions and powers under:\n\n(a) an SPF provision, other than a provision of the Regulatory\nPowers Act; or\n\n(b) if the SPF sector regulator is the Commission—the\nCommission’s powers under section 155 as described in\nparagraph 58ED(3)(c);\nto a person to whom subsection (3) applies.\nNote:\nA function or power of the SPF sector regulator under a provision of\nthe Regulatory Powers Act may be able to be delegated under the\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ee-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ee"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ef",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58EF Arrangements for regulating the Scams Prevention",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ef"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.242",
      "values:originalText": "Framework\n\n(1) The SPF general regulator, and each SPF sector regulator, must\nenter into an arrangement relating to the regulation and\nenforcement of the SPF provisions.\n\n(2) The SPF general regulator may choose to comply with\nsubsection (1) by entering into:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nRegulating the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 5\n\nSection 58EFA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) a single arrangement with all, or one or more, SPF sector\nregulators; or\n\n(b) a separate arrangement with each SPF sector regulator.\nHowever, subsection (1) does not apply to the extent that the\nCommission is an SPF sector regulator.\n\n(3) The arrangement must include provisions relating to the matters (if\nany) prescribed by the SPF rules.\nNote:\nFor example, the SPF rules could require an SPF regulator that\nrequests a scam report under subsection 58BS(1) to:\n(a) notify each other SPF regulator of the request; and\n(b) give a copy of the scam report to any of those other SPF\nregulators that asks for one.\n\n(4) Each SPF regulator that is a party to such an arrangement must\npublish the arrangement on its website.\n\n(5) A failure to comply with this section does not invalidate the\nperformance or exercise of a function or power by an SPF\nregulator.\n58EFA  Roles and responsibilities statement\n\n(1) The SPF general regulator must publish a statement on its website\nsummarising, in general terms, the roles and responsibilities of:\n\n(a) each SPF regulator; and\n\n(b) each operator of an SPF EDR scheme; and\n\n(c) any other entity the SPF general regulator considers\nappropriate;\nwith respect to the regulation, enforcement and administration of\nthe SPF provisions.\nNote:\nThe purpose of the statement is to explain these matters at a high\nlevel.\n\n(2) Before publishing the statement, the SPF general regulator must\nconsult the entities mentioned in subsection (1).\n\n(3) The statement is not a legislative instrument.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "Framework\n\n(1) The SPF general regulator, and each SPF sector regulator, must\nenter into an arrangement relating to the regulation and\nenforcement of the SPF provisions.\n\n(2) The SPF general regulator may choose to comply with\nsubsection (1) by entering into:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nRegulating the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 5\n\nSection 58EFA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) a single arrangement with all, or one or more, SPF sector\nregulators; or\n\n(b) a separate arrangement with each SPF sector regulator.\nHowever, subsection (1) does not apply to the extent that the\nCommission is an SPF sector regulator.\n\n(3) The arrangement must include provisions relating to the matters (if\nany) prescribed by the SPF rules.\nNote:\nFor example, the SPF rules could require an SPF regulator that\nrequests a scam report under subsection 58BS(1) to:\n(a) notify each other SPF regulator of the request; and\n(b) give a copy of the scam report to any of those other SPF\nregulators that asks for one.\n\n(4) Each SPF regulator that is a party to such an arrangement must\npublish the arrangement on its website.\n\n(5) A failure to comply with this section does not invalidate the\nperformance or exercise of a function or power by an SPF\nregulator.\n58EFA  Roles and responsibilities statement\n\n(1) The SPF general regulator must publish a statement on its website\nsummarising, in general terms, the roles and responsibilities of:\n\n(a) each SPF regulator; and\n\n(b) each operator of an SPF EDR scheme; and\n\n(c) any other entity the SPF general regulator considers\nappropriate;\nwith respect to the regulation, enforcement and administration of\nthe SPF provisions.\nNote:\nThe purpose of the statement is to explain these matters at a high\nlevel.\n\n(2) Before publishing the statement, the SPF general regulator must\nconsult the entities mentioned in subsection (1).\n\n(3) The statement ",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ef-ss-1"
        },
