    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58eg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58EG SPF regulators may disclose information to each other",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58eg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.244",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An SPF regulator may disclose to another SPF regulator:\n\n(a) particular information or documents; or\n\n(b) information or documents of a particular kind;\nheld by the first-mentioned SPF regulator that are relevant to the\noperation (including enforcement) of the SPF provisions.\n\n(2) An SPF regulator may make a disclosure under subsection (1) on\nrequest or on its own initiative.\nNote:\nThis section means such a disclosure is permitted by provisions like:\n(a) paragraph 155AAA(1)(b); and\n(b) section 59DB of the Australian Communications and Media\nAuthority Act 2005; and\n(c) subsection 127(2) of the Australian Securities and Investments\nCommission Act 2001.\n\nSimilarly, the exception in paragraph 6.2(b) of Australian Privacy\nPrinciple 6 will apply to such a disclosure.\n\n(3) SPF personal information may be disclosed under subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An SPF regulator may disclose to another SPF regulator:\n\n(a) particular information or documents; or\n\n(b) information or documents of a particular kind;\nheld by the first-mentioned SPF regulator that are relevant to the\noperation (including enforcement) of the SPF provisions.\n\n(2) An SPF regulator may make a disclosure under subsection (1) on\nrequest or on its own initiative.\nNote:\nThis section means such a disclosure is permitted by provisions like:\n(a) paragraph 155AAA(1)(b); and\n(b) section 59DB of the Australian Communications and Media\nAuthority Act 2005; and\n(c) subsection 127(2) of the Australian Securities and Investments\nCommission Act 2001.\n\nSimilarly, the exception in paragraph 6.2(b) of Australian Privacy\nPrinciple 6 will apply to such a disclosure.\n\n(3) SPF personal information may be disclosed under subsection (1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58eg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58eg-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58eg-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a871ad70bb179e61f31f76a8a5c4699a0607ddf50c7010dbec1365bb8916fee9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58eg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58EG SPF regulators may disclose information to each other",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 244,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An SPF regulator may disclose to another SPF regulator:\n\n(a) particular information or documents; or\n\n(b) information or documents of a particular kind;\nheld by the first-mentioned SPF regulator that are relevant to the\noperation (including enforcement) of the SPF provisions.\n\n(2) An SPF regulator may make a disclosure under subsection (1) on\nrequest or on its own initiative.\nNote:\nThis section means such a disclosure is permitted by provisions like:\n(a) paragraph 155AAA(1)(b); and\n(b) section 59DB of the Australian Communications and Media\nAuthority Act 2005; and\n(c) subsection 127(2) of the Australian Securities and Investments\nCommission Act 2001.\n\nSimilarly, the exception in paragraph 6.2(b) of Australian Privacy\nPrinciple 6 will apply to such a disclosure.\n\n(3) SPF personal information may be disclosed under subsection (1)."
    },
