      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The SPF regulator plans to make a disclosure of information or documents under this Part",
      "cml:conclusionText": "No obligation to notify"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ej",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58EJ Information that need not be disclosed",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ej"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.245",
      "values:originalText": "Nothing in this Part requires an SPF regulator to disclose\ninformation or documents that:\n\n(a) concern the internal administrative functioning of that\nregulator; or\n\n(b) disclose a matter in respect of which that regulator or any\nother person has claimed legal professional privilege; or\n\n(c) are of a kind prescribed by the SPF rules.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "Nothing in this Part requires an SPF regulator to disclose\ninformation or documents that:\n\n(a) concern the internal administrative functioning of that\nregulator; or\n\n(b) disclose a matter in respect of which that regulator or any\nother person has claimed legal professional privilege; or\n\n(c) are of a kind prescribed by the SPF rules.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ej-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7c6349e8147acbe991b1bf75dafce3f2eb7aba8b7e72be07e8d35806403e6b6f",
      "skos:note": "No disclosure of certain information required"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ej",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58EJ Information that need not be disclosed",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 245,
      "values:originalText": "Nothing in this Part requires an SPF regulator to disclose\ninformation or documents that:\n\n(a) concern the internal administrative functioning of that\nregulator; or\n\n(b) disclose a matter in respect of which that regulator or any\nother person has claimed legal professional privilege; or\n\n(c) are of a kind prescribed by the SPF rules.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ej-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ej"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58FA Simplified outline of this Division",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.246",
      "values:originalText": "The Commission, in its role as the SPF general regulator or an SPF\nsector regulator, may use its powers under this Act (including\nsection 155) to monitor and investigate compliance with the\naspects of the Scams Prevention Framework that are relevant for\nthat role.\nIf the ACMA or ASIC is an SPF sector regulator, it must use\npowers in its own legislation to monitor and investigate\ncompliance with an SPF code for the sector. Other SPF sector\nregulators may monitor and investigate compliance with an SPF\ncode either using the powers in Subdivision B or, with the\nMinister’s permission, powers in their own legislation.\nThe maximum penalties for contraventions of the civil penalty\nprovisions of the Scams Prevention Framework are set out in\nSubdivision C.\nOther remedies for contraventions of the Framework are set out in\nlater Subdivisions of this Division, and include:\n\n(a)\ninfringement notices; and\n\n(b)\nenforceable undertakings; and\n\n(c)\ninjunctions; and\n\n(d)\nactions for damages; and\n\n(e)\npublic warning notices; and\n\n(f)\nremedial directions; and\n\n(g)\nadverse publicity orders; and\n\n(h)\nother punitive and non-punitive orders.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FB\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSome of these remedies may also be available against a person\ninvolved in a contravention of the Framework by a regulated\nentity, such as a senior officer of the regulated entity (for example,\nsee subsection 58FW(1)).\nNote:\nSections 58GA to 58GC extend the meaning of person for\npartnerships, unincorporated associations and trusts.",
      "skos:definition": "The Commission, in its role as the SPF general regulator or an SPF\nsector regulator, may use its powers under this Act (including\nsection 155) to monitor and investigate compliance with the\naspects of the Scams Prevention Framework that are relevant for\nthat role.\nIf the ACMA or ASIC is an SPF sector regulator, it must use\npowers in its own legislation to monitor and investigate\ncompliance with an SPF code for the sector. Other SPF sector\nregulators may monitor and investigate compliance with an SPF\ncode either using the powers in Subdivision B or, with the\nMinister’s permission, powers in their own legislation.\nThe maximum penalties for contraventions of the civil penalty\nprovisions of the Scams Prevention Framework are set out in\nSubdivision C.\nOther remedies for contraventions of the Framework are set out in\nlater Subdivisions of this Division, and include:\n\n(a)\ninfringement notices; and\n\n(b)\nenforceable undertakings; and\n\n(c)\ninjunctions; and\n\n(d)\nactions for damages; and\n\n(e)\npublic warning notices; and\n\n(f)\nremedial directions; and\n\n(g)\nadverse publicity orders; and\n\n(h)\nother punitive and non-punitive orders.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FB\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSome of these remedies may also be available against a person\ninvolved in a contravention of the Framework by a regulated\nentity, such as a senior officer of the regulated entity (for example,\nsee subsection 58FW(1)).\nNote:\nSections 58GA to 58GC extend the meaning of person for\npartnerships, unincorporated associations and trusts.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fa-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fa-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e24404bc9bf0b8bd12825d8948dd42bd4f77387c7bb64ac3e1980aa5874dd7ff",
      "skos:note": "The Commission may monitor and investigate compliance with the Scams Prevention Framework."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58FA Simplified outline of this Division",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 246,
      "values:originalText": "The Commission, in its role as the SPF general regulator or an SPF\nsector regulator, may use its powers under this Act (including\nsection 155) to monitor and investigate compliance with the\naspects of the Scams Prevention Framework that are relevant for\nthat role.\nIf the ACMA or ASIC is an SPF sector regulator, it must use\npowers in its own legislation to monitor and investigate\ncompliance with an SPF code for the sector. Other SPF sector\nregulators may monitor and investigate compliance with an SPF\ncode either using the powers in Subdivision B or, with the\nMinister’s permission, powers in their own legislation.\nThe maximum penalties for contraventions of the civil penalty\nprovisions of the Scams Prevention Framework are set out in\nSubdivision C.\nOther remedies for contraventions of the Framework are set out in\nlater Subdivisions of this Division, and include:\n\n(a)\ninfringement notices; and\n\n(b)\nenforceable undertakings; and\n\n(c)\ninjunctions; and\n\n(d)\nactions for damages; and\n\n(e)\npublic warning notices; and\n\n(f)\nremedial directions; and\n\n(g)\nadverse publicity orders; and\n\n(h)\nother punitive and non-punitive orders.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FB\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSome of these remedies may also be available against a person\ninvolved in a contravention of the Framework by a regulated\nentity, such as a senior officer of the regulated entity (for example,\nsee subsection 58FW(1)).\nNote:\nSections 58GA to 58GC extend the meaning of person for\npartnerships, unincorporated associations and trusts."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fa-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fa"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fa-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The Commission may perform an action.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58FB Appointment of inspectors",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.247",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An SPF regulator may, in writing, appoint a person who is one of\nthe following to be an inspector of that regulator for the purposes\nof one or more Subdivisions of this Division:\n\n(a) a person who is an employee of that regulator who:\n\n(i) is an SES employee or acting SES employee; or\n\n(ii) holds or performs the duties of an Executive Level 1 or\n2 position; or\n\n(iii) holds or performs the duties of a position that is\nequivalent to a position mentioned in subparagraph (i)\nor (ii);\n\n(b) a member or special member of the Australian Federal\nPolice.\n\n(2) However, the SPF regulator must not appoint a person as an\ninspector unless the SPF regulator is satisfied that the person has\nappropriate qualifications, training, skills or experience to exercise\nthe powers of an inspector.\n\n(3) A person must, in exercising powers as an inspector of an SPF\nregulator, comply with any directions of the SPF regulator that are\nof an administrative character.\n\n(4) If (and while) no appointments under subsection (1) by an SPF\nregulator are in force for the purposes of a Subdivision of this\nDivision, the SPF regulator is an inspector of the SPF regulator for\nthe purposes of that Subdivision.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An SPF regulator may, in writing, appoint a person who is one of\nthe following to be an inspector of that regulator for the purposes\nof one or more Subdivisions of this Division:\n\n(a) a person who is an employee of that regulator who:\n\n(i) is an SES employee or acting SES employee; or\n\n(ii) holds or performs the duties of an Executive Level 1 or\n2 position; or\n\n(iii) holds or performs the duties of a position that is\nequivalent to a position mentioned in subparagraph (i)\nor (ii);\n\n(b) a member or special member of the Australian Federal\nPolice.\n\n(2) However, the SPF regulator must not appoint a person as an\ninspector unless the SPF regulator is satisfied that the person has\nappropriate qualifications, training, skills or experience to exercise\nthe powers of an inspector.\n\n(3) A person must, in exercising powers as an inspector of an SPF\nregulator, comply with any directions of the SPF regulator that are\nof an administrative character.\n\n(4) If (and while) no appointments under subsection (1) by an SPF\nregulator are in force for the purposes of a Subdivision of this\nDivision, the SPF regulator is an inspector of the SPF regulator for\nthe purposes of that Subdivision.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fb-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fb-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fb-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "76d4e2163fac65cd6d2cb1476f34d2b765266493c3cd133368615c2994a2f345"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58FB Appointment of inspectors",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 247,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An SPF regulator may, in writing, appoint a person who is one of\nthe following to be an inspector of that regulator for the purposes\nof one or more Subdivisions of this Division:\n\n(a) a person who is an employee of that regulator who:\n\n(i) is an SES employee or acting SES employee; or\n\n(ii) holds or performs the duties of an Executive Level 1 or\n2 position; or\n\n(iii) holds or performs the duties of a position that is\nequivalent to a position mentioned in subparagraph (i)\nor (ii);\n\n(b) a member or special member of the Australian Federal\nPolice.\n\n(2) However, the SPF regulator must not appoint a person as an\ninspector unless the SPF regulator is satisfied that the person has\nappropriate qualifications, training, skills or experience to exercise\nthe powers of an inspector.\n\n(3) A person must, in exercising powers as an inspector of an SPF\nregulator, comply with any directions of the SPF regulator that are\nof an administrative character.\n\n(4) If (and while) no appointments under subsection (1) by an SPF\nregulator are in force for the purposes of a Subdivision of this\nDivision, the SPF regulator is an inspector of the SPF regulator for\nthe purposes of that Subdivision.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
