    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58FG Monitoring or investigating—the ACMA",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.252",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the ACMA is the SPF sector regulator for a\nregulated sector.\n\n(2) Part 26 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 also applies:\n\n(a) to the ACMA in the ACMA’s capacity as the SPF sector\nregulator; and\n\n(b) in relation to a contravention of the SPF code for the sector in\na corresponding way to the way that Part applies in relation\nto a contravention of that Act that does not relate to the\ncontent of a content service.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) Part 27 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 also applies:\n\n(a) to the ACMA in the ACMA’s capacity as the SPF sector\nregulator; and\n\n(b) in relation to the performance of any of the ACMA’s\nfunctions under the SPF code for the sector in a\ncorresponding way to the way that Part applies in relation to\nthe performance of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications\nfunctions; and\n\n(c) in relation to the exercise of any of the ACMA’s powers\nunder the SPF code for the sector in a corresponding way to\nthe way that Part applies in relation to the exercise of any of\nthe ACMA’s telecommunications powers.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this additional application of Parts 26 and 27 of\nthe Telecommunications Act 1997, the Minister may, by legislative\ninstrument, specify modifications of one or more provisions of\nthose Parts to remove any doubt about how those provisions apply\nin such a corresponding way in relation to the SPF code.\nNote:\nThe modifications are for this additional application of those Parts,\nand are not modifications of those Parts as they ordinarily apply.\n\n(4) The instrument has effect accordingly.\n\n(5) In this section:\nACMA’s telecommunications functions has the same meaning as\nin the Telecommunications Act 1997.\nACMA’s telecommunications powers has the same meaning as in\nthe Telecommunications Act 1997.\ncontent service has the same meaning as in the\nTelecommunications Act 1997.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if the ACMA is the SPF sector regulator for a\nregulated sector.\n\n(2) Part 26 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 also applies:\n\n(a) to the ACMA in the ACMA’s capacity as the SPF sector\nregulator; and\n\n(b) in relation to a contravention of the SPF code for the sector in\na corresponding way to the way that Part applies in relation\nto a contravention of that Act that does not relate to the\ncontent of a content service.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) Part 27 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 also applies:\n\n(a) to the ACMA in the ACMA’s capacity as the SPF sector\nregulator; and\n\n(b) in relation to the performance of any of the ACMA’s\nfunctions under the SPF code for the sector in a\ncorresponding way to the way that Part applies in relation to\nthe performance of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications\nfunctions; and\n\n(c) in relation to the exercise of any of the ACMA’s powers\nunder the SPF code for the sector in a corresponding way to\nthe way that Part applies in relation to the exercise of any of\nthe ACMA’s telecommunications powers.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this additional application of Parts 26 and 27 of\nthe Telecommunications Act 1997, the Minister may, by legislative\ninstrument, specify modifications of one or more provisions of\nthose Parts to remove any doubt about how those provisions apply\nin such a corresponding way in relation to the SPF code.\nNote:\nThe modifications are for this additional application of those Parts,\nand are not modifications of those Parts as they ordinarily apply.\n\n(4) The instrument has effect accordingly.\n\n(5) In this section:\nACMA’s telecommunications functions has the same meaning as\nin the Telecommunications Act 1997.\nACMA’s telecommunications powers has the same meaning as in\nthe Telecommunica",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fg-ss-1"
        },
