      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.252",
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of this additional application of Parts 26 and 27 of\nthe Telecommunications Act 1997, the Minister may, by legislative\ninstrument, specify modifications of one or more provisions of\nthose Parts to remove any doubt about how those provisions apply\nin such a corresponding way in relation to the SPF code.\nNote:\nThe modifications are for this additional application of those Parts,\nand are not modifications of those Parts as they ordinarily apply.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) For the purposes of this additional application of Parts 26 and 27 of\nthe Telecommunications Act 1997, the Minister may, by legislative\ninstrument, specify modifications of one or more provisions of\nthose Parts to remove any doubt about how those provisions apply\nin such a corresponding way in relation to the SPF code.\nNote:\nThe modifications are for this additional application of those Parts,\nand are not modifications of those Parts as they ordinarily apply.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fg"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fg-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fg-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "664f2f17af210da1c0fed7d77021b841721540a249f793b63abce2f4d6b6f907",
      "skos:note": "The Minister may specify modifications to remove doubt about how provisions apply in relation to the SPF code. Part 27 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 applies to ACMA in its capacity as SPF sector regulator and in relation to performance of functions under SPF code."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fg-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58FG(3) Monitoring or investigating—the ACMA",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 252,
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of this additional application of Parts 26 and 27 of\nthe Telecommunications Act 1997, the Minister may, by legislative\ninstrument, specify modifications of one or more provisions of\nthose Parts to remove any doubt about how those provisions apply\nin such a corresponding way in relation to the SPF code.\nNote:\nThe modifications are for this additional application of those Parts,\nand are not modifications of those Parts as they ordinarily apply."
    },
