    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fi",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58FI Monitoring or investigating—Minister may declare that",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fi"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.255",
      "values:originalText": "alternative powers apply for other SPF sector regulators\n\n(1) This section applies if provisions of another law (the alternative\npower provisions):\n\n(a) provide an entity with powers to:\n\n(i) monitor compliance or purported compliance with\nprovisions of a law (the alternative regulatory\nprovisions); or\n\n(ii) investigate provisions of a law (also the alternative\nregulatory provisions); or\n\n(b) enable the effective operation and enforcement of such\npowers.\nNote:\nParagraph (b) covers, for example, a provision making it an offence to\nfail to appear to answer questions in relation to an investigation.\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that specified\nalternative power provisions (that relate to a specified entity and\nspecified alternative regulatory provisions) also apply:\n\n(a) to the entity in the entity’s capacity as the SPF sector\nregulator for a regulated sector; and\n\n(b) in relation to specified provisions of the SPF code for the\nsector in a corresponding way to the way the alternative\npower provisions apply in relation to the alternative\nregulatory provisions.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this additional application of the alternative\npower provisions, the instrument may specify modifications of one\nor more of those provisions to remove any doubt about how those\nprovisions apply in such a corresponding way in relation to the\nspecified provisions of the SPF code.\nNote:\nThe modifications are for this additional application of the alternative\npower provisions, and are not modifications of those provisions as\nthey ordinarily apply.\n\n(4) The instrument has effect accordingly.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "alternative powers apply for other SPF sector regulators\n\n(1) This section applies if provisions of another law (the alternative\npower provisions):\n\n(a) provide an entity with powers to:\n\n(i) monitor compliance or purported compliance with\nprovisions of a law (the alternative regulatory\nprovisions); or\n\n(ii) investigate provisions of a law (also the alternative\nregulatory provisions); or\n\n(b) enable the effective operation and enforcement of such\npowers.\nNote:\nParagraph (b) covers, for example, a provision making it an offence to\nfail to appear to answer questions in relation to an investigation.\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that specified\nalternative power provisions (that relate to a specified entity and\nspecified alternative regulatory provisions) also apply:\n\n(a) to the entity in the entity’s capacity as the SPF sector\nregulator for a regulated sector; and\n\n(b) in relation to specified provisions of the SPF code for the\nsector in a corresponding way to the way the alternative\npower provisions apply in relation to the alternative\nregulatory provisions.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this additional application of the alternative\npower provisions, the instrument may specify modifications of one\nor more of those provisions to remove any doubt about how those\nprovisions apply in such a corresponding way in relation to the\nspecified provisions of the SPF code.\nNote:\nThe modifications are for this additional application of the alternative\npower provisions, and are not modifications of those provisions as\nthey ordinarily apply.\n\n(4) The instrument has effect accordingly.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fi-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fi-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fi-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fi-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "43ccfbcfe58dc4f6a84729d08808be645d2d90e1bf07e272a0559e605a4b808b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fi",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58FI Monitoring or investigating—Minister may declare that",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 255,
      "values:originalText": "alternative powers apply for other SPF sector regulators\n\n(1) This section applies if provisions of another law (the alternative\npower provisions):\n\n(a) provide an entity with powers to:\n\n(i) monitor compliance or purported compliance with\nprovisions of a law (the alternative regulatory\nprovisions); or\n\n(ii) investigate provisions of a law (also the alternative\nregulatory provisions); or\n\n(b) enable the effective operation and enforcement of such\npowers.\nNote:\nParagraph (b) covers, for example, a provision making it an offence to\nfail to appear to answer questions in relation to an investigation.\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that specified\nalternative power provisions (that relate to a specified entity and\nspecified alternative regulatory provisions) also apply:\n\n(a) to the entity in the entity’s capacity as the SPF sector\nregulator for a regulated sector; and\n\n(b) in relation to specified provisions of the SPF code for the\nsector in a corresponding way to the way the alternative\npower provisions apply in relation to the alternative\nregulatory provisions.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this additional application of the alternative\npower provisions, the instrument may specify modifications of one\nor more of those provisions to remove any doubt about how those\nprovisions apply in such a corresponding way in relation to the\nspecified provisions of the SPF code.\nNote:\nThe modifications are for this additional application of the alternative\npower provisions, and are not modifications of those provisions as\nthey ordinarily apply.\n\n(4) The instrument has effect accordingly.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fi-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58FI(1) Monitoring or investigating—Minister may declare that",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fi-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.255",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if provisions of another law (the alternative\npower provisions):\n\n(a) provide an entity with powers to:\n\n(i) monitor compliance or purported compliance with\nprovisions of a law (the alternative regulatory\nprovisions); or\n\n(ii) investigate provisions of a law (also the alternative\nregulatory provisions); or\n\n(b) enable the effective operation and enforcement of such\npowers.\nNote:\nParagraph (b) covers, for example, a provision making it an offence to\nfail to appear to answer questions in relation to an investigation.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if provisions of another law (the alternative\npower provisions):\n\n(a) provide an entity with powers to:\n\n(i) monitor compliance or purported compliance with\nprovisions of a law (the alternative regulatory\nprovisions); or\n\n(ii) investigate provisions of a law (also the alternative\nregulatory provisions); or\n\n(b) enable the effective operation and enforcement of such\npowers.\nNote:\nParagraph (b) covers, for example, a provision making it an offence to\nfail to appear to answer questions in relation to an investigation.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fi"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fi-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fi-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d81c9c5618b46eeb1848d0dd50e1c725d05d93532e3f7fe5154bcf136aeb655d",
      "skos:note": "The Minister may declare that the provisions of another law provide an entity with powers to monitor compliance or investigate provisions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fi-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58FI(1) Monitoring or investigating—Minister may declare that",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 255,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if provisions of another law (the alternative\npower provisions):\n\n(a) provide an entity with powers to:\n\n(i) monitor compliance or purported compliance with\nprovisions of a law (the alternative regulatory\nprovisions); or\n\n(ii) investigate provisions of a law (also the alternative\nregulatory provisions); or\n\n(b) enable the effective operation and enforcement of such\npowers.\nNote:\nParagraph (b) covers, for example, a provision making it an offence to\nfail to appear to answer questions in relation to an investigation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fi-ss-1-norm",
