      "cml:premiseText": "Part 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act allows a civil penalty provision to be enforced",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The provision is allowed under Part 4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fj-ss-1-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "authorized",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation authorization",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Part 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act allows an authorized applicant to enforce a civil penalty provision",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The applicant is authorized to enforce the provision"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fj-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58FJ(2) Civil penalty provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fj-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.256",
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purposes of Part 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act:\n\n(a) the SPF general regulator is an authorised applicant in\nrelation to each civil penalty provision of an SPF principle;\nand\n\n(b) the SPF sector regulator for a regulated sector is an\nauthorised applicant in relation to each civil penalty\nprovision of the SPF code for the sector.\nRelevant court",
      "skos:definition": "(2) For the purposes of Part 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act:\n\n(a) the SPF general regulator is an authorised applicant in\nrelation to each civil penalty provision of an SPF principle;\nand\n\n(b) the SPF sector regulator for a regulated sector is an\nauthorised applicant in relation to each civil penalty\nprovision of the SPF code for the sector.\nRelevant court",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fj"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fj-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fj-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bafd69bbd6716893fd7f154c8ca4b13e9b86297b1a2b08fe74c311811983ded8",
      "skos:note": "SPF general regulator and sector regulator are authorised applicants for civil penalty provisions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fj-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58FJ(2) Civil penalty provisions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 256,
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purposes of Part 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act:\n\n(a) the SPF general regulator is an authorised applicant in\nrelation to each civil penalty provision of an SPF principle;\nand\n\n(b) the SPF sector regulator for a regulated sector is an\nauthorised applicant in relation to each civil penalty\nprovision of the SPF code for the sector.\nRelevant court"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fj-ss-2-norm",
