      "cml:premiseText": "SPF general regulator and sector regulator are SPF applicants",
      "cml:conclusionText": "are authorized applicants"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fj-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58FJ(3) Civil penalty provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fj-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.256",
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of Part 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act, each of\nthe following courts is a relevant court in relation to each provision\nreferred to in subsection (1):\n\n(a) the Federal Court;\n\n(b) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2);\n\n(c) a court of a State or Territory that has jurisdiction in relation\nto the matter.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FK\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(3) For the purposes of Part 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act, each of\nthe following courts is a relevant court in relation to each provision\nreferred to in subsection (1):\n\n(a) the Federal Court;\n\n(b) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2);\n\n(c) a court of a State or Territory that has jurisdiction in relation\nto the matter.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FK\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fj"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fj-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fj-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f30adad6dee0e14b4f1987b29dd7fe21caa5653808f5f856215c4375a5a715f8",
      "skos:note": "List of relevant courts for purposes of Part 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fj-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58FJ(3) Civil penalty provisions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 256,
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of Part 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act, each of\nthe following courts is a relevant court in relation to each provision\nreferred to in subsection (1):\n\n(a) the Federal Court;\n\n(b) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2);\n\n(c) a court of a State or Territory that has jurisdiction in relation\nto the matter.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FK\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fj-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fj-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
