    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fm",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58FM Civil penalty double jeopardy",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fm"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.258",
      "values:originalText": "If a person is ordered under an SPF civil penalty order to pay a\npecuniary penalty in respect of particular conduct, the person is not\nliable to:\n\n(a) a pecuniary penalty for contravening another civil penalty\nprovision of an SPF principle or of an SPF code; or\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FN\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) a pecuniary penalty under some other provision of a law of\nthe Commonwealth;\nin respect of that conduct.\nNote:\nA court may make other kinds of orders under this Division, for\nexample under section 58FZC (actions for damages), in relation to\nparticular conduct even if the court has made an SPF civil penalty\norder in relation to that conduct.\nSubdivision D—Infringement notices",
      "skos:definition": "If a person is ordered under an SPF civil penalty order to pay a\npecuniary penalty in respect of particular conduct, the person is not\nliable to:\n\n(a) a pecuniary penalty for contravening another civil penalty\nprovision of an SPF principle or of an SPF code; or\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FN\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) a pecuniary penalty under some other provision of a law of\nthe Commonwealth;\nin respect of that conduct.\nNote:\nA court may make other kinds of orders under this Division, for\nexample under section 58FZC (actions for damages), in relation to\nparticular conduct even if the court has made an SPF civil penalty\norder in relation to that conduct.\nSubdivision D—Infringement notices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fm-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fm-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dbb832870deab07bb026cea545f969141690cab3de7187a14acb15db06569f7d",
      "skos:note": "No liability for pecuniary penalty in respect of particular conduct"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fm",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58FM Civil penalty double jeopardy",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 258,
      "values:originalText": "If a person is ordered under an SPF civil penalty order to pay a\npecuniary penalty in respect of particular conduct, the person is not\nliable to:\n\n(a) a pecuniary penalty for contravening another civil penalty\nprovision of an SPF principle or of an SPF code; or\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FN\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) a pecuniary penalty under some other provision of a law of\nthe Commonwealth;\nin respect of that conduct.\nNote:\nA court may make other kinds of orders under this Division, for\nexample under section 58FZC (actions for damages), in relation to\nparticular conduct even if the court has made an SPF civil penalty\norder in relation to that conduct.\nSubdivision D—Infringement notices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fm-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fm"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fm-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Classifies the legal effect as an obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fn",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58FN Purpose and effect of this Subdivision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fn"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.259",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The purpose of this Subdivision is to provide for the issue of an\ninfringement notice to a person for an alleged contravention of:\n\n(a) a civil penalty provision of an SPF principle in Subdivision B\nor E of Division 2 of this Part; or\n\n(b) a civil penalty provision of an SPF code;\nas an alternative to proceedings for an SPF civil penalty order.\n\n(2) This Subdivision does not:\n\n(a) require an SPF infringement notice to be issued for an\nalleged contravention of such a civil penalty provision; or\n\n(b) affect a person’s liability to proceedings for an SPF civil\npenalty order in relation to an alleged contravention of a civil\npenalty provision if:\n\n(i) an SPF infringement notice is not issued to the person\nfor the contravention; or\n\n(ii) an SPF infringement notice issued to the person for the\ncontravention is withdrawn under section 58FU; or\n\n(c) prevent a court from imposing a higher penalty than the\npenalty specified in the SPF infringement notice if the person\ndoes not comply with the notice.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The purpose of this Subdivision is to provide for the issue of an\ninfringement notice to a person for an alleged contravention of:\n\n(a) a civil penalty provision of an SPF principle in Subdivision B\nor E of Division 2 of this Part; or\n\n(b) a civil penalty provision of an SPF code;\nas an alternative to proceedings for an SPF civil penalty order.\n\n(2) This Subdivision does not:\n\n(a) require an SPF infringement notice to be issued for an\nalleged contravention of such a civil penalty provision; or\n\n(b) affect a person’s liability to proceedings for an SPF civil\npenalty order in relation to an alleged contravention of a civil\npenalty provision if:\n\n(i) an SPF infringement notice is not issued to the person\nfor the contravention; or\n\n(ii) an SPF infringement notice issued to the person for the\ncontravention is withdrawn under section 58FU; or\n\n(c) prevent a court from imposing a higher penalty than the\npenalty specified in the SPF infringement notice if the person\ndoes not comply with the notice.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fn-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fn-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a7cdeff9a37509438c463d3d22c9b764bf557821fdd9ce2d653178c13955eb95"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fn",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58FN Purpose and effect of this Subdivision",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 259,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The purpose of this Subdivision is to provide for the issue of an\ninfringement notice to a person for an alleged contravention of:\n\n(a) a civil penalty provision of an SPF principle in Subdivision B\nor E of Division 2 of this Part; or\n\n(b) a civil penalty provision of an SPF code;\nas an alternative to proceedings for an SPF civil penalty order.\n\n(2) This Subdivision does not:\n\n(a) require an SPF infringement notice to be issued for an\nalleged contravention of such a civil penalty provision; or\n\n(b) affect a person’s liability to proceedings for an SPF civil\npenalty order in relation to an alleged contravention of a civil\npenalty provision if:\n\n(i) an SPF infringement notice is not issued to the person\nfor the contravention; or\n\n(ii) an SPF infringement notice issued to the person for the\ncontravention is withdrawn under section 58FU; or\n\n(c) prevent a court from imposing a higher penalty than the\npenalty specified in the SPF infringement notice if the person\ndoes not comply with the notice.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
