    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fn-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "exemption",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Exempts from liability",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) This Subdivision does not:\n\n(a) require an SPF infringement notice to be issued for an\nalleged contravention of such a civil penalty provision;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "A person is exempt from liability."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fn-ss-2-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "permission",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permits withdrawal of infringement notice",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) This Subdivision does not:\n\n(ii) an SPF infringement notice issued to the person for the\ncrime is withdrawn under section 58FU;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The subdivision permits the withdrawal of the infringement notice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fn-ss-2-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "permission",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permits non-compliance with notice",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) This Subdivision does not:\n\n(c) prevent a court from imposing a higher penalty than the\npenalty specified in the SPF infringement notice if the person\ndoes not comply with the notice.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The subdivision permits non-compliance with the notice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fn-ss-2-logic-linearlogic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LinearLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "and",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Combines exemptions and permissions",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) This Subdivision does not:\n\n(a) require an SPF infringement notice to be issued for an\nalleged contravention of such a civil penalty provision; or\n\n(b) affect a person’s liability to proceedings for an SPF civil\npenalty order in relation to an alleged contravention of a civil\npenalty provision if:",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The subdivision combines exemptions and permissions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fo",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58FO Issuing an SPF infringement notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fo"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.260",
      "values:originalText": "Notices for contraventions of certain SPF principles\n\n(1) If an inspector of the SPF general regulator reasonably believes\nthat a person has contravened a civil penalty provision of an SPF\nprinciple in Subdivision B or E of Division 2 of this Part, the\ninspector may issue a notice (an SPF infringement notice) to the\nperson.\nNotices for contraventions of SPF codes\n\n(2) If an inspector of the SPF sector regulator for a regulated sector\nreasonably believes that a person has contravened a civil penalty\nprovision of the SPF code for the sector, the inspector may issue a\nnotice (an SPF infringement notice) to the person.\nOnly one notice for each contravention\n\n(3) Inspectors for an SPF regulator must not issue more than one SPF\ninfringement notice to the person for the same alleged\ncontravention of a civil penalty provision.\nWhen notices do not have any effect\n\n(4) An SPF infringement notice does not have any effect if the notice:\n\n(a) is issued more than 12 months after the day that the relevant\ncontravention is alleged to have occurred; or\n\n(b) relates to more than one alleged contravention of a civil\npenalty provision by the person.",
      "skos:definition": "Notices for contraventions of certain SPF principles\n\n(1) If an inspector of the SPF general regulator reasonably believes\nthat a person has contravened a civil penalty provision of an SPF\nprinciple in Subdivision B or E of Division 2 of this Part, the\ninspector may issue a notice (an SPF infringement notice) to the\nperson.\nNotices for contraventions of SPF codes\n\n(2) If an inspector of the SPF sector regulator for a regulated sector\nreasonably believes that a person has contravened a civil penalty\nprovision of the SPF code for the sector, the inspector may issue a\nnotice (an SPF infringement notice) to the person.\nOnly one notice for each contravention\n\n(3) Inspectors for an SPF regulator must not issue more than one SPF\ninfringement notice to the person for the same alleged\ncontravention of a civil penalty provision.\nWhen notices do not have any effect\n\n(4) An SPF infringement notice does not have any effect if the notice:\n\n(a) is issued more than 12 months after the day that the relevant\ncontravention is alleged to have occurred; or\n\n(b) relates to more than one alleged contravention of a civil\npenalty provision by the person.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fo-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fo-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fo-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fo-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f2a7a7a08aefba2cdfc000042c42bb04ccbb86aad9547fa132a73f7559586529"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fo",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58FO Issuing an SPF infringement notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 260,
      "values:originalText": "Notices for contraventions of certain SPF principles\n\n(1) If an inspector of the SPF general regulator reasonably believes\nthat a person has contravened a civil penalty provision of an SPF\nprinciple in Subdivision B or E of Division 2 of this Part, the\ninspector may issue a notice (an SPF infringement notice) to the\nperson.\nNotices for contraventions of SPF codes\n\n(2) If an inspector of the SPF sector regulator for a regulated sector\nreasonably believes that a person has contravened a civil penalty\nprovision of the SPF code for the sector, the inspector may issue a\nnotice (an SPF infringement notice) to the person.\nOnly one notice for each contravention\n\n(3) Inspectors for an SPF regulator must not issue more than one SPF\ninfringement notice to the person for the same alleged\ncontravention of a civil penalty provision.\nWhen notices do not have any effect\n\n(4) An SPF infringement notice does not have any effect if the notice:\n\n(a) is issued more than 12 months after the day that the relevant\ncontravention is alleged to have occurred; or\n\n(b) relates to more than one alleged contravention of a civil\npenalty provision by the person."
    },
