      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.260",
      "values:originalText": "An SPF infringement notice must:\n\n(a) be identified by a unique number; and\n\n(b) state the day on which it is issued; and\n\n(c) state the name of the person to whom it is issued; and\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FQ\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(d) state the name of the inspector who issued the notice, that the\ninspector is an inspector of the applicable SPF regulator, and\nhow that SPF regulator may be contacted; and\n\n(e) give details of the alleged contravention, including:\n\n(i) the day of the alleged contravention; and\n\n(ii) the civil penalty provision that was allegedly\ncontravened; and\n\n(f) state the maximum pecuniary penalty that a court could order\nthe person to pay if the court were to make an SPF civil\npenalty order for the alleged contravention; and\n\n(g) specify the penalty that is payable in relation to the alleged\ncontravention; and\n\n(h) state that the penalty is payable within the infringement\nnotice compliance period for the notice; and\n\n(i) state that the penalty is payable to the SPF regulator on\nbehalf of the Commonwealth; and\n\n(j) explain how payment of the penalty is to be made; and\n\n(k) explain the effect of sections 58FR to 58FU.",
      "skos:definition": "An SPF infringement notice must:\n\n(a) be identified by a unique number; and\n\n(b) state the day on which it is issued; and\n\n(c) state the name of the person to whom it is issued; and\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FQ\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(d) state the name of the inspector who issued the notice, that the\ninspector is an inspector of the applicable SPF regulator, and\nhow that SPF regulator may be contacted; and\n\n(e) give details of the alleged contravention, including:\n\n(i) the day of the alleged contravention; and\n\n(ii) the civil penalty provision that was allegedly\ncontravened; and\n\n(f) state the maximum pecuniary penalty that a court could order\nthe person to pay if the court were to make an SPF civil\npenalty order for the alleged contravention; and\n\n(g) specify the penalty that is payable in relation to the alleged\ncontravention; and\n\n(h) state that the penalty is payable within the infringement\nnotice compliance period for the notice; and\n\n(i) state that the penalty is payable to the SPF regulator on\nbehalf of the Commonwealth; and\n\n(j) explain how payment of the penalty is to be made; and\n\n(k) explain the effect of sections 58FR to 58FU.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fp-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fp-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "739bb31c56be91fa1ade36f203fdd6e11f7a349cdb5f009bf9a2ea65f9d6fac6",
      "skos:note": "Mandatory requirements for an SPF infringement notice",
      "dc:description": "a unique number, day of issue, name of person to whom issued, inspector's details, alleged contravention details, penalty information, and payment instructions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fp",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58FP Matters to be included in an SPF infringement notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 260,
      "values:originalText": "An SPF infringement notice must:\n\n(a) be identified by a unique number; and\n\n(b) state the day on which it is issued; and\n\n(c) state the name of the person to whom it is issued; and\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FQ\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(d) state the name of the inspector who issued the notice, that the\ninspector is an inspector of the applicable SPF regulator, and\nhow that SPF regulator may be contacted; and\n\n(e) give details of the alleged contravention, including:\n\n(i) the day of the alleged contravention; and\n\n(ii) the civil penalty provision that was allegedly\ncontravened; and\n\n(f) state the maximum pecuniary penalty that a court could order\nthe person to pay if the court were to make an SPF civil\npenalty order for the alleged contravention; and\n\n(g) specify the penalty that is payable in relation to the alleged\ncontravention; and\n\n(h) state that the penalty is payable within the infringement\nnotice compliance period for the notice; and\n\n(i) state that the penalty is payable to the SPF regulator on\nbehalf of the Commonwealth; and\n\n(j) explain how payment of the penalty is to be made; and\n\n(k) explain the effect of sections 58FR to 58FU."
    },
    {
