      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fs-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to pay penalty",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Notice specifies penalty amount and compliance period.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Failure to comply results in liability."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fs-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "within",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Compliance period must be within infringement notice period",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Notice specifies compliance period.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Compliance period overlaps with infringement notice period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ft",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58FT Infringement notice compliance period for infringement notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ft"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.262",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to this section, the infringement notice compliance period,\nfor an SPF infringement notice issued to a person, is the period of\n28 days beginning on the day after the day that the notice is so\nissued by an inspector of an SPF regulator.\n\n(2) The SPF regulator may, by giving written notice to the person,\nextend that infringement notice compliance period if the SPF\nregulator is satisfied that it is appropriate to do so.\n\n(3) Only one extension may be given and the extension must not be for\nlonger than 28 days.\n\n(4) A failure to give the person written notice of the extension does not\naffect the validity of the extension.\n\n(5) If an infringement notice compliance period for an SPF\ninfringement notice is extended under this section, a reference in\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FU\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthis Subdivision to the infringement notice compliance period is\ntaken to be a reference to that period as so extended.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to this section, the infringement notice compliance period,\nfor an SPF infringement notice issued to a person, is the period of\n28 days beginning on the day after the day that the notice is so\nissued by an inspector of an SPF regulator.\n\n(2) The SPF regulator may, by giving written notice to the person,\nextend that infringement notice compliance period if the SPF\nregulator is satisfied that it is appropriate to do so.\n\n(3) Only one extension may be given and the extension must not be for\nlonger than 28 days.\n\n(4) A failure to give the person written notice of the extension does not\naffect the validity of the extension.\n\n(5) If an infringement notice compliance period for an SPF\ninfringement notice is extended under this section, a reference in\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FU\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthis Subdivision to the infringement notice compliance period is\ntaken to be a reference to that period as so extended.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ft-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ft-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ft-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ft-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ft-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "01d52c781a4e11cda45c6021f5bd326b76c168e8203efbac7aad9c6cb325924c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ft",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58FT Infringement notice compliance period for infringement notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 262,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to this section, the infringement notice compliance period,\nfor an SPF infringement notice issued to a person, is the period of\n28 days beginning on the day after the day that the notice is so\nissued by an inspector of an SPF regulator.\n\n(2) The SPF regulator may, by giving written notice to the person,\nextend that infringement notice compliance period if the SPF\nregulator is satisfied that it is appropriate to do so.\n\n(3) Only one extension may be given and the extension must not be for\nlonger than 28 days.\n\n(4) A failure to give the person written notice of the extension does not\naffect the validity of the extension.\n\n(5) If an infringement notice compliance period for an SPF\ninfringement notice is extended under this section, a reference in\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FU\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthis Subdivision to the infringement notice compliance period is\ntaken to be a reference to that period as so extended."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ft-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58FT(1) Infringement notice compliance period for infringement notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ft-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.262",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to this section, the infringement notice compliance period,\nfor an SPF infringement notice issued to a person, is the period of\n28 days beginning on the day after the day that the notice is so\nissued by an inspector of an SPF regulator.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to this section, the infringement notice compliance period,\nfor an SPF infringement notice issued to a person, is the period of\n28 days beginning on the day after the day that the notice is so\nissued by an inspector of an SPF regulator.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ft"
      },
