    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fx",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58FX Particular kinds of injunctions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fx"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.266",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Court may grant an injunction under section 58FW restraining\na person from engaging in conduct:\n\n(a) whether or not it appears to the Court that the person intends\nto engage again, or to continue to engage, in conduct of that\nkind; and\n\n(b) whether or not the person has previously engaged in conduct\nof that kind; and\n\n(c) whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial\ndamage to any person if the first-mentioned person engages\nin conduct of that kind.\n\n(2) The Court may grant an injunction under section 58FW requiring a\nperson to do an act or thing:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FY\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) whether or not it appears to the Court that the person intends\nto refuse or fail again, or to continue to refuse or fail, to do\nthat act or thing; and\n\n(b) whether or not the person has previously refused or failed to\ndo that act or thing; and\n\n(c) whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial\ndamage to any person if the first-mentioned person refuses or\nfails to do that act or thing.\n\n(3) The Court may grant an injunction under section 58FW by consent\nof all the parties to the proceedings whether or not the Court is\nsatisfied that a person has engaged, or is proposing to engage, in\nconduct of a kind mentioned in that section.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Court may grant an injunction under section 58FW restraining\na person from engaging in conduct:\n\n(a) whether or not it appears to the Court that the person intends\nto engage again, or to continue to engage, in conduct of that\nkind; and\n\n(b) whether or not the person has previously engaged in conduct\nof that kind; and\n\n(c) whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial\ndamage to any person if the first-mentioned person engages\nin conduct of that kind.\n\n(2) The Court may grant an injunction under section 58FW requiring a\nperson to do an act or thing:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FY\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) whether or not it appears to the Court that the person intends\nto refuse or fail again, or to continue to refuse or fail, to do\nthat act or thing; and\n\n(b) whether or not the person has previously refused or failed to\ndo that act or thing; and\n\n(c) whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial\ndamage to any person if the first-mentioned person refuses or\nfails to do that act or thing.\n\n(3) The Court may grant an injunction under section 58FW by consent\nof all the parties to the proceedings whether or not the Court is\nsatisfied that a person has engaged, or is proposing to engage, in\nconduct of a kind mentioned in that section.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fx-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fx-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fx-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7ee61fef37cb5949bf562018abd7ba6efb29943060c4c0703c5485483bf6bbdb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fx",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58FX Particular kinds of injunctions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 266,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Court may grant an injunction under section 58FW restraining\na person from engaging in conduct:\n\n(a) whether or not it appears to the Court that the person intends\nto engage again, or to continue to engage, in conduct of that\nkind; and\n\n(b) whether or not the person has previously engaged in conduct\nof that kind; and\n\n(c) whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial\ndamage to any person if the first-mentioned person engages\nin conduct of that kind.\n\n(2) The Court may grant an injunction under section 58FW requiring a\nperson to do an act or thing:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FY\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) whether or not it appears to the Court that the person intends\nto refuse or fail again, or to continue to refuse or fail, to do\nthat act or thing; and\n\n(b) whether or not the person has previously refused or failed to\ndo that act or thing; and\n\n(c) whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial\ndamage to any person if the first-mentioned person refuses or\nfails to do that act or thing.\n\n(3) The Court may grant an injunction under section 58FW by consent\nof all the parties to the proceedings whether or not the Court is\nsatisfied that a person has engaged, or is proposing to engage, in\nconduct of a kind mentioned in that section."
    },
