      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.266",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Court may grant an injunction under section 58FW requiring a\nperson to do an act or thing:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FY\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) whether or not it appears to the Court that the person intends\nto refuse or fail again, or to continue to refuse or fail, to do\nthat act or thing; and\n\n(b) whether or not the person has previously refused or failed to\ndo that act or thing; and\n\n(c) whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial\ndamage to any person if the first-mentioned person refuses or\nfails to do that act or thing.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Court may grant an injunction under section 58FW requiring a\nperson to do an act or thing:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FY\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) whether or not it appears to the Court that the person intends\nto refuse or fail again, or to continue to refuse or fail, to do\nthat act or thing; and\n\n(b) whether or not the person has previously refused or failed to\ndo that act or thing; and\n\n(c) whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial\ndamage to any person if the first-mentioned person refuses or\nfails to do that act or thing.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fx"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fx-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fx-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "20cedd546e44eead6b1044ff96a81596c0276698402b7966d300af449fdca739",
      "skos:note": "Court may grant injunction requiring a person to do an act or thing under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fx-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58FX(2) Particular kinds of injunctions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 266,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Court may grant an injunction under section 58FW requiring a\nperson to do an act or thing:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nEnforcing the Scams Prevention Framework  Division 6\n\nSection 58FY\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) whether or not it appears to the Court that the person intends\nto refuse or fail again, or to continue to refuse or fail, to do\nthat act or thing; and\n\n(b) whether or not the person has previously refused or failed to\ndo that act or thing; and\n\n(c) whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial\ndamage to any person if the first-mentioned person refuses or\nfails to do that act or thing."
    },
