    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fz",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58FZ Rescinding or varying injunctions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fz"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.267",
      "values:originalText": "The Court may rescind or vary an injunction granted under this\nSubdivision.\n58FZA  Applying for injunctions\n\n(1) An application for an injunction under this Subdivision may be\nmade by an SPF regulator or any other person.\n\n(2) If an SPF regulator applies for such an injunction, the Court must\nnot require the applicant or any other person, as a condition of\ngranting an interim injunction, to give any undertakings as to\ndamages.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) a person other than an SPF regulator:\n\n(i) applies for such an injunction; and\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "The Court may rescind or vary an injunction granted under this\nSubdivision.\n58FZA  Applying for injunctions\n\n(1) An application for an injunction under this Subdivision may be\nmade by an SPF regulator or any other person.\n\n(2) If an SPF regulator applies for such an injunction, the Court must\nnot require the applicant or any other person, as a condition of\ngranting an interim injunction, to give any undertakings as to\ndamages.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) a person other than an SPF regulator:\n\n(i) applies for such an injunction; and\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fz-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fz-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58fz-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "28462d416566522c722b8d171a12258648a22206f504076ec634cc67859d1ed4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58fz",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58FZ Rescinding or varying injunctions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 267,
      "values:originalText": "The Court may rescind or vary an injunction granted under this\nSubdivision.\n58FZA  Applying for injunctions\n\n(1) An application for an injunction under this Subdivision may be\nmade by an SPF regulator or any other person.\n\n(2) If an SPF regulator applies for such an injunction, the Court must\nnot require the applicant or any other person, as a condition of\ngranting an interim injunction, to give any undertakings as to\ndamages.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) a person other than an SPF regulator:\n\n(i) applies for such an injunction; and\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
