        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58ga-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bad72a3bf715539f2e2822bfbcb374abc1c2fc2964c65faece974494ee940e1e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58ga",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58GA Treatment of partnerships",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 283,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The SPF provisions apply to a partnership as if it were a person,\nbut with the changes set out in this section.\n\n(2) An obligation that would otherwise be imposed on the partnership\nby an SPF provision is imposed on each partner instead, but may\nbe discharged by any of the partners.\n\n(3) If an SPF provision would otherwise permit something to be done\nby the partnership, the thing may be done by one or more of the\npartners on behalf of the partnership.\n\n(4) For the purposes of the SPF provisions, a change in the\ncomposition of a partnership does not affect the continuity of the\npartnership."
    },
