    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58gd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58GD Compensation for acquisition of property",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58gd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.284",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the operation of the SPF provisions would\nresult in an acquisition of property (within the meaning of\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution) from a person otherwise\nthan on just terms (within the meaning of that paragraph).\n\n(2) The person who acquires the property is liable to pay a reasonable\namount of compensation to the first-mentioned person.\n\n(3) If the 2 persons do not agree on the amount of the compensation,\nthe person to whom compensation is payable may institute\nproceedings in:\n\n(a) the Federal Court; or\n\n(b) the Supreme Court of a State or Territory;\nfor the recovery from the other person of such reasonable amount\nof compensation as the Court determines.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nOther provisions  Division 7\n\nSection 58GE\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if the operation of the SPF provisions would\nresult in an acquisition of property (within the meaning of\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution) from a person otherwise\nthan on just terms (within the meaning of that paragraph).\n\n(2) The person who acquires the property is liable to pay a reasonable\namount of compensation to the first-mentioned person.\n\n(3) If the 2 persons do not agree on the amount of the compensation,\nthe person to whom compensation is payable may institute\nproceedings in:\n\n(a) the Federal Court; or\n\n(b) the Supreme Court of a State or Territory;\nfor the recovery from the other person of such reasonable amount\nof compensation as the Court determines.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nOther provisions  Division 7\n\nSection 58GE\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58gd-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58gd-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-58gd-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "57523af282865f6c5c11aa8baada8c90e7483ea809572608221684874433974b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-58gd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58GD Compensation for acquisition of property",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 284,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the operation of the SPF provisions would\nresult in an acquisition of property (within the meaning of\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution) from a person otherwise\nthan on just terms (within the meaning of that paragraph).\n\n(2) The person who acquires the property is liable to pay a reasonable\namount of compensation to the first-mentioned person.\n\n(3) If the 2 persons do not agree on the amount of the compensation,\nthe person to whom compensation is payable may institute\nproceedings in:\n\n(a) the Federal Court; or\n\n(b) the Supreme Court of a State or Territory;\nfor the recovery from the other person of such reasonable amount\nof compensation as the Court determines.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nScams Prevention Framework  Part IVF\nOther provisions  Division 7\n\nSection 58GE\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
