    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-60"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.287",
      "values:originalText": "•\nAn entity must not engage in price exploitation in relation to\nthe carbon tax repeal.\n•\nThe Commission may monitor prices in relation to the carbon\ntax repeal and the carbon tax scheme.\n•\nAn entity must not make false or misleading representations\nabout the effect of the carbon tax repeal, or the carbon tax\nscheme, on the price for the supply of goods or services.\n•\nAn entity that sells electricity or natural gas, or an entity that\nis a bulk SGG importer and sells synthetic greenhouse gas,\nwill be required to explain and substantiate:\n\n(a)\nhow the carbon tax repeal has affected, or is affecting,\nthe entity’s regulated supply input costs; and\n\n(b)\nhow reductions in the entity’s regulated supply input\ncosts that are directly or indirectly attributable to the\ncarbon tax repeal are reflected in the prices charged by\nthe entity for regulated supplies of electricity, natural\ngas or synthetic greenhouse gas.\n•\nAn entity that sells electricity or natural gas to customers, or\nan entity that is a bulk SGG importer and sells synthetic\ngreenhouse gas to customers, must:\n\n(a)\ngive a carbon tax removal substantiation statement to the\nCommission; and\n\n(b)\ninclude in the statement the entity’s estimate, on an\naverage annual percentage price basis, or an average\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "•\nAn entity must not engage in price exploitation in relation to\nthe carbon tax repeal.\n•\nThe Commission may monitor prices in relation to the carbon\ntax repeal and the carbon tax scheme.\n•\nAn entity must not make false or misleading representations\nabout the effect of the carbon tax repeal, or the carbon tax\nscheme, on the price for the supply of goods or services.\n•\nAn entity that sells electricity or natural gas, or an entity that\nis a bulk SGG importer and sells synthetic greenhouse gas,\nwill be required to explain and substantiate:\n\n(a)\nhow the carbon tax repeal has affected, or is affecting,\nthe entity’s regulated supply input costs; and\n\n(b)\nhow reductions in the entity’s regulated supply input\ncosts that are directly or indirectly attributable to the\ncarbon tax repeal are reflected in the prices charged by\nthe entity for regulated supplies of electricity, natural\ngas or synthetic greenhouse gas.\n•\nAn entity that sells electricity or natural gas to customers, or\nan entity that is a bulk SGG importer and sells synthetic\ngreenhouse gas to customers, must:\n\n(a)\ngive a carbon tax removal substantiation statement to the\nCommission; and\n\n(b)\ninclude in the statement the entity’s estimate, on an\naverage annual percentage price basis, or an average\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ebbf75e1f85fb44fe7272db428c82355c6f72135694f44af352f8ede89f2270d",
      "skos:note": "Entity must not engage in price exploitation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-60",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "60 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 287,
      "values:originalText": "•\nAn entity must not engage in price exploitation in relation to\nthe carbon tax repeal.\n•\nThe Commission may monitor prices in relation to the carbon\ntax repeal and the carbon tax scheme.\n•\nAn entity must not make false or misleading representations\nabout the effect of the carbon tax repeal, or the carbon tax\nscheme, on the price for the supply of goods or services.\n•\nAn entity that sells electricity or natural gas, or an entity that\nis a bulk SGG importer and sells synthetic greenhouse gas,\nwill be required to explain and substantiate:\n\n(a)\nhow the carbon tax repeal has affected, or is affecting,\nthe entity’s regulated supply input costs; and\n\n(b)\nhow reductions in the entity’s regulated supply input\ncosts that are directly or indirectly attributable to the\ncarbon tax repeal are reflected in the prices charged by\nthe entity for regulated supplies of electricity, natural\ngas or synthetic greenhouse gas.\n•\nAn entity that sells electricity or natural gas to customers, or\nan entity that is a bulk SGG importer and sells synthetic\ngreenhouse gas to customers, must:\n\n(a)\ngive a carbon tax removal substantiation statement to the\nCommission; and\n\n(b)\ninclude in the statement the entity’s estimate, on an\naverage annual percentage price basis, or an average\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
