    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60aa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60AA Objects etc.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-60aa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.288",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The main objects of this Part are:\n\n(a) to deter price exploitation in relation to the carbon tax repeal\nat each point in the supply chain for regulated goods; and\n\n(b) to ensure that all cost savings attributable to the carbon tax\nrepeal are passed through the supply chain for regulated\ngoods.\n\n(2) The intention of the Parliament in enacting this Part is to ensure\nthat all cost savings attributable to the carbon tax repeal are passed\non to consumers of regulated goods through lower prices.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The main objects of this Part are:\n\n(a) to deter price exploitation in relation to the carbon tax repeal\nat each point in the supply chain for regulated goods; and\n\n(b) to ensure that all cost savings attributable to the carbon tax\nrepeal are passed through the supply chain for regulated\ngoods.\n\n(2) The intention of the Parliament in enacting this Part is to ensure\nthat all cost savings attributable to the carbon tax repeal are passed\non to consumers of regulated goods through lower prices.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60aa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60aa-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9264eb3350ef5f9588526c2602b85a998f222f6aaf04d8d78209fa9c9ce29706"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-60aa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "60AA Objects etc.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 288,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The main objects of this Part are:\n\n(a) to deter price exploitation in relation to the carbon tax repeal\nat each point in the supply chain for regulated goods; and\n\n(b) to ensure that all cost savings attributable to the carbon tax\nrepeal are passed through the supply chain for regulated\ngoods.\n\n(2) The intention of the Parliament in enacting this Part is to ensure\nthat all cost savings attributable to the carbon tax repeal are passed\non to consumers of regulated goods through lower prices."
    },
