      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide carbon tax removal substantiation notices",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) This section applies to an entity if the entity:\n\n(a) is an electricity retailer that sells electricity to electricity\ncustomers; or\n\n(b) is a natural gas retailer that sells natural gas to natural gas\ncustomers; or\n\n(c) is a bulk SGG importer that sells synthetic greenhouse gas to\nSGG customers."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60fa-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60FA(2) Carbon tax removal substantiation notices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-60fa-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.300",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Commission must, within 30 days after the Royal Assent day,\nby written notice given to the entity, require the entity:\n\n(a) to give to the Commission, within the period specified in the\nnotice, a written statement that explains:\n\n(i) how the carbon tax repeal has affected, or is affecting,\nthe entity’s regulated supply input costs; and\n\n(ii) how reductions in the entity’s regulated supply input\ncosts that are directly or indirectly attributable to the\ncarbon tax repeal are reflected in the prices charged by\nthe entity for regulated supplies of electricity, natural\ngas or synthetic greenhouse gas; and\n\n(b) to do either or both of the following:\n\n(i) give to the Commission, within the period and in the\nmanner and form specified in the notice, information\nthat substantiates the explanation set out in the\nstatement;\n\n(ii) produce to the Commission, within the period and in the\nmanner specified in the notice, documents that\nsubstantiate the explanation set out in the statement.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nCarbon tax price reduction obligation  Part V\nCarbon tax removal substantiation notices  Division 2A\n\nSection 60FB\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Commission must, within 30 days after the Royal Assent day,\nby written notice given to the entity, require the entity:\n\n(a) to give to the Commission, within the period specified in the\nnotice, a written statement that explains:\n\n(i) how the carbon tax repeal has affected, or is affecting,\nthe entity’s regulated supply input costs; and\n\n(ii) how reductions in the entity’s regulated supply input\ncosts that are directly or indirectly attributable to the\ncarbon tax repeal are reflected in the prices charged by\nthe entity for regulated supplies of electricity, natural\ngas or synthetic greenhouse gas; and\n\n(b) to do either or both of the following:\n\n(i) give to the Commission, within the period and in the\nmanner and form specified in the notice, information\nthat substantiates the explanation set out in the\nstatement;\n\n(ii) produce to the Commission, within the period and in the\nmanner specified in the notice, documents that\nsubstantiate the explanation set out in the statement.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nCarbon tax price reduction obligation  Part V\nCarbon tax removal substantiation notices  Division 2A\n\nSection 60FB\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60fa"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60fa-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60fa-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8bb7fe1afb9eb270c2f7cec5cab9c0e2440b867149dcaf42373484f54d3590d0",
      "skos:note": "Entity must provide written statement and supporting information within a specified period.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-60fa-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "60FA(2) Carbon tax removal substantiation notices",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 300,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Commission must, within 30 days after the Royal Assent day,\nby written notice given to the entity, require the entity:\n\n(a) to give to the Commission, within the period specified in the\nnotice, a written statement that explains:\n\n(i) how the carbon tax repeal has affected, or is affecting,\nthe entity’s regulated supply input costs; and\n\n(ii) how reductions in the entity’s regulated supply input\ncosts that are directly or indirectly attributable to the\ncarbon tax repeal are reflected in the prices charged by\nthe entity for regulated supplies of electricity, natural\ngas or synthetic greenhouse gas; and\n\n(b) to do either or both of the following:\n\n(i) give to the Commission, within the period and in the\nmanner and form specified in the notice, information\nthat substantiates the explanation set out in the\nstatement;\n\n(ii) produce to the Commission, within the period and in the\nmanner specified in the notice, documents that\nsubstantiate the explanation set out in the statement.\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nCarbon tax price reduction obligation  Part V\nCarbon tax removal substantiation notices  Division 2A\n\nSection 60FB\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
