    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60fe-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60FE(3) Statements for customers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-60fe-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.306",
      "values:originalText": "(3) During the period:\n\n(a) beginning 30 days after the Royal Assent day; and\n\n(b) ending 60 days after the Royal Assent day;\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nCarbon tax price reduction obligation  Part V\nStatements for customers  Division 2C\n\nSection 60FE\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe entity must ensure that the contents of the statement prepared\nby it under subsection (2) that relates to a class of electricity\ncustomers or natural gas customers is communicated to each\ncustomer of that class.\nNote:\nSection 137.1 of the Criminal Code creates an offence of providing\nfalse or misleading information.\nCompliance",
      "skos:definition": "(3) During the period:\n\n(a) beginning 30 days after the Royal Assent day; and\n\n(b) ending 60 days after the Royal Assent day;\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nCarbon tax price reduction obligation  Part V\nStatements for customers  Division 2C\n\nSection 60FE\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe entity must ensure that the contents of the statement prepared\nby it under subsection (2) that relates to a class of electricity\ncustomers or natural gas customers is communicated to each\ncustomer of that class.\nNote:\nSection 137.1 of the Criminal Code creates an offence of providing\nfalse or misleading information.\nCompliance",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60fe"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60fe-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60fe-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60fe-ss-3-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9d09be0bb49aa9ddc1d94f5d0959869e7cf383382c81fc6979027a8a5939d227",
      "skos:note": "Entity must communicate statement contents to customers within 30-60 days after Royal Assent day.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-60fe-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "60FE(3) Statements for customers",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 306,
      "values:originalText": "(3) During the period:\n\n(a) beginning 30 days after the Royal Assent day; and\n\n(b) ending 60 days after the Royal Assent day;\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nCarbon tax price reduction obligation  Part V\nStatements for customers  Division 2C\n\nSection 60FE\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe entity must ensure that the contents of the statement prepared\nby it under subsection (2) that relates to a class of electricity\ncustomers or natural gas customers is communicated to each\ncustomer of that class.\nNote:\nSection 137.1 of the Criminal Code creates an offence of providing\nfalse or misleading information.\nCompliance"
    },
