    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60fe-ss-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60FE(7) Statements for customers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-60fe-ss-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.306",
      "values:originalText": "(7) If subsection (2) or (3) of this section applies to an individual\n(whether or not because of subsection 6(2)), the individual is\nexcused from:\n\n(a) preparing a statement under subsection (2) of this section; or\n\n(b) communicating the contents of a statement under\nsubsection (3) of this section;\non the ground that the information in the statement might tend to\nincriminate the individual or expose the individual to a penalty.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(7) If subsection (2) or (3) of this section applies to an individual\n(whether or not because of subsection 6(2)), the individual is\nexcused from:\n\n(a) preparing a statement under subsection (2) of this section; or\n\n(b) communicating the contents of a statement under\nsubsection (3) of this section;\non the ground that the information in the statement might tend to\nincriminate the individual or expose the individual to a penalty.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60fe"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60fe-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60fe-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7ae1840f830404fa4c48c6904fbc5aced3a520d68844f4553d6f42496b69d88f",
      "skos:note": "Excuse from preparing and communicating statements under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-60fe-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "60FE(7) Statements for customers",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 306,
      "values:originalText": "(7) If subsection (2) or (3) of this section applies to an individual\n(whether or not because of subsection 6(2)), the individual is\nexcused from:\n\n(a) preparing a statement under subsection (2) of this section; or\n\n(b) communicating the contents of a statement under\nsubsection (3) of this section;\non the ground that the information in the statement might tend to\nincriminate the individual or expose the individual to a penalty.\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60fe-ss-7-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60fe-ss-7"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60fe-ss-7-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "excuse",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to provide information",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Subsection (2) or (3) applies",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Individual is excused"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60G Commission may monitor prices in relation to the carbon tax",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-60g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.308",
      "values:originalText": "repeal etc.\nPrice monitoring—carbon tax repeal transition period\n\n(1) The Commission may monitor prices to assess the general effect of\nthe carbon tax repeal on prices charged by entities for supplies, in\nthe carbon tax repeal transition period, of relevant goods.\nNote:\nFor relevant goods, see subsection (11).\n\n(2) The Commission may monitor prices to assess the general effect of\nthe carbon tax repeal on prices:\n\n(a) advertised; or\n\n(b) displayed; or\n\n(c) offered;\nfor supplies, in the carbon tax repeal transition period, of relevant\ngoods by entities.\nNote:\nFor relevant goods, see subsection (11).\n\n(3) The Commission may monitor prices to assess the general effect of\nthe carbon tax repeal on prices charged for supplies, in the carbon\ntax repeal transition period, of goods by an entity for which there is\nan entry in the Information Database (within the meaning of the\nClean Energy Act 2011).\n\n(4) The Commission may monitor prices to assess the general effect of\nthe carbon tax repeal on prices:\n\n(a) advertised; or\n\n(b) displayed; or\n\n(c) offered;\nfor supplies, in the carbon tax repeal transition period, of goods by\nan entity for which there is an entry in the Information Database\n(within the meaning of the Clean Energy Act 2011).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nCarbon tax price reduction obligation  Part V\nPrice monitoring in relation to the carbon tax repeal etc.  Division 3\n\nSection 60G\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nPrice monitoring—price exploitation\n\n(5) The Commission may monitor prices to assist the Commission’s\nconsideration of whether an entity has engaged, is engaging, or\nmay in the future engage, in price exploitation in relation to the\ncarbon tax repeal.\nPrice monitoring—pre-repeal transition period\n\n(6) The Commission may monitor prices to assess the general effect of\nthe carbon tax scheme on prices charged by entities for supplies, in\nthe pre-repeal transition period, of relevant goods.\nNote 1:\nFor pre-repeal transition period, see subsection (13).\nNote 2:\nFor relevant goods, see subsection (11).\n\n(7) The Commission may monitor prices to assess the general effect of\nthe carbon tax scheme on prices:\n\n(a) advertised; or\n\n(b) displayed; or\n\n(c) offered;\nfor supplies, in the pre-repeal transition period, of relevant goods\nby entities.\nNote 1:\nFor pre-repeal transition period, see subsection (13).\nNote 2:\nFor relevant goods, see subsection (11).\n\n(8) The Commission may monitor prices to assess the general effect of\nthe carbon tax scheme on prices charged for supplies, in the\npre-repeal transition period, of goods by an entity for which there\nis an entry in the Information Database (within the meaning of the\nClean Energy Act 2011).\nNote:\nFor pre-repeal transition period, see subsection (13).\n\n(9) The Commission may monitor prices to assess the general effect of\nthe carbon tax scheme on prices:\n\n(a) advertised; or\n\n(b) displayed; or\n\n(c) offered;\n\nChapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.",
      "skos:definition": "repeal etc.\nPrice monitoring—carbon tax repeal transition period\n\n(1) The Commission may monitor prices to assess the general effect of\nthe carbon tax repeal on prices charged by entities for supplies, in\nthe carbon tax repeal transition period, of relevant goods.\nNote:\nFor relevant goods, see subsection (11).\n\n(2) The Commission may monitor prices to assess the general effect of\nthe carbon tax repeal on prices:\n\n(a) advertised; or\n\n(b) displayed; or\n\n(c) offered;\nfor supplies, in the carbon tax repeal transition period, of relevant\ngoods by entities.\nNote:\nFor relevant goods, see subsection (11).\n\n(3) The Commission may monitor prices to assess the general effect of\nthe carbon tax repeal on prices charged for supplies, in the carbon\ntax repeal transition period, of goods by an entity for which there is\nan entry in the Information Database (within the meaning of the\nClean Energy Act 2011).\n\n(4) The Commission may monitor prices to assess the general effect of\nthe carbon tax repeal on prices:\n\n(a) advertised; or\n\n(b) displayed; or\n\n(c) offered;\nfor supplies, in the carbon tax repeal transition period, of goods by\nan entity for which there is an entry in the Information Database\n(within the meaning of the Clean Energy Act 2011).\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nCarbon tax price reduction obligation  Part V\nPrice monitoring in relation to the carbon tax repeal etc.  Division 3\n\nSection 60G\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nPrice monitoring—price exploitation\n\n(5) The Commission may monitor prices to assist the Commission’s\nconsideration of whether an entity has engaged, is engaging, or\nmay in the future engage, in price exploitation in relation to the\ncarbon tax repeal.\nPrice monitoring—pre-repeal transition period\n\n(6) The Commission may monitor prices to assess the general effect of\nthe carbon tax scheme on prices charged by entities for supplies, in\nthe pre-repeal transition period, of ",
