      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) is issued more than 12 months after the day on which the\ncontravention of the infringement notice provision is alleged\nto have occurred;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60l-ss-3-logic-ltl-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recurrent",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Notice has no effect if issued more than 12 months after alleged contravention.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) is issued more than 12 months after the day on which the\ncontravention of the infringement notice provision is alleged\nto have occurred;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60l-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60L(4) Issuing an infringement notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-60l-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.314",
      "values:originalText": "(4) An infringement notice must:\n\n(a) be identified by a unique number; and\n\n(b) state the day on which it is issued; and\n\n(c) state the name and address of the person to whom it is issued;\nand\n\n(d) identify the Commission; and\n\n(e) state how the Commission may be contacted; and\n\n(f) give details of the alleged contravention by the person,\nincluding:\n\n(i) the date of the alleged contravention; and\n\n(ii) the particular infringement notice provision that was\nallegedly contravened; and\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nCarbon tax price reduction obligation  Part V\nInfringement notices  Division 5\n\nSection 60M\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(g) state the maximum pecuniary penalty that the court could\norder the person to pay under section 76 for the alleged\ncontravention; and\n\n(h) specify the penalty that is payable in relation to the alleged\ncontravention; and\n\n(i) state that the penalty is payable within the infringement\nnotice compliance period for the notice; and\n\n(j) state that the penalty is payable to the Commission on behalf\nof the Commonwealth; and\n\n(k) explain how payment of the penalty is to be made; and\n\n(l) explain the effect of sections 60M, 60N, 60P and 60Q.\nAmount of penalty",
      "skos:definition": "(4) An infringement notice must:\n\n(a) be identified by a unique number; and\n\n(b) state the day on which it is issued; and\n\n(c) state the name and address of the person to whom it is issued;\nand\n\n(d) identify the Commission; and\n\n(e) state how the Commission may be contacted; and\n\n(f) give details of the alleged contravention by the person,\nincluding:\n\n(i) the date of the alleged contravention; and\n\n(ii) the particular infringement notice provision that was\nallegedly contravened; and\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nCarbon tax price reduction obligation  Part V\nInfringement notices  Division 5\n\nSection 60M\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(g) state the maximum pecuniary penalty that the court could\norder the person to pay under section 76 for the alleged\ncontravention; and\n\n(h) specify the penalty that is payable in relation to the alleged\ncontravention; and\n\n(i) state that the penalty is payable within the infringement\nnotice compliance period for the notice; and\n\n(j) state that the penalty is payable to the Commission on behalf\nof the Commonwealth; and\n\n(k) explain how payment of the penalty is to be made; and\n\n(l) explain the effect of sections 60M, 60N, 60P and 60Q.\nAmount of penalty",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60l"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60l-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60l-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60l-ss-4-logic-linearlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e110c615f1b0be54b27cdc86c1abb29890e8642dc7ced77708f9078afd7eeb0c",
      "skos:note": "Infringement notice requirements",
      "dc:description": "Details of alleged contravention, penalty information, and contact details"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-60l-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "60L(4) Issuing an infringement notice",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 314,
      "values:originalText": "(4) An infringement notice must:\n\n(a) be identified by a unique number; and\n\n(b) state the day on which it is issued; and\n\n(c) state the name and address of the person to whom it is issued;\nand\n\n(d) identify the Commission; and\n\n(e) state how the Commission may be contacted; and\n\n(f) give details of the alleged contravention by the person,\nincluding:\n\n(i) the date of the alleged contravention; and\n\n(ii) the particular infringement notice provision that was\nallegedly contravened; and\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nCarbon tax price reduction obligation  Part V\nInfringement notices  Division 5\n\nSection 60M\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(g) state the maximum pecuniary penalty that the court could\norder the person to pay under section 76 for the alleged\ncontravention; and\n\n(h) specify the penalty that is payable in relation to the alleged\ncontravention; and\n\n(i) state that the penalty is payable within the infringement\nnotice compliance period for the notice; and\n\n(j) state that the penalty is payable to the Commission on behalf\nof the Commonwealth; and\n\n(k) explain how payment of the penalty is to be made; and\n\n(l) explain the effect of sections 60M, 60N, 60P and 60Q.\nAmount of penalty"
    },
