    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60r",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60R Effect of this Division",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-60r"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.318",
      "values:originalText": "This Division does not:\n\n(a) require an infringement notice to be issued to a person for an\nalleged contravention of an infringement notice provision; or\n\n(b) affect the liability of a person to proceedings under Part VI in\nrelation to an alleged contravention of an infringement notice\nprovision if:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nCarbon tax price reduction obligation  Part V\nInfringement notices  Division 5\n\nSection 60R\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(i) an infringement notice is not issued to the person for the\nalleged contravention; or\n\n(ii) an infringement notice issued to a person for the alleged\ncontravention is withdrawn under section 60Q; or\n\n(c) prevent a court from imposing a higher penalty than the\npenalty specified in the infringement notice if the person\ndoes not comply with the notice.\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies",
      "skos:definition": "This Division does not:\n\n(a) require an infringement notice to be issued to a person for an\nalleged contravention of an infringement notice provision; or\n\n(b) affect the liability of a person to proceedings under Part VI in\nrelation to an alleged contravention of an infringement notice\nprovision if:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nCarbon tax price reduction obligation  Part V\nInfringement notices  Division 5\n\nSection 60R\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(i) an infringement notice is not issued to the person for the\nalleged contravention; or\n\n(ii) an infringement notice issued to a person for the alleged\ncontravention is withdrawn under section 60Q; or\n\n(c) prevent a court from imposing a higher penalty than the\npenalty specified in the infringement notice if the person\ndoes not comply with the notice.\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60r-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60r-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f68f05bf5864060ecaec6f8bd1f4b056e028161567cd5acc3ecd29623b5f0bad",
      "skos:note": "Does not require an infringement notice or affect liability for alleged contravention."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-60r",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "60R Effect of this Division",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 318,
      "values:originalText": "This Division does not:\n\n(a) require an infringement notice to be issued to a person for an\nalleged contravention of an infringement notice provision; or\n\n(b) affect the liability of a person to proceedings under Part VI in\nrelation to an alleged contravention of an infringement notice\nprovision if:\n\nProvisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4\nCarbon tax price reduction obligation  Part V\nInfringement notices  Division 5\n\nSection 60R\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(i) an infringement notice is not issued to the person for the\nalleged contravention; or\n\n(ii) an infringement notice issued to a person for the alleged\ncontravention is withdrawn under section 60Q; or\n\n(c) prevent a court from imposing a higher penalty than the\npenalty specified in the infringement notice if the person\ndoes not comply with the notice.\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60r-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60r"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-60r-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "!",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Classifies obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-75b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "75B Interpretation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-75b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.320",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A reference in this Part to a person involved in a contravention of a\nprovision of Part IV, IVB, IVBA, IVBB or IVE, or of section 55B,\nsubsection 56BN(1), 56BO(1) or 56BU(1), section 56BZA, 56BZB\nor 56BZC, subsection 56BZD(1) or 56BZI(1), section 56BZJ, 60C,\n60K or 92, a civil penalty provision of a gas market instrument or a\ncivil penalty provision of the consumer data rules, shall be read as\na reference to a person who:\n\n(a) has aided, abetted, counselled or procured the contravention;\n\n(b) has induced, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, the\ncontravention;\n\n(c) has been in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly\nconcerned in, or party to, the contravention; or\n\n(d) has conspired with others to effect the contravention.\n\n(2) In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears:\n\n(a) a reference to the Court in relation to a matter is a reference\nto any court having jurisdiction in the matter;\n\n(b) a reference to the Federal Court is a reference to the Federal\nCourt of Australia; and\n\n(c) a reference to a judgment is a reference to a judgment, decree\nor order, whether final or interlocutory.\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nEnforcement and remedies  Part VI\nPecuniary penalties  Division 2\n\nSection 76\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A reference in this Part to a person involved in a contravention of a\nprovision of Part IV, IVB, IVBA, IVBB or IVE, or of section 55B,\nsubsection 56BN(1), 56BO(1) or 56BU(1), section 56BZA, 56BZB\nor 56BZC, subsection 56BZD(1) or 56BZI(1), section 56BZJ, 60C,\n60K or 92, a civil penalty provision of a gas market instrument or a\ncivil penalty provision of the consumer data rules, shall be read as\na reference to a person who:\n\n(a) has aided, abetted, counselled or procured the contravention;\n\n(b) has induced, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, the\ncontravention;\n\n(c) has been in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly\nconcerned in, or party to, the contravention; or\n\n(d) has conspired with others to effect the contravention.\n\n(2) In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears:\n\n(a) a reference to the Court in relation to a matter is a reference\nto any court having jurisdiction in the matter;\n\n(b) a reference to the Federal Court is a reference to the Federal\nCourt of Australia; and\n\n(c) a reference to a judgment is a reference to a judgment, decree\nor order, whether final or interlocutory.\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nEnforcement and remedies  Part VI\nPecuniary penalties  Division 2\n\nSection 76\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-75b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-75b-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e1ed087c655a55b4f2bf3a8461eb306b57043cfc7179af6afbfbaafd1e2bd8f9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-75b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "75B Interpretation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 320,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A reference in this Part to a person involved in a contravention of a\nprovision of Part IV, IVB, IVBA, IVBB or IVE, or of section 55B,\nsubsection 56BN(1), 56BO(1) or 56BU(1), section 56BZA, 56BZB\nor 56BZC, subsection 56BZD(1) or 56BZI(1), section 56BZJ, 60C,\n60K or 92, a civil penalty provision of a gas market instrument or a\ncivil penalty provision of the consumer data rules, shall be read as\na reference to a person who:\n\n(a) has aided, abetted, counselled or procured the contravention;\n\n(b) has induced, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, the\ncontravention;\n\n(c) has been in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly\nconcerned in, or party to, the contravention; or\n\n(d) has conspired with others to effect the contravention.\n\n(2) In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears:\n\n(a) a reference to the Court in relation to a matter is a reference\nto any court having jurisdiction in the matter;\n\n(b) a reference to the Federal Court is a reference to the Federal\nCourt of Australia; and\n\n(c) a reference to a judgment is a reference to a judgment, decree\nor order, whether final or interlocutory.\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nEnforcement and remedies  Part VI\nPecuniary penalties  Division 2\n\nSection 76\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
