    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-75b-ss-1-logic-linearlogic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LinearLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "&",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Combines multiple conditions for determining responsibility.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person involved in a contravention is defined as...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...who has aided, abetted, counselled or procured the contravention; who has induced, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, the contravention; who has been in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in, or party to, the contravention; or who has conspired with others to effect the contravention."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-75b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "75B(2) Interpretation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-75b-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.320",
      "values:originalText": "(2) In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears:\n\n(a) a reference to the Court in relation to a matter is a reference\nto any court having jurisdiction in the matter;\n\n(b) a reference to the Federal Court is a reference to the Federal\nCourt of Australia; and\n\n(c) a reference to a judgment is a reference to a judgment, decree\nor order, whether final or interlocutory.\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nEnforcement and remedies  Part VI\nPecuniary penalties  Division 2\n\nSection 76\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(2) In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears:\n\n(a) a reference to the Court in relation to a matter is a reference\nto any court having jurisdiction in the matter;\n\n(b) a reference to the Federal Court is a reference to the Federal\nCourt of Australia; and\n\n(c) a reference to a judgment is a reference to a judgment, decree\nor order, whether final or interlocutory.\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nEnforcement and remedies  Part VI\nPecuniary penalties  Division 2\n\nSection 76\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-75b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-75b-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-75b-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7dc6bd74423617c167105b9798aed6adaa3de8af9439e79b179c28efe1d39727",
      "skos:note": "Reference to court is a reference to any court having jurisdiction in the matter."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-75b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "75B(2) Interpretation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 320,
      "values:originalText": "(2) In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears:\n\n(a) a reference to the Court in relation to a matter is a reference\nto any court having jurisdiction in the matter;\n\n(b) a reference to the Federal Court is a reference to the Federal\nCourt of Australia; and\n\n(c) a reference to a judgment is a reference to a judgment, decree\nor order, whether final or interlocutory.\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nEnforcement and remedies  Part VI\nPecuniary penalties  Division 2\n\nSection 76\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
