    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 Section 10",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.325",
      "values:originalText": "60(1) or 10.65(1): see subsection 10.49A(2), 10.60(2) or 10.65(2).\nNote 2:\nPecuniary penalties may not be ordered under subsection (1) against\ncertain individuals in relation to contraventions of section 153E, 153F,\n153G or 153H in certain circumstances: see section 153ZD.\n\n(1B) For the purposes of items 1, 3, 6, 7A, 7C, 7D and 13 of the table in\nsubsection (1A), the amounts are as follows:\n\n(a) $100,000,000;\n\n(b) if item 1 or 13 of the table applies, and the Court can\ndetermine the total value of the benefits that have been\nobtained (within the meaning of Division 1 of Part IV) by\none or more persons and that are reasonably attributable to\nthe act or omission—3 times that total value;\n\n(c) if item 3, 6, 7A, 7C or 7D of the table applies, and the Court\ncan determine the value of the benefit that the body\ncorporate, and any body corporate related to the body\ncorporate, have obtained directly or indirectly and that is\nreasonably attributable to the act or omission—3 times the\nvalue of that benefit;\n\n(d) if the Court cannot determine the value of those benefits or\nthat benefit—30% of the body corporate’s adjusted turnover\nduring the breach turnover period for the act or omission.\n\n(1C) For the purposes of item 9 of the table in subsection (1A), the\namounts are as follows:\n\n(a) $10,000,000;\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies",
      "skos:definition": "60(1) or 10.65(1): see subsection 10.49A(2), 10.60(2) or 10.65(2).\nNote 2:\nPecuniary penalties may not be ordered under subsection (1) against\ncertain individuals in relation to contraventions of section 153E, 153F,\n153G or 153H in certain circumstances: see section 153ZD.\n\n(1B) For the purposes of items 1, 3, 6, 7A, 7C, 7D and 13 of the table in\nsubsection (1A), the amounts are as follows:\n\n(a) $100,000,000;\n\n(b) if item 1 or 13 of the table applies, and the Court can\ndetermine the total value of the benefits that have been\nobtained (within the meaning of Division 1 of Part IV) by\none or more persons and that are reasonably attributable to\nthe act or omission—3 times that total value;\n\n(c) if item 3, 6, 7A, 7C or 7D of the table applies, and the Court\ncan determine the value of the benefit that the body\ncorporate, and any body corporate related to the body\ncorporate, have obtained directly or indirectly and that is\nreasonably attributable to the act or omission—3 times the\nvalue of that benefit;\n\n(d) if the Court cannot determine the value of those benefits or\nthat benefit—30% of the body corporate’s adjusted turnover\nduring the breach turnover period for the act or omission.\n\n(1C) For the purposes of item 9 of the table in subsection (1A), the\namounts are as follows:\n\n(a) $10,000,000;\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-ss-1b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-ss-1c"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e75760a7fc08f3144ffde4d245e44dedf898552a9ddd2a7d204a764898256461"
    },
    {
