      "skos:definition": "(4) Criminal proceedings may be started against a person for conduct\nthat is substantially the same as conduct constituting a\ncontravention of Part IV, subsection 56BO(1) or section 56BZJ or\n92 regardless of whether a pecuniary penalty order has been made\nagainst the person in respect of the contravention.\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nEnforcement and remedies  Part VI\nPecuniary penalties  Division 2\n\nSection 77\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-76b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-76b-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-76b-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "606c1c3c2312a155c31981a08b71aaf6e146c5cd3949ee87d487aa383f314eb3",
      "skos:note": "Starting criminal proceedings against a person for substantially the same conduct as a contravention of certain laws."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-76b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "76B(4) Consequences in some cases if substantially the same conduct",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 328,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Criminal proceedings may be started against a person for conduct\nthat is substantially the same as conduct constituting a\ncontravention of Part IV, subsection 56BO(1) or section 56BZJ or\n92 regardless of whether a pecuniary penalty order has been made\nagainst the person in respect of the contravention.\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nEnforcement and remedies  Part VI\nPecuniary penalties  Division 2\n\nSection 77\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
