    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-76b-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "76B(5) Consequences in some cases if substantially the same conduct",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-76b-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.328",
      "values:originalText": "(5) Evidence of information given, or evidence of production of\ndocuments, by an individual is not admissible in criminal\nproceedings against the individual if:\n\n(a) the individual previously gave the evidence or produced the\ndocuments in proceedings for a pecuniary penalty order\nagainst the individual for a contravention of Part IV,\nsubsection 56BO(1) or section 56BZJ or 92 (whether or not\nthe order was made); and\n\n(b) the conduct alleged to constitute the offence is substantially\nthe same as the conduct that was claimed to constitute the\ncontravention.\nHowever, this does not apply to a criminal proceeding in respect of\nthe falsity of the evidence given by the individual in the\nproceedings for the pecuniary penalty order.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) Evidence of information given, or evidence of production of\ndocuments, by an individual is not admissible in criminal\nproceedings against the individual if:\n\n(a) the individual previously gave the evidence or produced the\ndocuments in proceedings for a pecuniary penalty order\nagainst the individual for a contravention of Part IV,\nsubsection 56BO(1) or section 56BZJ or 92 (whether or not\nthe order was made); and\n\n(b) the conduct alleged to constitute the offence is substantially\nthe same as the conduct that was claimed to constitute the\ncontravention.\nHowever, this does not apply to a criminal proceeding in respect of\nthe falsity of the evidence given by the individual in the\nproceedings for the pecuniary penalty order.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-76b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-76b-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-76b-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-76b-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-76b-ss-5-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-76b-ss-5-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-76b-ss-5-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ac5df5c476f5402dff65e428b7e770bf8eae1e9124aeebad6827d7d68ea1b7e3",
      "skos:note": "Prevents admissibility of evidence in criminal proceedings if individual previously gave the same evidence or produced documents in a previous proceeding for a pecuniary penalty order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-76b-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "76B(5) Consequences in some cases if substantially the same conduct",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 328,
      "values:originalText": "(5) Evidence of information given, or evidence of production of\ndocuments, by an individual is not admissible in criminal\nproceedings against the individual if:\n\n(a) the individual previously gave the evidence or produced the\ndocuments in proceedings for a pecuniary penalty order\nagainst the individual for a contravention of Part IV,\nsubsection 56BO(1) or section 56BZJ or 92 (whether or not\nthe order was made); and\n\n(b) the conduct alleged to constitute the offence is substantially\nthe same as the conduct that was claimed to constitute the\ncontravention.\nHowever, this does not apply to a criminal proceeding in respect of\nthe falsity of the evidence given by the individual in the\nproceedings for the pecuniary penalty order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-76b-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
