    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-79a-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "79A(3) Enforcement and recovery of certain fines",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-79a-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.335",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Where the Court makes an order in relation to a person in respect\nof a fine, the Court may, at any time before the order is executed in\nrespect of the fine, allow the person a specified time in which to\npay the fine or allow the person to pay the fine by specified\ninstalments, and, in that case:\n\n(a) the order shall not be executed unless the person fails to pay\nthe fine within that time or fails to pay an instalment at or\nbefore the time when it becomes payable, as the case may be;\nand\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Where the Court makes an order in relation to a person in respect\nof a fine, the Court may, at any time before the order is executed in\nrespect of the fine, allow the person a specified time in which to\npay the fine or allow the person to pay the fine by specified\ninstalments, and, in that case:\n\n(a) the order shall not be executed unless the person fails to pay\nthe fine within that time or fails to pay an instalment at or\nbefore the time when it becomes payable, as the case may be;\nand\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-79a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-79a-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-79a-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "262b19a46e48b468a118687758c3435c9ae5fa244358911e767c6ee3c42d283c",
      "skos:note": "Allow person to pay fine within specified time or by instalments."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-79a-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "79A(3) Enforcement and recovery of certain fines",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 335,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Where the Court makes an order in relation to a person in respect\nof a fine, the Court may, at any time before the order is executed in\nrespect of the fine, allow the person a specified time in which to\npay the fine or allow the person to pay the fine by specified\ninstalments, and, in that case:\n\n(a) the order shall not be executed unless the person fails to pay\nthe fine within that time or fails to pay an instalment at or\nbefore the time when it becomes payable, as the case may be;\nand\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies"
    },
