      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Court must give preference to making an order for compensation.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80 Injunctions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-80"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.337",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsections (1A), (1AAA) and (1B), where, on the\napplication of the Commission or any other person, the Court is\nsatisfied that a person has engaged, or is proposing to engage, in\nconduct that constitutes or would constitute:\n\n(a) a contravention of any of the following provisions:\n\n(i) a provision of Part IV;\n\n(ii) a provision of Division 2 or 5 of Part IVB;\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsections (1A), (1AAA) and (1B), where, on the\napplication of the Commission or any other person, the Court is\nsatisfied that a person has engaged, or is proposing to engage, in\nconduct that constitutes or would constitute:\n\n(a) a contravention of any of the following provisions:\n\n(i) a provision of Part IV;\n\n(ii) a provision of Division 2 or 5 of Part IVB;\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f6e21741e22fbbf879148bab9f5f66c9d5a65f2621394fcbd87fb6688ebf1568",
      "skos:note": "Prohibition of conduct that constitutes or would constitute a contravention of certain provisions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-80",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80 Injunctions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 337,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsections (1A), (1AAA) and (1B), where, on the\napplication of the Commission or any other person, the Court is\nsatisfied that a person has engaged, or is proposing to engage, in\nconduct that constitutes or would constitute:\n\n(a) a contravention of any of the following provisions:\n\n(i) a provision of Part IV;\n\n(ii) a provision of Division 2 or 5 of Part IVB;\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "forbid",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition of conduct.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) Subject to subsections (1A), (1AAA) and (1B)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(a) a contravention of any of the following provisions:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80A Price exploitation in relation to the carbon tax repeal—orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-80a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.341",
      "values:originalText": "limiting prices or requiring refunds of money\n\n(1) If, on the application of the Commission, the Court is satisfied that\na person has engaged in conduct constituting a contravention of\nsection 60C, the Court may make either or both of the following\norders:\n\n(a) an order requiring that person, or a person involved in the\ncontravention, not to make a regulated supply of a kind\nspecified in the order for a price in excess of the price\nspecified in the order while the order remains in force;\n\n(b) an order requiring that person, or a person involved in the\ncontravention, to refund money to a person specified in the\norder.\nNote:\nSection 60C is about price exploitation in relation to the carbon tax\nrepeal.\n\n(2) This section does not limit section 80.\n\n(3) In this section:\nprice has the same meaning as in Part V.\nregulated supply has the same meaning as in Part V.\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies",
      "skos:definition": "limiting prices or requiring refunds of money\n\n(1) If, on the application of the Commission, the Court is satisfied that\na person has engaged in conduct constituting a contravention of\nsection 60C, the Court may make either or both of the following\norders:\n\n(a) an order requiring that person, or a person involved in the\ncontravention, not to make a regulated supply of a kind\nspecified in the order for a price in excess of the price\nspecified in the order while the order remains in force;\n\n(b) an order requiring that person, or a person involved in the\ncontravention, to refund money to a person specified in the\norder.\nNote:\nSection 60C is about price exploitation in relation to the carbon tax\nrepeal.\n\n(2) This section does not limit section 80.\n\n(3) In this section:\nprice has the same meaning as in Part V.\nregulated supply has the same meaning as in Part V.\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "53080fdd26da69aa5791d04b88727dd42801cbd454a2f84a40f3e11d6eeac993"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-80a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80A Price exploitation in relation to the carbon tax repeal—orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 341,
      "values:originalText": "limiting prices or requiring refunds of money\n\n(1) If, on the application of the Commission, the Court is satisfied that\na person has engaged in conduct constituting a contravention of\nsection 60C, the Court may make either or both of the following\norders:\n\n(a) an order requiring that person, or a person involved in the\ncontravention, not to make a regulated supply of a kind\nspecified in the order for a price in excess of the price\nspecified in the order while the order remains in force;\n\n(b) an order requiring that person, or a person involved in the\ncontravention, to refund money to a person specified in the\norder.\nNote:\nSection 60C is about price exploitation in relation to the carbon tax\nrepeal.\n\n(2) This section does not limit section 80.\n\n(3) In this section:\nprice has the same meaning as in Part V.\nregulated supply has the same meaning as in Part V.\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80A(1) Price exploitation in relation to the carbon tax repeal—orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-80a-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.341",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, on the application of the Commission, the Court is satisfied that\na person has engaged in conduct constituting a contravention of\nsection 60C, the Court may make either or both of the following\norders:\n\n(a) an order requiring that person, or a person involved in the\ncontravention, not to make a regulated supply of a kind\nspecified in the order for a price in excess of the price\nspecified in the order while the order remains in force;\n\n(b) an order requiring that person, or a person involved in the\ncontravention, to refund money to a person specified in the\norder.\nNote:\nSection 60C is about price exploitation in relation to the carbon tax\nrepeal.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If, on the application of the Commission, the Court is satisfied that\na person has engaged in conduct constituting a contravention of\nsection 60C, the Court may make either or both of the following\norders:\n\n(a) an order requiring that person, or a person involved in the\ncontravention, not to make a regulated supply of a kind\nspecified in the order for a price in excess of the price\nspecified in the order while the order remains in force;\n\n(b) an order requiring that person, or a person involved in the\ncontravention, to refund money to a person specified in the\norder.\nNote:\nSection 60C is about price exploitation in relation to the carbon tax\nrepeal.",
      "values:partOf": {
