          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80a-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80a-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "da84f2ece8cd341a297c48db143cd397161b9ecf5d3cddecd542851dc82bfe10",
      "skos:note": "Order not to make regulated supply at excessive price"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-80a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80A(1) Price exploitation in relation to the carbon tax repeal—orders",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 341,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, on the application of the Commission, the Court is satisfied that\na person has engaged in conduct constituting a contravention of\nsection 60C, the Court may make either or both of the following\norders:\n\n(a) an order requiring that person, or a person involved in the\ncontravention, not to make a regulated supply of a kind\nspecified in the order for a price in excess of the price\nspecified in the order while the order remains in force;\n\n(b) an order requiring that person, or a person involved in the\ncontravention, to refund money to a person specified in the\norder.\nNote:\nSection 60C is about price exploitation in relation to the carbon tax\nrepeal."
    },
