    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80ab-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80AB(3) Stay of injunctions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-80ab-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.342",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the proceeding referred to in paragraph (1)(b) is terminated\nbecause the State or Territory court, tribunal or authority has\nsettled the dispute to which the conduct relates by conciliation, the\nCourt must not make any order in relation to the costs of the\nproceedings in respect of the granting of the injunction or in\nrelation to the costs of any proceedings for the rescission of the\ninjunction.\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nEnforcement and remedies  Part VI\nOther provisions  Division 5\n\nSection 80AC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If the proceeding referred to in paragraph (1)(b) is terminated\nbecause the State or Territory court, tribunal or authority has\nsettled the dispute to which the conduct relates by conciliation, the\nCourt must not make any order in relation to the costs of the\nproceedings in respect of the granting of the injunction or in\nrelation to the costs of any proceedings for the rescission of the\ninjunction.\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nEnforcement and remedies  Part VI\nOther provisions  Division 5\n\nSection 80AC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80ab"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80ab-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80ab-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2ccb65e0496737bbd1a63600cc111c98015523df4683fa7154978f785b816750",
      "skos:note": "Court must not make any order in relation to the costs of the proceedings."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-80ab-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80AB(3) Stay of injunctions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 342,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the proceeding referred to in paragraph (1)(b) is terminated\nbecause the State or Territory court, tribunal or authority has\nsettled the dispute to which the conduct relates by conciliation, the\nCourt must not make any order in relation to the costs of the\nproceedings in respect of the granting of the injunction or in\nrelation to the costs of any proceedings for the rescission of the\ninjunction.\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nEnforcement and remedies  Part VI\nOther provisions  Division 5\n\nSection 80AC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
    {
