    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80ab-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80AB(5) Stay of injunctions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-80ab-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.342",
      "values:originalText": "(5) In this section:\nassociated contravention means:\n\n(a) attempting to contravene subsection 45D(1), 45DA(1),\n45DB(1), 45E(2) or 45E(3) or section 45EA; or\n\n(b) aiding, abetting, counselling or procuring a person to\ncontravene any of those provisions; or\n\n(c) inducing, or attempting to induce, a person (whether by\nthreats, promises or otherwise) to contravene any of those\nprovisions; or\n\n(d) being in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned\nin, or party to, the contravention by a person of any of those\nprovisions; or\n\n(e) conspiring with others to contravene any of those provisions.\ninjunction includes an interim injunction.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) In this section:\nassociated contravention means:\n\n(a) attempting to contravene subsection 45D(1), 45DA(1),\n45DB(1), 45E(2) or 45E(3) or section 45EA; or\n\n(b) aiding, abetting, counselling or procuring a person to\ncontravene any of those provisions; or\n\n(c) inducing, or attempting to induce, a person (whether by\nthreats, promises or otherwise) to contravene any of those\nprovisions; or\n\n(d) being in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned\nin, or party to, the contravention by a person of any of those\nprovisions; or\n\n(e) conspiring with others to contravene any of those provisions.\ninjunction includes an interim injunction.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80ab"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80ab-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80ab-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80ab-ss-5-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "64537909c41746017b06aac1a3163cf6cf66bda1a4f825e17c924138f6df5061",
      "skos:note": "Definition of associated contravention"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-80ab-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80AB(5) Stay of injunctions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 342,
      "values:originalText": "(5) In this section:\nassociated contravention means:\n\n(a) attempting to contravene subsection 45D(1), 45DA(1),\n45DB(1), 45E(2) or 45E(3) or section 45EA; or\n\n(b) aiding, abetting, counselling or procuring a person to\ncontravene any of those provisions; or\n\n(c) inducing, or attempting to induce, a person (whether by\nthreats, promises or otherwise) to contravene any of those\nprovisions; or\n\n(d) being in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned\nin, or party to, the contravention by a person of any of those\nprovisions; or\n\n(e) conspiring with others to contravene any of those provisions.\ninjunction includes an interim injunction."
    },
