    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80ac",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80AC Injunctions to prevent mergers if authorisation granted on the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-80ac"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.343",
      "values:originalText": "basis of false or misleading information\n\nIf, on the application of the Commission, the Court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) a person is proposing to acquire shares in the capital of a\nbody corporate or assets of a person; and\n\n(b) the person was granted a merger authorisation for the\nproposed acquisition on the basis of information that was\nfalse or misleading in a material particular; and\n\n(c) that information was given by the person or a body corporate\nthat was related to the person; and\n\n(d) if that information had not been given, the authorisation\nwould not have been granted; and\n\n(e) apart from the authorisation, the acquisition would\ncontravene section 50 if it occurred;\nthen the Court may grant an injunction in such terms as the Court\ndetermines to be appropriate.\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies",
      "skos:definition": "basis of false or misleading information\n\nIf, on the application of the Commission, the Court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) a person is proposing to acquire shares in the capital of a\nbody corporate or assets of a person; and\n\n(b) the person was granted a merger authorisation for the\nproposed acquisition on the basis of information that was\nfalse or misleading in a material particular; and\n\n(c) that information was given by the person or a body corporate\nthat was related to the person; and\n\n(d) if that information had not been given, the authorisation\nwould not have been granted; and\n\n(e) apart from the authorisation, the acquisition would\ncontravene section 50 if it occurred;\nthen the Court may grant an injunction in such terms as the Court\ndetermines to be appropriate.\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80ac-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80ac-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f6dcbb6d997c96053b1efb8d55fd6b3bbcc35d86eabc189e171fdd5d4a6dde1e",
      "skos:note": "Granting merger authorization on false or misleading information is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-80ac",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80AC Injunctions to prevent mergers if authorisation granted on the",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 343,
      "values:originalText": "basis of false or misleading information\n\nIf, on the application of the Commission, the Court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) a person is proposing to acquire shares in the capital of a\nbody corporate or assets of a person; and\n\n(b) the person was granted a merger authorisation for the\nproposed acquisition on the basis of information that was\nfalse or misleading in a material particular; and\n\n(c) that information was given by the person or a body corporate\nthat was related to the person; and\n\n(d) if that information had not been given, the authorisation\nwould not have been granted; and\n\n(e) apart from the authorisation, the acquisition would\ncontravene section 50 if it occurred;\nthen the Court may grant an injunction in such terms as the Court\ndetermines to be appropriate.\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80ac-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80ac"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80ac-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition of granting merger authorization on false or misleading information.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person was granted a merger authorisation for the proposed acquisition on the basis of information that was false or misleading in a material particular.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Court may not grant the authorisation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-80ad",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80AD Injunctions if acquisition determinations made on the basis of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-80ad"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
