    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-86d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "86D Punitive orders—adverse publicity",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-86d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.360",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Court may, on application by the Commission, make an\nadverse publicity order in relation to a person who:\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nEnforcement and remedies  Part VI\nOther provisions  Division 5\n\nSection 86E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) has been ordered to pay a pecuniary penalty under section 76;\nor\n\n(b) is guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG or\nsubsection 56BN(1) or 56BZI(1).\n\n(1A) The Court may, on application by the Director of Public\nProsecutions, make an adverse publicity order in relation to a\nperson who is guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG\nor subsection 56BN(1) or 56BZI(1).\n\n(2) In this section, an adverse publicity order, in relation to a person,\nmeans an order that:\n\n(a) requires the person to disclose, in the way and to the persons\nspecified in the order, such information as is so specified,\nbeing information that the person has possession of or access\nto; and\n\n(b) requires the person to publish, at the person’s expense and in\nthe way specified in the order, an advertisement in the terms\nspecified in, or determined in accordance with, the order.\n\n(3) This section does not limit the Court’s powers under any other\nprovision of this Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Court may, on application by the Commission, make an\nadverse publicity order in relation to a person who:\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nEnforcement and remedies  Part VI\nOther provisions  Division 5\n\nSection 86E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) has been ordered to pay a pecuniary penalty under section 76;\nor\n\n(b) is guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG or\nsubsection 56BN(1) or 56BZI(1).\n\n(1A) The Court may, on application by the Director of Public\nProsecutions, make an adverse publicity order in relation to a\nperson who is guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG\nor subsection 56BN(1) or 56BZI(1).\n\n(2) In this section, an adverse publicity order, in relation to a person,\nmeans an order that:\n\n(a) requires the person to disclose, in the way and to the persons\nspecified in the order, such information as is so specified,\nbeing information that the person has possession of or access\nto; and\n\n(b) requires the person to publish, at the person’s expense and in\nthe way specified in the order, an advertisement in the terms\nspecified in, or determined in accordance with, the order.\n\n(3) This section does not limit the Court’s powers under any other\nprovision of this Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-86d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-86d-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-86d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-86d-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a86f893ffdc8072bd77cee1ceb275ee93c631af5db4c7a77c82ed895f728673e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-86d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "86D Punitive orders—adverse publicity",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 360,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Court may, on application by the Commission, make an\nadverse publicity order in relation to a person who:\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nEnforcement and remedies  Part VI\nOther provisions  Division 5\n\nSection 86E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) has been ordered to pay a pecuniary penalty under section 76;\nor\n\n(b) is guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG or\nsubsection 56BN(1) or 56BZI(1).\n\n(1A) The Court may, on application by the Director of Public\nProsecutions, make an adverse publicity order in relation to a\nperson who is guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG\nor subsection 56BN(1) or 56BZI(1).\n\n(2) In this section, an adverse publicity order, in relation to a person,\nmeans an order that:\n\n(a) requires the person to disclose, in the way and to the persons\nspecified in the order, such information as is so specified,\nbeing information that the person has possession of or access\nto; and\n\n(b) requires the person to publish, at the person’s expense and in\nthe way specified in the order, an advertisement in the terms\nspecified in, or determined in accordance with, the order.\n\n(3) This section does not limit the Court’s powers under any other\nprovision of this Act."
    },
