      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) On application by the Commission, the Court may make an order disqualifying a person from managing corporations...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...for a period that the Court considers appropriate if: ..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-86f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "86F Privilege against exposure to penalty—disqualification from",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-86f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.363",
      "values:originalText": "managing corporations\nCourt proceeding\n\n(1) In a civil or criminal proceeding under, or arising out of, this Act, a\ngas market instrument or the consumer data rules, a person is not\nentitled to refuse or fail to comply with a requirement:\n\n(a) to answer a question or give information; or\n\n(b) to produce a document or any other thing; or\n\n(c) to do any other act;\non the ground that the answer or information, production of the\ndocument or other thing, or doing that other act, as the case may\nbe, might tend to expose the person to a penalty by way of an order\nunder section 86E.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the person is a defendant in\nthe proceeding or in any other proceeding.\nStatutory requirement\n\n(3) A person is not entitled to refuse or fail to comply with a\nrequirement under this Act, a gas market instrument or the\nconsumer data rules:\n\n(a) to answer a question or give information; or\n\n(b) to produce a document or any other thing; or\n\n(c) to do any other act;\non the ground that the answer or information, production of the\ndocument or other thing, or doing that other act, as the case may\nbe, might tend to expose the person to a penalty by way of an order\nunder section 86E.\nDefinition\n\n(4) In this section:\npenalty includes forfeiture.\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies",
      "skos:definition": "managing corporations\nCourt proceeding\n\n(1) In a civil or criminal proceeding under, or arising out of, this Act, a\ngas market instrument or the consumer data rules, a person is not\nentitled to refuse or fail to comply with a requirement:\n\n(a) to answer a question or give information; or\n\n(b) to produce a document or any other thing; or\n\n(c) to do any other act;\non the ground that the answer or information, production of the\ndocument or other thing, or doing that other act, as the case may\nbe, might tend to expose the person to a penalty by way of an order\nunder section 86E.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the person is a defendant in\nthe proceeding or in any other proceeding.\nStatutory requirement\n\n(3) A person is not entitled to refuse or fail to comply with a\nrequirement under this Act, a gas market instrument or the\nconsumer data rules:\n\n(a) to answer a question or give information; or\n\n(b) to produce a document or any other thing; or\n\n(c) to do any other act;\non the ground that the answer or information, production of the\ndocument or other thing, or doing that other act, as the case may\nbe, might tend to expose the person to a penalty by way of an order\nunder section 86E.\nDefinition\n\n(4) In this section:\npenalty includes forfeiture.\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-86f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-86f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-86f-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-86f-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c313f84308ae50796196a0075c9977a13eb3b914eb30f2adcc909c899b6a7653"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-86f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "86F Privilege against exposure to penalty—disqualification from",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 363,
      "values:originalText": "managing corporations\nCourt proceeding\n\n(1) In a civil or criminal proceeding under, or arising out of, this Act, a\ngas market instrument or the consumer data rules, a person is not\nentitled to refuse or fail to comply with a requirement:\n\n(a) to answer a question or give information; or\n\n(b) to produce a document or any other thing; or\n\n(c) to do any other act;\non the ground that the answer or information, production of the\ndocument or other thing, or doing that other act, as the case may\nbe, might tend to expose the person to a penalty by way of an order\nunder section 86E.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the person is a defendant in\nthe proceeding or in any other proceeding.\nStatutory requirement\n\n(3) A person is not entitled to refuse or fail to comply with a\nrequirement under this Act, a gas market instrument or the\nconsumer data rules:\n\n(a) to answer a question or give information; or\n\n(b) to produce a document or any other thing; or\n\n(c) to do any other act;\non the ground that the answer or information, production of the\ndocument or other thing, or doing that other act, as the case may\nbe, might tend to expose the person to a penalty by way of an order\nunder section 86E.\nDefinition\n\n(4) In this section:\npenalty includes forfeiture.\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies"
    },
    {
