    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87cc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "87CC Certain concurrent wrongdoers not to have benefit of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-87cc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.372",
      "values:originalText": "apportionment\n\n(1) Nothing in this Part operates to exclude the liability of a concurrent\nwrongdoer (an excluded concurrent wrongdoer) in proceedings\ninvolving an apportionable claim if:\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nProportionate liability for misleading and deceptive conduct  Part VIA\n\nSection 87CD\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) the concurrent wrongdoer intended to cause the economic\nloss or damage to property that is the subject of the claim; or\n\n(b) the concurrent wrongdoer fraudulently caused the economic\nloss or damage to property that is the subject of the claim.\n\n(2) The liability of an excluded concurrent wrongdoer is to be\ndetermined in accordance with the legal rules (if any) that (apart\nfrom this Part) are relevant.\n\n(3) The liability of any other concurrent wrongdoer who is not an\nexcluded concurrent wrongdoer is to be determined in accordance\nwith the provisions of this Part.",
      "skos:definition": "apportionment\n\n(1) Nothing in this Part operates to exclude the liability of a concurrent\nwrongdoer (an excluded concurrent wrongdoer) in proceedings\ninvolving an apportionable claim if:\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nProportionate liability for misleading and deceptive conduct  Part VIA\n\nSection 87CD\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) the concurrent wrongdoer intended to cause the economic\nloss or damage to property that is the subject of the claim; or\n\n(b) the concurrent wrongdoer fraudulently caused the economic\nloss or damage to property that is the subject of the claim.\n\n(2) The liability of an excluded concurrent wrongdoer is to be\ndetermined in accordance with the legal rules (if any) that (apart\nfrom this Part) are relevant.\n\n(3) The liability of any other concurrent wrongdoer who is not an\nexcluded concurrent wrongdoer is to be determined in accordance\nwith the provisions of this Part.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87cc-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87cc-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87cc-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cdd4180d337fe745db769c843690d058e2ec43141db595f0d16d76af31d9f94c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-87cc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "87CC Certain concurrent wrongdoers not to have benefit of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 372,
      "values:originalText": "apportionment\n\n(1) Nothing in this Part operates to exclude the liability of a concurrent\nwrongdoer (an excluded concurrent wrongdoer) in proceedings\ninvolving an apportionable claim if:\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nProportionate liability for misleading and deceptive conduct  Part VIA\n\nSection 87CD\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) the concurrent wrongdoer intended to cause the economic\nloss or damage to property that is the subject of the claim; or\n\n(b) the concurrent wrongdoer fraudulently caused the economic\nloss or damage to property that is the subject of the claim.\n\n(2) The liability of an excluded concurrent wrongdoer is to be\ndetermined in accordance with the legal rules (if any) that (apart\nfrom this Part) are relevant.\n\n(3) The liability of any other concurrent wrongdoer who is not an\nexcluded concurrent wrongdoer is to be determined in accordance\nwith the provisions of this Part."
    },
