    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87ce",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "87CE Defendant to notify plaintiff of concurrent wrongdoer of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-87ce"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.374",
      "values:originalText": "whom defendant aware\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a defendant in proceedings involving an apportionable claim\nhas reasonable grounds to believe that a particular person (the\nother person) may be a concurrent wrongdoer in relation to\nthe claim; and\n\n(b) the defendant fails to give the plaintiff, as soon as\npracticable, written notice of the information that the\ndefendant has about:\n\n(i) the identity of the other person; and\n\n(ii) the circumstances that may make the other person a\nconcurrent wrongdoer in relation to the claim; and\n\n(c) the plaintiff unnecessarily incurs costs in the proceedings\nbecause the plaintiff was not aware that the other person may\nbe a concurrent wrongdoer in relation to the claim;\nthe court hearing the proceedings may order that the defendant pay\nall or any of those costs of the plaintiff.\n\n(2) The court may order that the costs to be paid by the defendant be\nassessed on an indemnity basis or otherwise.\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nProportionate liability for misleading and deceptive conduct  Part VIA\n\nSection 87CF\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "whom defendant aware\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a defendant in proceedings involving an apportionable claim\nhas reasonable grounds to believe that a particular person (the\nother person) may be a concurrent wrongdoer in relation to\nthe claim; and\n\n(b) the defendant fails to give the plaintiff, as soon as\npracticable, written notice of the information that the\ndefendant has about:\n\n(i) the identity of the other person; and\n\n(ii) the circumstances that may make the other person a\nconcurrent wrongdoer in relation to the claim; and\n\n(c) the plaintiff unnecessarily incurs costs in the proceedings\nbecause the plaintiff was not aware that the other person may\nbe a concurrent wrongdoer in relation to the claim;\nthe court hearing the proceedings may order that the defendant pay\nall or any of those costs of the plaintiff.\n\n(2) The court may order that the costs to be paid by the defendant be\nassessed on an indemnity basis or otherwise.\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nProportionate liability for misleading and deceptive conduct  Part VIA\n\nSection 87CF\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87ce-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87ce-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "04fbff1b7fde069dcacc794b05cf296d1f66c2d597da3502469f03b1a91cf68a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-87ce",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "87CE Defendant to notify plaintiff of concurrent wrongdoer of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 374,
      "values:originalText": "whom defendant aware\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a defendant in proceedings involving an apportionable claim\nhas reasonable grounds to believe that a particular person (the\nother person) may be a concurrent wrongdoer in relation to\nthe claim; and\n\n(b) the defendant fails to give the plaintiff, as soon as\npracticable, written notice of the information that the\ndefendant has about:\n\n(i) the identity of the other person; and\n\n(ii) the circumstances that may make the other person a\nconcurrent wrongdoer in relation to the claim; and\n\n(c) the plaintiff unnecessarily incurs costs in the proceedings\nbecause the plaintiff was not aware that the other person may\nbe a concurrent wrongdoer in relation to the claim;\nthe court hearing the proceedings may order that the defendant pay\nall or any of those costs of the plaintiff.\n\n(2) The court may order that the costs to be paid by the defendant be\nassessed on an indemnity basis or otherwise.\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nProportionate liability for misleading and deceptive conduct  Part VIA\n\nSection 87CF\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87ce-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "87CE(1) Defendant to notify plaintiff of concurrent wrongdoer of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-87ce-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.374",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a defendant in proceedings involving an apportionable claim\nhas reasonable grounds to believe that a particular person (the\nother person) may be a concurrent wrongdoer in relation to\nthe claim; and\n\n(b) the defendant fails to give the plaintiff, as soon as\npracticable, written notice of the information that the\ndefendant has about:\n\n(i) the identity of the other person; and\n\n(ii) the circumstances that may make the other person a\nconcurrent wrongdoer in relation to the claim; and\n\n(c) the plaintiff unnecessarily incurs costs in the proceedings\nbecause the plaintiff was not aware that the other person may\nbe a concurrent wrongdoer in relation to the claim;\nthe court hearing the proceedings may order that the defendant pay\nall or any of those costs of the plaintiff.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a defendant in proceedings involving an apportionable claim\nhas reasonable grounds to believe that a particular person (the\nother person) may be a concurrent wrongdoer in relation to\nthe claim; and\n\n(b) the defendant fails to give the plaintiff, as soon as\npracticable, written notice of the information that the\ndefendant has about:\n\n(i) the identity of the other person; and\n\n(ii) the circumstances that may make the other person a\nconcurrent wrongdoer in relation to the claim; and\n\n(c) the plaintiff unnecessarily incurs costs in the proceedings\nbecause the plaintiff was not aware that the other person may\nbe a concurrent wrongdoer in relation to the claim;\nthe court hearing the proceedings may order that the defendant pay\nall or any of those costs of the plaintiff.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87ce"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87ce-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87ce-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1e9b8078e9f98fcefff3d647eec94111515a03d01b8853f5966db27ffa00ec43",
      "skos:note": "Notify plaintiff of concurrent wrongdoer if reasonable grounds exist.",
      "dc:description": "Written notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-87ce-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "87CE(1) Defendant to notify plaintiff of concurrent wrongdoer of",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 374,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a defendant in proceedings involving an apportionable claim\nhas reasonable grounds to believe that a particular person (the\nother person) may be a concurrent wrongdoer in relation to\nthe claim; and\n\n(b) the defendant fails to give the plaintiff, as soon as\npracticable, written notice of the information that the\ndefendant has about:\n\n(i) the identity of the other person; and\n\n(ii) the circumstances that may make the other person a\nconcurrent wrongdoer in relation to the claim; and\n\n(c) the plaintiff unnecessarily incurs costs in the proceedings\nbecause the plaintiff was not aware that the other person may\nbe a concurrent wrongdoer in relation to the claim;\nthe court hearing the proceedings may order that the defendant pay\nall or any of those costs of the plaintiff."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87ce-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
