      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87cf-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Cannot",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition of contribution and indemnification",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87cg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "87CG Subsequent actions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-87cg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.375",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In relation to an apportionable claim, nothing in this Part or any\nother law prevents a plaintiff who has previously recovered\njudgment against a concurrent wrongdoer for an apportionable part\nof any damage or loss from bringing another action against any\nother concurrent wrongdoer for that damage or loss.\n\n(2) However, in any proceedings in respect of any such action, the\nplaintiff cannot recover an amount of damages that, having regard\nto any damages previously recovered by the plaintiff in respect of\nthe damage or loss, would result in the plaintiff receiving\ncompensation for damage or loss that is greater than the damage or\nloss actually sustained by the plaintiff.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In relation to an apportionable claim, nothing in this Part or any\nother law prevents a plaintiff who has previously recovered\njudgment against a concurrent wrongdoer for an apportionable part\nof any damage or loss from bringing another action against any\nother concurrent wrongdoer for that damage or loss.\n\n(2) However, in any proceedings in respect of any such action, the\nplaintiff cannot recover an amount of damages that, having regard\nto any damages previously recovered by the plaintiff in respect of\nthe damage or loss, would result in the plaintiff receiving\ncompensation for damage or loss that is greater than the damage or\nloss actually sustained by the plaintiff.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87cg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87cg-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b52de5db6ea761ea2b5e95136240ed15bb4dca146f10bf79cf7184244e4b2650"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-87cg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "87CG Subsequent actions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 375,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In relation to an apportionable claim, nothing in this Part or any\nother law prevents a plaintiff who has previously recovered\njudgment against a concurrent wrongdoer for an apportionable part\nof any damage or loss from bringing another action against any\nother concurrent wrongdoer for that damage or loss.\n\n(2) However, in any proceedings in respect of any such action, the\nplaintiff cannot recover an amount of damages that, having regard\nto any damages previously recovered by the plaintiff in respect of\nthe damage or loss, would result in the plaintiff receiving\ncompensation for damage or loss that is greater than the damage or\nloss actually sustained by the plaintiff."
    },
    {
