      "values:originalText": "(4) If the plaintiff:\n\n(a) would have provided the services during a quarter for which,\nat the time the award was made, the amount of average\nweekly earnings was not ascertainable; or\n\n(b) would have provided the services after the time the award\nwas made;\nthe court must not award as personal injury damages for the\nservices:\n\n(c) if the services were provided for at least 40 hours per week—\nan amount per week that exceeds average weekly earnings\nfor the quarter that, at the time the award was made, was the\nmost recent quarter for which the amount of average weekly\nearnings was ascertainable; or\n\n(d) if the services were provided for less than 40 hours per\nweek—an amount per hour that exceeds 1/40 of average\nweekly earnings for that quarter.\n\nChapter 5  Enforcement and remedies"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87x-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87x-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87x-ss-4-logic-linearlogic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LinearLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "<",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Service duration comparison",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Services provided for less than 40 hours/week",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Court must not award damages exceeding 1/40 of average weekly earnings"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87x-ss-4-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Service duration restriction",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Services provided for at least 40 hours/week",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Court must not award damages exceeding this threshold"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87y",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "87Y Damages for future economic loss—discount rate",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-87y"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.394",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an award of personal injury damages in a proceeding to which\nthis Part applies is to include any component, assessed as a lump\nsum, for future economic loss of any kind, the present value of that\nfuture economic loss is to be determined by applying:\n\n(a) a discount rate of the percentage prescribed by the\nregulations; or\n\n(b) if no percentage is prescribed—a discount rate of 5%.\n\n(2) A regulation made for the purposes of paragraph (1)(a) does not\ncommence before the end of the period of 6 months starting:\n\n(a) if the regulation is laid before each House of the Parliament\nunder section 38 of the Legislation Act 2003 on the same\nday—on that day; or\n\n(b) if it is laid before each House of the Parliament under that\nsection on different days—on the later of those days.\n\n(3) Except as provided by this section, this section does not affect any\nother law relating to the discounting of sums awarded as damages\nor compensation.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If an award of personal injury damages in a proceeding to which\nthis Part applies is to include any component, assessed as a lump\nsum, for future economic loss of any kind, the present value of that\nfuture economic loss is to be determined by applying:\n\n(a) a discount rate of the percentage prescribed by the\nregulations; or\n\n(b) if no percentage is prescribed—a discount rate of 5%.\n\n(2) A regulation made for the purposes of paragraph (1)(a) does not\ncommence before the end of the period of 6 months starting:\n\n(a) if the regulation is laid before each House of the Parliament\nunder section 38 of the Legislation Act 2003 on the same\nday—on that day; or\n\n(b) if it is laid before each House of the Parliament under that\nsection on different days—on the later of those days.\n\n(3) Except as provided by this section, this section does not affect any\nother law relating to the discounting of sums awarded as damages\nor compensation.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87y-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87y-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87y-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "89f223588067768070e4eed2b66cdf9a5e5fcedc84fc20b767cae85f14850c41"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-87y",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "87Y Damages for future economic loss—discount rate",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 394,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an award of personal injury damages in a proceeding to which\nthis Part applies is to include any component, assessed as a lump\nsum, for future economic loss of any kind, the present value of that\nfuture economic loss is to be determined by applying:\n\n(a) a discount rate of the percentage prescribed by the\nregulations; or\n\n(b) if no percentage is prescribed—a discount rate of 5%.\n\n(2) A regulation made for the purposes of paragraph (1)(a) does not\ncommence before the end of the period of 6 months starting:\n\n(a) if the regulation is laid before each House of the Parliament\nunder section 38 of the Legislation Act 2003 on the same\nday—on that day; or\n\n(b) if it is laid before each House of the Parliament under that\nsection on different days—on the later of those days.\n\n(3) Except as provided by this section, this section does not affect any\nother law relating to the discounting of sums awarded as damages\nor compensation."
    },
