    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87z",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "87Z Damages for loss of superannuation entitlements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-87z"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.394",
      "values:originalText": "A court must not, in a proceeding to which this Part applies, award\npersonal injury damages for economic loss due to the loss of\nemployer superannuation contributions an amount that exceeds the\nfollowing amount:\n\nwhere:\ndamages for earnings loss are the personal injury damages\npayable (in accordance with this Part) for:\nSuperannuation percentage\nDamages for earnings loss\n´\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nClaims for damages or compensation for death or personal injury  Part VIB\nOther limits on personal injury damages  Division 6\n\nSection 87ZA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) any past economic loss due to loss of earnings, or the\ndeprivation or impairment of earning capacity, on which the\nentitlement to those contributions is based; and\n\n(b) any future economic loss due to the deprivation or\nimpairment of earning capacity on which the entitlement to\nthose contributions would be based.\nsuperannuation percentage is the highest employer’s charge\npercentage for a quarter under section 19 of the Superannuation\nGuarantee (Administration) Act 1992.",
      "skos:definition": "A court must not, in a proceeding to which this Part applies, award\npersonal injury damages for economic loss due to the loss of\nemployer superannuation contributions an amount that exceeds the\nfollowing amount:\n\nwhere:\ndamages for earnings loss are the personal injury damages\npayable (in accordance with this Part) for:\nSuperannuation percentage\nDamages for earnings loss\n´\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nClaims for damages or compensation for death or personal injury  Part VIB\nOther limits on personal injury damages  Division 6\n\nSection 87ZA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) any past economic loss due to loss of earnings, or the\ndeprivation or impairment of earning capacity, on which the\nentitlement to those contributions is based; and\n\n(b) any future economic loss due to the deprivation or\nimpairment of earning capacity on which the entitlement to\nthose contributions would be based.\nsuperannuation percentage is the highest employer’s charge\npercentage for a quarter under section 19 of the Superannuation\nGuarantee (Administration) Act 1992.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87z-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87z-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87z-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87z-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-87z-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4ce5be489e718dbfa6157cd0bc4c3aaf051131ab0245c0fd2b26f4b5b1303d20",
      "skos:note": "Court cannot award personal injury damages exceeding a certain amount for economic loss due to loss of employer superannuation contributions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-87z",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "87Z Damages for loss of superannuation entitlements",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 394,
      "values:originalText": "A court must not, in a proceeding to which this Part applies, award\npersonal injury damages for economic loss due to the loss of\nemployer superannuation contributions an amount that exceeds the\nfollowing amount:\n\nwhere:\ndamages for earnings loss are the personal injury damages\npayable (in accordance with this Part) for:\nSuperannuation percentage\nDamages for earnings loss\n´\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nClaims for damages or compensation for death or personal injury  Part VIB\nOther limits on personal injury damages  Division 6\n\nSection 87ZA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) any past economic loss due to loss of earnings, or the\ndeprivation or impairment of earning capacity, on which the\nentitlement to those contributions is based; and\n\n(b) any future economic loss due to the deprivation or\nimpairment of earning capacity on which the entitlement to\nthose contributions would be based.\nsuperannuation percentage is the highest employer’s charge\npercentage for a quarter under section 19 of the Superannuation\nGuarantee (Administration) Act 1992."
    },
