      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.396",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A court must not, in a proceeding to which this Part applies, award\nexemplary damages or aggravated damages in respect of death or\npersonal injury.\n\n(2) This section does not affect whether a court has power to award\nexemplary damages or aggravated damages:\n\n(a) otherwise than in respect of death or personal injury; or\n\n(b) in a proceeding other than a proceeding to which this Part\napplies.\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nClaims for damages or compensation for death or personal injury  Part VIB\nStructured settlements  Division 7\n\nSection 87ZC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A court must not, in a proceeding to which this Part applies, award\nexemplary damages or aggravated damages in respect of death or\npersonal injury.\n\n(2) This section does not affect whether a court has power to award\nexemplary damages or aggravated damages:\n\n(a) otherwise than in respect of death or personal injury; or\n\n(b) in a proceeding other than a proceeding to which this Part\napplies.\n\nEnforcement and remedies  Chapter 5\nClaims for damages or compensation for death or personal injury  Part VIB\nStructured settlements  Division 7\n\nSection 87ZC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
