      "cof:title": "87ZP Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 398,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Division:\nindustry code of practice means a code regulating the conduct of\nparticipants in an industry towards other participants in the\nindustry or towards consumers in the industry.\nminor variation, in relation to an authorisation, is a single variation\nthat does not involve a material change in the effect of the\nauthorisation.\n\n(2) A reference in this Division to a proposal of the Commission is a\nreference to a notice of the Commission:\n\n(a) so far as the revocation of an authorisation is concerned—\nunder subsection 91B(3); and\n\n(b) so far as the revocation of an authorisation and the\nsubstitution of another—under subsection 91C(3).\n\n(3) A reference in this Division to an authorisation is a reference to an\nauthorisation under this Division."
    },
