    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-88",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "88 Commission may grant authorisations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-88"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.398",
      "values:originalText": "Granting an authorisation\n\n(1) Subject to this Part, the Commission may, on an application by a\nperson, grant an authorisation to a person to engage in conduct,\nspecified in the authorisation, to which one or more provisions of\nDivision 1 or 2 of Part IV specified in the authorisation would or\nmight apply.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nAuthorisations  Division 1\n\nSection 88\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote:\nFor an extended meaning of engaging in conduct, see subsection 4(2).\n\n(1A) The application must be made on or before 30 June 2025 if any of\nthe specified provisions is section 50.\nEffect of an authorisation\n\n(2) While the authorisation remains in force, the provisions of\nDivision 1 or 2 of Part IV specified in the authorisation do not\napply in relation to the conduct to the extent that it is engaged in\nby:\n\n(a) the applicant; and\n\n(b) any other person named or referred to in the application as a\nperson who is engaged in, or who is proposed to be engaged\nin, the conduct; and\n\n(c) any particular persons or classes of persons, as specified in\nthe authorisation, who become engaged in the conduct.\nConditions\n\n(3) The Commission may specify conditions in the authorisation.\nSubsection (2) does not apply if any of the conditions are not\ncomplied with.\n\n(4) Without limiting subsection (3), the Commission may grant a\nmerger authorisation on the condition that a person must give, and\ncomply with, an undertaking to the Commission under\nsection 87B.\nSingle authorisation may deal with several types of conduct\n\n(5) The Commission may grant a single authorisation for all the\nconduct specified in an application for authorisation, or may grant\nseparate authorisations for any of the conduct.\nPast conduct\n\n(6) The Commission does not have power to grant an authorisation for\nconduct engaged in before the Commission decides the application\nfor the authorisation.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "Granting an authorisation\n\n(1) Subject to this Part, the Commission may, on an application by a\nperson, grant an authorisation to a person to engage in conduct,\nspecified in the authorisation, to which one or more provisions of\nDivision 1 or 2 of Part IV specified in the authorisation would or\nmight apply.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nAuthorisations  Division 1\n\nSection 88\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote:\nFor an extended meaning of engaging in conduct, see subsection 4(2).\n\n(1A) The application must be made on or before 30 June 2025 if any of\nthe specified provisions is section 50.\nEffect of an authorisation\n\n(2) While the authorisation remains in force, the provisions of\nDivision 1 or 2 of Part IV specified in the authorisation do not\napply in relation to the conduct to the extent that it is engaged in\nby:\n\n(a) the applicant; and\n\n(b) any other person named or referred to in the application as a\nperson who is engaged in, or who is proposed to be engaged\nin, the conduct; and\n\n(c) any particular persons or classes of persons, as specified in\nthe authorisation, who become engaged in the conduct.\nConditions\n\n(3) The Commission may specify conditions in the authorisation.\nSubsection (2) does not apply if any of the conditions are not\ncomplied with.\n\n(4) Without limiting subsection (3), the Commission may grant a\nmerger authorisation on the condition that a person must give, and\ncomply with, an undertaking to the Commission under\nsection 87B.\nSingle authorisation may deal with several types of conduct\n\n(5) The Commission may grant a single authorisation for all the\nconduct specified in an application for authorisation, or may grant\nseparate authorisations for any of the conduct.\nPast conduct\n\n(6) The Commission does not have power to grant an authorisation for\nconduct engaged in before the Commission decides the application\nfor the authorisation.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-88-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-88-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-88-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-88-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-88-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-88-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-88-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "df50695fb6e2bbdace8b7cb1fd7d4cbe7c3fcdfc2c4868303572fc1d6b4a0d19"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-88",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "88 Commission may grant authorisations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 398,
      "values:originalText": "Granting an authorisation\n\n(1) Subject to this Part, the Commission may, on an application by a\nperson, grant an authorisation to a person to engage in conduct,\nspecified in the authorisation, to which one or more provisions of\nDivision 1 or 2 of Part IV specified in the authorisation would or\nmight apply.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nAuthorisations  Division 1\n\nSection 88\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote:\nFor an extended meaning of engaging in conduct, see subsection 4(2).\n\n(1A) The application must be made on or before 30 June 2025 if any of\nthe specified provisions is section 50.\nEffect of an authorisation\n\n(2) While the authorisation remains in force, the provisions of\nDivision 1 or 2 of Part IV specified in the authorisation do not\napply in relation to the conduct to the extent that it is engaged in\nby:\n\n(a) the applicant; and\n\n(b) any other person named or referred to in the application as a\nperson who is engaged in, or who is proposed to be engaged\nin, the conduct; and\n\n(c) any particular persons or classes of persons, as specified in\nthe authorisation, who become engaged in the conduct.\nConditions\n\n(3) The Commission may specify conditions in the authorisation.\nSubsection (2) does not apply if any of the conditions are not\ncomplied with.\n\n(4) Without limiting subsection (3), the Commission may grant a\nmerger authorisation on the condition that a person must give, and\ncomply with, an undertaking to the Commission under\nsection 87B.\nSingle authorisation may deal with several types of conduct\n\n(5) The Commission may grant a single authorisation for all the\nconduct specified in an application for authorisation, or may grant\nseparate authorisations for any of the conduct.\nPast conduct\n\n(6) The Commission does not have power to grant an authorisation for\nconduct engaged in before the Commission decides the application\nfor the authorisation.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
