    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-90a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "90A(4) Commission to afford opportunity for conference before",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-90a-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.408",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n\n(a) the draft determination does not provide for the granting of\nthe application or provides for the granting of the application\nsubject to conditions; or\n\n(b) the draft determination provides for the granting of the\napplication unconditionally but a written submission has, or\nwritten submissions have, been made to the Commission\nopposing the application;\nthe Commission shall send with each notice under subsection (2) a\ncopy of the draft determination and:\n\n(c) in a case to which paragraph (a) applies—a summary of the\nreasons why the Commission is not satisfied that the\napplication should be granted or why it is not satisfied that\nthe application should be granted unconditionally; or\n\n(d) in a case to which paragraph (b) applies—a summary of the\nreasons why it is satisfied that the application should be\ngranted unconditionally.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If:\n\n(a) the draft determination does not provide for the granting of\nthe application or provides for the granting of the application\nsubject to conditions; or\n\n(b) the draft determination provides for the granting of the\napplication unconditionally but a written submission has, or\nwritten submissions have, been made to the Commission\nopposing the application;\nthe Commission shall send with each notice under subsection (2) a\ncopy of the draft determination and:\n\n(c) in a case to which paragraph (a) applies—a summary of the\nreasons why the Commission is not satisfied that the\napplication should be granted or why it is not satisfied that\nthe application should be granted unconditionally; or\n\n(d) in a case to which paragraph (b) applies—a summary of the\nreasons why it is satisfied that the application should be\ngranted unconditionally.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-90a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-90a-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-90a-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "85de46c872be4bee10d73e15fa2b30c5b1fb41121ee9f902fb78c9aa24bd5ee3",
      "skos:note": "The Commission must send a copy of the draft determination and a summary of reasons with each notice under subsection (2).",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-90a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "90A(4) Commission to afford opportunity for conference before",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 408,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n\n(a) the draft determination does not provide for the granting of\nthe application or provides for the granting of the application\nsubject to conditions; or\n\n(b) the draft determination provides for the granting of the\napplication unconditionally but a written submission has, or\nwritten submissions have, been made to the Commission\nopposing the application;\nthe Commission shall send with each notice under subsection (2) a\ncopy of the draft determination and:\n\n(c) in a case to which paragraph (a) applies—a summary of the\nreasons why the Commission is not satisfied that the\napplication should be granted or why it is not satisfied that\nthe application should be granted unconditionally; or\n\n(d) in a case to which paragraph (b) applies—a summary of the\nreasons why it is satisfied that the application should be\ngranted unconditionally."
    },
