      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) the National Electricity Rules, as in force from time to time,",
      "cml:conclusionText": "National Electricity Rules means..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-90b-ss-3-logic-descriptionlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Includes rules from other jurisdictions",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) those Rules as they apply as a law of another State;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...or (c) those Rules as they apply as a law of a Territory;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-90b-ss-3-logic-descriptionlogic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Includes rules from the Commonwealth",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(d) those Rules as they apply as a law of the Commonwealth.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...or (c) those Rules as they apply as a law of the Commonwealth."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "91 Grant and variation of authorisations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-91"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.413",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authorisation may be expressed to be in force for a period\nspecified in the authorisation and, if so expressed, remains in force\nfor that period only.\n\n(1A) An authorisation, other than an authorisation deemed to have been\ngranted under subsection 90(10) or (11), comes into force on the\nday specified for the purpose in the authorisation, not being a day\nearlier than, and an authorisation deemed to have been granted\nunder subsection 90(10) or (11) comes into force on:\n\n(a) where paragraph (b) or (c) does not apply—the end of the\nperiod in which an application may be made to the Tribunal\nfor a review of the determination by the Commission of the\napplication for the authorisation;\n\n(b) if such an application is made to the Tribunal and the\napplication is not withdrawn—the day on which the Tribunal\nmakes a determination on the review;\n\n(c) if such an application is made to the Tribunal and the\napplication is withdrawn—the day on which the application\nis withdrawn.\n\n(1B) A minor variation of an authorisation comes into force on a day\nspecified by the Commission in the determination making the\nvariation, not being a day earlier than:\n\n(a) if neither paragraph (b) nor (c) applies—the end of the period\nin which an application may be made to the Tribunal for a\nreview of the determination of the Commission in respect of\nthe application for the minor variation; or\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An authorisation may be expressed to be in force for a period\nspecified in the authorisation and, if so expressed, remains in force\nfor that period only.\n\n(1A) An authorisation, other than an authorisation deemed to have been\ngranted under subsection 90(10) or (11), comes into force on the\nday specified for the purpose in the authorisation, not being a day\nearlier than, and an authorisation deemed to have been granted\nunder subsection 90(10) or (11) comes into force on:\n\n(a) where paragraph (b) or (c) does not apply—the end of the\nperiod in which an application may be made to the Tribunal\nfor a review of the determination by the Commission of the\napplication for the authorisation;\n\n(b) if such an application is made to the Tribunal and the\napplication is not withdrawn—the day on which the Tribunal\nmakes a determination on the review;\n\n(c) if such an application is made to the Tribunal and the\napplication is withdrawn—the day on which the application\nis withdrawn.\n\n(1B) A minor variation of an authorisation comes into force on a day\nspecified by the Commission in the determination making the\nvariation, not being a day earlier than:\n\n(a) if neither paragraph (b) nor (c) applies—the end of the period\nin which an application may be made to the Tribunal for a\nreview of the determination of the Commission in respect of\nthe application for the minor variation; or\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91-ss-1b"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "081db26b9617a2af1ed57fab30075a09f25a3ef6600f6f481d5c2dda08519dd6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-91",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "91 Grant and variation of authorisations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 413,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authorisation may be expressed to be in force for a period\nspecified in the authorisation and, if so expressed, remains in force\nfor that period only.\n\n(1A) An authorisation, other than an authorisation deemed to have been\ngranted under subsection 90(10) or (11), comes into force on the\nday specified for the purpose in the authorisation, not being a day\nearlier than, and an authorisation deemed to have been granted\nunder subsection 90(10) or (11) comes into force on:\n\n(a) where paragraph (b) or (c) does not apply—the end of the\nperiod in which an application may be made to the Tribunal\nfor a review of the determination by the Commission of the\napplication for the authorisation;\n\n(b) if such an application is made to the Tribunal and the\napplication is not withdrawn—the day on which the Tribunal\nmakes a determination on the review;\n\n(c) if such an application is made to the Tribunal and the\napplication is withdrawn—the day on which the application\nis withdrawn.\n\n(1B) A minor variation of an authorisation comes into force on a day\nspecified by the Commission in the determination making the\nvariation, not being a day earlier than:\n\n(a) if neither paragraph (b) nor (c) applies—the end of the period\nin which an application may be made to the Tribunal for a\nreview of the determination of the Commission in respect of\nthe application for the minor variation; or\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
