    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "91B(2) Revocation of an authorisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-91b-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.418",
      "values:originalText": "(2) On receipt of such an application, the Commission must, by notice\nin writing given to any persons who appear to the Commission to\nbe interested:\n\n(a) indicate that the revocation of the authorisation has been\napplied for; and\n\n(b) indicate the basis on which the revocation has been applied\nfor; and\n\n(c) invite submissions in respect of the revocation within a\nperiod specified by the Commission.\nNote:\nAlternatively, the Commission may rely on consultations undertaken\nby the AEMC: see section 90B.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) On receipt of such an application, the Commission must, by notice\nin writing given to any persons who appear to the Commission to\nbe interested:\n\n(a) indicate that the revocation of the authorisation has been\napplied for; and\n\n(b) indicate the basis on which the revocation has been applied\nfor; and\n\n(c) invite submissions in respect of the revocation within a\nperiod specified by the Commission.\nNote:\nAlternatively, the Commission may rely on consultations undertaken\nby the AEMC: see section 90B.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fca67b27fd4129aff1f14830646d563333027bd71ecb9ffd74e50efa643d80e9",
      "skos:note": "Commission must notify interested persons of revocation application and basis."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-91b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "91B(2) Revocation of an authorisation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 418,
      "values:originalText": "(2) On receipt of such an application, the Commission must, by notice\nin writing given to any persons who appear to the Commission to\nbe interested:\n\n(a) indicate that the revocation of the authorisation has been\napplied for; and\n\n(b) indicate the basis on which the revocation has been applied\nfor; and\n\n(c) invite submissions in respect of the revocation within a\nperiod specified by the Commission.\nNote:\nAlternatively, the Commission may rely on consultations undertaken\nby the AEMC: see section 90B."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
