      "cml:logicSummary": "Notification obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "91B(3) Revocation of an authorisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-91b-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.418",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If, at any time after granting an authorisation, it appears to the\nCommission that:\n\n(a) the authorisation was granted on the basis of evidence or\ninformation that was false or misleading in a material\nparticular; or\n\n(b) a condition to which the authorisation was expressed to be\nsubject has not been complied with; or\n\n(c) there has been a material change of circumstances since the\nauthorisation was granted;\nthe Commission may, by notice in writing given to any persons\nwho appear to the Commission to be interested:\n\n(d) inform those persons that it is considering the revocation of\nthe authorisation; and\n\n(e) indicate the basis on which the revocation is being proposed;\nand\n\n(f) invite submissions in respect of the revocation within a\nperiod specified by the Commission.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nAuthorisations  Division 1\n\nSection 91B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If, at any time after granting an authorisation, it appears to the\nCommission that:\n\n(a) the authorisation was granted on the basis of evidence or\ninformation that was false or misleading in a material\nparticular; or\n\n(b) a condition to which the authorisation was expressed to be\nsubject has not been complied with; or\n\n(c) there has been a material change of circumstances since the\nauthorisation was granted;\nthe Commission may, by notice in writing given to any persons\nwho appear to the Commission to be interested:\n\n(d) inform those persons that it is considering the revocation of\nthe authorisation; and\n\n(e) indicate the basis on which the revocation is being proposed;\nand\n\n(f) invite submissions in respect of the revocation within a\nperiod specified by the Commission.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nAuthorisations  Division 1\n\nSection 91B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b-ss-3-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b-ss-3-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b-ss-3-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bb4c64ca4bd58a9861682eb6861997b5612800de99e9e4dd80dab8c5aea0adaf",
      "skos:note": "Revocation of an authorisation if certain conditions are met"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-91b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "91B(3) Revocation of an authorisation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 418,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If, at any time after granting an authorisation, it appears to the\nCommission that:\n\n(a) the authorisation was granted on the basis of evidence or\ninformation that was false or misleading in a material\nparticular; or\n\n(b) a condition to which the authorisation was expressed to be\nsubject has not been complied with; or\n\n(c) there has been a material change of circumstances since the\nauthorisation was granted;\nthe Commission may, by notice in writing given to any persons\nwho appear to the Commission to be interested:\n\n(d) inform those persons that it is considering the revocation of\nthe authorisation; and\n\n(e) indicate the basis on which the revocation is being proposed;\nand\n\n(f) invite submissions in respect of the revocation within a\nperiod specified by the Commission.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nAuthorisations  Division 1\n\nSection 91B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b-ss-3-norm",
