    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "91B(4) Revocation of an authorisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-91b-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.418",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Commission may make a determination in writing revoking\nthe authorisation, or deciding not to revoke the authorisation, after\ntaking into account the following:\n\n(a) if subsection (2) applies—the application;\n\n(b) any submissions that are received within the period specified\nunder paragraph (2)(c) or (3)(f);\n\n(c) any information received under paragraph 90(6)(b) (as it\napplies because of subsection (3A) of this section) within the\nperiod specified in the notice mentioned in that paragraph;\n\n(d) any information received under paragraph 90(6)(c) (as it\napplies because of subsection (3A) or (3B) of this section)\nwithin the period specified in the notice mentioned in that\nparagraph;\n\n(e) any information obtained from consultations under\nparagraph 90(6)(d) (as it applies because of subsection (3A)\nor (3B) of this section).\nThe Commission may, but need not, take into account any\nsubmissions or information received after the end of those periods.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The Commission may make a determination in writing revoking\nthe authorisation, or deciding not to revoke the authorisation, after\ntaking into account the following:\n\n(a) if subsection (2) applies—the application;\n\n(b) any submissions that are received within the period specified\nunder paragraph (2)(c) or (3)(f);\n\n(c) any information received under paragraph 90(6)(b) (as it\napplies because of subsection (3A) of this section) within the\nperiod specified in the notice mentioned in that paragraph;\n\n(d) any information received under paragraph 90(6)(c) (as it\napplies because of subsection (3A) or (3B) of this section)\nwithin the period specified in the notice mentioned in that\nparagraph;\n\n(e) any information obtained from consultations under\nparagraph 90(6)(d) (as it applies because of subsection (3A)\nor (3B) of this section).\nThe Commission may, but need not, take into account any\nsubmissions or information received after the end of those periods.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ab5fe470952f9dbc917c8378a2d12fc18d3883eacc692a52c6be5740eea6981e",
      "skos:note": "Commission's decision on revoking an authorisation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-91b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "91B(4) Revocation of an authorisation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 418,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Commission may make a determination in writing revoking\nthe authorisation, or deciding not to revoke the authorisation, after\ntaking into account the following:\n\n(a) if subsection (2) applies—the application;\n\n(b) any submissions that are received within the period specified\nunder paragraph (2)(c) or (3)(f);\n\n(c) any information received under paragraph 90(6)(b) (as it\napplies because of subsection (3A) of this section) within the\nperiod specified in the notice mentioned in that paragraph;\n\n(d) any information received under paragraph 90(6)(c) (as it\napplies because of subsection (3A) or (3B) of this section)\nwithin the period specified in the notice mentioned in that\nparagraph;\n\n(e) any information obtained from consultations under\nparagraph 90(6)(d) (as it applies because of subsection (3A)\nor (3B) of this section).\nThe Commission may, but need not, take into account any\nsubmissions or information received after the end of those periods."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91b-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
