    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-91c-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "91C(2) Revocation of an authorisation and substitution of a",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 420,
      "values:originalText": "(2) On receipt of such an application, the Commission must, by notice\nin writing given to any persons who appear to the Commission to\nbe interested:\n\n(a) indicate that the revocation of the authorisation, and the\nsubstitution of another authorisation for it, has been applied\nfor; and\n\n(b) indicate the basis upon which the revocation and substitution\nhas been applied for and the nature of the substituted\nauthorisation so applied for; and\n\n(c) invite submissions in respect of the revocation and\nsubstitution within a period specified by the Commission.\nNote:\nAlternatively, the Commission may rely on consultations undertaken\nby the AEMC: see section 90B.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nAuthorisations  Division 1\n\nSection 91C\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91c-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91c-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91c-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Commission must provide notice",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91c-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "91C(3) Revocation of an authorisation and substitution of a",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-91c-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.420",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If, at any time after granting an authorisation, it appears to the\nCommission that:\n\n(a) the authorisation was granted on the basis of evidence or\ninformation that was false or misleading in a material\nparticular; or\n\n(b) a condition to which the authorisation was expressed to be\nsubject has not been complied with; or\n\n(c) there has been a material change of circumstances since the\nauthorisation was granted;\nthe Commission may, by notice in writing given to any persons\nwho appear to be interested:\n\n(d) inform those persons that it is considering the revocation of\nthe authorisation and the substitution of a new authorisation;\nand\n\n(e) indicate the basis on which the revocation and substitution is\nbeing proposed and the nature of the substituted authorisation\nproposed; and\n\n(f) invite submissions in respect of the proposed action within a\nperiod specified by the Commission.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If, at any time after granting an authorisation, it appears to the\nCommission that:\n\n(a) the authorisation was granted on the basis of evidence or\ninformation that was false or misleading in a material\nparticular; or\n\n(b) a condition to which the authorisation was expressed to be\nsubject has not been complied with; or\n\n(c) there has been a material change of circumstances since the\nauthorisation was granted;\nthe Commission may, by notice in writing given to any persons\nwho appear to be interested:\n\n(d) inform those persons that it is considering the revocation of\nthe authorisation and the substitution of a new authorisation;\nand\n\n(e) indicate the basis on which the revocation and substitution is\nbeing proposed and the nature of the substituted authorisation\nproposed; and\n\n(f) invite submissions in respect of the proposed action within a\nperiod specified by the Commission.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91c-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-91c-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2308364a6658eef7b55376f10f0713e4b8e76b397b0ea22f83b1e1715eb24fa1",
      "skos:note": "Commission may inform persons of proposed revocation and substitution of authorisation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-91c-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "91C(3) Revocation of an authorisation and substitution of a",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 420,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If, at any time after granting an authorisation, it appears to the\nCommission that:\n\n(a) the authorisation was granted on the basis of evidence or\ninformation that was false or misleading in a material\nparticular; or\n\n(b) a condition to which the authorisation was expressed to be\nsubject has not been complied with; or\n\n(c) there has been a material change of circumstances since the\nauthorisation was granted;\nthe Commission may, by notice in writing given to any persons\nwho appear to be interested:\n\n(d) inform those persons that it is considering the revocation of\nthe authorisation and the substitution of a new authorisation;\nand\n\n(e) indicate the basis on which the revocation and substitution is\nbeing proposed and the nature of the substituted authorisation\nproposed; and\n\n(f) invite submissions in respect of the proposed action within a\nperiod specified by the Commission."
    },
