    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-92b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "92B Commission may grant authorisations in exceptional",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-92b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.425",
      "values:originalText": "circumstances and emergencies\nGranting an authorisation in exceptional circumstances and\nemergencies\n\n(1) Subject to this Division, the Commission may, on an application by\na person, grant an authorisation to a person to engage in conduct,\nspecified in the authorisation, to which one or more provisions of\nDivision 1 or 2 of Part IV specified in the authorisation would or\nmight apply.\nNote:\nFor an extended meaning of engaging in conduct, see subsection 4(2).\nEffect of an authorisation\n\n(2) While the authorisation remains in force, the provisions of\nDivision 1 or 2 of Part IV specified in the authorisation do not\napply in relation to the conduct to the extent that it is engaged in\nby:\n\n(a) the applicant; and\n\n(b) any other person named or referred to in the application as a\nperson who is engaged in, or who is proposed to be engaged\nin, the conduct; and\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "circumstances and emergencies\nGranting an authorisation in exceptional circumstances and\nemergencies\n\n(1) Subject to this Division, the Commission may, on an application by\na person, grant an authorisation to a person to engage in conduct,\nspecified in the authorisation, to which one or more provisions of\nDivision 1 or 2 of Part IV specified in the authorisation would or\nmight apply.\nNote:\nFor an extended meaning of engaging in conduct, see subsection 4(2).\nEffect of an authorisation\n\n(2) While the authorisation remains in force, the provisions of\nDivision 1 or 2 of Part IV specified in the authorisation do not\napply in relation to the conduct to the extent that it is engaged in\nby:\n\n(a) the applicant; and\n\n(b) any other person named or referred to in the application as a\nperson who is engaged in, or who is proposed to be engaged\nin, the conduct; and\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-92b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-92b-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "563e1e9c9b1a3af0476e218c5a9226a1384b97f966fcce0bebf8fdeba65e6868"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-92b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "92B Commission may grant authorisations in exceptional",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 425,
      "values:originalText": "circumstances and emergencies\nGranting an authorisation in exceptional circumstances and\nemergencies\n\n(1) Subject to this Division, the Commission may, on an application by\na person, grant an authorisation to a person to engage in conduct,\nspecified in the authorisation, to which one or more provisions of\nDivision 1 or 2 of Part IV specified in the authorisation would or\nmight apply.\nNote:\nFor an extended meaning of engaging in conduct, see subsection 4(2).\nEffect of an authorisation\n\n(2) While the authorisation remains in force, the provisions of\nDivision 1 or 2 of Part IV specified in the authorisation do not\napply in relation to the conduct to the extent that it is engaged in\nby:\n\n(a) the applicant; and\n\n(b) any other person named or referred to in the application as a\nperson who is engaged in, or who is proposed to be engaged\nin, the conduct; and\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
