    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-92b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "92B(2) Commission may grant authorisations in exceptional",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 425,
      "values:originalText": "(2) While the authorisation remains in force, the provisions of\nDivision 1 or 2 of Part IV specified in the authorisation do not\napply in relation to the conduct to the extent that it is engaged in\nby:\n\n(a) the applicant; and\n\n(b) any other person named or referred to in the application as a\nperson who is engaged in, or who is proposed to be engaged\nin, the conduct; and\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
