      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-92f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "92F Variation of authorisations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-92f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.428",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may, at any time, make a determination in\nwriting to vary an authorisation under this Division if the\nCommission considers it appropriate to do so.\n\n(2) The Commission must not make a determination under\nsubsection (1) varying an authorisation unless the Commission is\nsatisfied that, in all the circumstances, the conduct specified in the\nauthorisation as varied would assist, or would be likely to assist, in\nthe response to or recovery from the exceptional circumstances or\nemergency to which the declaration relates.\n\n(3) In making a determination under subsection (1), the Commission:\n\n(a) must have regard to:\n\n(i) the likely benefit to the public resulting from the\nassistance, or likely assistance, in response to or\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nAuthorisations in exceptional circumstances and emergencies  Division 1A\n\nSection 92G\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nrecovery from the exceptional circumstances to which\nthe declaration relates; and\n\n(ii) the detriment to the public that would result, or be likely\nto result, from the conduct; and\n\n(b) may have regard to any other public benefit that would result\nor likely result from the conduct.\n\n(4) The Commission must give the person who applied for the\nauthorisation written notice stating:\n\n(a) that the authorisation is varied; and\n\n(b) details of the variation; and\n\n(c) the date on which the variation takes effect.\n\n(5) The variation takes effect on the business day after the day on\nwhich the notice is given.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commission may, at any time, make a determination in\nwriting to vary an authorisation under this Division if the\nCommission considers it appropriate to do so.\n\n(2) The Commission must not make a determination under\nsubsection (1) varying an authorisation unless the Commission is\nsatisfied that, in all the circumstances, the conduct specified in the\nauthorisation as varied would assist, or would be likely to assist, in\nthe response to or recovery from the exceptional circumstances or\nemergency to which the declaration relates.\n\n(3) In making a determination under subsection (1), the Commission:\n\n(a) must have regard to:\n\n(i) the likely benefit to the public resulting from the\nassistance, or likely assistance, in response to or\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nAuthorisations in exceptional circumstances and emergencies  Division 1A\n\nSection 92G\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nrecovery from the exceptional circumstances to which\nthe declaration relates; and\n\n(ii) the detriment to the public that would result, or be likely\nto result, from the conduct; and\n\n(b) may have regard to any other public benefit that would result\nor likely result from the conduct.\n\n(4) The Commission must give the person who applied for the\nauthorisation written notice stating:\n\n(a) that the authorisation is varied; and\n\n(b) details of the variation; and\n\n(c) the date on which the variation takes effect.\n\n(5) The variation takes effect on the business day after the day on\nwhich the notice is given.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-92f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-92f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-92f-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-92f-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-92f-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7a0290586a6b82966c9e1fe28519a9fcaaecf1d98aa61ca464216aa60722f069"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-92f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "92F Variation of authorisations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 428,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may, at any time, make a determination in\nwriting to vary an authorisation under this Division if the\nCommission considers it appropriate to do so.\n\n(2) The Commission must not make a determination under\nsubsection (1) varying an authorisation unless the Commission is\nsatisfied that, in all the circumstances, the conduct specified in the\nauthorisation as varied would assist, or would be likely to assist, in\nthe response to or recovery from the exceptional circumstances or\nemergency to which the declaration relates.\n\n(3) In making a determination under subsection (1), the Commission:\n\n(a) must have regard to:\n\n(i) the likely benefit to the public resulting from the\nassistance, or likely assistance, in response to or\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nAuthorisations in exceptional circumstances and emergencies  Division 1A\n\nSection 92G\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nrecovery from the exceptional circumstances to which\nthe declaration relates; and\n\n(ii) the detriment to the public that would result, or be likely\nto result, from the conduct; and\n\n(b) may have regard to any other public benefit that would result\nor likely result from the conduct.\n\n(4) The Commission must give the person who applied for the\nauthorisation written notice stating:\n\n(a) that the authorisation is varied; and\n\n(b) details of the variation; and\n\n(c) the date on which the variation takes effect.\n\n(5) The variation takes effect on the business day after the day on\nwhich the notice is given."
    },
