    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-93-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "93(2) Notification of exclusive dealing or resale price maintenance",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-93-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.431",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A corporation or other person may not give a notice under\nsubsection (1) for conduct or proposed conduct if:\n\n(a) the corporation or other person applied for an authorisation\nfor the conduct or proposed conduct; and\n\n(b) the Commission or the Trade Practices Commission made a\ndetermination dismissing the application; and\n\n(c) either:\n\n(i) the Tribunal or the Trade Practices Tribunal made a\ndetermination on an application for a review of a\ndetermination described in paragraph (b); or\n\n(ii) the time for making such an application for review has\nended without the making of an application.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A corporation or other person may not give a notice under\nsubsection (1) for conduct or proposed conduct if:\n\n(a) the corporation or other person applied for an authorisation\nfor the conduct or proposed conduct; and\n\n(b) the Commission or the Trade Practices Commission made a\ndetermination dismissing the application; and\n\n(c) either:\n\n(i) the Tribunal or the Trade Practices Tribunal made a\ndetermination on an application for a review of a\ndetermination described in paragraph (b); or\n\n(ii) the time for making such an application for review has\nended without the making of an application.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-93"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-93-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-93-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0b56716793d5a3981a3a847899af492cf5bc8428e01b46fffa54c10b1551bfc5",
      "skos:note": "No notice can be given for conduct or proposed conduct if certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-93-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "93(2) Notification of exclusive dealing or resale price maintenance",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 431,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A corporation or other person may not give a notice under\nsubsection (1) for conduct or proposed conduct if:\n\n(a) the corporation or other person applied for an authorisation\nfor the conduct or proposed conduct; and\n\n(b) the Commission or the Trade Practices Commission made a\ndetermination dismissing the application; and\n\n(c) either:\n\n(i) the Tribunal or the Trade Practices Tribunal made a\ndetermination on an application for a review of a\ndetermination described in paragraph (b); or\n\n(ii) the time for making such an application for review has\nended without the making of an application.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
