    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-93aa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "93AA Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-93aa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.438",
      "values:originalText": "In this Subdivision:\ncollective bargaining notice means a notice under\nsubsection 93AB(1A) or (1).\nconference notice means a notice under subsection 93A(2).\ncontract means a contract, arrangement or understanding.\nobjection notice means a notice under subsection 93AC(1), (2) or\n(2A).",
      "skos:definition": "In this Subdivision:\ncollective bargaining notice means a notice under\nsubsection 93AB(1A) or (1).\nconference notice means a notice under subsection 93A(2).\ncontract means a contract, arrangement or understanding.\nobjection notice means a notice under subsection 93AC(1), (2) or\n(2A).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-93aa-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "46fac7e6abe9b3c17e52e954fb059198ef951d133dcc6bbef62ea9c8787aa449",
      "skos:note": "Definitions for Subdivision"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-93aa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "93AA Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 438,
      "values:originalText": "In this Subdivision:\ncollective bargaining notice means a notice under\nsubsection 93AB(1A) or (1).\nconference notice means a notice under subsection 93A(2).\ncontract means a contract, arrangement or understanding.\nobjection notice means a notice under subsection 93AC(1), (2) or\n(2A)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-93aa-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-93aa"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-93ab",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "93AB Notification of collective bargaining",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-93ab"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.438",
      "values:originalText": "Notice to Commission—cartel provisions\n\n(1A) A corporation that:\n\n(a) has made, or proposes to make, a contract (the initial\ncontract) that contains a cartel provision that:\n\n(i) has the purpose; or\n\n(ii) has or is likely to have the effect;\n\nmentioned in subsection 45AD(2); or\n\n(b) has made, or proposes to make, a contract (the initial\ncontract) that contains a cartel provision that has the purpose\nmentioned in a paragraph of subsection 45AD(3) other than\nparagraph (c); or\n\n(c) proposes to give effect to a provision of a contract (the initial\ncontract) where the provision is a cartel provision that:\n\n(i) has the purpose; or\n\n(ii) has or is likely to have the effect;\n\nmentioned in subsection 45AD(2); or\n\n(d) proposes to give effect to a provision of a contract (the initial\ncontract) where the provision is a cartel provision that has\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nNotifications  Division 2\n\nSection 93AB\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe purpose mentioned in a paragraph of subsection 45AD(3)\nother than paragraph (c);\nmay give the Commission a notice (the collective bargaining\nnotice) setting out particulars of the contract or proposed contract,\nbut only if the 3 requirements set out in subsections (2), (3) and (4)\nare satisfied.\nNote 1:\nSubsection (6) deals with the form etc. of a collective bargaining\nnotice.\nNote 2:\nSection 93AD sets out when a collective bargaining notice comes into\nforce.\nNotice to Commission—competition provisions\n\n(1) A corporation that:\n\n(a) has made, or proposes to make, a contract (the initial\ncontract) containing a provision of the kind referred to in\nparagraph 45(1)(a); or\n\n(b) proposes to give effect to a provision of a contract (the initial\ncontract) where the provision is of the kind referred to in\nparagraph 45(1)(b);\nmay give the Commission a notice (the collective bargaining\nnotice) setting out particulars of the contract or proposed contract,\nbut only if the 3 requirements set out in subsections (2), (3) and (4)\nare satisfied.\nNote 1:\nSubsection (6) deals with the form etc. of a collective bargaining\nnotice.\nNote 2:\nSection 93AD sets out when a collective bargaining notice comes into\nforce.\nFirst—making of initial contract\n\n(2) First, the corporation must have made, or propose to make, the\ninitial contract with 1 or more persons (the contracting parties)\nabout:\n\n(a) the supply of particular goods or services to; or\n\n(b) the acquisition of particular goods or services from;\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "Notice to Commission—cartel provisions\n\n(1A) A corporation that:\n\n(a) has made, or proposes to make, a contract (the initial\ncontract) that contains a cartel provision that:\n\n(i) has the purpose; or\n\n(ii) has or is likely to have the effect;\n\nmentioned in subsection 45AD(2); or\n\n(b) has made, or proposes to make, a contract (the initial\ncontract) that contains a cartel provision that has the purpose\nmentioned in a paragraph of subsection 45AD(3) other than\nparagraph (c); or\n\n(c) proposes to give effect to a provision of a contract (the initial\ncontract) where the provision is a cartel provision that:\n\n(i) has the purpose; or\n\n(ii) has or is likely to have the effect;\n\nmentioned in subsection 45AD(2); or\n\n(d) proposes to give effect to a provision of a contract (the initial\ncontract) where the provision is a cartel provision that has\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nNotifications  Division 2\n\nSection 93AB\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe purpose mentioned in a paragraph of subsection 45AD(3)\nother than paragraph (c);\nmay give the Commission a notice (the collective bargaining\nnotice) setting out particulars of the contract or proposed contract,\nbut only if the 3 requirements set out in subsections (2), (3) and (4)\nare satisfied.\nNote 1:\nSubsection (6) deals with the form etc. of a collective bargaining\nnotice.\nNote 2:\nSection 93AD sets out when a collective bargaining notice comes into\nforce.\nNotice to Commission—competition provisions\n\n(1) A corporation that:\n\n(a) has made, or proposes to make, a contract (the initial\ncontract) containing a provision of the kind referred to in\nparagraph 45(1)(a); or\n\n(b) proposes to give effect to a provision of a contract (the initial\ncontract) where the provision is of the kind referred to in\nparagraph 45(1)(b);\nmay give the Commission a notice (the collective bargaining\nnotice) setting out particulars of the contract or proposed contract,\nbut only if the ",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-93ab-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-93ab-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-93ab-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "78932371096ab150a2ab4f340e037a6434158c5f50feb94387d8eeac3d39ab4b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-93ab",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "93AB Notification of collective bargaining",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 438,
      "values:originalText": "Notice to Commission—cartel provisions\n\n(1A) A corporation that:\n\n(a) has made, or proposes to make, a contract (the initial\ncontract) that contains a cartel provision that:\n\n(i) has the purpose; or\n\n(ii) has or is likely to have the effect;\n\nmentioned in subsection 45AD(2); or\n\n(b) has made, or proposes to make, a contract (the initial\ncontract) that contains a cartel provision that has the purpose\nmentioned in a paragraph of subsection 45AD(3) other than\nparagraph (c); or\n\n(c) proposes to give effect to a provision of a contract (the initial\ncontract) where the provision is a cartel provision that:\n\n(i) has the purpose; or\n\n(ii) has or is likely to have the effect;\n\nmentioned in subsection 45AD(2); or\n\n(d) proposes to give effect to a provision of a contract (the initial\ncontract) where the provision is a cartel provision that has\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nNotifications  Division 2\n\nSection 93AB\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe purpose mentioned in a paragraph of subsection 45AD(3)\nother than paragraph (c);\nmay give the Commission a notice (the collective bargaining\nnotice) setting out particulars of the contract or proposed contract,\nbut only if the 3 requirements set out in subsections (2), (3) and (4)\nare satisfied.\nNote 1:\nSubsection (6) deals with the form etc. of a collective bargaining\nnotice.\nNote 2:\nSection 93AD sets out when a collective bargaining notice comes into\nforce.\nNotice to Commission—competition provisions\n\n(1) A corporation that:\n\n(a) has made, or proposes to make, a contract (the initial\ncontract) containing a provision of the kind referred to in\nparagraph 45(1)(a); or\n\n(b) proposes to give effect to a provision of a contract (the initial\ncontract) where the provision is of the kind referred to in\nparagraph 45(1)(b);\nmay give the Commission a notice (the collective bargaining\nnotice) setting out particulars of the contract or proposed contract,\nbut only if the 3 requirements set out in subsections (2), (3) and (4)\nare satisfied.\nNote 1:\nSubsection (6) deals with the form etc. of a collective bargaining\nnotice.\nNote 2:\nSection 93AD sets out when a collective bargaining notice comes into\nforce.\nFirst—making of initial contract\n\n(2) First, the corporation must have made, or propose to make, the\ninitial contract with 1 or more persons (the contracting parties)\nabout:\n\n(a) the supply of particular goods or services to; or\n\n(b) the acquisition of particular goods or services from;\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
