    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95aa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "95AA Commission may determine class exemptions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95aa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.459",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may, by legislative instrument, determine that\none or more specified provisions of Division 1 or 2 of Part IV do\nnot apply to a kind of conduct specified in the determination, if the\nCommission is satisfied in all the circumstances:\n\n(a) that conduct of that kind would not have the effect, or would\nnot be likely to have the effect, of substantially lessening\ncompetition; or\n\n(b) that conduct of that kind would result, or would be likely to\nresult, in a benefit to the public that would outweigh the\ndetriment to the public that would result, or would be likely\nto result, from conduct of that kind.\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\n(2) The Commission may specify in the determination any one or more\nof the following limitations:\n\n(a) a limitation to persons of a specified kind;\n\n(b) a limitation to circumstances of a specified kind;\n\n(c) a limitation to conduct that complies with specified\nconditions.\n\n(3) The determination must specify the period, ending no later than the\nend of the period of 10 years beginning on the day it is made, for\nwhich it is to be in force.\n\n(4) The determination:\n\n(a) enters into force on the day it is made or on such later day (if\nany) as is specified in the determination; and\n\n(b) ceases to be in force at the earlier of the following times:\n\n(i) if the determination is revoked—at the time the\nrevocation takes effect;\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commission may, by legislative instrument, determine that\none or more specified provisions of Division 1 or 2 of Part IV do\nnot apply to a kind of conduct specified in the determination, if the\nCommission is satisfied in all the circumstances:\n\n(a) that conduct of that kind would not have the effect, or would\nnot be likely to have the effect, of substantially lessening\ncompetition; or\n\n(b) that conduct of that kind would result, or would be likely to\nresult, in a benefit to the public that would outweigh the\ndetriment to the public that would result, or would be likely\nto result, from conduct of that kind.\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\n(2) The Commission may specify in the determination any one or more\nof the following limitations:\n\n(a) a limitation to persons of a specified kind;\n\n(b) a limitation to circumstances of a specified kind;\n\n(c) a limitation to conduct that complies with specified\nconditions.\n\n(3) The determination must specify the period, ending no later than the\nend of the period of 10 years beginning on the day it is made, for\nwhich it is to be in force.\n\n(4) The determination:\n\n(a) enters into force on the day it is made or on such later day (if\nany) as is specified in the determination; and\n\n(b) ceases to be in force at the earlier of the following times:\n\n(i) if the determination is revoked—at the time the\nrevocation takes effect;\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95aa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95aa-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95aa-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95aa-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5089fb4e589b5564f157ac7405eeb5e47ca6a37238a1f6540aff6e97bf8f0724"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95aa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "95AA Commission may determine class exemptions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 459,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may, by legislative instrument, determine that\none or more specified provisions of Division 1 or 2 of Part IV do\nnot apply to a kind of conduct specified in the determination, if the\nCommission is satisfied in all the circumstances:\n\n(a) that conduct of that kind would not have the effect, or would\nnot be likely to have the effect, of substantially lessening\ncompetition; or\n\n(b) that conduct of that kind would result, or would be likely to\nresult, in a benefit to the public that would outweigh the\ndetriment to the public that would result, or would be likely\nto result, from conduct of that kind.\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\n(2) The Commission may specify in the determination any one or more\nof the following limitations:\n\n(a) a limitation to persons of a specified kind;\n\n(b) a limitation to circumstances of a specified kind;\n\n(c) a limitation to conduct that complies with specified\nconditions.\n\n(3) The determination must specify the period, ending no later than the\nend of the period of 10 years beginning on the day it is made, for\nwhich it is to be in force.\n\n(4) The determination:\n\n(a) enters into force on the day it is made or on such later day (if\nany) as is specified in the determination; and\n\n(b) ceases to be in force at the earlier of the following times:\n\n(i) if the determination is revoked—at the time the\nrevocation takes effect;\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95aa-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "95AA(1) Commission may determine class exemptions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95aa-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.459",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may, by legislative instrument, determine that\none or more specified provisions of Division 1 or 2 of Part IV do\nnot apply to a kind of conduct specified in the determination, if the\nCommission is satisfied in all the circumstances:\n\n(a) that conduct of that kind would not have the effect, or would\nnot be likely to have the effect, of substantially lessening\ncompetition; or\n\n(b) that conduct of that kind would result, or would be likely to\nresult, in a benefit to the public that would outweigh the\ndetriment to the public that would result, or would be likely\nto result, from conduct of that kind.\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commission may, by legislative instrument, determine that\none or more specified provisions of Division 1 or 2 of Part IV do\nnot apply to a kind of conduct specified in the determination, if the\nCommission is satisfied in all the circumstances:\n\n(a) that conduct of that kind would not have the effect, or would\nnot be likely to have the effect, of substantially lessening\ncompetition; or\n\n(b) that conduct of that kind would result, or would be likely to\nresult, in a benefit to the public that would outweigh the\ndetriment to the public that would result, or would be likely\nto result, from conduct of that kind.\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.",
