    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95ac",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "95AC Exceptional circumstances class exemptions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95ac"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.461",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a declaration mentioned in subsection (2) is in force, the\nCommission may, in writing, determine that one or more specified\nprovisions of Division 1 or 2 of Part IV do not apply to a kind of\nconduct specified in the determination.\n\n(2) The declarations are the following:\n\n(a) a declaration under section 95AE;\n\n(b) a national emergency declaration (within the meaning of the\nNational Emergency Declaration Act 2020).\n\n(3) The Commission must not make a determination under\nsubsection (1) unless the Commission is satisfied that, in all the\ncircumstances, the conduct of that kind would assist, or would be\nlikely to assist, in the response to or recovery from the exceptional\ncircumstances or emergency to which the declaration relates.\n\n(4) In making a determination under subsection (1), the Commission:\n\n(a) must have regard to:\n\n(i) the likely benefit to the public resulting from the\nassistance, or likely assistance, in response to or\nrecovery from the exceptional circumstances to which\nthe declaration relates; and\n\n(ii) the detriment to the public that would result, or be likely\nto result, from the conduct; and\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a declaration mentioned in subsection (2) is in force, the\nCommission may, in writing, determine that one or more specified\nprovisions of Division 1 or 2 of Part IV do not apply to a kind of\nconduct specified in the determination.\n\n(2) The declarations are the following:\n\n(a) a declaration under section 95AE;\n\n(b) a national emergency declaration (within the meaning of the\nNational Emergency Declaration Act 2020).\n\n(3) The Commission must not make a determination under\nsubsection (1) unless the Commission is satisfied that, in all the\ncircumstances, the conduct of that kind would assist, or would be\nlikely to assist, in the response to or recovery from the exceptional\ncircumstances or emergency to which the declaration relates.\n\n(4) In making a determination under subsection (1), the Commission:\n\n(a) must have regard to:\n\n(i) the likely benefit to the public resulting from the\nassistance, or likely assistance, in response to or\nrecovery from the exceptional circumstances to which\nthe declaration relates; and\n\n(ii) the detriment to the public that would result, or be likely\nto result, from the conduct; and\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95ac-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95ac-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95ac-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95ac-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d0a8c5612c703ab63a7cec10a4bfe8cbe17bbeab3b05b8c025bb467c55e96719"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95ac",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "95AC Exceptional circumstances class exemptions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 461,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a declaration mentioned in subsection (2) is in force, the\nCommission may, in writing, determine that one or more specified\nprovisions of Division 1 or 2 of Part IV do not apply to a kind of\nconduct specified in the determination.\n\n(2) The declarations are the following:\n\n(a) a declaration under section 95AE;\n\n(b) a national emergency declaration (within the meaning of the\nNational Emergency Declaration Act 2020).\n\n(3) The Commission must not make a determination under\nsubsection (1) unless the Commission is satisfied that, in all the\ncircumstances, the conduct of that kind would assist, or would be\nlikely to assist, in the response to or recovery from the exceptional\ncircumstances or emergency to which the declaration relates.\n\n(4) In making a determination under subsection (1), the Commission:\n\n(a) must have regard to:\n\n(i) the likely benefit to the public resulting from the\nassistance, or likely assistance, in response to or\nrecovery from the exceptional circumstances to which\nthe declaration relates; and\n\n(ii) the detriment to the public that would result, or be likely\nto result, from the conduct; and\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
