    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95ac-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "95AC(4) Exceptional circumstances class exemptions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 461,
      "values:originalText": "(4) In making a determination under subsection (1), the Commission:\n\n(a) must have regard to:\n\n(i) the likely benefit to the public resulting from the\nassistance, or likely assistance, in response to or\nrecovery from the exceptional circumstances to which\nthe declaration relates; and\n\n(ii) the detriment to the public that would result, or be likely\nto result, from the conduct; and\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95ac-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
