    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95ad-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "cease",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Ceases to be in force",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) The notice under subsection (1):...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the day after the\nday the Commission gives the person the written notice;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95ad-ss-4-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "cease",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Ceases to be in force at the earlier of two times.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) The notice under subsection (1):...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the time the determination under section 95AC ceases to\nbecome in force."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95ad-ss-4-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "until",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal interval required for LTL application",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(i) if the Commission revokes the notice—the day after the\nday the Commission gives the person the written notice;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the time the determination under section 95AC ceases to become in force."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95ad-ss-4-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "cease",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Ceases to be in force at the earlier of two times.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(ii) the time the determination under section 95AC ceases to become in force.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the day after the\nday the Commission gives the person the written notice;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95ae",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "95AE Minister may declare exceptional circumstances",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95ae"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.464",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make a declaration\nunder this section if the Minister is satisfied that:\n\n(a) either:\n\n(i) exceptional circumstances that are causing significant\nharm to the Australian economy or Australian\nconsumers exist; or\n\n(ii) exceptional circumstances that would cause significant\nharm to the Australian economy or Australian\nconsumers are likely to exist; and\n\n(b) it is in the public interest to empower the Commission to\nmake determinations under either or both of the following:\n\n(i) section 92D;\n\n(ii) section 95AC.\n\n(2) A declaration under subsection (1) is in force for the period:\n\n(a) starting on the day specified in the declaration (which may be\nbefore the commencement of this section, but must not be\nbefore 1 April 2026); and\n\n(b) ending at the earlier of:\n\n(i) the start of the day specified in the declaration; and\n\n(ii) if the declaration is revoked—the end of the day the\nrevocation takes effect.\n\n(3) A day specified for the purposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(i) must\nensure that the period the declaration is in force:\n\n(a) is no longer than the period that the Minister considers\nnecessary for the purposes of emergency management; and\n\n(b) is not longer than 6 months.\nNote 1:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nNote 2:\nThe period may be extended under section 95AF.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nDeclaration of exceptional circumstances  Division 4\n\nSection 95AF\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make a declaration\nunder this section if the Minister is satisfied that:\n\n(a) either:\n\n(i) exceptional circumstances that are causing significant\nharm to the Australian economy or Australian\nconsumers exist; or\n\n(ii) exceptional circumstances that would cause significant\nharm to the Australian economy or Australian\nconsumers are likely to exist; and\n\n(b) it is in the public interest to empower the Commission to\nmake determinations under either or both of the following:\n\n(i) section 92D;\n\n(ii) section 95AC.\n\n(2) A declaration under subsection (1) is in force for the period:\n\n(a) starting on the day specified in the declaration (which may be\nbefore the commencement of this section, but must not be\nbefore 1 April 2026); and\n\n(b) ending at the earlier of:\n\n(i) the start of the day specified in the declaration; and\n\n(ii) if the declaration is revoked—the end of the day the\nrevocation takes effect.\n\n(3) A day specified for the purposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(i) must\nensure that the period the declaration is in force:\n\n(a) is no longer than the period that the Minister considers\nnecessary for the purposes of emergency management; and\n\n(b) is not longer than 6 months.\nNote 1:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nNote 2:\nThe period may be extended under section 95AF.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nDeclaration of exceptional circumstances  Division 4\n\nSection 95AF\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95ae-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95ae-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95ae-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6125fa4316dadb7120b058b0f842bf3f8489436e03d940e0dd99c7f9864f8c4c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95ae",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "95AE Minister may declare exceptional circumstances",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 464,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make a declaration\nunder this section if the Minister is satisfied that:\n\n(a) either:\n\n(i) exceptional circumstances that are causing significant\nharm to the Australian economy or Australian\nconsumers exist; or\n\n(ii) exceptional circumstances that would cause significant\nharm to the Australian economy or Australian\nconsumers are likely to exist; and\n\n(b) it is in the public interest to empower the Commission to\nmake determinations under either or both of the following:\n\n(i) section 92D;\n\n(ii) section 95AC.\n\n(2) A declaration under subsection (1) is in force for the period:\n\n(a) starting on the day specified in the declaration (which may be\nbefore the commencement of this section, but must not be\nbefore 1 April 2026); and\n\n(b) ending at the earlier of:\n\n(i) the start of the day specified in the declaration; and\n\n(ii) if the declaration is revoked—the end of the day the\nrevocation takes effect.\n\n(3) A day specified for the purposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(i) must\nensure that the period the declaration is in force:\n\n(a) is no longer than the period that the Minister considers\nnecessary for the purposes of emergency management; and\n\n(b) is not longer than 6 months.\nNote 1:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nNote 2:\nThe period may be extended under section 95AF.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nDeclaration of exceptional circumstances  Division 4\n\nSection 95AF\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
