      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.464",
      "values:originalText": "(3) A day specified for the purposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(i) must\nensure that the period the declaration is in force:\n\n(a) is no longer than the period that the Minister considers\nnecessary for the purposes of emergency management; and\n\n(b) is not longer than 6 months.\nNote 1:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nNote 2:\nThe period may be extended under section 95AF.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nDeclaration of exceptional circumstances  Division 4\n\nSection 95AF\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(3) A day specified for the purposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(i) must\nensure that the period the declaration is in force:\n\n(a) is no longer than the period that the Minister considers\nnecessary for the purposes of emergency management; and\n\n(b) is not longer than 6 months.\nNote 1:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nNote 2:\nThe period may be extended under section 95AF.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nAuthorisations and notifications  Part VII\nDeclaration of exceptional circumstances  Division 4\n\nSection 95AF\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
