    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95af",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "95AF Extension of declaration of exceptional circumstances",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95af"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.465",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, extend the operation\nof a declaration under section 95AE if the Minister is satisfied that\nthe exceptional circumstances mentioned in\nsubparagraph 95AE(1)(a)(i) are likely to continue to exist beyond\nthe period in which the order will be in force.\n\n(2) The Minister may, under subsection (1), extend the operation of an\norder more than once. However, each period of extension must not\nexceed 3 months.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, extend the operation\nof a declaration under section 95AE if the Minister is satisfied that\nthe exceptional circumstances mentioned in\nsubparagraph 95AE(1)(a)(i) are likely to continue to exist beyond\nthe period in which the order will be in force.\n\n(2) The Minister may, under subsection (1), extend the operation of an\norder more than once. However, each period of extension must not\nexceed 3 months.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95af-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95af-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5b7f0ea15e7183ea75eda77d8d20330858dfe529d00ae4bffce1cd6b20d20144"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95af",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "95AF Extension of declaration of exceptional circumstances",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 465,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, extend the operation\nof a declaration under section 95AE if the Minister is satisfied that\nthe exceptional circumstances mentioned in\nsubparagraph 95AE(1)(a)(i) are likely to continue to exist beyond\nthe period in which the order will be in force.\n\n(2) The Minister may, under subsection (1), extend the operation of an\norder more than once. However, each period of extension must not\nexceed 3 months.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95af-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "95AF(1) Extension of declaration of exceptional circumstances",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95af-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
