    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "95G Commission’s functions under this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.473",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission’s functions under this Part are set out in this\nsection.\nPrice inquiries\n\n(2) The Commission is to hold such inquiries as it is required to hold\nunder section 95H.\n\n(3) The Commission may, with the Minister’s approval under\nsection 95H, hold such other inquiries as it thinks fit.\n\n(4) The Commission is to give the Minister a report on the results of\neach inquiry it holds.\nPrice notifications\n\n(5) The Commission is to consider locality notices and to take, in\nrelation to such notices, such action in accordance with this Part as\nit considers appropriate.\nPrice monitoring\n\n(6) The Commission is to monitor prices, costs and profits in any\nindustry or business that the Minister directs it to monitor and is to\ngive the Minister a report on the results of such monitoring.\nGeneral\n\n(7) In exercising its powers and performing its functions under this\nPart, the Commission must, subject to any directions given under\nsection 95ZH, have particular regard to the following:\n\n(a) the need to maintain investment and employment, including\nthe influence of profitability on investment and employment;\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commission’s functions under this Part are set out in this\nsection.\nPrice inquiries\n\n(2) The Commission is to hold such inquiries as it is required to hold\nunder section 95H.\n\n(3) The Commission may, with the Minister’s approval under\nsection 95H, hold such other inquiries as it thinks fit.\n\n(4) The Commission is to give the Minister a report on the results of\neach inquiry it holds.\nPrice notifications\n\n(5) The Commission is to consider locality notices and to take, in\nrelation to such notices, such action in accordance with this Part as\nit considers appropriate.\nPrice monitoring\n\n(6) The Commission is to monitor prices, costs and profits in any\nindustry or business that the Minister directs it to monitor and is to\ngive the Minister a report on the results of such monitoring.\nGeneral\n\n(7) In exercising its powers and performing its functions under this\nPart, the Commission must, subject to any directions given under\nsection 95ZH, have particular regard to the following:\n\n(a) the need to maintain investment and employment, including\nthe influence of profitability on investment and employment;\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95g-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95g-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95g-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95g-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95g-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95g-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95g-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0af121f99a24fdd61499ec435b2a247e1e71830cf4d0bdc628e64bfc337827e1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "95G Commission’s functions under this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 473,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission’s functions under this Part are set out in this\nsection.\nPrice inquiries\n\n(2) The Commission is to hold such inquiries as it is required to hold\nunder section 95H.\n\n(3) The Commission may, with the Minister’s approval under\nsection 95H, hold such other inquiries as it thinks fit.\n\n(4) The Commission is to give the Minister a report on the results of\neach inquiry it holds.\nPrice notifications\n\n(5) The Commission is to consider locality notices and to take, in\nrelation to such notices, such action in accordance with this Part as\nit considers appropriate.\nPrice monitoring\n\n(6) The Commission is to monitor prices, costs and profits in any\nindustry or business that the Minister directs it to monitor and is to\ngive the Minister a report on the results of such monitoring.\nGeneral\n\n(7) In exercising its powers and performing its functions under this\nPart, the Commission must, subject to any directions given under\nsection 95ZH, have particular regard to the following:\n\n(a) the need to maintain investment and employment, including\nthe influence of profitability on investment and employment;\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
