    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95q-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "95Q(4) Notification of proposed prices after receipt of report",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95q-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.482",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Commission must, within 14 days after it receives the notice\nunder subsection (2), make publicly available details of the price or\nprices specified in the notice.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nPrices surveillance  Part VIIA\nPrice inquiries  Division 3\n\nSection 95R\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSubdivision C—Procedure at inquiries",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The Commission must, within 14 days after it receives the notice\nunder subsection (2), make publicly available details of the price or\nprices specified in the notice.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nPrices surveillance  Part VIIA\nPrice inquiries  Division 3\n\nSection 95R\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSubdivision C—Procedure at inquiries",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95q"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95q-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95q-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6a1ac0e3917a66edfffd989a6538fe04fa94ca83e202baae47cd0ddb0f847e08",
      "skos:note": "Publicly available details of price or prices specified in the notice must be made available within 14 days.",
      "dc:description": "Details of price or prices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95q-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "95Q(4) Notification of proposed prices after receipt of report",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 482,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Commission must, within 14 days after it receives the notice\nunder subsection (2), make publicly available details of the price or\nprices specified in the notice.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nPrices surveillance  Part VIIA\nPrice inquiries  Division 3\n\nSection 95R\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSubdivision C—Procedure at inquiries"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95q-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95q-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95q-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide details within 14 days",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:conclusionText": "Details of price or prices must be made available"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95r",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "95R Public inquiries etc.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95r"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.483",
      "values:originalText": "Public inquiries\n\n(1) An inquiry body must hold an inquiry in public, unless the Minister\ndirects otherwise.\nTaking of evidence\n\n(2) The inquiry body may take evidence in private at an inquiry held in\npublic if:\n\n(a) a witness objects to giving, in public, evidence that the\ninquiry body is satisfied is of a confidential nature; and\n\n(b) the inquiry body considers that it is desirable to do so.\n\n(3) The inquiry body may permit a person appearing as a witness at the\ninquiry to give evidence by giving, and verifying by oath or\naffirmation, a written statement.\n\n(4) If a statement is so given in an inquiry held in public, the inquiry\nbody must make available to the public in such manner as it thinks\nfit the contents of the statement other than any matter:\n\n(a) that the person who gave the evidence objects to being made\npublic; and\n\n(b) the evidence of which the body is satisfied would have been\ntaken in private if that evidence had been given orally and the\nperson had objected to giving it in public.\nWritten submissions\n\n(5) The inquiry body may require or permit a person desiring to make\na submission to the body to make the submission in writing.\n\n(6) If a submission is so made in an inquiry held in public, the inquiry\nbody must make available to the public in such manner as it thinks\nfit the contents of the submission.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "Public inquiries\n\n(1) An inquiry body must hold an inquiry in public, unless the Minister\ndirects otherwise.\nTaking of evidence\n\n(2) The inquiry body may take evidence in private at an inquiry held in\npublic if:\n\n(a) a witness objects to giving, in public, evidence that the\ninquiry body is satisfied is of a confidential nature; and\n\n(b) the inquiry body considers that it is desirable to do so.\n\n(3) The inquiry body may permit a person appearing as a witness at the\ninquiry to give evidence by giving, and verifying by oath or\naffirmation, a written statement.\n\n(4) If a statement is so given in an inquiry held in public, the inquiry\nbody must make available to the public in such manner as it thinks\nfit the contents of the statement other than any matter:\n\n(a) that the person who gave the evidence objects to being made\npublic; and\n\n(b) the evidence of which the body is satisfied would have been\ntaken in private if that evidence had been given orally and the\nperson had objected to giving it in public.\nWritten submissions\n\n(5) The inquiry body may require or permit a person desiring to make\na submission to the body to make the submission in writing.\n\n(6) If a submission is so made in an inquiry held in public, the inquiry\nbody must make available to the public in such manner as it thinks\nfit the contents of the submission.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95r-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95r-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95r-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95r-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95r-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95r-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "334f0e078305c2cfb67f22608635a364176b9b8ff42f86c7f4d7613670465332"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95r",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "95R Public inquiries etc.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 483,
      "values:originalText": "Public inquiries\n\n(1) An inquiry body must hold an inquiry in public, unless the Minister\ndirects otherwise.\nTaking of evidence\n\n(2) The inquiry body may take evidence in private at an inquiry held in\npublic if:\n\n(a) a witness objects to giving, in public, evidence that the\ninquiry body is satisfied is of a confidential nature; and\n\n(b) the inquiry body considers that it is desirable to do so.\n\n(3) The inquiry body may permit a person appearing as a witness at the\ninquiry to give evidence by giving, and verifying by oath or\naffirmation, a written statement.\n\n(4) If a statement is so given in an inquiry held in public, the inquiry\nbody must make available to the public in such manner as it thinks\nfit the contents of the statement other than any matter:\n\n(a) that the person who gave the evidence objects to being made\npublic; and\n\n(b) the evidence of which the body is satisfied would have been\ntaken in private if that evidence had been given orally and the\nperson had objected to giving it in public.\nWritten submissions\n\n(5) The inquiry body may require or permit a person desiring to make\na submission to the body to make the submission in writing.\n\n(6) If a submission is so made in an inquiry held in public, the inquiry\nbody must make available to the public in such manner as it thinks\nfit the contents of the submission.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
