      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.483",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The inquiry body may take evidence in private at an inquiry held in\npublic if:\n\n(a) a witness objects to giving, in public, evidence that the\ninquiry body is satisfied is of a confidential nature; and\n\n(b) the inquiry body considers that it is desirable to do so.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The inquiry body may take evidence in private at an inquiry held in\npublic if:\n\n(a) a witness objects to giving, in public, evidence that the\ninquiry body is satisfied is of a confidential nature; and\n\n(b) the inquiry body considers that it is desirable to do so.",
