    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95s-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "95S(4) Taking of evidence on oath or affirmation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95s-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.484",
      "values:originalText": "(4) In an inquiry by the Commission, the power conferred on the\ninquiry Chair by subsection (3) may, at his or her discretion, be\nexercised on the application of another person.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nPrices surveillance  Part VIIA\nPrice inquiries  Division 3\n\nSection 95T\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(4) In an inquiry by the Commission, the power conferred on the\ninquiry Chair by subsection (3) may, at his or her discretion, be\nexercised on the application of another person.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nPrices surveillance  Part VIIA\nPrice inquiries  Division 3\n\nSection 95T\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95s"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95s-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95s-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4b495c9e31bb06b5bd08930530f527c440a5c1619db5680105f180a559d1307b",
      "skos:note": "Commission may exercise power on application of another person."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95s-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "95S(4) Taking of evidence on oath or affirmation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 484,
      "values:originalText": "(4) In an inquiry by the Commission, the power conferred on the\ninquiry Chair by subsection (3) may, at his or her discretion, be\nexercised on the application of another person.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nPrices surveillance  Part VIIA\nPrice inquiries  Division 3\n\nSection 95T\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95s-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95s-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95s-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "May",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permission to exercise power",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95t",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "95T Failure of witness to attend",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95t"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.485",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is given a summons to appear as a witness at an\ninquiry; and\n\n(b) the person fails to attend as required by the summons or fails\nto appear and report himself or herself from day to day; and\n\n(c) the person has not been excused, or released from further\nattendance, by:\n\n(i) in an inquiry by the Commission—a member of the\nCommission; or\n\n(ii) in an external inquiry—the person presiding at the\ninquiry.\nPenalty: 10 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is given a summons to appear as a witness at an\ninquiry; and\n\n(b) the person fails to attend as required by the summons or fails\nto appear and report himself or herself from day to day; and\n\n(c) the person has not been excused, or released from further\nattendance, by:\n\n(i) in an inquiry by the Commission—a member of the\nCommission; or\n\n(ii) in an external inquiry—the person presiding at the\ninquiry.\nPenalty: 10 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95t-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-95t-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "03f0b3fbc24791c41fd169c0af99c3259e688422263e1b9103157cddac5ffcb1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-95t",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "95T Failure of witness to attend",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 485,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is given a summons to appear as a witness at an\ninquiry; and\n\n(b) the person fails to attend as required by the summons or fails\nto appear and report himself or herself from day to day; and\n\n(c) the person has not been excused, or released from further\nattendance, by:\n\n(i) in an inquiry by the Commission—a member of the\nCommission; or\n\n(ii) in an external inquiry—the person presiding at the\ninquiry.\nPenalty: 10 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code)."
    },
