    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "100A Applications for review",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-100a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.519",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if a provision of this Act provides that a person\nmay apply under this Division for review of a decision of the\nCommission.\n\n(2) The person may:\n\n(a) as determined under subsection (3); and\n\n(b) within the time allowed by or under subsection (3);\napply to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine\nrequirements for making applications for review under\nsubsection (2), including requirements relating to the time by\nwhich such reviews are allowed to be made.\n\n(4) The Tribunal must review the decision.\n\n(5) For the purposes of the review, this Act applies in relation to the\nTribunal in like manner as it applies in relation to the Commission.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if a provision of this Act provides that a person\nmay apply under this Division for review of a decision of the\nCommission.\n\n(2) The person may:\n\n(a) as determined under subsection (3); and\n\n(b) within the time allowed by or under subsection (3);\napply to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine\nrequirements for making applications for review under\nsubsection (2), including requirements relating to the time by\nwhich such reviews are allowed to be made.\n\n(4) The Tribunal must review the decision.\n\n(5) For the purposes of the review, this Act applies in relation to the\nTribunal in like manner as it applies in relation to the Commission.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100a-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100a-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "71f93ae485b6368a7e9f675cc104fbe72516f25b7838b493ba47a6e54d044c7d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-100a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "100A Applications for review",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 519,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if a provision of this Act provides that a person\nmay apply under this Division for review of a decision of the\nCommission.\n\n(2) The person may:\n\n(a) as determined under subsection (3); and\n\n(b) within the time allowed by or under subsection (3);\napply to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine\nrequirements for making applications for review under\nsubsection (2), including requirements relating to the time by\nwhich such reviews are allowed to be made.\n\n(4) The Tribunal must review the decision.\n\n(5) For the purposes of the review, this Act applies in relation to the\nTribunal in like manner as it applies in relation to the Commission."
    },
