    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "100B Functions and powers of Tribunal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-100b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.519",
      "values:originalText": "(1) On a review under section 100A, the Tribunal:\n\n(a) may make a decision affirming, setting aside or varying the\ndecision of the Commission; and\n\n(b) for the purposes of the review, may perform all the functions\nand exercise all the powers of the Commission.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) On a review under section 100A, the Tribunal:\n\n(a) may make a decision affirming, setting aside or varying the\ndecision of the Commission; and\n\n(b) for the purposes of the review, may perform all the functions\nand exercise all the powers of the Commission.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100b-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7d0ef85d46d3fd2ea9e53e3cbeda53f27bcd6da0507e3a09dd4688afd3c958df",
      "skos:note": "Tribunal may make decisions and exercise Commission's powers during review"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-100b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "100B Functions and powers of Tribunal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 519,
      "values:originalText": "(1) On a review under section 100A, the Tribunal:\n\n(a) may make a decision affirming, setting aside or varying the\ndecision of the Commission; and\n\n(b) for the purposes of the review, may perform all the functions\nand exercise all the powers of the Commission.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100b-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100b"
      },
