      "cml:logicSummary": "Tribunal has the power to make decisions",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "100C Applications for review",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-100c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.521",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person dissatisfied with an acquisition determination in respect\nof a notification of an acquisition may:\n\n(a) as determined under subsection (2); and\n\n(b) before the end of 14 days after the statement of the\nCommission’s reasons for making the determination is\nincluded on the acquisitions register;\napply to the Tribunal for a review of the determination if the\nperson is:\n\n(c) the notifying party of the notification; or\n\n(d) is allowed to apply under subsection (3).\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine\nrequirements for making an application for the purposes of\nparagraph (1)(a).\n\n(3) The Tribunal may, by written notice given to a person, allow the\nperson to apply to the Tribunal for review of the determination.\n\n(4) In considering whether to allow a person to apply to the Tribunal\nunder subsection (3), the Tribunal must have regard to:\n\n(a) the person’s interest in the matter; and\n\n(b) the efficient administration of the acquisitions provisions;\nand\n\n(c) whether the application has any reasonable prospects of\nsuccess; and\n\n(d) any other matter that the Tribunal considers relevant.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person dissatisfied with an acquisition determination in respect\nof a notification of an acquisition may:\n\n(a) as determined under subsection (2); and\n\n(b) before the end of 14 days after the statement of the\nCommission’s reasons for making the determination is\nincluded on the acquisitions register;\napply to the Tribunal for a review of the determination if the\nperson is:\n\n(c) the notifying party of the notification; or\n\n(d) is allowed to apply under subsection (3).\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine\nrequirements for making an application for the purposes of\nparagraph (1)(a).\n\n(3) The Tribunal may, by written notice given to a person, allow the\nperson to apply to the Tribunal for review of the determination.\n\n(4) In considering whether to allow a person to apply to the Tribunal\nunder subsection (3), the Tribunal must have regard to:\n\n(a) the person’s interest in the matter; and\n\n(b) the efficient administration of the acquisitions provisions;\nand\n\n(c) whether the application has any reasonable prospects of\nsuccess; and\n\n(d) any other matter that the Tribunal considers relevant.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100c-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100c-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100c-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d5ae95afd7907ddb315ffa8f3887de30d56bf2217f76aa04dcf2f408d3d86334"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-100c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "100C Applications for review",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 521,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person dissatisfied with an acquisition determination in respect\nof a notification of an acquisition may:\n\n(a) as determined under subsection (2); and\n\n(b) before the end of 14 days after the statement of the\nCommission’s reasons for making the determination is\nincluded on the acquisitions register;\napply to the Tribunal for a review of the determination if the\nperson is:\n\n(c) the notifying party of the notification; or\n\n(d) is allowed to apply under subsection (3).\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine\nrequirements for making an application for the purposes of\nparagraph (1)(a).\n\n(3) The Tribunal may, by written notice given to a person, allow the\nperson to apply to the Tribunal for review of the determination.\n\n(4) In considering whether to allow a person to apply to the Tribunal\nunder subsection (3), the Tribunal must have regard to:\n\n(a) the person’s interest in the matter; and\n\n(b) the efficient administration of the acquisitions provisions;\nand\n\n(c) whether the application has any reasonable prospects of\nsuccess; and\n\n(d) any other matter that the Tribunal considers relevant.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
