    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "100E Applicants may withdraw applications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-100e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.522",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The applicant may, at any time, by giving written notice to the\nTribunal, withdraw an application for review made to the Tribunal\nunder subsection 100C(1).\n\n(2) If the application is withdrawn, a participant in the proceedings for\nreview (other than the applicant) may apply to the Tribunal for\nreinstatement of the application within 7 days after the person\nreceives notice that the application is withdrawn (or such longer\nperiod as the Tribunal, in special circumstances, allows).\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) a participant applies under subsection (2); and\n\n(b) the Tribunal believes it to be appropriate to reinstate the\napplication for review;\nthe Tribunal may reinstate the application and make such orders as\nappear to the Tribunal to be appropriate in the circumstances.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nReview by Tribunal of decisions of Commission  Part IX\nApplications for review of acquisition determinations  Division 1B\n\nSection 100F\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The applicant may, at any time, by giving written notice to the\nTribunal, withdraw an application for review made to the Tribunal\nunder subsection 100C(1).\n\n(2) If the application is withdrawn, a participant in the proceedings for\nreview (other than the applicant) may apply to the Tribunal for\nreinstatement of the application within 7 days after the person\nreceives notice that the application is withdrawn (or such longer\nperiod as the Tribunal, in special circumstances, allows).\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) a participant applies under subsection (2); and\n\n(b) the Tribunal believes it to be appropriate to reinstate the\napplication for review;\nthe Tribunal may reinstate the application and make such orders as\nappear to the Tribunal to be appropriate in the circumstances.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nReview by Tribunal of decisions of Commission  Part IX\nApplications for review of acquisition determinations  Division 1B\n\nSection 100F\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100e-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100e-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e42b245cc561601a0bfb1b1f6bcfdbe498a05e23d5c5a10f920d2ea78cc3ff4e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-100e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "100E Applicants may withdraw applications",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 522,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The applicant may, at any time, by giving written notice to the\nTribunal, withdraw an application for review made to the Tribunal\nunder subsection 100C(1).\n\n(2) If the application is withdrawn, a participant in the proceedings for\nreview (other than the applicant) may apply to the Tribunal for\nreinstatement of the application within 7 days after the person\nreceives notice that the application is withdrawn (or such longer\nperiod as the Tribunal, in special circumstances, allows).\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) a participant applies under subsection (2); and\n\n(b) the Tribunal believes it to be appropriate to reinstate the\napplication for review;\nthe Tribunal may reinstate the application and make such orders as\nappear to the Tribunal to be appropriate in the circumstances.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nReview by Tribunal of decisions of Commission  Part IX\nApplications for review of acquisition determinations  Division 1B\n\nSection 100F\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
