    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "100H Tribunal may dismiss applications if applicants fail to comply",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-100h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.523",
      "values:originalText": "with order etc.\n\nThe Tribunal may dismiss an application for review made to the\nTribunal under subsection 100C(1) if the applicant fails to comply\nwith:\n\n(a) this Act; or\n\n(b) an order of the Tribunal in relation to the proceedings for\nreview.\n100J  Tribunal may dismiss application if frivolous, vexatious etc.\n\nThe Tribunal may, at any time, dismiss an application made to the\nTribunal under subsection 100C(1) if the Tribunal is satisfied that\nthe application:\n\n(a) is frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance;\nor\n\n(b) has no reasonable prospects of success; or\n\n(c) is otherwise an abuse of the process of the Tribunal.\nNote:\nSee also section 111 (costs).\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "with order etc.\n\nThe Tribunal may dismiss an application for review made to the\nTribunal under subsection 100C(1) if the applicant fails to comply\nwith:\n\n(a) this Act; or\n\n(b) an order of the Tribunal in relation to the proceedings for\nreview.\n100J  Tribunal may dismiss application if frivolous, vexatious etc.\n\nThe Tribunal may, at any time, dismiss an application made to the\nTribunal under subsection 100C(1) if the Tribunal is satisfied that\nthe application:\n\n(a) is frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance;\nor\n\n(b) has no reasonable prospects of success; or\n\n(c) is otherwise an abuse of the process of the Tribunal.\nNote:\nSee also section 111 (costs).\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100h-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100h-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "028bfab068a8186312b6c3af9e2bfb831b0dfecd3d0b9e82abf3670f6088c854",
      "skos:note": "Failure to comply with order or Act results in dismissal of application."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-100h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "100H Tribunal may dismiss applications if applicants fail to comply",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 523,
      "values:originalText": "with order etc.\n\nThe Tribunal may dismiss an application for review made to the\nTribunal under subsection 100C(1) if the applicant fails to comply\nwith:\n\n(a) this Act; or\n\n(b) an order of the Tribunal in relation to the proceedings for\nreview.\n100J  Tribunal may dismiss application if frivolous, vexatious etc.\n\nThe Tribunal may, at any time, dismiss an application made to the\nTribunal under subsection 100C(1) if the Tribunal is satisfied that\nthe application:\n\n(a) is frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance;\nor\n\n(b) has no reasonable prospects of success; or\n\n(c) is otherwise an abuse of the process of the Tribunal.\nNote:\nSee also section 111 (costs).\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100h-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
