      "cml:conclusionText": "Dismissal of application."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100k",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "100K Certain participants may seek to withdraw from being",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-100k"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.524",
      "values:originalText": "participants\nGeneral rule\n\n(1) The Tribunal may order that a participant in a proceeding before\nthe Tribunal under this Division ceases to be a participant in the\nproceeding if the participant gives written notice to the Tribunal\nthat the participant wishes to cease being a participant in the\nproceeding.\nException\n\n(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to the applicant.\nNote:\nThe applicant may withdraw the application (see section 100E).",
      "skos:definition": "participants\nGeneral rule\n\n(1) The Tribunal may order that a participant in a proceeding before\nthe Tribunal under this Division ceases to be a participant in the\nproceeding if the participant gives written notice to the Tribunal\nthat the participant wishes to cease being a participant in the\nproceeding.\nException\n\n(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to the applicant.\nNote:\nThe applicant may withdraw the application (see section 100E).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100k-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100k-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dce47ffdd711eb18fac5e8d2364062e26d844de7b21e6227c901433276ef8a7c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-100k",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "100K Certain participants may seek to withdraw from being",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 524,
      "values:originalText": "participants\nGeneral rule\n\n(1) The Tribunal may order that a participant in a proceeding before\nthe Tribunal under this Division ceases to be a participant in the\nproceeding if the participant gives written notice to the Tribunal\nthat the participant wishes to cease being a participant in the\nproceeding.\nException\n\n(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to the applicant.\nNote:\nThe applicant may withdraw the application (see section 100E)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100k-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "100K(1) Certain participants may seek to withdraw from being",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-100k-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
