    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100m-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prevents review of acquisition determination",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Public benefit application made",
      "cml:conclusionText": "No review allowed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100n",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "100N Functions and powers of Tribunal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-100n"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.526",
      "values:originalText": "(1) On a review of an acquisition determination under this Division,\nthe Tribunal:\n\n(a) may make a determination affirming, setting aside or varying\nthe determination; and\n\n(b) for the purposes of the review, may perform all the functions\nand exercise all the powers of the Commission.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (3) of this section:\n\n(a) paragraph 51ABZE(2)(c); or\n\n(b) subsection 51ABZF(2); or\n\n(c) subsection 51ABZW(2);\n(whichever is relevant) applies in relation to the Tribunal in the\nsame way as it applies in relation to the Commission.\n\n(3) The Tribunal may, if the Tribunal determines it to be appropriate,\nmake an acquisition determination by consent of:\n\n(a) the applicant for the review; and\n\n(b) if the applicant for the review is not the notifying party of the\nnotification of the acquisition—the notifying party; and\n\n(c) all persons (if any) who have been permitted under\nsubsection 109(2) to intervene in the proceedings for review;\neven if the Tribunal does not have the satisfaction referred to in\nparagraph 51ABZE(2)(c) or subsection 51ABZF(2) or\n51ABZW(2) (whichever is relevant).\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nReview by Tribunal of decisions of Commission  Part IX\nApplications for review of acquisition determinations  Division 1B\n\nSection 100P\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(4) For the purposes of this Act other than this Part, a determination of\nthe Tribunal affirming, setting aside or varying an acquisition\ndetermination is taken to be a determination of the Commission.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) On a review of an acquisition determination under this Division,\nthe Tribunal:\n\n(a) may make a determination affirming, setting aside or varying\nthe determination; and\n\n(b) for the purposes of the review, may perform all the functions\nand exercise all the powers of the Commission.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (3) of this section:\n\n(a) paragraph 51ABZE(2)(c); or\n\n(b) subsection 51ABZF(2); or\n\n(c) subsection 51ABZW(2);\n(whichever is relevant) applies in relation to the Tribunal in the\nsame way as it applies in relation to the Commission.\n\n(3) The Tribunal may, if the Tribunal determines it to be appropriate,\nmake an acquisition determination by consent of:\n\n(a) the applicant for the review; and\n\n(b) if the applicant for the review is not the notifying party of the\nnotification of the acquisition—the notifying party; and\n\n(c) all persons (if any) who have been permitted under\nsubsection 109(2) to intervene in the proceedings for review;\neven if the Tribunal does not have the satisfaction referred to in\nparagraph 51ABZE(2)(c) or subsection 51ABZF(2) or\n51ABZW(2) (whichever is relevant).\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nReview by Tribunal of decisions of Commission  Part IX\nApplications for review of acquisition determinations  Division 1B\n\nSection 100P\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(4) For the purposes of this Act other than this Part, a determination of\nthe Tribunal affirming, setting aside or varying an acquisition\ndetermination is taken to be a determination of the Commission.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100n-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100n-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100n-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100n-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1d3e503cbd25ef61aa6f024dd3c3fd56446510b6e043a606f6c92a692bf9a7de"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-100n",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "100N Functions and powers of Tribunal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 526,
      "values:originalText": "(1) On a review of an acquisition determination under this Division,\nthe Tribunal:\n\n(a) may make a determination affirming, setting aside or varying\nthe determination; and\n\n(b) for the purposes of the review, may perform all the functions\nand exercise all the powers of the Commission.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (3) of this section:\n\n(a) paragraph 51ABZE(2)(c); or\n\n(b) subsection 51ABZF(2); or\n\n(c) subsection 51ABZW(2);\n(whichever is relevant) applies in relation to the Tribunal in the\nsame way as it applies in relation to the Commission.\n\n(3) The Tribunal may, if the Tribunal determines it to be appropriate,\nmake an acquisition determination by consent of:\n\n(a) the applicant for the review; and\n\n(b) if the applicant for the review is not the notifying party of the\nnotification of the acquisition—the notifying party; and\n\n(c) all persons (if any) who have been permitted under\nsubsection 109(2) to intervene in the proceedings for review;\neven if the Tribunal does not have the satisfaction referred to in\nparagraph 51ABZE(2)(c) or subsection 51ABZF(2) or\n51ABZW(2) (whichever is relevant).\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nReview by Tribunal of decisions of Commission  Part IX\nApplications for review of acquisition determinations  Division 1B\n\nSection 100P\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(4) For the purposes of this Act other than this Part, a determination of\nthe Tribunal affirming, setting aside or varying an acquisition\ndetermination is taken to be a determination of the Commission."
    },
