    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100s",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "100S Information gathering etc.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-100s"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.529",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of a review under this Division, the Tribunal:\n\n(a) may consult, in such a manner as it sees fit, any consumer\nassociations or consumer interest groups; and\n\n(b) may have regard to any information furnished, documents\nproduced or evidence given to the Tribunal in connection\nwith such consultation.\n\n(2) For the purposes of a review under this Division in relation to an\nacquisition determination in respect of a notification of an\nacquisition, the Tribunal may allow a person to provide new\ninformation, documents or evidence if:\n\n(a) the Tribunal is satisfied that the information, document or\nevidence was not in existence at the time the Commission\nmade the determination; or\n\n(b) the person is the notifying party of the notification, and the\nTribunal is satisfied that:\n\n(i) the information, documents or evidence are relevant to\nthe grounds on which the Commission made the\ndetermination; and\n\n(ii) the person was not given a reasonable opportunity to\nmake submissions to the Commission in relation to\nthose grounds, or the evidence or other material on\nwhich those grounds were based, before the\nCommission made the determination (including because\nthe person was not informed of the grounds, evidence or\nother material).\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of a review under this Division, the Tribunal:\n\n(a) may consult, in such a manner as it sees fit, any consumer\nassociations or consumer interest groups; and\n\n(b) may have regard to any information furnished, documents\nproduced or evidence given to the Tribunal in connection\nwith such consultation.\n\n(2) For the purposes of a review under this Division in relation to an\nacquisition determination in respect of a notification of an\nacquisition, the Tribunal may allow a person to provide new\ninformation, documents or evidence if:\n\n(a) the Tribunal is satisfied that the information, document or\nevidence was not in existence at the time the Commission\nmade the determination; or\n\n(b) the person is the notifying party of the notification, and the\nTribunal is satisfied that:\n\n(i) the information, documents or evidence are relevant to\nthe grounds on which the Commission made the\ndetermination; and\n\n(ii) the person was not given a reasonable opportunity to\nmake submissions to the Commission in relation to\nthose grounds, or the evidence or other material on\nwhich those grounds were based, before the\nCommission made the determination (including because\nthe person was not informed of the grounds, evidence or\nother material).\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100s-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-100s-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d1f9b3dd803a674cfe1910366ccdb8a8bed3d695945c743dc2c340e4e55d4577"
    },
