    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-102",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "102 Functions and powers of Tribunal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-102"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.533",
      "values:originalText": "(1) On a review of a determination of the Commission under\nDivision 1 of Part VII in relation to:\n\n(a) an application for an authorisation; or\n\n(b) an application for a minor variation of an authorisation; or\n\n(c) an application for, or the Commission’s proposal for, the\nrevocation of an authorisation; or\n\n(d) an application for, or the Commission’s proposal for, the\nrevocation of an authorisation and the substitution of another\nauthorisation;\nthe Tribunal may make a determination affirming, setting aside or\nvarying the determination of the Commission and, for the purposes\nof the review, may perform all the functions and exercise all the\npowers of the Commission.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) On a review of a determination of the Commission under\nDivision 1 of Part VII in relation to:\n\n(a) an application for an authorisation; or\n\n(b) an application for a minor variation of an authorisation; or\n\n(c) an application for, or the Commission’s proposal for, the\nrevocation of an authorisation; or\n\n(d) an application for, or the Commission’s proposal for, the\nrevocation of an authorisation and the substitution of another\nauthorisation;\nthe Tribunal may make a determination affirming, setting aside or\nvarying the determination of the Commission and, for the purposes\nof the review, may perform all the functions and exercise all the\npowers of the Commission.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-102-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-102-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "33e16614687920818dd3e0d52c5c4761ddddb02cde2926a2ef941fdb802e37a6",
      "skos:note": "Tribunal may perform all functions and exercise all powers of Commission during review."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-102",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "102 Functions and powers of Tribunal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 533,
      "values:originalText": "(1) On a review of a determination of the Commission under\nDivision 1 of Part VII in relation to:\n\n(a) an application for an authorisation; or\n\n(b) an application for a minor variation of an authorisation; or\n\n(c) an application for, or the Commission’s proposal for, the\nrevocation of an authorisation; or\n\n(d) an application for, or the Commission’s proposal for, the\nrevocation of an authorisation and the substitution of another\nauthorisation;\nthe Tribunal may make a determination affirming, setting aside or\nvarying the determination of the Commission and, for the purposes\nof the review, may perform all the functions and exercise all the\npowers of the Commission.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-102-norm",
