      "skos:note": "Exercise powers regardless of Tribunal constitution"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-103-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "103(3) Procedure generally",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 543,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The powers mentioned in subsection (2) may be exercised by a\npresidential member:\n\n(a) whether or not the Tribunal has been constituted under\nsection 37 in relation to the proceedings; and\n\n(b) once the Tribunal is so constituted—whether or not that\nmember is part of the Division of the Tribunal so constituted.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
