    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-110",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "110 Representation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-110"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.546",
      "values:originalText": "In proceedings before the Tribunal:\n\n(a) a natural person may appear in person;\n\n(aa) a person other than a body corporate may be represented by\nan employee of the person approved by the Tribunal;\n\n(b) a body corporate may be represented by an employee, or a\ndirector or other officer, of the body corporate approved by\nthe Tribunal;\n\n(c) an unincorporated association of persons or a member of an\nunincorporated association of persons may be represented by\na member or officer of the association approved by the\nTribunal; and\n\n(d) any person may be represented by a barrister or a solicitor of\nthe Supreme Court of a State or Territory or of the High\nCourt.",
      "skos:definition": "In proceedings before the Tribunal:\n\n(a) a natural person may appear in person;\n\n(aa) a person other than a body corporate may be represented by\nan employee of the person approved by the Tribunal;\n\n(b) a body corporate may be represented by an employee, or a\ndirector or other officer, of the body corporate approved by\nthe Tribunal;\n\n(c) an unincorporated association of persons or a member of an\nunincorporated association of persons may be represented by\na member or officer of the association approved by the\nTribunal; and\n\n(d) any person may be represented by a barrister or a solicitor of\nthe Supreme Court of a State or Territory or of the High\nCourt.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-110-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-110-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-110-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-110-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-110-logic-alleninterval-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0294dd5dd44c42aa67f3051d1e4f54f51bcfabde175d6ea240db62cf9ae7b6f2",
      "skos:note": "Representation in proceedings before the Tribunal"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-110",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "110 Representation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 546,
      "values:originalText": "In proceedings before the Tribunal:\n\n(a) a natural person may appear in person;\n\n(aa) a person other than a body corporate may be represented by\nan employee of the person approved by the Tribunal;\n\n(b) a body corporate may be represented by an employee, or a\ndirector or other officer, of the body corporate approved by\nthe Tribunal;\n\n(c) an unincorporated association of persons or a member of an\nunincorporated association of persons may be represented by\na member or officer of the association approved by the\nTribunal; and\n\n(d) any person may be represented by a barrister or a solicitor of\nthe Supreme Court of a State or Territory or of the High\nCourt."
    },
    {
