      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MAY BE REPRESENTED BY",
      "cml:logicSummary": "May be represented by an employee or a director",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Body corporate may be represented by an employee or a director"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-110-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must be approved by the Tribunal",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Employee, director, or officer must be approved by the Tribunal"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-110-logic-alleninterval-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "BETWEEN",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal interval for representation approval",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Tribunal approves representation at some point in time"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-111",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "111 Tribunal may order costs be awarded",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-111"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.546",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Tribunal is satisfied that it is appropriate to do so, the\nTribunal may order that a participant in proceedings for review\nunder Division 1A or 1B pay all or a specified part of the costs of\nanother participant in the proceedings.\n\n(2) If the Tribunal makes an order under subsection (1), it may make\nfurther orders that it believes appropriate in relation to the\nassessment or taxation of the costs.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nReview by Tribunal of decisions of Commission  Part IX\nProcedure and Evidence  Division 2\n\nSection 112\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make provision for\nand in relation to fees payable for the assessment or taxation of\ncosts ordered by the Tribunal to be paid.\n\n(4) If a participant (the first participant) is ordered to pay some or all\nof the costs of another participant under subsection (1), the amount\nof the costs may be recovered in the Federal Court as a debt due by\nthe first participant to the other participant.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Tribunal is satisfied that it is appropriate to do so, the\nTribunal may order that a participant in proceedings for review\nunder Division 1A or 1B pay all or a specified part of the costs of\nanother participant in the proceedings.\n\n(2) If the Tribunal makes an order under subsection (1), it may make\nfurther orders that it believes appropriate in relation to the\nassessment or taxation of the costs.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nReview by Tribunal of decisions of Commission  Part IX\nProcedure and Evidence  Division 2\n\nSection 112\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make provision for\nand in relation to fees payable for the assessment or taxation of\ncosts ordered by the Tribunal to be paid.\n\n(4) If a participant (the first participant) is ordered to pay some or all\nof the costs of another participant under subsection (1), the amount\nof the costs may be recovered in the Federal Court as a debt due by\nthe first participant to the other participant.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-111-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-111-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-111-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-111-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "893f2d5b874fb8dd8fee45c1661e44577f774e2058f57fd8e28da12b5da89e47"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-111",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "111 Tribunal may order costs be awarded",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 546,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Tribunal is satisfied that it is appropriate to do so, the\nTribunal may order that a participant in proceedings for review\nunder Division 1A or 1B pay all or a specified part of the costs of\nanother participant in the proceedings.\n\n(2) If the Tribunal makes an order under subsection (1), it may make\nfurther orders that it believes appropriate in relation to the\nassessment or taxation of the costs.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nReview by Tribunal of decisions of Commission  Part IX\nProcedure and Evidence  Division 2\n\nSection 112\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make provision for\nand in relation to fees payable for the assessment or taxation of\ncosts ordered by the Tribunal to be paid.\n\n(4) If a participant (the first participant) is ordered to pay some or all\nof the costs of another participant under subsection (1), the amount\nof the costs may be recovered in the Federal Court as a debt due by\nthe first participant to the other participant."
    },
