    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-112",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "112 Tribunal may charge fees",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-112"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.547",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of Division 1A or 1B, the Tribunal may, on behalf\nof the Commonwealth, charge fees determined under\nsubsection (2) for the purposes of this subsection.\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine fees for the\npurposes of subsection (1).\n\n(3) A determination under subsection (2) may provide for fees to be\npayable in respect of the following:\n\n(a) applications to the Tribunal under Division 1A or 1B;\n\n(b) proceedings in the Tribunal under Division 1A or 1B;\n\n(c) taxation of costs by the Tribunal in relation to such\nproceedings.\n\n(4) Without limiting the scope of a determination that may be made\nunder subsection (2), such a determination may determine, or\ndetermine matters relating to, any or all of the following:\n\n(a) the circumstances in which a fee is to be paid;\n\n(b) who must pay;\n\n(c) the time when payment is required;\n\n(d) remittal, refund and waiver of fees.\n\n(5) A determination made under subsection (2) may do any or all of\nthe following:\n\n(a) determine fees in respect of a particular class or classes of\napplications, costs or proceedings;\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of Division 1A or 1B, the Tribunal may, on behalf\nof the Commonwealth, charge fees determined under\nsubsection (2) for the purposes of this subsection.\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine fees for the\npurposes of subsection (1).\n\n(3) A determination under subsection (2) may provide for fees to be\npayable in respect of the following:\n\n(a) applications to the Tribunal under Division 1A or 1B;\n\n(b) proceedings in the Tribunal under Division 1A or 1B;\n\n(c) taxation of costs by the Tribunal in relation to such\nproceedings.\n\n(4) Without limiting the scope of a determination that may be made\nunder subsection (2), such a determination may determine, or\ndetermine matters relating to, any or all of the following:\n\n(a) the circumstances in which a fee is to be paid;\n\n(b) who must pay;\n\n(c) the time when payment is required;\n\n(d) remittal, refund and waiver of fees.\n\n(5) A determination made under subsection (2) may do any or all of\nthe following:\n\n(a) determine fees in respect of a particular class or classes of\napplications, costs or proceedings;\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-112-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-112-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-112-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-112-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-112-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9784b3e51c4d5190e0708c610e4f81faa2e799d78bb6619d297bd559e7f06bab"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-112",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "112 Tribunal may charge fees",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 547,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of Division 1A or 1B, the Tribunal may, on behalf\nof the Commonwealth, charge fees determined under\nsubsection (2) for the purposes of this subsection.\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine fees for the\npurposes of subsection (1).\n\n(3) A determination under subsection (2) may provide for fees to be\npayable in respect of the following:\n\n(a) applications to the Tribunal under Division 1A or 1B;\n\n(b) proceedings in the Tribunal under Division 1A or 1B;\n\n(c) taxation of costs by the Tribunal in relation to such\nproceedings.\n\n(4) Without limiting the scope of a determination that may be made\nunder subsection (2), such a determination may determine, or\ndetermine matters relating to, any or all of the following:\n\n(a) the circumstances in which a fee is to be paid;\n\n(b) who must pay;\n\n(c) the time when payment is required;\n\n(d) remittal, refund and waiver of fees.\n\n(5) A determination made under subsection (2) may do any or all of\nthe following:\n\n(a) determine fees in respect of a particular class or classes of\napplications, costs or proceedings;\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
