    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-113",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "113 Standing of Commission to seek judicial review",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-113"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.548",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section extends (and does not limit) the meaning of the term\nperson aggrieved in the Administrative Decisions (Judicial\nReview) Act 1977 for the purposes of the application of that Act in\nrelation to:\n\n(a) a decision made by the Tribunal under this Part (including a\ndecision of the Tribunal that is taken to be a decision of the\nCommission); or\n\n(b) a failure to make a decision under this Part; or\n\n(c) conduct engaged in for the purpose of making a decision\nunder this Part.\n\n(2) The Commission is taken to be a person aggrieved by the decision,\nfailure or conduct.\n\n(3) A term (except person aggrieved) used in this section and in the\nAdministrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act 1977 has the same\nmeaning in this section as it has in that Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section extends (and does not limit) the meaning of the term\nperson aggrieved in the Administrative Decisions (Judicial\nReview) Act 1977 for the purposes of the application of that Act in\nrelation to:\n\n(a) a decision made by the Tribunal under this Part (including a\ndecision of the Tribunal that is taken to be a decision of the\nCommission); or\n\n(b) a failure to make a decision under this Part; or\n\n(c) conduct engaged in for the purpose of making a decision\nunder this Part.\n\n(2) The Commission is taken to be a person aggrieved by the decision,\nfailure or conduct.\n\n(3) A term (except person aggrieved) used in this section and in the\nAdministrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act 1977 has the same\nmeaning in this section as it has in that Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-113-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-113-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-113-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4629a1c899473d040a70e98a19fadf1682b5b19d6ad8b27930fcfaba6a829c36"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-113",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "113 Standing of Commission to seek judicial review",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 548,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section extends (and does not limit) the meaning of the term\nperson aggrieved in the Administrative Decisions (Judicial\nReview) Act 1977 for the purposes of the application of that Act in\nrelation to:\n\n(a) a decision made by the Tribunal under this Part (including a\ndecision of the Tribunal that is taken to be a decision of the\nCommission); or\n\n(b) a failure to make a decision under this Part; or\n\n(c) conduct engaged in for the purpose of making a decision\nunder this Part.\n\n(2) The Commission is taken to be a person aggrieved by the decision,\nfailure or conduct.\n\n(3) A term (except person aggrieved) used in this section and in the\nAdministrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act 1977 has the same\nmeaning in this section as it has in that Act."
    },
